xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hematopoietic stem cells (HSCs) are progenitor cells that differentiate into all other blood cell types via the process of hematopoiesis.    Signaling description: Classically, HSCs are thought to differentiate into two distinct leneages, i.e. lymphoid and myelo-erythroid cells. Hematopoetic lineage cell can be identified by the expression of specific cell surface lineage markers. In mice common lymphoid progenitor cells are the earliest lymphoid progenitor cells, and give rise to T-lineage cells, B-lineage cells, natural killer (NK) cells.     Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hematopoietic stem cells (HSCs) are progenitor cells that differentiate into all other blood cell types via the process of hematopoiesis.    Signaling description: Classically, HSCs are thought to differentiate into two distinct leneages, i.e. lymphoid and myelo-erythroid cells. Hematopoetic lineage cell can be identified by the expression of specific cell surface lineage markers. In mice common lymphoid progenitor cells are the earliest lymphoid progenitor cells, and give rise to T-lineage cells, B-lineage cells, natural killer (NK) cells.     Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

