ins interacting with DICER1, such as FMR, TARBP2, and PRKRA, are also key regulators of RISC complex and DICER1 activity.    Outcome effects: In siRNA-guided RNA silencing, RISC complex cleaves the target mRNA at a single site in the center of the duplex region between the guide siRNA and the target mRNA, resulting in gene silencing. In contrast, miRNAs typically have incomplete base pairing to a target and thus may inhibit translation of many different mRNAs with similar sequences." EXACT []

