xref: PS:Description "The mammalian cell cycle divides into two stages: mitosis (M) - the process of nuclear division and interphase. Interphase is the interlude between two M phases. Interphase includes G1, S and G 2 phases. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: The mammalian cell cycle divides into two stages: mitosis (M) - the process of nuclear division and interphase. Interphase is the interlude between two M phases. Interphase includes G1, S and G 2 phases. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
