xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: In eukaryotes, the cell cycle consists of two major phases: the mitotic (M) phase (the process of nuclear division) and interphase (the interlude between two M phases). The interphase is further divided into three periods G1, S and G 2 phases. The G2/M DNA damage checkpoint prevents the cell from entering mitosis if the genome is damaged.    Signaling description: DNA damage up-regulates the ATM/ATR which leads to the activation of p53, Chk1 and Chk2. Further, Chks phosphorylates CDC25C. The phosphorylated, 14-3-3-bound form of CDC25C is prohibited from dephosphorylating and activating the mitotic CyclB-CDC2 kinase. The phosphorylation of p53 activates its DNA binding activity. The genes that are turned on by p53 include GADD45 which apparently binds to and dissociates the CycB-CDC2 kinase.    Outcome effects: As a result, the damaged cells are effectively blocked from entering mitosis."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: In eukaryotes, the cell cycle consists of two major phases: the mitotic (M) phase (the process of nuclear division) and interphase (the interlude between two M phases). The interphase is further divided into three periods G1, S and G 2 phases. The G2/M DNA damage checkpoint prevents the cell from entering mitosis if the genome is damaged.    Signaling description: DNA damage up-regulates the ATM/ATR which leads to the activation of p53, Chk1 and Chk2. Further, Chks phosphorylates CDC25C. The phosphorylated, 14-3-3-bound form of CDC25C is prohibited from dephosphorylating and activating the mitotic CyclB-CDC2 kinase. The phosphorylation of p53 activates its DNA binding activity. The genes that are turned on by p53 include GADD45 which apparently binds to and dissociates the CycB-CDC2 kinase.    Outcome effects: As a result, the damaged cells are effectively blocked from entering mitosis." EXACT []

