xref: PS:Description "Transfer RNA (tRNA) is a small RNA chain of 74-93 nucleotides that transfers a specific amino acid to a growing polypeptide chain during translation. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Transfer RNA (tRNA) is a small RNA chain of 74-93 nucleotides that transfers a specific amino acid to a growing polypeptide chain during translation. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
