xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The adherens junctions initiate cell-cell contacts and mediate maturation and maintenance of the contact. They consist of nectin and cadherin family cell adhesion molecules linked to the actin cytoskeleton through their binding proteins. Nectin and nectin-like molecules are cellular adhesion molecules involved in calcium-independent cellular adhesion.    Signaling description: Generally, all nectins have one intracellular domain, a single transmembrane helix, and three extracellular domains. The binding of MLLT4 and F-actin at nectin-nectin junctions induces major cytoskeletal regulators such as TJP1, LMO7, SSX2IP, ACTN1, CTNNA1, ZYX, SORBS1, vinculin (VCL), KEAP1, epsin (EPN1), tubulins, and myosins to modulate cytoskeletal reorganization and actin polymerization. Nectin recruits and activates SRC, which then phosphorylates CDC42 and VAV2 through the CRK-RAPGEF1 complex. Nectin-induced activation of CDC42 and RAC1 signaling pathway leads to the formation of filopodia and lamellipodia, respectively.    Outcome effects: Activated CDC42 and RAC1 bind to and specifically activate their downstream effectors which include scaffolding proteins such as BAIAP2, WAS, WASL, IQGAP1, and WASFs. This allows signals to flow through the actin related protein 2/3 complex to coordinate the initiation of new filaments. Nectin-induced activation of PARD3 and CDC42 enhance cell adhesion through the regulation of tight junctions in a highly-controlled manner."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The adherens junctions initiate cell-cell contacts and mediate maturation and maintenance of the contact. They consist of nectin and cadherin family cell adhesion molecules linked to the actin cytoskeleton through their binding proteins. Nectin and nectin-like molecules are cellular adhesion molecules involved in calcium-independent cellular adhesion.    Signaling description: Generally, all nectins have one intracellular domain, a single transmembrane helix, and three extracellular domains. The binding of MLLT4 and F-actin at nectin-nectin junctions induces major cytoskeletal regulators such as TJP1, LMO7, SSX2IP, ACTN1, CTNNA1, ZYX, SORBS1, vinculin (VCL), KEAP1, epsin (EPN1), tubulins, and myosins to modulate cytoskeletal reorganization and actin polymerization. Nectin recruits and activates SRC, which then phosphorylates CDC42 and VAV2 through the CRK-RAPGEF1 complex. Nectin-induced activation of CDC42 and RAC1 signaling pathway leads to the formation of filopodia and lamellipodia, respectively.    Outcome effects: Activated CDC42 and RAC1 bind to and specifically activate their downstream effectors which include scaffolding proteins such as BAIAP2, WAS, WASL, IQGAP1, and WASFs. This allows signals to flow through the actin related protein 2/3 complex to coordinate the initiation of new filaments. Nectin-induced activation of PARD3 and CDC42 enhance cell adhesion through the regulation of tight junctions in a highly-controlled manner." EXACT []

