xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The adherens junctions initiate cell-cell contacts and mediate maturation and maintenance of the contact. They consist of nectin and cadherin family cell adhesion molecules linked to the actin cytoskeleton through their binding proteins.    Signaling description: The cytoplasmic regions of classical cadherins such as CDH1, CDH2, CDH3, and CDH12 bind catenins including CTNNA1, CTNNB1, JUP, and CTNND1, which in turn bind vinculin (VCL), EPB41, MAGI1, MAGI2, MLLT4, and other proteins to regulate actin polymerization. MAGI2-CTNNB1 interaction at epithelial-cadherin junctions prevents the degradation of PTEN, which significantly decreases cell proliferation activity of AKT1. Similarly, MAGI1-CTNNB1 interaction at neuronal-cadherin junctions activates NOTCH1 on neighboring cells resulting in lateral inhibition of cell differentiation and firm adhesion. IQGAP1 regulates cadherin/catenin-mediated intercellular adhesion both positively and negatively. It captures and stabilizes microtubules/tubulins, leading to the establishment of polarized cell morphology and directional cell migration.    Outcome effects: Weak adhesions are formed due to growth factor-induced activation of receptor protein tyrosine kinases such as MET which causes the dissociation of CTNND1 and CTNNB1 from the cadherin/catenin complex, leading to the loss of cell adhesion function."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The adherens junctions initiate cell-cell contacts and mediate maturation and maintenance of the contact. They consist of nectin and cadherin family cell adhesion molecules linked to the actin cytoskeleton through their binding proteins.    Signaling description: The cytoplasmic regions of classical cadherins such as CDH1, CDH2, CDH3, and CDH12 bind catenins including CTNNA1, CTNNB1, JUP, and CTNND1, which in turn bind vinculin (VCL), EPB41, MAGI1, MAGI2, MLLT4, and other proteins to regulate actin polymerization. MAGI2-CTNNB1 interaction at epithelial-cadherin junctions prevents the degradation of PTEN, which significantly decreases cell proliferation activity of AKT1. Similarly, MAGI1-CTNNB1 interaction at neuronal-cadherin junctions activates NOTCH1 on neighboring cells resulting in lateral inhibition of cell differentiation and firm adhesion. IQGAP1 regulates cadherin/catenin-mediated intercellular adhesion both positively and negatively. It captures and stabilizes microtubules/tubulins, leading to the establishment of polarized cell morphology and directional cell migration.    Outcome effects: Weak adhesions are formed due to growth factor-induced activation of receptor protein tyrosine kinases such as MET which causes the dissociation of CTNND1 and CTNNB1 from the cadherin/catenin complex, leading to the loss of cell adhesion function." EXACT []

