xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The SCF complex (SKP, Cullin, F-box containing complex) is a multi-protein E3-ubiquitin ligase complex catalyzing the ubiquitination of proteins destined for proteasomal degradation. It has important roles in the ubiquitination of proteins involved in cell cycle and also marks various other cellular proteins for destruction. The SCF complex consists of four components: three constant subunits SKP1, RBX1 and CUL1, and a variable subunit, the F-box-protein. CUL1 (Cullin) is the core subunit on which the subunits RBX1 and SKP1 are assembled. RBX1 connects to E2 and SKP1 binds to the F-box-protein. Each F-box protein binds to a specific subset of substrate proteins, promoting their degradation. In SCF/FBXO11 complex, FBXO11 acts as the substrate recognition F-box protein.    Signaling description: Through a specific subset of substrate proteins, the core of SCF/FBXO11 related signaling leads to cell cycle progression, apoptosis and epithelial-mesenchymal transition (EMT). The precise mechanism of this is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: SCF/FBXO11 targets SNAI1, DTL and TP53. SNAI1 degradation by SCF/FBXO11 is dependent upon phosphorylation by PKD1. SCF/FBXO11 blocks SNAI1-induced EMT, tumor initiation and metastasis in multiple cancer models. During S and G2/M phases, SCF/FBXO11 promotes proteasomal degradation of DTL, a protein that controls cell cycle progression and response to DNA damage. CAND1 modulates the assembly of FBXO11 into cullin 1-RING ubiquitin ligase and NEDD8 leads to neddylation of TP53 and suppression of its function.    Animal data: Role of SCF/FBXO11 in the signaling was revealed partially from animal model experiments."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The SCF complex (SKP, Cullin, F-box containing complex) is a multi-protein E3-ubiquitin ligase complex catalyzing the ubiquitination of proteins destined for proteasomal degradation. It has important roles in the ubiquitination of proteins involved in cell cycle and also marks various other cellular proteins for destruction. The SCF complex consists of four components: three constant subunits SKP1, RBX1 and CUL1, and a variable subunit, the F-box-protein. CUL1 (Cullin) is the core subunit on which the subunits RBX1 and SKP1 are assembled. RBX1 connects to E2 and SKP1 binds to the F-box-protein. Each F-box protein binds to a specific subset of substrate proteins, promoting their degradation. In SCF/FBXO11 complex, FBXO11 acts as the substrate recognition F-box protein.    Signaling description: Through a specific subset of substrate proteins, the core of SCF/FBXO11 related signaling leads to cell cycle progression, apoptosis and epithelial-mesenchymal transition (EMT). The precise mechanism of this is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: SCF/FBXO11 targets SNAI1, DTL and TP53. SNAI1 degradation by SCF/FBXO11 is dependent upon phosphorylation by PKD1. SCF/FBXO11 blocks SNAI1-induced EMT, tumor initiation and metastasis in multiple cancer models. During S and G2/M phases, SCF/FBXO11 promotes proteasomal degradation of DTL, a protein that controls cell cycle progression and response to DNA damage. CAND1 modulates the assembly of FBXO11 into cullin 1-RING ubiquitin ligase and NEDD8 leads to neddylation of TP53 and suppression of its function.    Animal data: Role of SCF/FBXO11 in the signaling was revealed partially from animal model experiments." EXACT []

