xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: DNA in eukaryotic cells is packaged into chromatin, a complex structure in which DNA is associated with histones and a multitude of other proteins. TRRAP/TIP60 chromatin remodeling complex is a common component of many histone acetyltransferase (HAT) complexes.    Signaling description: A variety of mechanisms can be used to remodel chromatin; some act locally on a single nucleosome and others act more broadly. Chromatin remodeling can be accomplished by covalent modification of histones or by the action of ATP-dependent remodeling complexes. In addition to histone acetylase activity on chromatin, the TRRAP/TIP60 complex possesses ATPase, helicase, and structural DNA binding activities.    Outcome effects: TRRAP/TIP60 chromatin remodeling complex performs critical functions in a variety of cellular processes including chromatin remodeling, double-strand DNA break repair, and apoptosis. TRRAP is required for mitotic checkpoint and normal cell cycle progression."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: DNA in eukaryotic cells is packaged into chromatin, a complex structure in which DNA is associated with histones and a multitude of other proteins. TRRAP/TIP60 chromatin remodeling complex is a common component of many histone acetyltransferase (HAT) complexes.    Signaling description: A variety of mechanisms can be used to remodel chromatin; some act locally on a single nucleosome and others act more broadly. Chromatin remodeling can be accomplished by covalent modification of histones or by the action of ATP-dependent remodeling complexes. In addition to histone acetylase activity on chromatin, the TRRAP/TIP60 complex possesses ATPase, helicase, and structural DNA binding activities.    Outcome effects: TRRAP/TIP60 chromatin remodeling complex performs critical functions in a variety of cellular processes including chromatin remodeling, double-strand DNA break repair, and apoptosis. TRRAP is required for mitotic checkpoint and normal cell cycle progression." EXACT []

