xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: DNA in eukaryotic cells is packaged into chromatin, a complex structure in which DNA is associated with histones, and a multitude of other proteins. Inositol requiring 80 (INO80) chromatin remodeling complex regulates the expression of a subset of genes through its ATP-dependent chromatin remodeling activity.    Signaling description: A variety of mechanisms can be used to remodel chromatin; some act locally on a single nucleosome and others act more broadly. Chromatin remodeling, can be accomplished by covalent modification of histones or by the action of ATP-dependent remodeling complexes. In addition to its function in transcriptional regulation, the INO80 complex participates in multiple DNA repair pathways by its nucleosome remodeling ability and by regulating the accessibility of DNA repair proteins around the double strand DNA break site. The INO80 complex is enriched at stalled replication forks, where it promotes the resumption of replication upon recovery from the replication arrest.    Outcome effects: Ubiquitously expressed transcription factor YY1 controls the expression of many genes. YY1 is tightly associated with INO80 which recruited by YY1 to YY1-activated genes where it functions as an essential coactivator. RUVBL1 and RUVBL2, which have ATPase and DNA helicase activities, are also proposed core components of the INO80 complex."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: DNA in eukaryotic cells is packaged into chromatin, a complex structure in which DNA is associated with histones, and a multitude of other proteins. Inositol requiring 80 (INO80) chromatin remodeling complex regulates the expression of a subset of genes through its ATP-dependent chromatin remodeling activity.    Signaling description: A variety of mechanisms can be used to remodel chromatin; some act locally on a single nucleosome and others act more broadly. Chromatin remodeling, can be accomplished by covalent modification of histones or by the action of ATP-dependent remodeling complexes. In addition to its function in transcriptional regulation, the INO80 complex participates in multiple DNA repair pathways by its nucleosome remodeling ability and by regulating the accessibility of DNA repair proteins around the double strand DNA break site. The INO80 complex is enriched at stalled replication forks, where it promotes the resumption of replication upon recovery from the replication arrest.    Outcome effects: Ubiquitously expressed transcription factor YY1 controls the expression of many genes. YY1 is tightly associated with INO80 which recruited by YY1 to YY1-activated genes where it functions as an essential coactivator. RUVBL1 and RUVBL2, which have ATPase and DNA helicase activities, are also proposed core components of the INO80 complex." EXACT []

