xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The SCF complex (SKP, Cullin, F-box containing complex) is a multi-protein E3-ubiquitin ligase complex catalyzing the ubiquitination of proteins destined for proteasomal degradation. It has important roles in the ubiquitination of proteins involved in cell cycle and also marks various other cellular proteins for destruction. The SCF complex consists of four components: three constant subunits SKP1, RBX1 and CUL1, and a variable subunit, the F-box-protein. CUL1 (Cullin) is the core subunit on which the subunits RBX1 and SKP1 are assembled. RBX1 connects to E2 and SKP1 binds the F-box-protein. Each F-box protein binds to a specific subset of substrate proteins, promoting their degradation. In SCF/FBXW7 complex, FBXW7 acts as the substrate recognition F-box protein.    Signaling description: Through a specific subset of substrate proteins, the core of SCF/FBXW7 related signaling leads to regulation of cell cycle progression, and cell proliferation. The precise mechanism of the molecular signaling on this pathway is well known and is associated with negative regulation of AURKA, MYC, JUN, MYB, NFKB2, CSF3R, KLF5, MCL1, MTOR, NOTCH1, JUNB, CCNE1/2 and CDC6.    Outcome effects: SCF/FBXW7 targets and degrades the CCNE1/2, CDC6, MTOR and AURKA needed for G1/S transition, S phase regulation and G2/M transition. Degradation of MYC, JUN, JUNB, MYB, NFKB2, CSF3R, KLF5, MCL1, MTOR and NOTCH1 leads to regulation of cell proliferation and tumor suppression.    Animal data: Role of SCF/FBXW7 in the signaling was revealed partially from animal model experiments."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The SCF complex (SKP, Cullin, F-box containing complex) is a multi-protein E3-ubiquitin ligase complex catalyzing the ubiquitination of proteins destined for proteasomal degradation. It has important roles in the ubiquitination of proteins involved in cell cycle and also marks various other cellular proteins for destruction. The SCF complex consists of four components: three constant subunits SKP1, RBX1 and CUL1, and a variable subunit, the F-box-protein. CUL1 (Cullin) is the core subunit on which the subunits RBX1 and SKP1 are assembled. RBX1 connects to E2 and SKP1 binds the F-box-protein. Each F-box protein binds to a specific subset of substrate proteins, promoting their degradation. In SCF/FBXW7 complex, FBXW7 acts as the substrate recognition F-box protein.    Signaling description: Through a specific subset of substrate proteins, the core of SCF/FBXW7 related signaling leads to regulation of cell cycle progression, and cell proliferation. The precise mechanism of the molecular signaling on this pathway is well known and is associated with negative regulation of AURKA, MYC, JUN, MYB, NFKB2, CSF3R, KLF5, MCL1, MTOR, NOTCH1, JUNB, CCNE1/2 and CDC6.    Outcome effects: SCF/FBXW7 targets and degrades the CCNE1/2, CDC6, MTOR and AURKA needed for G1/S transition, S phase regulation and G2/M transition. Degradation of MYC, JUN, JUNB, MYB, NFKB2, CSF3R, KLF5, MCL1, MTOR and NOTCH1 leads to regulation of cell proliferation and tumor suppression.    Animal data: Role of SCF/FBXW7 in the signaling was revealed partially from animal model experiments." EXACT []

