xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: DNA in eukaryotic cells is packaged into chromatin, a complex structure in which DNA is associated with histones and a multitude of other proteins. The nucleosome-remodeling and histone deacetylation (NURD) chromatin remodeling complex is a novel regulator of DNA damage responses that orchestrates proper signaling and repair of double-strand breaks (DSBs).    Signaling description: A variety of mechanisms can be used to remodel chromatin; some act locally on a single nucleosome and others act more broadly. Chromatin remodeling can be accomplished by covalent modification of histones or by the action of ATP-dependent remodeling complexes. NURD has both ATP-dependent nucleosome remodeling and core histone acetylation and deacetylation activities to alter nucleosome structure. NURD cooperates with histone deacetylase complex (SIN3A) and together they are involved in transcriptional repression of methylated DNA.    Outcome effects: The methyl CpG binding protein (MECP2) as a subunit of NURD complex provides silencing of some methylated genes. In addition, NURD has been shown to be associated with zinc-finger DNA binding proteins such as IKZF1 and to be involved in centromeric silencing."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: DNA in eukaryotic cells is packaged into chromatin, a complex structure in which DNA is associated with histones and a multitude of other proteins. The nucleosome-remodeling and histone deacetylation (NURD) chromatin remodeling complex is a novel regulator of DNA damage responses that orchestrates proper signaling and repair of double-strand breaks (DSBs).    Signaling description: A variety of mechanisms can be used to remodel chromatin; some act locally on a single nucleosome and others act more broadly. Chromatin remodeling can be accomplished by covalent modification of histones or by the action of ATP-dependent remodeling complexes. NURD has both ATP-dependent nucleosome remodeling and core histone acetylation and deacetylation activities to alter nucleosome structure. NURD cooperates with histone deacetylase complex (SIN3A) and together they are involved in transcriptional repression of methylated DNA.    Outcome effects: The methyl CpG binding protein (MECP2) as a subunit of NURD complex provides silencing of some methylated genes. In addition, NURD has been shown to be associated with zinc-finger DNA binding proteins such as IKZF1 and to be involved in centromeric silencing." EXACT []

