xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: the SCF complex (SKP, Cullin, F-box containing complex) is a multi-protein E3-ubiquitin ligase complex catalyzing the ubiquitination of proteins destined for proteasomal degradation. It has important roles in the ubiquitination of proteins involved in cell cycle and also marks various other cellular proteins for destruction.The SCF complex consists of four components: three constant subunits SKP1, RBX1 and CUL1, and a variable subunit, the F-box-protein. CUL1 (Cullin) is the core subunit on which the subunits RBX1 and SKP1 are assembled. RBX1 connects to E2 and SKP1 binds to the F-box-protein. Each F-box protein binds to a specific subset of substrate proteins, promoting their degradation. In SCF/FBXO7 complex, FBXO7 (PKPS) acts as the substrate recognition F-box protein.    Signaling description: Through a specific subset of substrate proteins, the core of canonical SCF/FBXO7-ligase related signaling leads to regulation of mitotic spindle assembly and apoptosis. The precise mechanism of this is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: SCF/FBXO7 targets and degrades the DLGAP5, a protein that involved in mitotic spindle assembly. Degradation of TRAF2 and BIRC2 leads to the inhibition of NFKB1 anti-apoptotic activity.    Animal data: Role of SCF/FBXO7 in the signaling was revealed partially from animal model experiments."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: the SCF complex (SKP, Cullin, F-box containing complex) is a multi-protein E3-ubiquitin ligase complex catalyzing the ubiquitination of proteins destined for proteasomal degradation. It has important roles in the ubiquitination of proteins involved in cell cycle and also marks various other cellular proteins for destruction.The SCF complex consists of four components: three constant subunits SKP1, RBX1 and CUL1, and a variable subunit, the F-box-protein. CUL1 (Cullin) is the core subunit on which the subunits RBX1 and SKP1 are assembled. RBX1 connects to E2 and SKP1 binds to the F-box-protein. Each F-box protein binds to a specific subset of substrate proteins, promoting their degradation. In SCF/FBXO7 complex, FBXO7 (PKPS) acts as the substrate recognition F-box protein.    Signaling description: Through a specific subset of substrate proteins, the core of canonical SCF/FBXO7-ligase related signaling leads to regulation of mitotic spindle assembly and apoptosis. The precise mechanism of this is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: SCF/FBXO7 targets and degrades the DLGAP5, a protein that involved in mitotic spindle assembly. Degradation of TRAF2 and BIRC2 leads to the inhibition of NFKB1 anti-apoptotic activity.    Animal data: Role of SCF/FBXO7 in the signaling was revealed partially from animal model experiments." EXACT []

