xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Lamellipodia are cytoskeletal actin projections on the leading edge of the cell found mostly in mobile cells. Filopodia are slim cytoplasmic protrusions that extend from the leading edge of lamellipodia in migrating cells. Both lamellipodia and filopodia are implicated in cancer cell metastatic progression.    Signaling description: It is not completely clear what triggers the formation of these cytoskeletal projections. Most probably, the activation of receptor tyrosine kinases leads to PI3K signaling activation and triggers the process. The lamellipodia formation is regulated mostly through the RAC1/ WAVE complex/actin related protein 2/3 complex, RAC1/DIAPH and RAC1/PAK1/LIMK/CFL1 pathways. All these signaling routes eventually lead to actin polymerization. The filopodia formation is regulated mainly through the CDC42/WAS/actin related protein 2/3 complex and CDC42/ DIAPH, CDC42/ BAIAP2, CDC42/ PAK1/LIMK/CFL1 pathways which similarly lead to actin polymerization.    Outcome effects: Actin polymerization promotes lamellipodia/filopodia formation and cancer cell migration."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Lamellipodia are cytoskeletal actin projections on the leading edge of the cell found mostly in mobile cells. Filopodia are slim cytoplasmic protrusions that extend from the leading edge of lamellipodia in migrating cells. Both lamellipodia and filopodia are implicated in cancer cell metastatic progression.    Signaling description: It is not completely clear what triggers the formation of these cytoskeletal projections. Most probably, the activation of receptor tyrosine kinases leads to PI3K signaling activation and triggers the process. The lamellipodia formation is regulated mostly through the RAC1/ WAVE complex/actin related protein 2/3 complex, RAC1/DIAPH and RAC1/PAK1/LIMK/CFL1 pathways. All these signaling routes eventually lead to actin polymerization. The filopodia formation is regulated mainly through the CDC42/WAS/actin related protein 2/3 complex and CDC42/ DIAPH, CDC42/ BAIAP2, CDC42/ PAK1/LIMK/CFL1 pathways which similarly lead to actin polymerization.    Outcome effects: Actin polymerization promotes lamellipodia/filopodia formation and cancer cell migration." EXACT []

