xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The localization of PKD1/2, PKHD1, DCDC2, KIF3A, CEP290 and NPHP1/3/4 and INVS at the primary cilium and basal bodies is proposed to be crucial for their function as mechanosensory antennae of fluid flow in the kidney. However, precise mechanisms by which cilia participate in normal physiology and CKD pathogenesis are largely undefined. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Signaling description: The PKD1-PKD2 complex located at the primary cilia surface and functions as a fluid shear sensor to regulate the calcium signal. KIF3A-KIF3B-KIFAP3 complex are the essential intraflagellar transport-associated kinesin-2 motors.     Outcome effects: PKHD1 stimulates PKD2 channel activity in the presence of the kinesin-2 motor. CEP290 and DCDC2 interact with KIF3A to microtubule organization. PKD1 binds with NPHP1-4 complex that localized to microtubule-based structures. INVS and KIF3A modulate cytoskeleton organization and cell polarity via interaction with CTNNB1."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The localization of PKD1/2, PKHD1, DCDC2, KIF3A, CEP290 and NPHP1/3/4 and INVS at the primary cilium and basal bodies is proposed to be crucial for their function as mechanosensory antennae of fluid flow in the kidney. However, precise mechanisms by which cilia participate in normal physiology and CKD pathogenesis are largely undefined. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Signaling description: The PKD1-PKD2 complex located at the primary cilia surface and functions as a fluid shear sensor to regulate the calcium signal. KIF3A-KIF3B-KIFAP3 complex are the essential intraflagellar transport-associated kinesin-2 motors.     Outcome effects: PKHD1 stimulates PKD2 channel activity in the presence of the kinesin-2 motor. CEP290 and DCDC2 interact with KIF3A to microtubule organization. PKD1 binds with NPHP1-4 complex that localized to microtubule-based structures. INVS and KIF3A modulate cytoskeleton organization and cell polarity via interaction with CTNNB1." EXACT []

