synonym: "Source: Cell Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Misfolded proteins are selectively transferred from the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) into the cytosol where they undergo subsequent ubiquitylation and degradation by the proteasome. This process is called ER-associated degradation (ERAD).    Signaling description: Unfolded polypeptides enter the ER through SEC61 translocon. These polypeptides are bound by chaperones and glycosylating enzymes that facilitate their structural maturation. The polypeptides that are terminally misfolded are dislocated back into the cytoplasm to undergo polyubiquitylation and subsequent degradation. The export of such aberrant polypeptides from the ER is determined by members of the ERAD machinery including DERL1, DERL2, DERL3, HERPUD1, SEL1L, and SYVN1 that dynamically form oligomeric pore complexes. DERL1 and DERL2 interact with VCP and potentiate it to directly bind the substrate and deliver it to the proteasome for final degradation. AMFR protein then interacts with VCP to accelerate the degradation.    Outcome effects: After deglycosylation of the aberrant polypeptide by NGLY1, RAD23A, and UBQLN, the polypeptide becomes available to be bound by polyubiquitin and RPN1 protein for final targeting to the proteasome."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Misfolded proteins are selectively transferred from the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) into the cytosol where they undergo subsequent ubiquitylation and degradation by the proteasome. This process is called ER-associated degradation (ERAD).    Signaling description: Unfolded polypeptides enter the ER through SEC61 translocon. These polypeptides are bound by chaperones and glycosylating enzymes that facilitate their structural maturation. The polypeptides that are terminally misfolded are dislocated back into the cytoplasm to undergo polyubiquitylation and subsequent degradation. The export of such aberrant polypeptides from the ER is determined by members of the ERAD machinery including DERL1, DERL2, DERL3, HERPUD1, SEL1L, and SYVN1 that dynamically form oligomeric pore complexes. DERL1 and DERL2 interact with VCP and potentiate it to directly bind the substrate and deliver it to the proteasome for final degradation. AMFR protein then interacts with VCP to accelerate the degradation.    Outcome effects: After deglycosylation of the aberrant polypeptide by NGLY1, RAD23A, and UBQLN, the polypeptide becomes available to be bound by polyubiquitin and RPN1 protein for final targeting to the proteasome." EXACT []

