xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The BBSome is an octameric protein complex. It is a component of the basal body and is involved in cargo trafficking to the primary cilium and flagella, cilium biogenesis and microtubule organization.    Signaling description: The BBSome is a complex of seven Bardet-Biedl syndrome (BBS) proteins: BBS1, BBS2, BBS4, BBS5, BBS7, BBS8 (TTC8), BBS9 and BBIP10 protein that is linked to the ciliary membrane by the small GTPase BBS3 (ARL6). BBSome is proposed to serve as an adaptor involved in the export of signaling proteins from the cilium, as an IFT regulator and a core IFT component, or as a cargo adaptor. BBSome interaction with SMO, PTCH1 and LEPR leads to receptor internalization. BBSome interaction with PABIN8 (RAB3IP), CEP290, PCM1, and DCTN1 promotes cilium biogenesis and microtubule organization. The precise mechanism of this is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: BBSome is a proposed regulator of intraflagellar transport, cilium biogenesis and microtubule organization.    Animal data: Some of the data was revealed from animal model experiments."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The BBSome is an octameric protein complex. It is a component of the basal body and is involved in cargo trafficking to the primary cilium and flagella, cilium biogenesis and microtubule organization.    Signaling description: The BBSome is a complex of seven Bardet-Biedl syndrome (BBS) proteins: BBS1, BBS2, BBS4, BBS5, BBS7, BBS8 (TTC8), BBS9 and BBIP10 protein that is linked to the ciliary membrane by the small GTPase BBS3 (ARL6). BBSome is proposed to serve as an adaptor involved in the export of signaling proteins from the cilium, as an IFT regulator and a core IFT component, or as a cargo adaptor. BBSome interaction with SMO, PTCH1 and LEPR leads to receptor internalization. BBSome interaction with PABIN8 (RAB3IP), CEP290, PCM1, and DCTN1 promotes cilium biogenesis and microtubule organization. The precise mechanism of this is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: BBSome is a proposed regulator of intraflagellar transport, cilium biogenesis and microtubule organization.    Animal data: Some of the data was revealed from animal model experiments." EXACT []

