synonym: "Source: Cell Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: DNA repair by means of homologous recombination takes place when an identical or a near identical sequence exists to provide the template for DNA recovery.    Signaling description: The protein machinery responsible for this recovery process is similar to that in meiotic crossing-over when homologous chromatids serve as the templates. The double strand bases (DSBs) appear as the result of mistakes in filling single-nucleotide gaps in the replicative fork or as the result of unfixed errors that occurred during single-stranded DNA synthesis. After DSBs are detected by ATM, the 5' strands are removed producing long 3' single-stranded DNA tails.    Outcome effects: The single-stranded 3' tails serve as the substrate for RAD51 nucleoprotein filament nucleation. RAD52, BRCA1, and BRCA2 proteins are also recruited in this process. When assembled, this protein complex screens the genome for homologous DNA sequences that can be used for the recombination."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: DNA repair by means of homologous recombination takes place when an identical or a near identical sequence exists to provide the template for DNA recovery.    Signaling description: The protein machinery responsible for this recovery process is similar to that in meiotic crossing-over when homologous chromatids serve as the templates. The double strand bases (DSBs) appear as the result of mistakes in filling single-nucleotide gaps in the replicative fork or as the result of unfixed errors that occurred during single-stranded DNA synthesis. After DSBs are detected by ATM, the 5' strands are removed producing long 3' single-stranded DNA tails.    Outcome effects: The single-stranded 3' tails serve as the substrate for RAD51 nucleoprotein filament nucleation. RAD52, BRCA1, and BRCA2 proteins are also recruited in this process. When assembled, this protein complex screens the genome for homologous DNA sequences that can be used for the recombination." EXACT []

