xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Direct DNA repair includes single-enzyme mechanisms that can repair lesions without the incision of DNA sugar-phosphate backbone or base excision.    Signaling description: In humans, the main type of direct DNA damage reversal systems repair alkylating damage by alkyltransferases and dioxygenases. Alkylation damage may be the result of environmental exposure of DNA to compounds like nitrosoguanidine or methyl mesylate, which cause a variety of O-alkylated and N-alkylated adducts. Biologically important lesions formed in double-stranded DNA (dsDNA) are 6-methoxyguanine, 3-methylcytosine, and 1-methyladenine. Although alkylated bases can be removed by multistep excision repair processes, several lesions are also subject to effective and highly specific direct repair mechanisms.    Outcome effects: Dioxygenases ALKBH2 and ALKBH3 preferentially repair 1-methyladenine and 3-methylcytosine lesions by oxidative demethylation. ALKBH3 prefers single-stranded DNA (ssDNA) or RNA substrates while ALKBH2 preferentially acts on dsDNA. MGMT directly dealkylates mutagenic 6-methoxyguanine lesions within DNA."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Direct DNA repair includes single-enzyme mechanisms that can repair lesions without the incision of DNA sugar-phosphate backbone or base excision.    Signaling description: In humans, the main type of direct DNA damage reversal systems repair alkylating damage by alkyltransferases and dioxygenases. Alkylation damage may be the result of environmental exposure of DNA to compounds like nitrosoguanidine or methyl mesylate, which cause a variety of O-alkylated and N-alkylated adducts. Biologically important lesions formed in double-stranded DNA (dsDNA) are 6-methoxyguanine, 3-methylcytosine, and 1-methyladenine. Although alkylated bases can be removed by multistep excision repair processes, several lesions are also subject to effective and highly specific direct repair mechanisms.    Outcome effects: Dioxygenases ALKBH2 and ALKBH3 preferentially repair 1-methyladenine and 3-methylcytosine lesions by oxidative demethylation. ALKBH3 prefers single-stranded DNA (ssDNA) or RNA substrates while ALKBH2 preferentially acts on dsDNA. MGMT directly dealkylates mutagenic 6-methoxyguanine lesions within DNA." EXACT []

