xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The deficiency of interleukin-1 receptor antagonist (DIRA) is an autosomal recessive autoinflammatory disease caused by mutations in the IL1RN gene on chromosome 2. DIRA manifests itself clinically with perinatal-onset pustular dermatitis, joint swelling, painful osteolytic lesions, and periostitis. Fever is rare and neurologic inflammation is absent. Laboratory findings in DIRA include persistent elevation of acute-phase inflammatory indicators.    Signaling description: Mutations in the IL1RN gene lead to the absence of IL1RN and subsequent IL1 overactivity. The IL1B signaling receptor complex has a role in the autocrine feedback induction of the pro-IL1B gene promoter region.    Outcome effects: Mutations in IL1RN cause loss of inhibitory function in IL1B and IL1A signaling through IL1R1, and result in systemic inflammation with skin and bone involvement.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The deficiency of interleukin-1 receptor antagonist (DIRA) is an autosomal recessive autoinflammatory disease caused by mutations in the IL1RN gene on chromosome 2. DIRA manifests itself clinically with perinatal-onset pustular dermatitis, joint swelling, painful osteolytic lesions, and periostitis. Fever is rare and neurologic inflammation is absent. Laboratory findings in DIRA include persistent elevation of acute-phase inflammatory indicators.    Signaling description: Mutations in the IL1RN gene lead to the absence of IL1RN and subsequent IL1 overactivity. The IL1B signaling receptor complex has a role in the autocrine feedback induction of the pro-IL1B gene promoter region.    Outcome effects: Mutations in IL1RN cause loss of inhibitory function in IL1B and IL1A signaling through IL1R1, and result in systemic inflammation with skin and bone involvement.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

