xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: PAPA (pyogenic arthritis, pyoderma gangrenosum, and acne) syndrome (MIM 604416) is an autosomal dominant disease caused by mutations in the PSTPIP1 gene encoding CD2-binding protein 1 (CD2BP1). The disease appears in early childhood and is characterized by joint involvement manifested by severe self-limiting pyogenic arthritis. In terms of skin involvement, the appearance of pyoderma gangrenosum and nodular-cystic acne are also described in early childhood.    Signaling description: CD2BP1 is involved in the proper assembly of the cytoskeleton and normally inhibits pyrin-mediated inflammatory signals and the activation of CASP1.    Outcome effects: Increased IL1B production has been demonstrated in a patient with clinically active PAPA syndrome caused by Ala230Thr PSTPIP1 mutation.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: PAPA (pyogenic arthritis, pyoderma gangrenosum, and acne) syndrome (MIM 604416) is an autosomal dominant disease caused by mutations in the PSTPIP1 gene encoding CD2-binding protein 1 (CD2BP1). The disease appears in early childhood and is characterized by joint involvement manifested by severe self-limiting pyogenic arthritis. In terms of skin involvement, the appearance of pyoderma gangrenosum and nodular-cystic acne are also described in early childhood.    Signaling description: CD2BP1 is involved in the proper assembly of the cytoskeleton and normally inhibits pyrin-mediated inflammatory signals and the activation of CASP1.    Outcome effects: Increased IL1B production has been demonstrated in a patient with clinically active PAPA syndrome caused by Ala230Thr PSTPIP1 mutation.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

