xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Familial cold autoinflammatory syndrome 2 (FCAS2; MIM 611762) is a rare disease caused by mutations in NLRP12 (also known as NALP12) gene, which encodes a member of the NLR family. The clinical features of these patients resemble familial cold autoinflammatory syndrome (FCAS). The reported patients describe attacks of fever and arthralgia lasting 2 to10 days and are induced by exposure to cold. Some attacks are accompanied by urticaria, abdominal pain, and lymphadenopathy. Hearing loss has been observed in at least two patients.    Signaling description: NLRP12 has been shown to associate with ASC and activate CASP-1. In addition, NLRP12 can block the hyperphosphorylation of IRAK, eventually limiting downstream NF-kB signaling.    Outcome effects: NF-kB signaling pathway regulates the production of cytokines involved in inflammatory responses. Activated CASP1 can convert pro-IL-1beta to its mature form (IL1B). IL-1beta maturation and secretion activates inflammatory response.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Familial cold autoinflammatory syndrome 2 (FCAS2; MIM 611762) is a rare disease caused by mutations in NLRP12 (also known as NALP12) gene, which encodes a member of the NLR family. The clinical features of these patients resemble familial cold autoinflammatory syndrome (FCAS). The reported patients describe attacks of fever and arthralgia lasting 2 to10 days and are induced by exposure to cold. Some attacks are accompanied by urticaria, abdominal pain, and lymphadenopathy. Hearing loss has been observed in at least two patients.    Signaling description: NLRP12 has been shown to associate with ASC and activate CASP-1. In addition, NLRP12 can block the hyperphosphorylation of IRAK, eventually limiting downstream NF-kB signaling.    Outcome effects: NF-kB signaling pathway regulates the production of cytokines involved in inflammatory responses. Activated CASP1 can convert pro-IL-1beta to its mature form (IL1B). IL-1beta maturation and secretion activates inflammatory response.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

