xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hirschsprung disease (HSCR) is a congenital disorder that is characterized by intestinal dysmotility due to an absence of enteric ganglia along variable lengths of the intestinal tract, preferably in the colon. HSCR results from aberrant migration, proliferation, or differentiation of vagal neural crest cells.    Signaling description: A mutation in KIF1-binding protein (KIAA1279) gene is one of the causes of Hirschsprung disease development. Normally, KIAA1279 is required for the organization of axonal microtubules and axonal outgrowth. It also regulates mitochondrial transport by modulating KIF1B motor activity.    Outcome effects: When KIAA1279 is mutated, axonal outgrowth and mitochondrial distribution in axons are impaired leading to aganglionosis development.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hirschsprung disease (HSCR) is a congenital disorder that is characterized by intestinal dysmotility due to an absence of enteric ganglia along variable lengths of the intestinal tract, preferably in the colon. HSCR results from aberrant migration, proliferation, or differentiation of vagal neural crest cells.    Signaling description: A mutation in KIF1-binding protein (KIAA1279) gene is one of the causes of Hirschsprung disease development. Normally, KIAA1279 is required for the organization of axonal microtubules and axonal outgrowth. It also regulates mitochondrial transport by modulating KIF1B motor activity.    Outcome effects: When KIAA1279 is mutated, axonal outgrowth and mitochondrial distribution in axons are impaired leading to aganglionosis development.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

