xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Mutant huntingtin (HTT) leads to multiple cellular dysfunctions in Huntington disease (HD) via different mechanisms, including transcriptional repression of the mitochondrial master regulator peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor gamma, coactivator 1 alpha (PGC1alpha, PPARGC1A).    Signaling description: PPARGC1A forms complexes with transcription factors, including nuclear respiratory factors, NRF1/2, and the nuclear receptors, PPARalpha/delta/gamma, estrogen related receptor alpha (ERRalpha). These transcription factors, in turn, regulate the expression of many nuclear-encoded mitochondrial genes, such as cytochrome c (CYCS), mitochondrial complexes I-V and the mitochondrial transcription factors TFAM, TFB1M/2M. Deficiency of these factors leads to mitochondrial dysfunction.PPARGC1A plays a role in myelination regulating expression of myelin basic protein (MBP) and myelin-associated oligodendrocyte basic protein (MOBP). PPARGC1A controls enzymes 3-hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl-CoA reductase (HMGCR) and 3-hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl-CoA synthase 1 (HMGCS1) taking part in cholesterol metabolism and thereby making impact to myelin synthesis.PPARGC1A plays a role in the suppression of oxidative stress, and it induces antioxidant enzymes superoxide dismutase 1/2 (SOD1/2) and glutathione peroxidase (GPX1). In HD these functions are impaired.Protein with decreased expression or activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Mutant huntingtin (HTT) leads to multiple cellular dysfunctions in Huntington disease (HD) via different mechanisms, including transcriptional repression of the mitochondrial master regulator peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor gamma, coactivator 1 alpha (PGC1alpha, PPARGC1A).    Signaling description: PPARGC1A forms complexes with transcription factors, including nuclear respiratory factors, NRF1/2, and the nuclear receptors, PPARalpha/delta/gamma, estrogen related receptor alpha (ERRalpha). These transcription factors, in turn, regulate the expression of many nuclear-encoded mitochondrial genes, such as cytochrome c (CYCS), mitochondrial complexes I-V and the mitochondrial transcription factors TFAM, TFB1M/2M. Deficiency of these factors leads to mitochondrial dysfunction.PPARGC1A plays a role in myelination regulating expression of myelin basic protein (MBP) and myelin-associated oligodendrocyte basic protein (MOBP). PPARGC1A controls enzymes 3-hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl-CoA reductase (HMGCR) and 3-hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl-CoA synthase 1 (HMGCS1) taking part in cholesterol metabolism and thereby making impact to myelin synthesis.PPARGC1A plays a role in the suppression of oxidative stress, and it induces antioxidant enzymes superoxide dismutase 1/2 (SOD1/2) and glutathione peroxidase (GPX1). In HD these functions are impaired.Protein with decreased expression or activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

