xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The IkB kinase beta (IKBKB) is a prominent regulator of neuroinflammation, which is implicated in the pathogenesis of Huntington disease (HD). IKBKB may directly regulate the cleavage and neurotoxicity of huntingtin.     Signaling description: Activation of IKBKB by DNA damage triggers caspase-dependent cleavage of mutant huntingtin (mHTT) and enhances the accumulation of oligomeric fragments which have neurotoxic properties. Moreover, mHTT directly binds to and activate IKBKB thus forming a deleterious feed-forward loop. mHTT also may be cleaved to oligomeric fragments by caspase 3 and 6 (CASP3/6) and these caspases in turn may be activated by IKBKB. Activated caspases finally lead to apoptosis. IKBKB may activate NFkB and production of inflammatory cytokines and chemokines including IL6, IL8, IL1B, TNF, CCL2 inducing neuroinflammation. mHTT may also activate IKBKG leading to the same results.Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The IkB kinase beta (IKBKB) is a prominent regulator of neuroinflammation, which is implicated in the pathogenesis of Huntington disease (HD). IKBKB may directly regulate the cleavage and neurotoxicity of huntingtin.     Signaling description: Activation of IKBKB by DNA damage triggers caspase-dependent cleavage of mutant huntingtin (mHTT) and enhances the accumulation of oligomeric fragments which have neurotoxic properties. Moreover, mHTT directly binds to and activate IKBKB thus forming a deleterious feed-forward loop. mHTT also may be cleaved to oligomeric fragments by caspase 3 and 6 (CASP3/6) and these caspases in turn may be activated by IKBKB. Activated caspases finally lead to apoptosis. IKBKB may activate NFkB and production of inflammatory cytokines and chemokines including IL6, IL8, IL1B, TNF, CCL2 inducing neuroinflammation. mHTT may also activate IKBKG leading to the same results.Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

