xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Misfolded huntingtin (HTT) induces endoplasmic reticulum (ER) stress contributing to pathogenesis of Huntington Disease. ER stress is alleviated by the activation of an adaptive reaction known as the unfolded protein response (UPR), whereas chronic ER stress triggers apoptosis by the same pathway.     Signaling description: UPR signaling is initiated by the activation of at least three distinct stress sensors located at the ER membrane known as ERN1 (IRE1a), EIF2AK3 (PERK) and ATF6. ERN1 is as a regulator of mutant HTT clearance. ERN1 cleaves and activates XBP1 triggering autophagy via FOXO1 and its target genes. ERN1 also activates TRAF2/MAPK8 and my induce apoptosis. MAPK8 activation also increased expression of ATG5 and Beclin-1 responsible for autophagy.Upon activation EIF2AK3 phosphorylates eIF2alpha (EIF2S1) leading to activation of ATF4. ATF4 induces the expression of ATG12, ATG5 and BECN1, providing a direct link between UPR signaling and the control of autophagy. ATF6 activates XBP-1 with consequent events. CHOP (DDIT3) gene promoter contains binding sites for all of the major inducers of the unfolded protein response (UPR), including ATF4, ATF6, and XBP-1, and these transcription induce DDIT3 gene transcription. DDIT3 induces apoptosis, through a Bcl-2-inhibitable mechanism.    Outcome effects: Mutant HTT binds to and activates type 1 inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate receptor (ITPR1), mediating calcium release from the endoplasmic reticulum and cytoplasmic calcium overload.Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Misfolded huntingtin (HTT) induces endoplasmic reticulum (ER) stress contributing to pathogenesis of Huntington Disease. ER stress is alleviated by the activation of an adaptive reaction known as the unfolded protein response (UPR), whereas chronic ER stress triggers apoptosis by the same pathway.     Signaling description: UPR signaling is initiated by the activation of at least three distinct stress sensors located at the ER membrane known as ERN1 (IRE1a), EIF2AK3 (PERK) and ATF6. ERN1 is as a regulator of mutant HTT clearance. ERN1 cleaves and activates XBP1 triggering autophagy via FOXO1 and its target genes. ERN1 also activates TRAF2/MAPK8 and my induce apoptosis. MAPK8 activation also increased expression of ATG5 and Beclin-1 responsible for autophagy.Upon activation EIF2AK3 phosphorylates eIF2alpha (EIF2S1) leading to activation of ATF4. ATF4 induces the expression of ATG12, ATG5 and BECN1, providing a direct link between UPR signaling and the control of autophagy. ATF6 activates XBP-1 with consequent events. CHOP (DDIT3) gene promoter contains binding sites for all of the major inducers of the unfolded protein response (UPR), including ATF4, ATF6, and XBP-1, and these transcription induce DDIT3 gene transcription. DDIT3 induces apoptosis, through a Bcl-2-inhibitable mechanism.    Outcome effects: Mutant HTT binds to and activates type 1 inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate receptor (ITPR1), mediating calcium release from the endoplasmic reticulum and cytoplasmic calcium overload.Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

