xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Usher syndrome is a rare genetic disorder characterized by hearing loss and a gradual vision loss due to retinitis pigmentosa (progressive degeneration of photoreceptor cells in the retina). The disease is clinically and genetically heterogeneous with at least 15 chromosomal loci being assigned to three clinical Usher syndrome types, namely USH1A-G, USH2A-C, and USH3A.    Signaling description: Proteins whose genes are mutated in Usher syndrome are located in the stereocilia of the inner ear hair cells and involved in different molecular processes such as motor activity and cell adhesion.    Outcome effects: USH1 genes code for the molecular motor myosin VIIa (MYO7A, USH1B), two cell-cell adhesion cadherin proteins, cadherin 23 (CDH23, USH1D), protocadherin 15 (PCDH15, USH1F), and the scaffold proteins, harmonin (USH1C) and SANS (USH1G). Alterations in the CIB2 calcium- and integrin-binding protein cause Usher syndrome type 1J and nonsyndromic deafness DFNB48. USH2 genes code for the transmembrane protein USH2A (\"usherin\"), the G-protein-coupled 7-transmembrane receptor GPR98 (VLGR1b, USH2C), and DFNB31 (USH2D). USH3A gene encodes clarin-1 (CLRN1).    Mutated proteins: Mutated proteins are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Usher syndrome is a rare genetic disorder characterized by hearing loss and a gradual vision loss due to retinitis pigmentosa (progressive degeneration of photoreceptor cells in the retina). The disease is clinically and genetically heterogeneous with at least 15 chromosomal loci being assigned to three clinical Usher syndrome types, namely USH1A-G, USH2A-C, and USH3A.    Signaling description: Proteins whose genes are mutated in Usher syndrome are located in the stereocilia of the inner ear hair cells and involved in different molecular processes such as motor activity and cell adhesion.    Outcome effects: USH1 genes code for the molecular motor myosin VIIa (MYO7A, USH1B), two cell-cell adhesion cadherin proteins, cadherin 23 (CDH23, USH1D), protocadherin 15 (PCDH15, USH1F), and the scaffold proteins, harmonin (USH1C) and SANS (USH1G). Alterations in the CIB2 calcium- and integrin-binding protein cause Usher syndrome type 1J and nonsyndromic deafness DFNB48. USH2 genes code for the transmembrane protein USH2A (\"usherin\"), the G-protein-coupled 7-transmembrane receptor GPR98 (VLGR1b, USH2C), and DFNB31 (USH2D). USH3A gene encodes clarin-1 (CLRN1).    Mutated proteins: Mutated proteins are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

