xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Usher syndrome is a rare genetic disorder characterized by hearing loss and a gradual vision loss due to retinitis pigmentosa (progressive degeneration of photoreceptor cells in the retina). Some of the proteins whose genes are mutated in Usher syndrome are involved in synaptic transduction between the inner ear hair cell and neuron.    Mutated proteins: Mutated proteins are shown in white-out style."
