xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Congenital hypothyroidism is a condition of thyroid hormone deficiency present at birth. Approximately 1 out of 3000-4000 newborn infants has a severe deficiency of thyroid function. If left untreated, severe congenital hypothyroidism can lead to growth failure and permanent mental retardation. Treatment consists of a daily oral dosage of thyroxin. Most cases of congenital hypothyroidism are sporadic and an estimated 15 to 20 percent of cases are inherited.    Signaling description: Gene mutations cause the loss of thyroid function in one of two ways: 1) mutations which disrupt the normal development of the thyroid gland before birth and 2) mutations which reduce the production of thyroid hormones, even though the thyroid gland is present. Mutations in PAX8, FOXE1, GLIS3, NKX2-1, and some mutations in thyroid-stimulating hormone receptor (TSHR) prevent or disrupt the normal development of the thyroid gland before birth. These account for only 2% of thyroid dysgenesis cases while 98% are of unknown cause. The loss-of-function autosomal dominant mutations of the paired box 8 (PAX8) gene are considered to primarily cause congenital hypothyroidism due to thyroid hypoplasia. PAX8 regulates the expression of genes encoding thyroglobulin (TG), thyroid peroxidase (TPO), and the sodium-iodide symporter (NIS) by binding to their promoter regions through its 128-amino acid paired domain. PAX8 is also expressed in the mesonephros and ureteric buds which may explain the increased incidence of genitourinary malformations in patients with congenital hypothyroidism. The role of PAX8 in thyroid development is poorly understood. The pathway displays thyroid gland development in relation to a mutation in PAX8.    Outcome effects: PAX8 expression targets are shown to be important to thyroid gland function. The remaining proteins were added after the analysis of neighbors of PAX8 in Pathway Studio. Only those that are significant in the development of thyroid cells were included.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Congenital hypothyroidism is a condition of thyroid hormone deficiency present at birth. Approximately 1 out of 3000-4000 newborn infants has a severe deficiency of thyroid function. If left untreated, severe congenital hypothyroidism can lead to growth failure and permanent mental retardation. Treatment consists of a daily oral dosage of thyroxin. Most cases of congenital hypothyroidism are sporadic and an estimated 15 to 20 percent of cases are inherited.    Signaling description: Gene mutations cause the loss of thyroid function in one of two ways: 1) mutations which disrupt the normal development of the thyroid gland before birth and 2) mutations which reduce the production of thyroid hormones, even though the thyroid gland is present. Mutations in PAX8, FOXE1, GLIS3, NKX2-1, and some mutations in thyroid-stimulating hormone receptor (TSHR) prevent or disrupt the normal development of the thyroid gland before birth. These account for only 2% of thyroid dysgenesis cases while 98% are of unknown cause. The loss-of-function autosomal dominant mutations of the paired box 8 (PAX8) gene are considered to primarily cause congenital hypothyroidism due to thyroid hypoplasia. PAX8 regulates the expression of genes encoding thyroglobulin (TG), thyroid peroxidase (TPO), and the sodium-iodide symporter (NIS) by binding to their promoter regions through its 128-amino acid paired domain. PAX8 is also expressed in the mesonephros and ureteric buds which may explain the increased incidence of genitourinary malformations in patients with congenital hypothyroidism. The role of PAX8 in thyroid development is poorly understood. The pathway displays thyroid gland development in relation to a mutation in PAX8.    Outcome effects: PAX8 expression targets are shown to be important to thyroid gland function. The remaining proteins were added after the analysis of neighbors of PAX8 in Pathway Studio. Only those that are significant in the development of thyroid cells were included.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

