xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Familial partial lipodystrophies (FPL) are a heterogeneous group of disorders with several distinct phenotypes. FPL type 4 is the result of an autosomal dominantly inherited mutation in perilipin 1 (PLIN1) gene. FPL4 is characterized by childhood or young adult onset of loss of subcutaneous adipose tissue primarily affecting the lower limbs, insulin-resistant diabetes mellitus, hypertriglyceridemia, and hypertension.     Signaling description: PLIN1 is localized on the surface of lipid droplets which protects them until they can be broken down by hormone-sensitive lipase. PLIN1 regulates SREBF1, which promotes FASN, ACACB, and ACACA which are involved in lipid metabolism. SREBF1 promotes PPARG, which promotes AGPAT2, LPL, UCP3, RETN, and LEP. AGPAT2, LPL, and UCP3 are involved in adipocyte differentiation while RETN and LEP play an endocrine role. In addition, PPARG promotes SLC2A4, thus increasing glucose uptake. The abnormality in glucose uptake and the dysregulation of lipid and protein metabolism causes insulin resistance which ultimately leads to diabetes mellitus.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Familial partial lipodystrophies (FPL) are a heterogeneous group of disorders with several distinct phenotypes. FPL type 4 is the result of an autosomal dominantly inherited mutation in perilipin 1 (PLIN1) gene. FPL4 is characterized by childhood or young adult onset of loss of subcutaneous adipose tissue primarily affecting the lower limbs, insulin-resistant diabetes mellitus, hypertriglyceridemia, and hypertension.     Signaling description: PLIN1 is localized on the surface of lipid droplets which protects them until they can be broken down by hormone-sensitive lipase. PLIN1 regulates SREBF1, which promotes FASN, ACACB, and ACACA which are involved in lipid metabolism. SREBF1 promotes PPARG, which promotes AGPAT2, LPL, UCP3, RETN, and LEP. AGPAT2, LPL, and UCP3 are involved in adipocyte differentiation while RETN and LEP play an endocrine role. In addition, PPARG promotes SLC2A4, thus increasing glucose uptake. The abnormality in glucose uptake and the dysregulation of lipid and protein metabolism causes insulin resistance which ultimately leads to diabetes mellitus.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

