xref: PS:Notes "Friedreich's ataxia is a rare autosomal recessive disorder with one case 1 in 50,000 in general human population. Friedreich's ataxia is characterized by progressive nervous system damage with symptoms including poor coordination, neurological complications, scoliosis, heart disease and diabetes. Cognitive function is not affected. As the disease is progressed to an advanced stage, wheelchair may be required for mobility."
