xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: A missense mutation in the gene encoding the beta-3 subunit of the GABAA receptor (GABRB3) was detected in a patient with chronic insomnia who had a family history of sleep problems.     Signaling description: The Cl- conductance evoked by GABA decays faster in GABRB3 mutated channels than in wild-type channels. These results indicate that mutations in the GABAA-receptors may be involved in the pathogenesis of insomnia. Furthermore, sleep disorders including insomnia have been effectively treated with the therapeutic agents that stimulate GABAA-receptor Cl- channel activity. GABRB3 mutations / polymorphisms are also associated with development of epilepsy and autism.Also, adenosine was shown to play important role in sleep control. Adenosine deaminase (ADA) is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of adenosine to inosine. ADA polymorphism was shown to modulate the duration of slow-wave sleep as well as the intensity of sleep. ADA polymorphism was shown to modulate the duration of slow-wave sleep as well as the intensity of sleep."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: A missense mutation in the gene encoding the beta-3 subunit of the GABAA receptor (GABRB3) was detected in a patient with chronic insomnia who had a family history of sleep problems.     Signaling description: The Cl- conductance evoked by GABA decays faster in GABRB3 mutated channels than in wild-type channels. These results indicate that mutations in the GABAA-receptors may be involved in the pathogenesis of insomnia. Furthermore, sleep disorders including insomnia have been effectively treated with the therapeutic agents that stimulate GABAA-receptor Cl- channel activity. GABRB3 mutations / polymorphisms are also associated with development of epilepsy and autism.Also, adenosine was shown to play important role in sleep control. Adenosine deaminase (ADA) is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of adenosine to inosine. ADA polymorphism was shown to modulate the duration of slow-wave sleep as well as the intensity of sleep. ADA polymorphism was shown to modulate the duration of slow-wave sleep as well as the intensity of sleep." EXACT []

