xref: PS:Notes "Arylalkylamine N-acetyltransferase (AANAT) is an enzyme that is involved in the day/night rhythmic production of melatonin, by modification of serotonin. Melatonin is essential for the function of the circadian clock that influences activity and sleep. AANAT polymorphism is associated with circadian rhythm sleep disorders - delayed sleep phase syndrome."
synonym: "Notes: Arylalkylamine N-acetyltransferase (AANAT) is an enzyme that is involved in the day/night rhythmic production of melatonin, by modification of serotonin. Melatonin is essential for the function of the circadian clock that influences activity and sleep. AANAT polymorphism is associated with circadian rhythm sleep disorders - delayed sleep phase syndrome." EXACT []

