xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Serotonin is one of the most important brain neurotransmitters for regulating the sleep/wake cycle. High levels of serotonin are associated with wakefulness and lower levels with sleep. Serotonin is involved in wakefulness, in triggering sleep, and in REM sleep.    Signaling description: A serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SRI) is a type of drug which acts as a reuptake inhibitor of the neurotransmitter serotonin by blocking the action of the serotonin transporter (SLC6A4). This in turn leads to increased extracellular concentrations of serotonin and, therefore, an increase in serotonergic neurotransmission. SRIs are used predominantly as antidepressants, though they are also commonly used in the treatment of other psychological conditions such as anxiety disorders and eating disorders.     Outcome effects: Insomnia is one of the common side effects of SRI."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Serotonin is one of the most important brain neurotransmitters for regulating the sleep/wake cycle. High levels of serotonin are associated with wakefulness and lower levels with sleep. Serotonin is involved in wakefulness, in triggering sleep, and in REM sleep.    Signaling description: A serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SRI) is a type of drug which acts as a reuptake inhibitor of the neurotransmitter serotonin by blocking the action of the serotonin transporter (SLC6A4). This in turn leads to increased extracellular concentrations of serotonin and, therefore, an increase in serotonergic neurotransmission. SRIs are used predominantly as antidepressants, though they are also commonly used in the treatment of other psychological conditions such as anxiety disorders and eating disorders.     Outcome effects: Insomnia is one of the common side effects of SRI." EXACT []

