xref: PS:Notes "Prostaglandin D2 (PTGDS) is a potent endogenous hormone for promoting sleep. Down-regulation of PTGDS in the aged hypothalamus and cortex may contribute to the sleep disorders associated with aging. Decrease of PTGDS in cerebrospinal fluid was detected in depressed patients, which could contribute to sleep disturbances in these patients."
