xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) is a progressive degenerative lethal disorder of both the upper and lower motor neurons leading to progressive atrophy and paralysis of skeletal muscles.    Signaling description: Neuroinflammation is now recognized as an important aspect amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) pathology. In ALS, astrocytes and microglia are markedly activated and produce many pro-inflammatory molecules including TNF, IL6, IL1B, IGF1, PGE2, and others. Normally, motor neurons produce CX3CL1 and CD200, which prevent microglia from becoming neurotoxic. However, in ALS these factors are downregulated.    Outcome effects: As a result, the pro-inflammatory factors can ultimately cause damage to motor neurons.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) is a progressive degenerative lethal disorder of both the upper and lower motor neurons leading to progressive atrophy and paralysis of skeletal muscles.    Signaling description: Neuroinflammation is now recognized as an important aspect amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) pathology. In ALS, astrocytes and microglia are markedly activated and produce many pro-inflammatory molecules including TNF, IL6, IL1B, IGF1, PGE2, and others. Normally, motor neurons produce CX3CL1 and CD200, which prevent microglia from becoming neurotoxic. However, in ALS these factors are downregulated.    Outcome effects: As a result, the pro-inflammatory factors can ultimately cause damage to motor neurons.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

