xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Muscular dystrophy refers to a group of progressive muscular disorders with muscle weakening and breakdown being the major symptom.    Signaling description: Myostatin (MSTN) is a member of the TGF-beta family that acts as a repressor of muscle differentiation and growth. MSTN is produced by muscle cells and once secreted binds to FST, FSTL3, and WFIKKN2 which are extracellular regulators of MSTN activity. MSTN acts on muscle cells through activin type II receptor (ACVR2A and ACVR2B). Upon ligand-receptor binding, ACVR1B and TGFBR1 coreceptors are recruited to initiate SMAD activation. Another mechanism of repressing myogenesis is MSTN-induced activation of MAPKs through MAP3K7/ mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase (MAPKK) and Ras/Raf/MEK cascades.    Outcome effects: SMADs repress myogenic factors such as MYOD1, MYOG, and PAX3 and positively regulate protein degradation through FOXO3/TRIM63 and FBXO32.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Muscular dystrophy refers to a group of progressive muscular disorders with muscle weakening and breakdown being the major symptom.    Signaling description: Myostatin (MSTN) is a member of the TGF-beta family that acts as a repressor of muscle differentiation and growth. MSTN is produced by muscle cells and once secreted binds to FST, FSTL3, and WFIKKN2 which are extracellular regulators of MSTN activity. MSTN acts on muscle cells through activin type II receptor (ACVR2A and ACVR2B). Upon ligand-receptor binding, ACVR1B and TGFBR1 coreceptors are recruited to initiate SMAD activation. Another mechanism of repressing myogenesis is MSTN-induced activation of MAPKs through MAP3K7/ mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase (MAPKK) and Ras/Raf/MEK cascades.    Outcome effects: SMADs repress myogenic factors such as MYOD1, MYOG, and PAX3 and positively regulate protein degradation through FOXO3/TRIM63 and FBXO32.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

