xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Muscular dystrophy refers to a group of progressive muscular disorders with muscle weakening and breakdown being the major symptom.    Signaling description: Interleukin 6 (IL6) is a pleiotropic cytokine that plays a key role in a broad range of processes including inflammation, immune response, metabolism, muscle function, and oncogenesis.IL6 plays a dual role in inflammation: it can repress inflammation through the inhibition of TNFA and some pro-inflammatory cytokines and enhance inflammation through the up-regulation of acute phase proteins. IL6 binding to IL6R activates signaling through JAK/STAT cascade. resulting in the overexpression of STAT-regulated genes, including genes coding for acute phase proteins. JAK phosphorylates SHP2 protein (PTPN11) that activates Ras/Raf/MEK/MAPK1, VAV1/RAC1, and PI3K/AKT1 signaling pathways.    Outcome effects: The increased activity of PI3K/Akt/NF-kB pathway represses apoptosis and promotes cell survival. Activation of the JAK/STAT cascade results in the overexpression of STAT-regulated genes, including genes coding for acute phase proteins.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Muscular dystrophy refers to a group of progressive muscular disorders with muscle weakening and breakdown being the major symptom.    Signaling description: Interleukin 6 (IL6) is a pleiotropic cytokine that plays a key role in a broad range of processes including inflammation, immune response, metabolism, muscle function, and oncogenesis.IL6 plays a dual role in inflammation: it can repress inflammation through the inhibition of TNFA and some pro-inflammatory cytokines and enhance inflammation through the up-regulation of acute phase proteins. IL6 binding to IL6R activates signaling through JAK/STAT cascade. resulting in the overexpression of STAT-regulated genes, including genes coding for acute phase proteins. JAK phosphorylates SHP2 protein (PTPN11) that activates Ras/Raf/MEK/MAPK1, VAV1/RAC1, and PI3K/AKT1 signaling pathways.    Outcome effects: The increased activity of PI3K/Akt/NF-kB pathway represses apoptosis and promotes cell survival. Activation of the JAK/STAT cascade results in the overexpression of STAT-regulated genes, including genes coding for acute phase proteins.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

