xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Muscular dystrophy refers to a group of progressive muscular disorders with muscle weakening and breakdown being the major symptom.    Signaling description: Plasma levels of IL6 significantly increase after exercise. Several mechanisms may link exercise to IL6 production, although the exact details are yet to be elucidated. During prolonged exercise, IL6 expression can be induced by Ca2+/calcineurin-NFATC1/ Jun/Fos pathway. A more intense contraction with higher Ca2+ amplitudes can activate NF-kB and MAPK8 signaling for IL6 production. Another signal for IL6 induction is a decreased glycogen level, by p38 kinase directly or through activating NF-kB. An epinephrine response is also a likely cause of IL6 up-regulation.    Outcome effects: Interleukin 6 (IL6) is a pleiotropic cytokine that plays a key role in a broad range of processes including inflammation, immune response, metabolism, muscle function, and oncogenesis. Acting in a hormone-like fashion, IL6 affects glucose homeostasis and lipolysis in liver and adipose tissue, and decreases inflammation through inhibiting pro-inflammatory cytokines such as TNFA."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Muscular dystrophy refers to a group of progressive muscular disorders with muscle weakening and breakdown being the major symptom.    Signaling description: Plasma levels of IL6 significantly increase after exercise. Several mechanisms may link exercise to IL6 production, although the exact details are yet to be elucidated. During prolonged exercise, IL6 expression can be induced by Ca2+/calcineurin-NFATC1/ Jun/Fos pathway. A more intense contraction with higher Ca2+ amplitudes can activate NF-kB and MAPK8 signaling for IL6 production. Another signal for IL6 induction is a decreased glycogen level, by p38 kinase directly or through activating NF-kB. An epinephrine response is also a likely cause of IL6 up-regulation.    Outcome effects: Interleukin 6 (IL6) is a pleiotropic cytokine that plays a key role in a broad range of processes including inflammation, immune response, metabolism, muscle function, and oncogenesis. Acting in a hormone-like fashion, IL6 affects glucose homeostasis and lipolysis in liver and adipose tissue, and decreases inflammation through inhibiting pro-inflammatory cytokines such as TNFA." EXACT []

