xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Muscular dystrophy refers to a group of progressive muscular disorders with muscle weakening and breakdown being the major symptom.    Signaling description: The size of skeletal muscle can change in response to a variety of environmental signals such as loading, nutrients, and starvation. Insulin growth factor 1 (IGF1) regulates muscle mass via the IGF1/MAPK and IGF1/AKT1 signaling pathways. Hypertrophic signaling through IGF1 is also coupled with mechanical signals by means of the calcium-induced activation of calcineurin.    Outcome effects: IGF1 signaling regulates muscle mass in three ways: 1) increasing the number of myofibers through the activation of stem cell proliferation, differentiation, and myoblast fusion into myotubes via IGF1/MAPK and IGF1/AKT1 branches; 2) increasing protein synthesis by mTOR activation through IGF1/AKT1 and; 3) repressing muscle atrophy pathways via FOXO repression through IGF1/AKT1.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Muscular dystrophy refers to a group of progressive muscular disorders with muscle weakening and breakdown being the major symptom.    Signaling description: The size of skeletal muscle can change in response to a variety of environmental signals such as loading, nutrients, and starvation. Insulin growth factor 1 (IGF1) regulates muscle mass via the IGF1/MAPK and IGF1/AKT1 signaling pathways. Hypertrophic signaling through IGF1 is also coupled with mechanical signals by means of the calcium-induced activation of calcineurin.    Outcome effects: IGF1 signaling regulates muscle mass in three ways: 1) increasing the number of myofibers through the activation of stem cell proliferation, differentiation, and myoblast fusion into myotubes via IGF1/MAPK and IGF1/AKT1 branches; 2) increasing protein synthesis by mTOR activation through IGF1/AKT1 and; 3) repressing muscle atrophy pathways via FOXO repression through IGF1/AKT1.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

