xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Neuroblastoma (NB), the most common extracranial solid tumor in childhood, is derived from precursor cells of the peripheral (sympathetic) nervous system (neural crest neuroblasts). Tumors are most frequently found in the adrenal medulla and paraspinal ganglia, but can arise anywhere along the sympathetic chain.Signaling descripton: Anaplastic lymphoma kinase (ALK) is a receptor tyrosine kinase that is normally expressed in neurons of the central and peripheral nervous systems at late embryonic stages and promotes cell growth and neurite outgrowth. Activating germline mutations of ALK are responsible for the majority of hereditary neuroblastoma (NB) cases. Moreover, ALK point mutations are often found in sporadic NB cases. ALK may function through the PI3K/AKT1, MAPK, and JAK/STAT signaling cascades.    Outcome effects: The resulting signaling events lead to the upregulation of cell proliferation and inhibition of apoptosis. Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Neuroblastoma (NB), the most common extracranial solid tumor in childhood, is derived from precursor cells of the peripheral (sympathetic) nervous system (neural crest neuroblasts). Tumors are most frequently found in the adrenal medulla and paraspinal ganglia, but can arise anywhere along the sympathetic chain.Signaling descripton: Anaplastic lymphoma kinase (ALK) is a receptor tyrosine kinase that is normally expressed in neurons of the central and peripheral nervous systems at late embryonic stages and promotes cell growth and neurite outgrowth. Activating germline mutations of ALK are responsible for the majority of hereditary neuroblastoma (NB) cases. Moreover, ALK point mutations are often found in sporadic NB cases. ALK may function through the PI3K/AKT1, MAPK, and JAK/STAT signaling cascades.    Outcome effects: The resulting signaling events lead to the upregulation of cell proliferation and inhibition of apoptosis. Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

