xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Cataract is clouding of the eye's lens that affects vision. Mutations in the EPHA2 proteins gene cause congenital cataract and are associated with age-related cataract resulting in the posterior subcapsular form of the disease.    Signaling description: EPHA2, a receptor of the ephrin receptor subfamily, regulates processes of cell migration in the lens independent of ligand stimulation. Normally, EPHA2 exerts its effects through the activation of AKT1.    Outcome effects: AKT1 involves IKBK, which phosphorylates NFKBIA disrupting its interaction with NF-kB, which is then released from its inhibitor, NFKBIA and binds to the promoter regions of integrins. In addition, AKT1 phosphorylates CTNNB1 which interacts with proteins of the cytoskeleton leading to cell migration.    Mutated proteins: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Cataract is clouding of the eye's lens that affects vision. Mutations in the EPHA2 proteins gene cause congenital cataract and are associated with age-related cataract resulting in the posterior subcapsular form of the disease.    Signaling description: EPHA2, a receptor of the ephrin receptor subfamily, regulates processes of cell migration in the lens independent of ligand stimulation. Normally, EPHA2 exerts its effects through the activation of AKT1.    Outcome effects: AKT1 involves IKBK, which phosphorylates NFKBIA disrupting its interaction with NF-kB, which is then released from its inhibitor, NFKBIA and binds to the promoter regions of integrins. In addition, AKT1 phosphorylates CTNNB1 which interacts with proteins of the cytoskeleton leading to cell migration.    Mutated proteins: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

