xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss. Mutations of PITX2, PAX6, LMX1B, and CYP1B1 cause dysgenesis of the anterior segment of the eye and are associated with glaucoma.    Signaling description: PITX2, PAX6, and LMX1B control tyrosine hydroxylase (TH) activity. CYP1B1 catalyzes a rate limiting step in retinoic acid (RA) biosynthesis necessary for eye development, and activates TFAP2A, which can regulate TH.    Outcome effects: TH converts L-tyrosine to L-DOPA, which affects exit from the cell cycle, and is a precursor of developmentally important catecholamines. Therefore, TH may contribute to angle development by producing L-DOPA.    Mutated proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss. Mutations of PITX2, PAX6, LMX1B, and CYP1B1 cause dysgenesis of the anterior segment of the eye and are associated with glaucoma.    Signaling description: PITX2, PAX6, and LMX1B control tyrosine hydroxylase (TH) activity. CYP1B1 catalyzes a rate limiting step in retinoic acid (RA) biosynthesis necessary for eye development, and activates TFAP2A, which can regulate TH.    Outcome effects: TH converts L-tyrosine to L-DOPA, which affects exit from the cell cycle, and is a precursor of developmentally important catecholamines. Therefore, TH may contribute to angle development by producing L-DOPA.    Mutated proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

