xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss. CDKN2B-AS1 is a long, non-coding RNA encoded in chromosome 9p21 region. This locus is a hotspot for disease-associated polymorphisms and has been consistently associated with cardiovascular disease, several cancers, diabetes, glaucoma, and other conditions.    Signaling description: The distinctive role of CDKN2B-AS1 in the pathogenesis of these conditions is yet to be determined. CDKN2B-AS1 binds PRC2 to induce methylation of histone H3 and results in silencing of the CDKN2A/B locus. CDKN2B-AS1 binds PRC1, which allows the recognition of histone H3 necessary for monoubiquitination at histone H2A and silencing maintenance. The expression of CDKN2B-AS1 may be regulated by Ras, STAT1, and ATM/E2F1.    Outcome effects: CDKN2B-AS1 modulation impacts the repressing ability of PRC1/2 proteins, inducing or inhibiting expression of CDKN2A/B, and possibly other distant loci by histone modification.    Mutated proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss. CDKN2B-AS1 is a long, non-coding RNA encoded in chromosome 9p21 region. This locus is a hotspot for disease-associated polymorphisms and has been consistently associated with cardiovascular disease, several cancers, diabetes, glaucoma, and other conditions.    Signaling description: The distinctive role of CDKN2B-AS1 in the pathogenesis of these conditions is yet to be determined. CDKN2B-AS1 binds PRC2 to induce methylation of histone H3 and results in silencing of the CDKN2A/B locus. CDKN2B-AS1 binds PRC1, which allows the recognition of histone H3 necessary for monoubiquitination at histone H2A and silencing maintenance. The expression of CDKN2B-AS1 may be regulated by Ras, STAT1, and ATM/E2F1.    Outcome effects: CDKN2B-AS1 modulation impacts the repressing ability of PRC1/2 proteins, inducing or inhibiting expression of CDKN2A/B, and possibly other distant loci by histone modification.    Mutated proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

