xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss. Approximately 4% of adult-onset primary open-angle glaucoma cases and more than 10% of juvenile-onset cases are associated with myocilin (MYOC) mutations.    Signaling description: The exact function of MYOC is unknown. Elevated amounts of wild-type MYOC in the aqueous humor of transgenic mice produce significant changes in the expression of genes involved in cell adhesion and cell-matrix interactions.    Outcome effects: Therefore, MYOC is suggested to have a role in modulating cellular adhesion. Among the genes that were found to be differentially regulatedby MYOC are WASL, CEACAM1, and SPON2. All of these genes are involved in cell adhesion and cell-matrix interactions.    Animal data: Experimental data obtained from transgenic mice.    Mutated proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss. Approximately 4% of adult-onset primary open-angle glaucoma cases and more than 10% of juvenile-onset cases are associated with myocilin (MYOC) mutations.    Signaling description: The exact function of MYOC is unknown. Elevated amounts of wild-type MYOC in the aqueous humor of transgenic mice produce significant changes in the expression of genes involved in cell adhesion and cell-matrix interactions.    Outcome effects: Therefore, MYOC is suggested to have a role in modulating cellular adhesion. Among the genes that were found to be differentially regulatedby MYOC are WASL, CEACAM1, and SPON2. All of these genes are involved in cell adhesion and cell-matrix interactions.    Animal data: Experimental data obtained from transgenic mice.    Mutated proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

