xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss.    Signaling description: Prostaglandin F2A (PGF2alpha) analogs are effectively used in current glaucoma treatment. These agents are the most effective of the intraocular pressure (IOP)-lowering agents and a single daily dose is effective at reducing IOP throughout the day and during the night.    Outcome effects: PGF2alpha analogs increase uveoscleral outflow by increasing matrix metalloproteinase expression and altering the extracellular matrix in the ciliary muscle and trabecular meshwork. The adverse effects are lengthening and thickening of eyelashes and they can also cause hazel and blue irides with brown patches to become diffusely brown."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss.    Signaling description: Prostaglandin F2A (PGF2alpha) analogs are effectively used in current glaucoma treatment. These agents are the most effective of the intraocular pressure (IOP)-lowering agents and a single daily dose is effective at reducing IOP throughout the day and during the night.    Outcome effects: PGF2alpha analogs increase uveoscleral outflow by increasing matrix metalloproteinase expression and altering the extracellular matrix in the ciliary muscle and trabecular meshwork. The adverse effects are lengthening and thickening of eyelashes and they can also cause hazel and blue irides with brown patches to become diffusely brown." EXACT []

