xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss.    Signaling description: Noradrenalin has an important role in the regulation of aqueous humor (AH) production by the ciliary body and intraocular pressure (IOP) regulation. Alpha-2-adrenergic receptor (ADRA2A) agonist and beta-1-adrenergic receptor (ADRB1) blockers are commonly used as anti-glaucoma treatment.    Outcome effects: ADRA2A agonist activates presynaptic ADRA2A, thus inhibiting the release of noradrenalin. ADRB1 blockers act post-synaptically and inhibit cAMP production, thereby decreasing AH production."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss.    Signaling description: Noradrenalin has an important role in the regulation of aqueous humor (AH) production by the ciliary body and intraocular pressure (IOP) regulation. Alpha-2-adrenergic receptor (ADRA2A) agonist and beta-1-adrenergic receptor (ADRB1) blockers are commonly used as anti-glaucoma treatment.    Outcome effects: ADRA2A agonist activates presynaptic ADRA2A, thus inhibiting the release of noradrenalin. ADRB1 blockers act post-synaptically and inhibit cAMP production, thereby decreasing AH production." EXACT []

