xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss.    Signaling description: The interruption of axonal transport and neurotrophic factor (NTF) deprivation due to elevated intraocular pressure are believed to cause retinal ganglion cell (RGC) apoptosis in glaucoma. A range of NTFs, including BDNF, NTF3/4, NGF, and CNTF, are implicated in this process. The presence of NTFs supports cell survival and NTF deprivation may lead to apoptosis. The selective activation of NTRK1 by NGF promotes the survival of injured RGCs. The co-expression of NGFR and NTRK1 increases NGF binding and enhances NGF-mediated NTRK1 activation.    Outcome effects: However, when NTRK1/NGFR ratios are low or when neurotrophin levels are limited, NGFR activation leads to neuronal death. Pro-NGF may initiate cell apoptosis by binding to NGFR-SORT1 receptor complex. In addition, CNTF has been shown to stimulate axonal regeneration via STAT3 signaling. NTF4 may be absent due to mutation in rare cases of glaucoma. The knockdown of endogenous OPTN induces apoptotic cell death due to the reduced secretion of NTF3 and CNTF. NTFs are regarded as potential therapeutic agents in glaucoma.    Mutated proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss.    Signaling description: The interruption of axonal transport and neurotrophic factor (NTF) deprivation due to elevated intraocular pressure are believed to cause retinal ganglion cell (RGC) apoptosis in glaucoma. A range of NTFs, including BDNF, NTF3/4, NGF, and CNTF, are implicated in this process. The presence of NTFs supports cell survival and NTF deprivation may lead to apoptosis. The selective activation of NTRK1 by NGF promotes the survival of injured RGCs. The co-expression of NGFR and NTRK1 increases NGF binding and enhances NGF-mediated NTRK1 activation.    Outcome effects: However, when NTRK1/NGFR ratios are low or when neurotrophin levels are limited, NGFR activation leads to neuronal death. Pro-NGF may initiate cell apoptosis by binding to NGFR-SORT1 receptor complex. In addition, CNTF has been shown to stimulate axonal regeneration via STAT3 signaling. NTF4 may be absent due to mutation in rare cases of glaucoma. The knockdown of endogenous OPTN induces apoptotic cell death due to the reduced secretion of NTF3 and CNTF. NTFs are regarded as potential therapeutic agents in glaucoma.    Mutated proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

