xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss.    Signaling description: The aqueous humor (AH) of the eye is a transparent fluid consisting of water (98%), ions, amino acids, and biomolecules such as signaling molecules, growth factors, and extracellular matrix molecules. Serotonin signaling is implicated in the regulation of AH production by the ciliary body and intraocular pressure (IOP) regulation. The topical application of serotonin may both elevate and lower IOP.    Outcome effects: HTR1A, HTR2A/2C, and HTR7 are expressed in the iris and ciliary body. HTR1A and HTR7 are linked to adenylate cyclase (ADCY) activity modulation. HTR1A activation inhibits cAMP production and decreases AH production, while HTR7 has the opposite effect. HTR2A/2C activation leads to IP3 production and an increase of AH production. HTR1B and HTR1D are localized at pre-synaptic membranes. Upon stimulation, they lead to the inhibition of serotonin release. The role of HTR1B/1D in IOP regulation has yet to be determined. The reuptake of serotonin is completed by SLC6A4. Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors may provoke glaucoma."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Glaucoma refers to a group of eye disoders in which ocular hypertension damages the optic nerve eventually leading to vision loss.    Signaling description: The aqueous humor (AH) of the eye is a transparent fluid consisting of water (98%), ions, amino acids, and biomolecules such as signaling molecules, growth factors, and extracellular matrix molecules. Serotonin signaling is implicated in the regulation of AH production by the ciliary body and intraocular pressure (IOP) regulation. The topical application of serotonin may both elevate and lower IOP.    Outcome effects: HTR1A, HTR2A/2C, and HTR7 are expressed in the iris and ciliary body. HTR1A and HTR7 are linked to adenylate cyclase (ADCY) activity modulation. HTR1A activation inhibits cAMP production and decreases AH production, while HTR7 has the opposite effect. HTR2A/2C activation leads to IP3 production and an increase of AH production. HTR1B and HTR1D are localized at pre-synaptic membranes. Upon stimulation, they lead to the inhibition of serotonin release. The role of HTR1B/1D in IOP regulation has yet to be determined. The reuptake of serotonin is completed by SLC6A4. Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors may provoke glaucoma." EXACT []

