xref: PS:Source "Diseases"
synonym: "Source: Diseases" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Resistance to progesterone action is one of hallmarks of endometriosis. The molecular basis of progesterone resistance in endometriosis may be related to an overall reduction in the levels of progesterone receptor (PGR).     Signaling description: In endometriotic cells, pathologically high ERB suppress PGR expression. Progesterone induces HSD17B2 expression which normally metabolizes the biologically potent estradiol (E2). The end result is deficient metabolism of E2 in endometriosis giving rise to high local concentrations of this mitogen. Progesterone receptor (PGR) is necessary for CRABP2 expression in endometrial cells. CRABP2 directs retinoic acid toward RARA, which results in growth arrest and apoptosis.     Outcome effects: Thereby low PGR expression inhibits apoptosis and stimulates cell proliferation. Low PGR expression leads to inability to induce FOXO1 expression, activation of proliferation and impairment of apoptosis and decidualization."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Resistance to progesterone action is one of hallmarks of endometriosis. The molecular basis of progesterone resistance in endometriosis may be related to an overall reduction in the levels of progesterone receptor (PGR).     Signaling description: In endometriotic cells, pathologically high ERB suppress PGR expression. Progesterone induces HSD17B2 expression which normally metabolizes the biologically potent estradiol (E2). The end result is deficient metabolism of E2 in endometriosis giving rise to high local concentrations of this mitogen. Progesterone receptor (PGR) is necessary for CRABP2 expression in endometrial cells. CRABP2 directs retinoic acid toward RARA, which results in growth arrest and apoptosis.     Outcome effects: Thereby low PGR expression inhibits apoptosis and stimulates cell proliferation. Low PGR expression leads to inability to induce FOXO1 expression, activation of proliferation and impairment of apoptosis and decidualization." EXACT []

