xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Premature ovarian failure, also known as premature ovarian insufficiency, primary ovarian insufficiency, premature menopause, hypergonadotropic hypogonadism, is the loss of function of the ovaries before age 40. It is characterized by amenorrhea, hypergonadotropinism, and hypoestrogenism. Mutations in several oocyte-specific genes may cause primary ovarian insufficiency, among them newborn ovary homeobox (NOBOX), factor in the germline alpha (FIGLA), bone morphogenetic protein 15 (BMP15), growth differentiation factor 9 (GDF9), zona pellucida glycoprotein 1 (ZP1).    Signaling description: NOBOX is a homeobox gene that is critical for specifying an oocyte-restricted gene expression pattern including OCT4 (POU5F1), ZAR1, GDF9, BMP15, and H1FOO transcripts. FIGLA is involved in formation of the primordial follicle. It is also involved in coordinating expression of the zona pellucida (ZP) genes. Regulators of the development of primordial to primary follicles also include spermatogenesis- and oogenesis-specific basic HLH1 (SOHLH1) and 2 (SOHLH2) transcription factors and Lim homeobox protein 8 (LHX8). All of these are expressed in the late embryonic and newborn ovaries, and knockout models lack primordial follicles and are sterile. SOHLH1 and SOHLH2 appear to be master-master regulators of other master transcription factors. Zona pellucida sperm-binding protein 1 is a protein that cross-links ZP2 and ZP3. Aberrant ZP1 results in sequestration of ZP3 in the cytoplasm, thereby preventing the formation of the zona pellucida around the oocyte. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Premature ovarian failure, also known as premature ovarian insufficiency, primary ovarian insufficiency, premature menopause, hypergonadotropic hypogonadism, is the loss of function of the ovaries before age 40. It is characterized by amenorrhea, hypergonadotropinism, and hypoestrogenism. Mutations in several oocyte-specific genes may cause primary ovarian insufficiency, among them newborn ovary homeobox (NOBOX), factor in the germline alpha (FIGLA), bone morphogenetic protein 15 (BMP15), growth differentiation factor 9 (GDF9), zona pellucida glycoprotein 1 (ZP1).    Signaling description: NOBOX is a homeobox gene that is critical for specifying an oocyte-restricted gene expression pattern including OCT4 (POU5F1), ZAR1, GDF9, BMP15, and H1FOO transcripts. FIGLA is involved in formation of the primordial follicle. It is also involved in coordinating expression of the zona pellucida (ZP) genes. Regulators of the development of primordial to primary follicles also include spermatogenesis- and oogenesis-specific basic HLH1 (SOHLH1) and 2 (SOHLH2) transcription factors and Lim homeobox protein 8 (LHX8). All of these are expressed in the late embryonic and newborn ovaries, and knockout models lack primordial follicles and are sterile. SOHLH1 and SOHLH2 appear to be master-master regulators of other master transcription factors. Zona pellucida sperm-binding protein 1 is a protein that cross-links ZP2 and ZP3. Aberrant ZP1 results in sequestration of ZP3 in the cytoplasm, thereby preventing the formation of the zona pellucida around the oocyte. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

