xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Inhibins plays important role in regulating ovarian function either as a negative modulators of pituitary FSH synthesis or as a paracrine factor.    Signaling description: Inhibin consists of alpha (a) and beta (b) subunits. The b-subunit is of two types, A and B. Thus there are two forms of inhibin: inhibin A (a-bA) and inhibin B (a-bB). Inhibins are structurally related to activins. Activin is a homodimer of two b subunits, which antagonizes the effect of inhibin. The genes INHA, INHBA and INHBB encode for inhibin a, inhibin bA and inhibin bB subunits, respectively. The gene products of INHA, INHBA and INHBB are restricted to granulosa cells from the primordial follicle stage. If there is any mutation in the INHA gene, the association of a and b will be severely diminished, the homodimerization of two b subunits will take place dominantly. In other words, the concentration of inhibin will diminish and concentration of activins will rise.    Outcome effects: In granulosa cells impairment of inhibin signaling may lead to CCND2 activation, cell proliferation and predispose to cancerogenesis.Protein with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Inhibins plays important role in regulating ovarian function either as a negative modulators of pituitary FSH synthesis or as a paracrine factor.    Signaling description: Inhibin consists of alpha (a) and beta (b) subunits. The b-subunit is of two types, A and B. Thus there are two forms of inhibin: inhibin A (a-bA) and inhibin B (a-bB). Inhibins are structurally related to activins. Activin is a homodimer of two b subunits, which antagonizes the effect of inhibin. The genes INHA, INHBA and INHBB encode for inhibin a, inhibin bA and inhibin bB subunits, respectively. The gene products of INHA, INHBA and INHBB are restricted to granulosa cells from the primordial follicle stage. If there is any mutation in the INHA gene, the association of a and b will be severely diminished, the homodimerization of two b subunits will take place dominantly. In other words, the concentration of inhibin will diminish and concentration of activins will rise.    Outcome effects: In granulosa cells impairment of inhibin signaling may lead to CCND2 activation, cell proliferation and predispose to cancerogenesis.Protein with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

