xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Premature ovarian failure, also known as premature ovarian insufficiency, primary ovarian insufficiency, premature menopause, or hypergonadotropic hypogonadism, is the loss of function of the ovaries before age 40. It is characterized by amenorrhea, hypergonadotropinism, and hypoestrogenism. Mutations in BMP15 and GDF9 are associated with primary ovarian insufficiency.    Signaling description: bone morphogenetic proteins 15 and 6 (BMP15/6) are expressed in the ovaries by oocytes and is involved in folliculogenesis by forming heterodimers with GDF9. BMP15/16 and GDF9 stimulate granulosa cell proliferation, folliculogenesis and oocyte-cumulus matrix formation. BMPs and GDF9 were shown to induce expression of hyaluronan synthase 2 (HAS2), cyclooxygenase 2 (PTGS2), tumour necrosis factor-induced protein-6 (TNFIP6), pentraxin 3 (PTX3), gremlin 1 (GREM1), versican (VCAN) and perlecan (HSPG2). Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Premature ovarian failure, also known as premature ovarian insufficiency, primary ovarian insufficiency, premature menopause, or hypergonadotropic hypogonadism, is the loss of function of the ovaries before age 40. It is characterized by amenorrhea, hypergonadotropinism, and hypoestrogenism. Mutations in BMP15 and GDF9 are associated with primary ovarian insufficiency.    Signaling description: bone morphogenetic proteins 15 and 6 (BMP15/6) are expressed in the ovaries by oocytes and is involved in folliculogenesis by forming heterodimers with GDF9. BMP15/16 and GDF9 stimulate granulosa cell proliferation, folliculogenesis and oocyte-cumulus matrix formation. BMPs and GDF9 were shown to induce expression of hyaluronan synthase 2 (HAS2), cyclooxygenase 2 (PTGS2), tumour necrosis factor-induced protein-6 (TNFIP6), pentraxin 3 (PTX3), gremlin 1 (GREM1), versican (VCAN) and perlecan (HSPG2). Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

