xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Primordial follicles are long-lived structures assembled early in life. The mechanisms that control the balance between the conservation and activation of primordial follicles are critically important for fertility and dictate the onset of menopause. FOXO3 plays an essential role in these processes by suppressing the growth of primordial follicles, thereby preserving them until later in life.    Signaling description: Deletion of FOXO3 (or PTEN) in mice oocytes results in inappropriate oocyte activation, premature entry of primordial follicles into the growing pool, oocyte loss and primary ovarian failure (POF). These findings raised the possibility that mutations or naturally occurring polymorphisms of the human orthologue FOXO3 might contribute to POF or idiopathic primary amenorrhea. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Primordial follicles are long-lived structures assembled early in life. The mechanisms that control the balance between the conservation and activation of primordial follicles are critically important for fertility and dictate the onset of menopause. FOXO3 plays an essential role in these processes by suppressing the growth of primordial follicles, thereby preserving them until later in life.    Signaling description: Deletion of FOXO3 (or PTEN) in mice oocytes results in inappropriate oocyte activation, premature entry of primordial follicles into the growing pool, oocyte loss and primary ovarian failure (POF). These findings raised the possibility that mutations or naturally occurring polymorphisms of the human orthologue FOXO3 might contribute to POF or idiopathic primary amenorrhea. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

