xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hyperhomocysteinemia is a condition characterized by abnormally high homocysteine in the blood. Mutations in MTHFR (5-MTHF reductase) may lead to hyperhomocysteinemia (HHcy). HHcy was shown to be associated with hypercoagulable states.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and protein with decreased expression or activity is highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hyperhomocysteinemia is a condition characterized by abnormally high homocysteine in the blood. Mutations in MTHFR (5-MTHF reductase) may lead to hyperhomocysteinemia (HHcy). HHcy was shown to be associated with hypercoagulable states.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and protein with decreased expression or activity is highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

