xref: PS:Source "Diseases"
synonym: "Source: Diseases" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Obstetric complications are the hallmark of antiphospholipid syndrome (APS). Recurrent miscarriage, early delivery, prematurity, intrauterine growth restriction, fetal distress, fetal or neonatal thrombosis, pre-eclampsia/eclampsia, HELLP syndrome, arterial or venous thrombosis and placental insufficiency are the most severe APS-related complication for pregnant women.     Signaling description: Antiphospholipid antibodies (aPL) promote activation of endothelial cells, monocytes and platelets.aPL antibodies bind to beta-2GPI (APOH) that in turn binds to endothelial cell membrane receptors (TLR4 and ANXA2) and induces phosphorylation of p38 MAPK (MAPK14) and NFkB activation leading to a proinflammatory and prothrombotic effect (expression of VCAM1, ICAM1, SELE, F3, IL-1A, IL-6 and IL-8)."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Obstetric complications are the hallmark of antiphospholipid syndrome (APS). Recurrent miscarriage, early delivery, prematurity, intrauterine growth restriction, fetal distress, fetal or neonatal thrombosis, pre-eclampsia/eclampsia, HELLP syndrome, arterial or venous thrombosis and placental insufficiency are the most severe APS-related complication for pregnant women.     Signaling description: Antiphospholipid antibodies (aPL) promote activation of endothelial cells, monocytes and platelets.aPL antibodies bind to beta-2GPI (APOH) that in turn binds to endothelial cell membrane receptors (TLR4 and ANXA2) and induces phosphorylation of p38 MAPK (MAPK14) and NFkB activation leading to a proinflammatory and prothrombotic effect (expression of VCAM1, ICAM1, SELE, F3, IL-1A, IL-6 and IL-8)." EXACT []

