xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Antiphospholipid syndrome (APS) is an autoimmune hypercoagulable state provoked by antiphospholipid antibodies. APS manifests as recurrent venous or arterial thrombosis and/or fetal loss. Obstetric complications are the hallmark of APS.    Signaling description: Antiphospholipid antibodies (aPL) promote activation of platelets. aPL antibodies bind to APOH that in turn binds to platelet receptor LRP8 and GP1BA and induce a procoagulant state."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Antiphospholipid syndrome (APS) is an autoimmune hypercoagulable state provoked by antiphospholipid antibodies. APS manifests as recurrent venous or arterial thrombosis and/or fetal loss. Obstetric complications are the hallmark of APS.    Signaling description: Antiphospholipid antibodies (aPL) promote activation of platelets. aPL antibodies bind to APOH that in turn binds to platelet receptor LRP8 and GP1BA and induce a procoagulant state." EXACT []

