xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Breast cancer (BC) is the most commonly diagnosed cancer in women (excluding skin cancer) and the second leading cause of cancer death in women. Men may also develop BC, but this accounts for less than 1% of all BCs. Most BCs are luminal tumors that start in the inner (luminal) cells lining the mammary ducts.    Signaling description: NOTCH signaling is a crucial regulator of multiple cellular processes including differentiation, proliferation, motility, and survival. The transmembrane receptors NOTCH (1-4) interact with surface-bound ligands including JAG1, JAG2, DLL1, and DLL4. NOTCH1 has been identified as a proto-oncogene.    Outcome effects: The constitutive activation of NOTCH signaling leads to loss of differentiation and hyperplastic growth of mammary epithelial cells. Activated membrane-bound NOTCH1 receptor is cleaved by gamma-secretase complex and ADAM metallopeptidase domain 17 (ADAM17). NOTCH intracellular domain (NICD) is transported to the nucleus and participates in the formation the chromatin remodeling complexes, KAT2B/MYSM1 and KAT2A/TADA2A/TADA3. In addition, NICD interacts with LEF1/TCF7/CTNNB1 and SMAD family members 2/3/4 (SMAD2/3/4) complexes which induce the expression of downstream target genes that are involved in cell proliferation, differentiation, and migration.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and protein with decreased expression or activity is highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Breast cancer (BC) is the most commonly diagnosed cancer in women (excluding skin cancer) and the second leading cause of cancer death in women. Men may also develop BC, but this accounts for less than 1% of all BCs. Most BCs are luminal tumors that start in the inner (luminal) cells lining the mammary ducts.    Signaling description: NOTCH signaling is a crucial regulator of multiple cellular processes including differentiation, proliferation, motility, and survival. The transmembrane receptors NOTCH (1-4) interact with surface-bound ligands including JAG1, JAG2, DLL1, and DLL4. NOTCH1 has been identified as a proto-oncogene.    Outcome effects: The constitutive activation of NOTCH signaling leads to loss of differentiation and hyperplastic growth of mammary epithelial cells. Activated membrane-bound NOTCH1 receptor is cleaved by gamma-secretase complex and ADAM metallopeptidase domain 17 (ADAM17). NOTCH intracellular domain (NICD) is transported to the nucleus and participates in the formation the chromatin remodeling complexes, KAT2B/MYSM1 and KAT2A/TADA2A/TADA3. In addition, NICD interacts with LEF1/TCF7/CTNNB1 and SMAD family members 2/3/4 (SMAD2/3/4) complexes which induce the expression of downstream target genes that are involved in cell proliferation, differentiation, and migration.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and protein with decreased expression or activity is highlighted in blue." EXACT []

