xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Cholesteatoma is a destructive disease characterized by the progressive expansion of keratinizing squamous epithelium in the middle ear and mastoid and chronic inflammatory reaction of the subepithelial connective tissue, which gradually expands and causes serious complications due to destruction of nearby bony structures.    Signaling description: MIF expression in human cholesteatomas is related to the level of their biologic aggressiveness estimated by the recurrence status and the level of MMP expression; as well as the cholesteatoma differentiation status reflected in galactin and RARbeta expressions.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Cholesteatoma is a destructive disease characterized by the progressive expansion of keratinizing squamous epithelium in the middle ear and mastoid and chronic inflammatory reaction of the subepithelial connective tissue, which gradually expands and causes serious complications due to destruction of nearby bony structures.    Signaling description: MIF expression in human cholesteatomas is related to the level of their biologic aggressiveness estimated by the recurrence status and the level of MMP expression; as well as the cholesteatoma differentiation status reflected in galactin and RARbeta expressions.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

