xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Age-related hearing loss (ARHL) is the result of genetic predispositions combined with various insults to the inner ear accumulated during a lifetime.    Signaling description: ARHL is associated with an age-dependent loss of sensory hair cells. An example of a predisposing allele is cadherin 23 (CDH23) Cdh23ahl.    Signaling description: The Cdh23ahl allele encodes a protein present in the tip links of the outer hair cells and is associated with a rapid progression of ARHL. Polymorphisms in PCDH15, also present in stereocilia tip links, are similarly associated with ARHL. Myosin 15A (MYO15A) and myosin 6 (MYO6) polymorphisms also predispose to ARHL."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Age-related hearing loss (ARHL) is the result of genetic predispositions combined with various insults to the inner ear accumulated during a lifetime.    Signaling description: ARHL is associated with an age-dependent loss of sensory hair cells. An example of a predisposing allele is cadherin 23 (CDH23) Cdh23ahl.    Signaling description: The Cdh23ahl allele encodes a protein present in the tip links of the outer hair cells and is associated with a rapid progression of ARHL. Polymorphisms in PCDH15, also present in stereocilia tip links, are similarly associated with ARHL. Myosin 15A (MYO15A) and myosin 6 (MYO6) polymorphisms also predispose to ARHL." EXACT []

