xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Noise-induced hearing loss is the result of prolonged exposure to excessive noise that damages cochlear sensory hair cells.    Signaling description: Noise exposure induces production of cytokines (TNF, IL1B, IL-6), chemokines (CCL2, CCL4, CXCL12) and cell adhesion molecules (ICAM1, PECAM1, VCAM1) in the inner ear cell and recruitment of inflammatory cells into the cochlear with subsequent cochlear cell damage.    Outcome effects: NFkB and JAK2/STAT3 signaling were shown to be involved in pro-inflammatory molecules production in noise-induced hearing loss."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Noise-induced hearing loss is the result of prolonged exposure to excessive noise that damages cochlear sensory hair cells.    Signaling description: Noise exposure induces production of cytokines (TNF, IL1B, IL-6), chemokines (CCL2, CCL4, CXCL12) and cell adhesion molecules (ICAM1, PECAM1, VCAM1) in the inner ear cell and recruitment of inflammatory cells into the cochlear with subsequent cochlear cell damage.    Outcome effects: NFkB and JAK2/STAT3 signaling were shown to be involved in pro-inflammatory molecules production in noise-induced hearing loss." EXACT []

