xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Melanoma is the most aggressive form of skin cancer caused by malignant transformation of melanocytes. It accounts for only 4-7% of all skin malignancies, yet it is responsible for about 80% of all skin tumor deaths. The strongest risk factors for melanoma are a family history of melanoma, multiple benign or atypical nevi, and a previous melanoma. The exposure to ultraviolet radiation is one of the primary triggers of melanoma. Wnt signalling is known to have a role in melanoma.    Signaling description: During embryogenesis, the canonical WNT signaling is important for the positioning of stem cells and differentiation of melanoblasts into melanocytes; whereas, the non-canonical WNT signaling causes de-differentiation of melanocytes and other cell types through the suppression of CTNNB, thus maintaining the pluripotency of stem cells. Both WNT signaling pathways are critical in melanoma. WNT3A signaling is important in the early stages of tumor development promoting cell proliferation and tumor transformation; however, this pathway may inhibit metastasis. In contrast, WNT5A signaling is absent in the early stages of the tumor. Following melanocyte transformation, WNT5A activation represses the canonical WNT sinaling and promotes metastasis mainly via the PKC-mediated downregulation of KISS1 and CDH1 and the up-regulation of VIM and CD44.    Outcome effects: Canonical (WNT3A-regulated) and non-canonical (WNT5A-regulated) WNT-signaling pathways are implicated at different stages of melanoma development.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Melanoma is the most aggressive form of skin cancer caused by malignant transformation of melanocytes. It accounts for only 4-7% of all skin malignancies, yet it is responsible for about 80% of all skin tumor deaths. The strongest risk factors for melanoma are a family history of melanoma, multiple benign or atypical nevi, and a previous melanoma. The exposure to ultraviolet radiation is one of the primary triggers of melanoma. Wnt signalling is known to have a role in melanoma.    Signaling description: During embryogenesis, the canonical WNT signaling is important for the positioning of stem cells and differentiation of melanoblasts into melanocytes; whereas, the non-canonical WNT signaling causes de-differentiation of melanocytes and other cell types through the suppression of CTNNB, thus maintaining the pluripotency of stem cells. Both WNT signaling pathways are critical in melanoma. WNT3A signaling is important in the early stages of tumor development promoting cell proliferation and tumor transformation; however, this pathway may inhibit metastasis. In contrast, WNT5A signaling is absent in the early stages of the tumor. Following melanocyte transformation, WNT5A activation represses the canonical WNT sinaling and promotes metastasis mainly via the PKC-mediated downregulation of KISS1 and CDH1 and the up-regulation of VIM and CD44.    Outcome effects: Canonical (WNT3A-regulated) and non-canonical (WNT5A-regulated) WNT-signaling pathways are implicated at different stages of melanoma development.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

