xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Acute promyelocytic leukemia (AML-M3) is a form of acute myeloid leukemia with an abnormal accumulation of immature granulocytes called promyelocytes. It is characterized by chromosomal translocations involving the retinoic acid receptor alpha (RARA).    Signaling description: The most common translocation is PML-RAR, which is found in more than 98% of AML-M3 cases. PLZF-RAR and NPM-RAR are more rare translocations. PML-RAR, NPM-RAR, and PLZF-RAR fusion proteins modulate retinoid-responsive gene expression by disrupting the retinoid acid signal pathway and inhibiting myeloid differentiation at the promyelocyte stage. Cell differentiation is also blocked through SPI1, NCOR1/2, and histone deacetylase. In addition, FLT3, a class III receptor tyrosine kinase may be mutated in up to 38% of AML-M3 cases.    Outcome effects: In AML, cell proliferation is triggered through the activation of catenin-beta1 (CTNNB1) while CCND1, GATA4, CCNA1, and MYC play a role in cell cycle activation.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Acute promyelocytic leukemia (AML-M3) is a form of acute myeloid leukemia with an abnormal accumulation of immature granulocytes called promyelocytes. It is characterized by chromosomal translocations involving the retinoic acid receptor alpha (RARA).    Signaling description: The most common translocation is PML-RAR, which is found in more than 98% of AML-M3 cases. PLZF-RAR and NPM-RAR are more rare translocations. PML-RAR, NPM-RAR, and PLZF-RAR fusion proteins modulate retinoid-responsive gene expression by disrupting the retinoid acid signal pathway and inhibiting myeloid differentiation at the promyelocyte stage. Cell differentiation is also blocked through SPI1, NCOR1/2, and histone deacetylase. In addition, FLT3, a class III receptor tyrosine kinase may be mutated in up to 38% of AML-M3 cases.    Outcome effects: In AML, cell proliferation is triggered through the activation of catenin-beta1 (CTNNB1) while CCND1, GATA4, CCNA1, and MYC play a role in cell cycle activation.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

