xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Prostate cancer is a cancer that develops in the prostate gland. Prostate cancer cases are characterized by considerable heterogeneity especially during the progression to hormone-refractory status. It is generally accepted that androgen receptor (AR) plays a significant role in prostate cancer even upon transition to an androgen-independent state.    Signaling description: Protein kinase C delta (PRKCD) is a member of serine- and threonine-specific kinases involved in the regulation of various cell processes such as growth, apoptosis, and differentiation. It has been demonstrated that the PRKCD gene promoter has an androgen response element and is highly responsive to androgens.    Outcome effects: Activated PRKCD can initiate proapoptotic program through the stimulation of tumor necrosis factor (TNF) expression and induction of p38 MAPK signaling cascade. There is also evidence that PRKCD can inhibit Akt survival pathway inducing Akt kinase dephosphorylation."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Prostate cancer is a cancer that develops in the prostate gland. Prostate cancer cases are characterized by considerable heterogeneity especially during the progression to hormone-refractory status. It is generally accepted that androgen receptor (AR) plays a significant role in prostate cancer even upon transition to an androgen-independent state.    Signaling description: Protein kinase C delta (PRKCD) is a member of serine- and threonine-specific kinases involved in the regulation of various cell processes such as growth, apoptosis, and differentiation. It has been demonstrated that the PRKCD gene promoter has an androgen response element and is highly responsive to androgens.    Outcome effects: Activated PRKCD can initiate proapoptotic program through the stimulation of tumor necrosis factor (TNF) expression and induction of p38 MAPK signaling cascade. There is also evidence that PRKCD can inhibit Akt survival pathway inducing Akt kinase dephosphorylation." EXACT []

