xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hodgkin lymphoma (HL) is one of the most frequent types of lymphoma in the Western world. The main clinical presentation is lymph node enlargement. It is subdivided into classical HL and nodular lymphocyte-predominant HL (NLPHL which accounts for only 5% of cases). The role of microenvironment is extremely important in Hodgkin lymphoma (HL) development.    Signaling description: NF-kB and JUN/FOS are major expression regulators involved in the formation of HL lesions. The majority of cells in HL lesions are a mixed infiltrate of various types of cells of the immune system (CD4 T-cells, neutrophils, eosinophils, mast cells, and others).    Outcome effects: Hodgkin and Reed-Sternberg (HRS) cells produce several molecules to attract various types of immune cells. They also produce specific molecules to inhibit CD8 cytotoxic T-cell activity. Prominent lymph node fibrosis is a typical feature of most types of HL and originates from HRS cell-mediated fibroblast activation."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hodgkin lymphoma (HL) is one of the most frequent types of lymphoma in the Western world. The main clinical presentation is lymph node enlargement. It is subdivided into classical HL and nodular lymphocyte-predominant HL (NLPHL which accounts for only 5% of cases). The role of microenvironment is extremely important in Hodgkin lymphoma (HL) development.    Signaling description: NF-kB and JUN/FOS are major expression regulators involved in the formation of HL lesions. The majority of cells in HL lesions are a mixed infiltrate of various types of cells of the immune system (CD4 T-cells, neutrophils, eosinophils, mast cells, and others).    Outcome effects: Hodgkin and Reed-Sternberg (HRS) cells produce several molecules to attract various types of immune cells. They also produce specific molecules to inhibit CD8 cytotoxic T-cell activity. Prominent lymph node fibrosis is a typical feature of most types of HL and originates from HRS cell-mediated fibroblast activation." EXACT []

