xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Mantle cell lymphoma (MCL) represents approximately 4-10% of all cases of non-Hodgkin lymphoma. It occurs primarily among elderly individuals with a median age of approximately 60 years (range 29-85). Most MCL patients have disseminated disease including generalized lymphadenopathies and bone marrow involvement. The clinical behavior of MCL patients is aggressive with a median overall survival of approximately 3-4 years. MCL is a mature B-cell neoplasm arising from antigen-experienced B cells.    Signaling description: Key regulators of apoptosis are frequently mutated as secondary genetic events in MCL. TP53 and BCL2L11 are inactivated by point mutations or gene deletions, while BCL2 and MDM2 are activated by gene amplifications. The constitutive activation of NF-kB has been detected in MCL with the overexpression of antiapoptotic proteins including CFLAR, BCL2L1, and XIAP.    Outcome effects: The described events lead to block of apoptosis and tumor survival.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Mantle cell lymphoma (MCL) represents approximately 4-10% of all cases of non-Hodgkin lymphoma. It occurs primarily among elderly individuals with a median age of approximately 60 years (range 29-85). Most MCL patients have disseminated disease including generalized lymphadenopathies and bone marrow involvement. The clinical behavior of MCL patients is aggressive with a median overall survival of approximately 3-4 years. MCL is a mature B-cell neoplasm arising from antigen-experienced B cells.    Signaling description: Key regulators of apoptosis are frequently mutated as secondary genetic events in MCL. TP53 and BCL2L11 are inactivated by point mutations or gene deletions, while BCL2 and MDM2 are activated by gene amplifications. The constitutive activation of NF-kB has been detected in MCL with the overexpression of antiapoptotic proteins including CFLAR, BCL2L1, and XIAP.    Outcome effects: The described events lead to block of apoptosis and tumor survival.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

