xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Increased levels of nuclear epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) were found in the nuclei in a variety of tumors such as skin, breast, and thyroid tumors. The accumulation of EGFR in the nucleus enhances cell proliferation and contributes to drug resistance.    Signaling description: Although the exact mechanism of EGFR transport from the cellular membrane to the nucleus is unknown, several players involved in its internalization and trafficking have been recently discovered. First, EGFR has to undergo endocytosis and then is redistributed to the Golgi complex and endoplasmic reticulum. Finally, with the interaction of importins and nuclear pore complex, EGFR enters the nucleus using Sec61 to detach from the membrane. The downstream targets of nuclear EGFR can be used as markers of EGFR translocation.    Outcome effects: Nuclear EGFR phosphorylates PCNA and PRKDC, which affects cell proliferation and DNA repair. Also, EGFR interacts with transcription factors, STAT3, STAT5A, and E2F1, and increases their activity."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Increased levels of nuclear epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) were found in the nuclei in a variety of tumors such as skin, breast, and thyroid tumors. The accumulation of EGFR in the nucleus enhances cell proliferation and contributes to drug resistance.    Signaling description: Although the exact mechanism of EGFR transport from the cellular membrane to the nucleus is unknown, several players involved in its internalization and trafficking have been recently discovered. First, EGFR has to undergo endocytosis and then is redistributed to the Golgi complex and endoplasmic reticulum. Finally, with the interaction of importins and nuclear pore complex, EGFR enters the nucleus using Sec61 to detach from the membrane. The downstream targets of nuclear EGFR can be used as markers of EGFR translocation.    Outcome effects: Nuclear EGFR phosphorylates PCNA and PRKDC, which affects cell proliferation and DNA repair. Also, EGFR interacts with transcription factors, STAT3, STAT5A, and E2F1, and increases their activity." EXACT []

