xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties.    Signaling description: Mast cells localize within the bronchial smooth muscle bundles in patients with asthma, but not in normal subjects or those with eosinophilic bronchitis. The mechanism of mast cell recruitment by asthmatic airway smooth muscle involves the CXCL10/CXCR3 axis.    Outcome effects: Chemokine receptors most commonly expressed by human lung mast cells are CCR3, CXCR1, CXCR3 and CXCR4. ASM (airway smooth muscle) derived factors (such as SCF, CXCL10) are chemotactic for mast cells and are essential for their differentiation, maturation, proliferation and survival.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties.    Signaling description: Mast cells localize within the bronchial smooth muscle bundles in patients with asthma, but not in normal subjects or those with eosinophilic bronchitis. The mechanism of mast cell recruitment by asthmatic airway smooth muscle involves the CXCL10/CXCR3 axis.    Outcome effects: Chemokine receptors most commonly expressed by human lung mast cells are CCR3, CXCR1, CXCR3 and CXCR4. ASM (airway smooth muscle) derived factors (such as SCF, CXCL10) are chemotactic for mast cells and are essential for their differentiation, maturation, proliferation and survival.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression are highlighted in red." EXACT []

