xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties.    Signaling description: The antigen presenting cells (dendritic cells, macrophages, lung epithelial cells) are the primary cells in allergen recognition. Antigens, which induce the immune response are called immunogens, and if they elicit allergies they are referred to as allergens. According to the AllFam database of inhaled allergen families, there are now 137 allergens. Antigen presenting cells take up the allergen, process it, and present it in a complex with the MHC molecule as an antigen on their cell surface. The antigen presenting cells induce naïve T-cells towards Th1- or Th2-cell response. Mucosal dendritic cells loaded with antigen migrate from the lungs to the T-cell area of mediastinal lymph nodes (MLNs). Mature dendritic cells in the MLNs select naive T-cells from the polyclonal repertoire of cells. Within 4 days, this will lead to clonal expansion of antigen-specific Th-cells. The allergens also induce signaling when recognized through antigen presenting cell surface pattern recognition receptors (PPRs), such as TLRs, C-type lectins (such as DC-SIGN, MR, dectin1, DEC205 and langerin) and NOD-like receptors. Glycosylation of allergens is required for recognition and uptake by PPRs in dendritic cells as well in other APCs. Mannosylation is the most common glycosylation pattern among allergens with an exception of Der p 2 (Dermatophagoides pteronyssinus) in asthma.The endotoxin lipopolysaccharide (LPS) (cell wall component of Gram-negative bacteria) exposure is positively associated with an increased risk of asthma and asthma severity in both adults and children.    Outcome effects: PPRs signaling leads to the release of PGD2, LTC4 and LTD4, histamine, chemokines (CCL17 and CCL22), cytokines (IL4 and TNF). These mediators induce smooth-muscle contraction, goblet-cell hyperplasia and changes to the vessel wall. The allergen increases the expression of CCR7 required for the migration of allergen-loaded DCs to the draining lymph nodes. In the case of house dust mite allergens, the epithelium releases granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF), leading to local activation of DC function. The antigen presenting cells can all bind allergen-specific IgE either through FcgRI or CD23, possibly enhancing recognition of the allergen."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties.    Signaling description: The antigen presenting cells (dendritic cells, macrophages, lung epithelial cells) are the primary cells in allergen recognition. Antigens, which induce the immune response are called immunogens, and if they elicit allergies they are referred to as allergens. According to the AllFam database of inhaled allergen families, there are now 137 allergens. Antigen presenting cells take up the allergen, process it, and present it in a complex with the MHC molecule as an antigen on their cell surface. The antigen presenting cells induce naïve T-cells towards Th1- or Th2-cell response. Mucosal dendritic cells loaded with antigen migrate from the lungs to the T-cell area of mediastinal lymph nodes (MLNs). Mature dendritic cells in the MLNs select naive T-cells from the polyclonal repertoire of cells. Within 4 days, this will lead to clonal expansion of antigen-specific Th-cells. The allergens also induce signaling when recognized through antigen presenting cell surface pattern recognition receptors (PPRs), such as TLRs, C-type lectins (such as DC-SIGN, MR, dectin1, DEC205 and langerin) and NOD-like receptors. Glycosylation of allergens is required for recognition and uptake by PPRs in dendritic cells as well in other APCs. Mannosylation is the most common glycosylation pattern among allergens with an exception of Der p 2 (Dermatophagoides pteronyssinus) in asthma.The endotoxin lipopolysaccharide (LPS) (cell wall component of Gram-negative bacteria) exposure is positively associated with an increased risk of asthma and asthma severity in both adults and children.    Outcome effects: PPRs signaling leads to the release of PGD2, LTC4 and LTD4, histamine, chemokines (CCL17 and CCL22), cytokines (IL4 and TNF). These mediators induce smooth-muscle contraction, goblet-cell hyperplasia and changes to the vessel wall. The allergen increases the expression of CCR7 required for the migration of allergen-loaded DCs to the draining lymph nodes. In the case of house dust mite allergens, the epithelium releases granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF), leading to local activation of DC function. The antigen presenting cells can all bind allergen-specific IgE either through FcgRI or CD23, possibly enhancing recognition of the allergen." EXACT []

