xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties. Periostin may be a systemic biomarker of airway eosinophilia in asthmatic patients.    Signaling description: Serum periostin levels are significantly increased in asthmatic patients exhibiting eosinophilic airway inflammation relative to those with minimal eosinophilic airway inflammation. Periostin is a secreted matricellular protein associated with fibrosis, and its expression is upregulated by recombinant IL13 in cultured bronchial epithelial cells.    Outcome effects: In human asthmatic patients, periostin expression levels correlate with reticular basement membrane thickness, an indicator of subepithelial fibrosis.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties. Periostin may be a systemic biomarker of airway eosinophilia in asthmatic patients.    Signaling description: Serum periostin levels are significantly increased in asthmatic patients exhibiting eosinophilic airway inflammation relative to those with minimal eosinophilic airway inflammation. Periostin is a secreted matricellular protein associated with fibrosis, and its expression is upregulated by recombinant IL13 in cultured bronchial epithelial cells.    Outcome effects: In human asthmatic patients, periostin expression levels correlate with reticular basement membrane thickness, an indicator of subepithelial fibrosis.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression are highlighted in red." EXACT []

