xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties.    Signaling description: The asthmatic patients have a significantly higher level of serum IL17F protein as compared to that of healthy subjects. IL17F is expressed in activated CD4 T cells, basophils, and mast cells, the three major cell types involved in allergic airway inflammation. Bronchial epithelial cells are a novel cell source of IL17F in response to IL33, which they produce in response to IL33.    Outcome effects: IL33 induces IL17F via the ST2-ERK1/2-MSK1 signaling pathway in bronchial epithelial cells. Further, IL17F induces IL11, IGFI and CCL20 expression in bronchial epithelial cells. IL17F receptor is a heterodimer of I17RA and IL17RC, which recruits TRAF6, leading to the activation of MAP3K7. The Raf1-MEK1/2-ERK1/2-p90RSK/MSK1-CREB is the central signaling pathway activated by I17RA and IL17RC. On the other hand, IL17F also activates transcriptional factors such as NF-?B. In addition, in humans, the expression of IGFI is significantly increased within the airways of subjects with severe asthma.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties.    Signaling description: The asthmatic patients have a significantly higher level of serum IL17F protein as compared to that of healthy subjects. IL17F is expressed in activated CD4 T cells, basophils, and mast cells, the three major cell types involved in allergic airway inflammation. Bronchial epithelial cells are a novel cell source of IL17F in response to IL33, which they produce in response to IL33.    Outcome effects: IL33 induces IL17F via the ST2-ERK1/2-MSK1 signaling pathway in bronchial epithelial cells. Further, IL17F induces IL11, IGFI and CCL20 expression in bronchial epithelial cells. IL17F receptor is a heterodimer of I17RA and IL17RC, which recruits TRAF6, leading to the activation of MAP3K7. The Raf1-MEK1/2-ERK1/2-p90RSK/MSK1-CREB is the central signaling pathway activated by I17RA and IL17RC. On the other hand, IL17F also activates transcriptional factors such as NF-?B. In addition, in humans, the expression of IGFI is significantly increased within the airways of subjects with severe asthma.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression are highlighted in red." EXACT []

