xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties.    Signaling description: In asthma, excessive shortening of ASM (airway smooth muscle) cells leading to narrowing of the airways contributes significantly to obstruction. This is partially due to the fact that the smooth muscle mass within the airway wall is increased in asthma via hypertrophy and/or hyperplasia, with the intrinsic contractile properties of individual muscle cells being unchanged. ASM cells express both FceRII/CD23 and FceRI, and IgE can modulate the contractile and synthetic function of the human ASM cells. IgE was recently shown to induce ASM cell proliferation via MAPK, Akt, and STAT3 signaling pathways.    Outcome effects: IgE stimulation of ASM induced the release of Th2 and proinflammatory mediators IL4, -5, -13, TNF, IL6, CCL11/eotaxin-1, and TSLP, and enhanced intracellular Ca2+ mobilization.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Asthma is a common long-term lung disorder in which inflammation of the bronchi leads to narrowing of the airways creating breathing difficulties.    Signaling description: In asthma, excessive shortening of ASM (airway smooth muscle) cells leading to narrowing of the airways contributes significantly to obstruction. This is partially due to the fact that the smooth muscle mass within the airway wall is increased in asthma via hypertrophy and/or hyperplasia, with the intrinsic contractile properties of individual muscle cells being unchanged. ASM cells express both FceRII/CD23 and FceRI, and IgE can modulate the contractile and synthetic function of the human ASM cells. IgE was recently shown to induce ASM cell proliferation via MAPK, Akt, and STAT3 signaling pathways.    Outcome effects: IgE stimulation of ASM induced the release of Th2 and proinflammatory mediators IL4, -5, -13, TNF, IL6, CCL11/eotaxin-1, and TSLP, and enhanced intracellular Ca2+ mobilization.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

