xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) refers to a group of progressive lung diseases characterized by a long-term worsening airway obstruction.    Signaling description: Glucocorticoid resistance in COPD is associated with reduced activation and expression of histone deacetylase 2 (HDAC2). Superoxide anions and nitric oxide (NO) generated by cigarette smoke and inflammatory cells combine to form peroxynitrite. Peroxynitrite nitrates HDAC2, which inactivates it and results in its degradation by the proteasome. Oxidative stress also activates PI3K, which inactivates HDAC2.    Outcome effects: The loss of HDAC2 function results in an enhanced inflammatory gene expression and blocks the anti-inflammatory action of corticosteroids. SIRT1 and SIRT6 normally inhibit RELA-associated cytokine production; however they are downregulated in lung cells from COPD patients as a result of cigarette smoke exposure. In normal conditions, deacetylation of the glucocorticoid receptor (NR3C1) by HDAC2 enables RELA suppression. When HDAC2 is downregulated, RELA suppression by NR3C1 fails to occur.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue"
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) refers to a group of progressive lung diseases characterized by a long-term worsening airway obstruction.    Signaling description: Glucocorticoid resistance in COPD is associated with reduced activation and expression of histone deacetylase 2 (HDAC2). Superoxide anions and nitric oxide (NO) generated by cigarette smoke and inflammatory cells combine to form peroxynitrite. Peroxynitrite nitrates HDAC2, which inactivates it and results in its degradation by the proteasome. Oxidative stress also activates PI3K, which inactivates HDAC2.    Outcome effects: The loss of HDAC2 function results in an enhanced inflammatory gene expression and blocks the anti-inflammatory action of corticosteroids. SIRT1 and SIRT6 normally inhibit RELA-associated cytokine production; however they are downregulated in lung cells from COPD patients as a result of cigarette smoke exposure. In normal conditions, deacetylation of the glucocorticoid receptor (NR3C1) by HDAC2 enables RELA suppression. When HDAC2 is downregulated, RELA suppression by NR3C1 fails to occur.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue" EXACT []

