xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) refers to a group of progressive lung diseases characterized by a long-term worsening airway obstruction.    Signaling description: Neutrophils are important effector cells in COPD. The number of neutrophils is increased in sputum and bronchoalveolar lavage fluid of patients with COPD.    Outcome effects: Activated neutrophils cause tissue damage by the release of neutrophil elastase (ELANE), MMPs, and ROS. Neutrophils also release other serine proteases including cathepsin G and B (CTSG and CTSB) and proteinase 3 (PRTN3)."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) refers to a group of progressive lung diseases characterized by a long-term worsening airway obstruction.    Signaling description: Neutrophils are important effector cells in COPD. The number of neutrophils is increased in sputum and bronchoalveolar lavage fluid of patients with COPD.    Outcome effects: Activated neutrophils cause tissue damage by the release of neutrophil elastase (ELANE), MMPs, and ROS. Neutrophils also release other serine proteases including cathepsin G and B (CTSG and CTSB) and proteinase 3 (PRTN3)." EXACT []

