xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) refers to a group of progressive lung diseases characterized by a long-term worsening airway obstruction.    Signaling description: Fibroblasts have an important role in repair and lung homeostasis. There is a reduced growth rate of lung fibroblasts in patients with COPD. Cigarette smoke extract induces the premature senescence of lung fibroblasts in a CAV1-dependent manner. Following oxidative stress, the CAV1 gene promoter is activated through p38 MAPK-SP1-dependent and NF-kB-dependent pathways.    Outcome effects: The upregulation of CAV1 promotes cellular senescence by activating TP53/CDKN1A.The activation of TP53 by CAV1 occurs through different mechanisms: 1) interaction of CAV1 with MDM2 prevents the MDM2-dependent degradation of TP53; 2) inhibition of TXNRD1 through direct interaction with CAV1 activates TP53; 3) sequestration of PPP2CB into caveolar membranes activates ATM, which in turns phosphorylates and activates TP53. The activation of TP53 leads to the upregulation of CDKN1A, inhibition of cell proliferation, and induction of cellular senescence.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) refers to a group of progressive lung diseases characterized by a long-term worsening airway obstruction.    Signaling description: Fibroblasts have an important role in repair and lung homeostasis. There is a reduced growth rate of lung fibroblasts in patients with COPD. Cigarette smoke extract induces the premature senescence of lung fibroblasts in a CAV1-dependent manner. Following oxidative stress, the CAV1 gene promoter is activated through p38 MAPK-SP1-dependent and NF-kB-dependent pathways.    Outcome effects: The upregulation of CAV1 promotes cellular senescence by activating TP53/CDKN1A.The activation of TP53 by CAV1 occurs through different mechanisms: 1) interaction of CAV1 with MDM2 prevents the MDM2-dependent degradation of TP53; 2) inhibition of TXNRD1 through direct interaction with CAV1 activates TP53; 3) sequestration of PPP2CB into caveolar membranes activates ATM, which in turns phosphorylates and activates TP53. The activation of TP53 leads to the upregulation of CDKN1A, inhibition of cell proliferation, and induction of cellular senescence.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

