xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) refers to a group of progressive lung diseases characterized by a long-term worsening airway obstruction.    Signaling description: in patients with COPD, CD8 cytotoxic T-cells are the predominant T-cells in the airway and alveolar compartment. Cigarette smoke increases TLR4 and TLR9 expression and induces cytokine production from CD8 T-cells. CD8 cytotoxic T-cells are activated by pathogen-associated molecular patterns (PAMPs) and damage-associated molecular patterns (DAMPs). DAMPs include HMGB1, BGN, heat shock proteins, hyaluronic acid, VCAN, and heparan sulfate. One of the most important PAMPs in COPD is bacterial LPS.    Outcome effects: CD8 T-cells contribute to the cytotoxicity of lung tissue cells through the release of proteolytic enzymes perforin (PRF1) and granzyme B (GZMB). They also release IL6, IL1B, IL18, TNF, and IFNG leading to inflammation.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) refers to a group of progressive lung diseases characterized by a long-term worsening airway obstruction.    Signaling description: in patients with COPD, CD8 cytotoxic T-cells are the predominant T-cells in the airway and alveolar compartment. Cigarette smoke increases TLR4 and TLR9 expression and induces cytokine production from CD8 T-cells. CD8 cytotoxic T-cells are activated by pathogen-associated molecular patterns (PAMPs) and damage-associated molecular patterns (DAMPs). DAMPs include HMGB1, BGN, heat shock proteins, hyaluronic acid, VCAN, and heparan sulfate. One of the most important PAMPs in COPD is bacterial LPS.    Outcome effects: CD8 T-cells contribute to the cytotoxicity of lung tissue cells through the release of proteolytic enzymes perforin (PRF1) and granzyme B (GZMB). They also release IL6, IL1B, IL18, TNF, and IFNG leading to inflammation.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

