xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) is increased blood pressure in the pulmonary artery.    Signaling description: BMP2 protein is involved in PAH as it regulates pulmonary artery endothelial cell (PAEC) proliferation, survival, and motility. BMP2 can act through the non-canonical WNT-pathway. Namely, BMP2 is responsible for SMAD1 phosphorylation, or with the loss of BMPR2 (as in some cases of familial and idiopathic pulmonary arterial hypertension), ACVR2A/SMAD3-dependent recruitment of DVL1 to promote RHOA/RAC1 signaling necessary for actin cytoskeleton rearrangement, cell contraction, and motility.    Outcome effects: BMP2 recruits both canonical and non-canonical WNT signaling pathways to promote pulmonary artery endothelial cell (PAEC) proliferation, survival, and motility."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) is increased blood pressure in the pulmonary artery.    Signaling description: BMP2 protein is involved in PAH as it regulates pulmonary artery endothelial cell (PAEC) proliferation, survival, and motility. BMP2 can act through the non-canonical WNT-pathway. Namely, BMP2 is responsible for SMAD1 phosphorylation, or with the loss of BMPR2 (as in some cases of familial and idiopathic pulmonary arterial hypertension), ACVR2A/SMAD3-dependent recruitment of DVL1 to promote RHOA/RAC1 signaling necessary for actin cytoskeleton rearrangement, cell contraction, and motility.    Outcome effects: BMP2 recruits both canonical and non-canonical WNT signaling pathways to promote pulmonary artery endothelial cell (PAEC) proliferation, survival, and motility." EXACT []

