xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) is increased blood pressure in the pulmonary artery.    Signaling description: BMP2 protein is involved in PAH as it regulates pulmonary artery endothelial cell (PAEC) proliferation, survival, and motility. BMP2 can act through the canonical or non-canonical WNT-pathway. In the case of canonical WNT-activation, BMP2, via BMPR2, activates MAPK1/3 in a SMAD-independent manner.    Outcome effects: MAPK1/3-mediated inhibition of GSK3B induces beta-catenin (CTNNB1) accumulation and transcriptional activity necessary for PAEC survival and proliferation in addition to the inhibition of apoptosis."
