xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) is increased blood pressure in the pulmonary artery.    Signaling description: BMP2 regulates pulmonary artery smooth muscle cell (PASMC) cytoskeleton organization and motility via consecutive canonical and non-canonical WNT signaling activation. BMP2 triggers beta-catenin (CTNNB1) accumulation via AKT1-mediated GSK3B inhibition followed by the production and release of fibronectin (FN1) to the extracellular space.    Outcome effects: FN1 binds to the VLA-4 receptor and activates ILK leading to the formation of a complex between ILK and DVL1 with subsequent RHOA and RAC1 activation and cytoskeleton rearrangement."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) is increased blood pressure in the pulmonary artery.    Signaling description: BMP2 regulates pulmonary artery smooth muscle cell (PASMC) cytoskeleton organization and motility via consecutive canonical and non-canonical WNT signaling activation. BMP2 triggers beta-catenin (CTNNB1) accumulation via AKT1-mediated GSK3B inhibition followed by the production and release of fibronectin (FN1) to the extracellular space.    Outcome effects: FN1 binds to the VLA-4 receptor and activates ILK leading to the formation of a complex between ILK and DVL1 with subsequent RHOA and RAC1 activation and cytoskeleton rearrangement." EXACT []

