xref: PS:Notes "Nephrolithiasis refers to the process of forming a kidney stone. The pathology of nephrolithiasis is related to increased excretion of Ca2+. Mutations in TRPV5/6, VDR, CALB1 genes and a high level of parathyroid hormone (PTH) may lead to impaired Ca2+ reabsorption in the renal tubule."
synonym: "Notes: Nephrolithiasis refers to the process of forming a kidney stone. The pathology of nephrolithiasis is related to increased excretion of Ca2+. Mutations in TRPV5/6, VDR, CALB1 genes and a high level of parathyroid hormone (PTH) may lead to impaired Ca2+ reabsorption in the renal tubule." EXACT []

