xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Reactive derivatives of non-enzymatic glucose-protein condensation reactions integrate a heterogeneous group of irreversible adducts called advanced glycation end-products (AGEs). AGEs have multiple effects in cavernous tissue.     Signaling description: AGEs upregulate the expression and activity of nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate (NADPH) oxidase, an important source of vascular oxidative stress and decrease expression of enzymes involved in antioxidant systems such as Mn-superoxide dismutase (SOD2). AGEs may also diminish eNOS (NOS3) activity. Furthermore, AGEs are able to antagonize erectile function by upregulating the expression of the vasoconstrictor endothelin-1 (EDN1) in endothelial cells. AGEs induce TGFB1 and collagens expressions leading to decreased elasticity of vascular bed and dysfunction of cavernous tissue. AGEs are chemotactic for monocytes, which allows its migration through the endothelial monolayer, and subsequent secretion of IGF1, PDGFB and other factors promoting increased blood vessels rigidity. AGEs attenuate composition and trapping of low-density lipoprotein (LDL) leading to the accumulation of perivascular amorphous hyalinized material that characterizes diabetic vascular disease.Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Compound with elevated level is highlighted in red and compound with reduced level is highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Reactive derivatives of non-enzymatic glucose-protein condensation reactions integrate a heterogeneous group of irreversible adducts called advanced glycation end-products (AGEs). AGEs have multiple effects in cavernous tissue.     Signaling description: AGEs upregulate the expression and activity of nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate (NADPH) oxidase, an important source of vascular oxidative stress and decrease expression of enzymes involved in antioxidant systems such as Mn-superoxide dismutase (SOD2). AGEs may also diminish eNOS (NOS3) activity. Furthermore, AGEs are able to antagonize erectile function by upregulating the expression of the vasoconstrictor endothelin-1 (EDN1) in endothelial cells. AGEs induce TGFB1 and collagens expressions leading to decreased elasticity of vascular bed and dysfunction of cavernous tissue. AGEs are chemotactic for monocytes, which allows its migration through the endothelial monolayer, and subsequent secretion of IGF1, PDGFB and other factors promoting increased blood vessels rigidity. AGEs attenuate composition and trapping of low-density lipoprotein (LDL) leading to the accumulation of perivascular amorphous hyalinized material that characterizes diabetic vascular disease.Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Compound with elevated level is highlighted in red and compound with reduced level is highlighted in blue." EXACT []

