xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Atherosclerosis is a progressive chronic disease characterized by the accumulation of lipids and fibrous elements in the large arteries. The buildup of fat and cholesterol leads to the formation of plaques in the artery walls which can hamper the blood flow.    Signaling description: The majority of pathogenic T-cells in atherosclerosis are of the Th1 profile, which represents the prevailing subtype in atherosclerotic lesions. Th1-cells are thought to posess proinflammatory and pro-atherogenic properties.    Outcome effects: The principal Th1 cytokine, IFNG is directly related to atherosclerosis by contributing to all the events that induce the disease progression. In addition, CD40-CD40LG interactions transduce immune and inflammatory signals, which promote the generation of Th1 cytokines. The expression of IL27 is elevated in human atheromas, yet its function in atherosclerosis remains unknown. IL27 promotes early Th1 differentiation. Furthermore, the circulating level of IL27 is strongly correlated with Gensini score, which reflects the severity of coronary artery stenosis, indicating that IL27 may promote the development and progression of coronary artery disease by inducing Th1 differentiation and related cytokine production. Lastly, the proinflammatory cytokine, LTA is thought to contribute to the pathogenesis of atherosclerosis.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Atherosclerosis is a progressive chronic disease characterized by the accumulation of lipids and fibrous elements in the large arteries. The buildup of fat and cholesterol leads to the formation of plaques in the artery walls which can hamper the blood flow.    Signaling description: The majority of pathogenic T-cells in atherosclerosis are of the Th1 profile, which represents the prevailing subtype in atherosclerotic lesions. Th1-cells are thought to posess proinflammatory and pro-atherogenic properties.    Outcome effects: The principal Th1 cytokine, IFNG is directly related to atherosclerosis by contributing to all the events that induce the disease progression. In addition, CD40-CD40LG interactions transduce immune and inflammatory signals, which promote the generation of Th1 cytokines. The expression of IL27 is elevated in human atheromas, yet its function in atherosclerosis remains unknown. IL27 promotes early Th1 differentiation. Furthermore, the circulating level of IL27 is strongly correlated with Gensini score, which reflects the severity of coronary artery stenosis, indicating that IL27 may promote the development and progression of coronary artery disease by inducing Th1 differentiation and related cytokine production. Lastly, the proinflammatory cytokine, LTA is thought to contribute to the pathogenesis of atherosclerosis.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

