xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Arterial hypertension is a chronic increase in blood pressure, which may lead to a variety of cardiovascular diseases, stroke, congestive heart failure, peripheral vascular disease, and renal disease. Hypertension risk factors include obesity, alcohol, smoking, kidney or endocrine diseases, diabetes mellitus, and family history. The pathogenesis of arterial hypertension is associated with mechanisms of vasoconstriction, which is believed to be an early component of the arterial hypertensive process.    Signaling description: Endothelin 1 (EDN1) is one of the most potent vasoconstrictors, which is secreted by endothelial cells and adrenal zona glomerulosa cells in response to specific stimuli such as hypoxia. However, factors that regulate the adrenal EDN1 production are yet to be identified. EDN1 acts as a local regulator of vascular tone and endothelial cell proliferation and acts as an independent stimulator of aldosterone secretion in adrenal zona glomerulosa. Abundant levels of EDN1 elevate the production of aldosterone and promote adrenal zona glomerulosa cell proliferation, which leads to arterial hypertension. EDN1 binds EDNRA/B on adrenal zona glomerulosa cells. The activity of these receptors is mediated by G proteins such as GNA11 and GNAQ, which activate PLCB1 and phosphatidyl-inositol-calcium second messenger system resulting in the release of Ca2+ into the cytoplasm from the endoplasmic reticulum (ER). PLCB1 mediates the cleavage of PIP2 to diacylglycerol and IP3. Further, IP3 binds ITPR1 on the ER, thus releasing Ca2+ and raising cytosolic Ca2+ concentrations. Diacylglycerol activates PKC, which phosphorylates PRKD1.    Outcome effects: PRKD1 directly phosphorylates and activates CREB1, and PKC activates the MAPK pathway via PTK2B/SRC and is involved in adrenal zona glomerulosa cell proliferation and growth. GNA11 binds PIK3CA, via activated PDPK1 by PIP3, to induce the activation of AKT1. Next, AKT1 activates CREB1, which binds NR4A2, which in turn has a critical role in the stimulation of CYP11B2 gene expression. Aldosterone is synthesized by CYP11B2 and regulates salt and water homeostasis and blood pressure.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Arterial hypertension is a chronic increase in blood pressure, which may lead to a variety of cardiovascular diseases, stroke, congestive heart failure, peripheral vascular disease, and renal disease. Hypertension risk factors include obesity, alcohol, smoking, kidney or endocrine diseases, diabetes mellitus, and family history. The pathogenesis of arterial hypertension is associated with mechanisms of vasoconstriction, which is believed to be an early component of the arterial hypertensive process.    Signaling description: Endothelin 1 (EDN1) is one of the most potent vasoconstrictors, which is secreted by endothelial cells and adrenal zona glomerulosa cells in response to specific stimuli such as hypoxia. However, factors that regulate the adrenal EDN1 production are yet to be identified. EDN1 acts as a local regulator of vascular tone and endothelial cell proliferation and acts as an independent stimulator of aldosterone secretion in adrenal zona glomerulosa. Abundant levels of EDN1 elevate the production of aldosterone and promote adrenal zona glomerulosa cell proliferation, which leads to arterial hypertension. EDN1 binds EDNRA/B on adrenal zona glomerulosa cells. The activity of these receptors is mediated by G proteins such as GNA11 and GNAQ, which activate PLCB1 and phosphatidyl-inositol-calcium second messenger system resulting in the release of Ca2+ into the cytoplasm from the endoplasmic reticulum (ER). PLCB1 mediates the cleavage of PIP2 to diacylglycerol and IP3. Further, IP3 binds ITPR1 on the ER, thus releasing Ca2+ and raising cytosolic Ca2+ concentrations. Diacylglycerol activates PKC, which phosphorylates PRKD1.    Outcome effects: PRKD1 directly phosphorylates and activates CREB1, and PKC activates the MAPK pathway via PTK2B/SRC and is involved in adrenal zona glomerulosa cell proliferation and growth. GNA11 binds PIK3CA, via activated PDPK1 by PIP3, to induce the activation of AKT1. Next, AKT1 activates CREB1, which binds NR4A2, which in turn has a critical role in the stimulation of CYP11B2 gene expression. Aldosterone is synthesized by CYP11B2 and regulates salt and water homeostasis and blood pressure.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

