xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Myocardial ischemia is a restriction of the blood supply to myocardium, which occurs due to a coronary artery obstruction and causes oxygen shortage and myocardial damage.    Signaling description: Angiotensin II (AGT) plays a key role in cardiac remodeling and functions as a growth factor influencing cell proliferation and growth, cell differentiation, and tissue fibrosis. AGT acts through the AGTR1 receptor. The primary transduction pathway of AGTR1 is the coupling to the G-protein GNA11 and GNAQ with activation of phospholipase C (PLCB1) cascade resulting in the release of Ca2+ into the cytoplasm from the endoplasmic reticulum and activation of PRKCD/PRKCE. AGTR1 also activates MAPK3/MAPK1 pathway directly through PKC, through the transactivation of EGFR, or through the ARRB1/ARRB2 with MAP kinases.    Outcome effects: The signaling pathways induce a variety of proteins and activate transcriptional regulators involved in cardiomyocyte proliferation, growth, and differentiation. AGTR1 also signals directly through AKT1, and activated AKT1 promotes MTOR and matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs) involved in vasculature remodeling, tissue repair, fibrosis, and extracellular matrix degradation.    Highlighted proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Myocardial ischemia is a restriction of the blood supply to myocardium, which occurs due to a coronary artery obstruction and causes oxygen shortage and myocardial damage.    Signaling description: Angiotensin II (AGT) plays a key role in cardiac remodeling and functions as a growth factor influencing cell proliferation and growth, cell differentiation, and tissue fibrosis. AGT acts through the AGTR1 receptor. The primary transduction pathway of AGTR1 is the coupling to the G-protein GNA11 and GNAQ with activation of phospholipase C (PLCB1) cascade resulting in the release of Ca2+ into the cytoplasm from the endoplasmic reticulum and activation of PRKCD/PRKCE. AGTR1 also activates MAPK3/MAPK1 pathway directly through PKC, through the transactivation of EGFR, or through the ARRB1/ARRB2 with MAP kinases.    Outcome effects: The signaling pathways induce a variety of proteins and activate transcriptional regulators involved in cardiomyocyte proliferation, growth, and differentiation. AGTR1 also signals directly through AKT1, and activated AKT1 promotes MTOR and matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs) involved in vasculature remodeling, tissue repair, fibrosis, and extracellular matrix degradation.    Highlighted proteins: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

