xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Autosomal recessive congenital ichthyosis (ARCI) refers to a group of rare disorders of keratinization classified as nonsyndromic forms of ichthyosis. This group was traditionally divided into lamellar ichthyosis and congenital ichthyosiform erythroderma. Both forms of ARCI are associated with mutations in ALOXE3 and ALOX12B genes.    Signaling description: 12-hydroperoxyeicosatetraenoic acid (12-HPETE) generated via the 12-LOX pathway is converted by eLOX-3 to hepoxilin A3 and hepoxilin B3, which are further metabolized to the corresponding trioxilins. The ALOXE3 and ALOX12B genes encode the epidermal LOXs eLOX-3 and 12R-LOX. The mechanisms for the involvement of 12-LOX and eLOX-3 in non syndromic forms of ichthyosis are described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: The ALOXE3 and ALOX12B genes are predominantly expressed in the suprabasal layers of the epidermis, which supports their role in the advanced phases of epidermal differentiation, with participation in the processing of lamellar bodies. These enzymes act on adjacent steps in the hepoxilin pathway. 12R-LOX transforms arachidonic acid into 12R-hydroxyeicosatetraenoic acid, while eLOX-3 converts this product into an epoxyalcohol isomer of the hepoxilin A3 family. The hepoxilin product is unstable and is hydrolyzed in cells to a specific trihydroxy derivative (trioxilin). The products of the hepoxilin pathway may participate in the formation of intercellular lipids of the stratum corneum or act as signals for inducing keratinocyte differentiation. Patients with mutations in the ALOX12B gene show more limited, whitish desquamation compared with carriers of mutations in the ALOXE3 gene. The presence of erythema, palmoplantar hyperkeratosis, and accentuation of the palmoplantar folds are also associated with ALOX12B mutations.    Highlighted proteins: Trioxilin A3 and trioxilin B3 are highlighted in blue in order to emphasize the protective skin barrier disruption in the stratum corneum.    Mutated proteins: ALOX12B and ALOXE3 genes mutated in congenital ichthyosiform erythroderma and lamellar ichthyosis are in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Autosomal recessive congenital ichthyosis (ARCI) refers to a group of rare disorders of keratinization classified as nonsyndromic forms of ichthyosis. This group was traditionally divided into lamellar ichthyosis and congenital ichthyosiform erythroderma. Both forms of ARCI are associated with mutations in ALOXE3 and ALOX12B genes.    Signaling description: 12-hydroperoxyeicosatetraenoic acid (12-HPETE) generated via the 12-LOX pathway is converted by eLOX-3 to hepoxilin A3 and hepoxilin B3, which are further metabolized to the corresponding trioxilins. The ALOXE3 and ALOX12B genes encode the epidermal LOXs eLOX-3 and 12R-LOX. The mechanisms for the involvement of 12-LOX and eLOX-3 in non syndromic forms of ichthyosis are described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: The ALOXE3 and ALOX12B genes are predominantly expressed in the suprabasal layers of the epidermis, which supports their role in the advanced phases of epidermal differentiation, with participation in the processing of lamellar bodies. These enzymes act on adjacent steps in the hepoxilin pathway. 12R-LOX transforms arachidonic acid into 12R-hydroxyeicosatetraenoic acid, while eLOX-3 converts this product into an epoxyalcohol isomer of the hepoxilin A3 family. The hepoxilin product is unstable and is hydrolyzed in cells to a specific trihydroxy derivative (trioxilin). The products of the hepoxilin pathway may participate in the formation of intercellular lipids of the stratum corneum or act as signals for inducing keratinocyte differentiation. Patients with mutations in the ALOX12B gene show more limited, whitish desquamation compared with carriers of mutations in the ALOXE3 gene. The presence of erythema, palmoplantar hyperkeratosis, and accentuation of the palmoplantar folds are also associated with ALOX12B mutations.    Highlighted proteins: Trioxilin A3 and trioxilin B3 are highlighted in blue in order to emphasize the protective skin barrier disruption in the stratum corneum.    Mutated proteins: ALOX12B and ALOXE3 genes mutated in congenital ichthyosiform erythroderma and lamellar ichthyosis are in white-out style." EXACT []

