synonym: "Source: Diseases" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Psoriasis is a chronic autoimmune skin disorder characterized by scaly and itchy patches of red skin, and is generally considered to be a hereditary disease triggered by environmental factors. Most of the genetic changes associated with psoriasis relate to the immune system. Interleukin-17 is an essential element in the pathology of autoimmune diseases including psoriasis.    Signaling description: IL17 signaling activates NF-kB and MAPK pathways through the conserved SEF/IL-17R (SEFIR) domain containing the adaptor protein, Act1 (TRAF3IP2). TRAF3IP2 further interacts with TRAF6 to promote signal transduction in addition to cytokine and chemokine secretion.    Outcome effects: IL17 stimulates the production of chemokines CXCL1, CXCL5, IL8, CCL2, and CCL7 which are responsible for the recruitment of neutrophils to the site of inflammation. Signal transduction activation by IL17 positively regulates cell proliferation and activates the immune response.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: TRAF3IP2 mutated in psoriasis is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Psoriasis is a chronic autoimmune skin disorder characterized by scaly and itchy patches of red skin, and is generally considered to be a hereditary disease triggered by environmental factors. Most of the genetic changes associated with psoriasis relate to the immune system. Interleukin-17 is an essential element in the pathology of autoimmune diseases including psoriasis.    Signaling description: IL17 signaling activates NF-kB and MAPK pathways through the conserved SEF/IL-17R (SEFIR) domain containing the adaptor protein, Act1 (TRAF3IP2). TRAF3IP2 further interacts with TRAF6 to promote signal transduction in addition to cytokine and chemokine secretion.    Outcome effects: IL17 stimulates the production of chemokines CXCL1, CXCL5, IL8, CCL2, and CCL7 which are responsible for the recruitment of neutrophils to the site of inflammation. Signal transduction activation by IL17 positively regulates cell proliferation and activates the immune response.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: TRAF3IP2 mutated in psoriasis is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

