xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Vitiligo is a chronic pigmentary skin disorder in which patches of skin lose their pigmentation. The disease may also involve mucous membranes and normally affects both sides of the body. Vitiligo is thought to be a disease with autoimmune origin that occurs due to a genetic predisposition. Cutaneous depigmentation in vitiligo involves cytotoxic activity of autoreactive T-cells.    Signaling description: Antigen-specific CD8+cells play a central role in the pathophysiology of vitiligo. The presence cytotoxic CD8+ T cells in the perilesional skin, coincides with the destruction of melanocytes.    Outcome effects: Sensitized CD8+ T-cells are attracted to melanocytic autoantigens and are responsible for melanocyte destruction as the primary event in vitiligo.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Vitiligo is a chronic pigmentary skin disorder in which patches of skin lose their pigmentation. The disease may also involve mucous membranes and normally affects both sides of the body. Vitiligo is thought to be a disease with autoimmune origin that occurs due to a genetic predisposition. Cutaneous depigmentation in vitiligo involves cytotoxic activity of autoreactive T-cells.    Signaling description: Antigen-specific CD8+cells play a central role in the pathophysiology of vitiligo. The presence cytotoxic CD8+ T cells in the perilesional skin, coincides with the destruction of melanocytes.    Outcome effects: Sensitized CD8+ T-cells are attracted to melanocytic autoantigens and are responsible for melanocyte destruction as the primary event in vitiligo.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

