xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Vitiligo is a chronic pigmentary skin disorder in which patches of skin lose their pigmentation. The disease may also involve mucous membranes and normally affects both sides of the body. Vitiligo is thought to be a disease with autoimmune origin that occurs due to a genetic predisposition. The autoimmune process in vitiligo leads to the destruction of melanocytes in the skin which creates the hypopigmented lesions.    Signaling description: The actual mechanism of autoimmune-mediated melanocyte apoptosis in vitiligo has not been definitively determined. Vitiligo develops as result of interplay between genetic and environmental factors.    Outcome effects: Dysregulation of the immune response in vitiligo makes the melanocyte an autoimmune target.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Vitiligo is a chronic pigmentary skin disorder in which patches of skin lose their pigmentation. The disease may also involve mucous membranes and normally affects both sides of the body. Vitiligo is thought to be a disease with autoimmune origin that occurs due to a genetic predisposition. The autoimmune process in vitiligo leads to the destruction of melanocytes in the skin which creates the hypopigmented lesions.    Signaling description: The actual mechanism of autoimmune-mediated melanocyte apoptosis in vitiligo has not been definitively determined. Vitiligo develops as result of interplay between genetic and environmental factors.    Outcome effects: Dysregulation of the immune response in vitiligo makes the melanocyte an autoimmune target.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

