xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Vitiligo is a chronic pigmentary skin disorder in which patches of skin lose their pigmentation. The disease may also involve mucous membranes and normally affects both sides of the body. Vitiligo is thought to be a disease with autoimmune origin that occurs due to a genetic predisposition. Cutaneous depigmentation in vitiligo involves cytotoxic activity of autoreactive T-cells.    Signaling description: The activation of CD4 may occur following the endocytosis of dying melanocytes, when antigen-presenting cells migrate to skin-draining lymph nodes to present peptides derived from melanosomal antigens.    Outcome effects: Studies have shown that CD4+ T-cells directly target melanocytes for destruction leading the development of hypopigmented patches in vitiligo.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Vitiligo susceptibility genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Vitiligo is a chronic pigmentary skin disorder in which patches of skin lose their pigmentation. The disease may also involve mucous membranes and normally affects both sides of the body. Vitiligo is thought to be a disease with autoimmune origin that occurs due to a genetic predisposition. Cutaneous depigmentation in vitiligo involves cytotoxic activity of autoreactive T-cells.    Signaling description: The activation of CD4 may occur following the endocytosis of dying melanocytes, when antigen-presenting cells migrate to skin-draining lymph nodes to present peptides derived from melanosomal antigens.    Outcome effects: Studies have shown that CD4+ T-cells directly target melanocytes for destruction leading the development of hypopigmented patches in vitiligo.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Vitiligo susceptibility genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

