xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Vitiligo is a chronic pigmentary skin disorder in which patches of skin lose their pigmentation. The disease may also involve mucous membranes and normally affects both sides of the body. Vitiligo is thought to be a disease with autoimmune origin that occurs due to a genetic predisposition.    Signaling description: Humoral immune response is implicated in vitiligo pathogenesis. Antibodies against melanocyte-derived antigens were found to be present in the serum of vitiligo patients.    Outcome effects: The disease-related antibodies in vitiligo are thought to be involved in melanocyte destruction by yet to be identified mechanism. .    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
