xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Acne vulgaris is a chronic inflammatory skin disorder which occurs due to the blockage of the hair follicles and their accompanying sebaceous glands with excess sebum and dead keratinocytes. Propionibacterium acnes (P. acnes) is a gram-positive anaerobic bacterium which plays a role in the development of inflammatory acne lesions.    Signaling description: P. acnes induces TLR2 signaling activation and provokes the inflammasome activation. The inflammasome is a protein complex comprised of NLRP3, PYCARD, and other proteins which promotes CASP1 activation. CASP1 cleaves pro-IL1B to generate its active form. TNF and IL1B play an important role in the inflammatory reaction in acne. They bind to their receptors on the cell surface and mediate inflammation through MAPK pathway.    Outcome effects: JUN/FOS induction leads to MMP synthesis and ECM degradation. In addition, NF-kB activation causes TNF and IL8 synthesis, which promotes neutrophil recruitment in the foci and also initiates IL1B, DEFB4A, IL12A, and IL12B transcription causing an immune response, contributing to the formation of acne lesions."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Acne vulgaris is a chronic inflammatory skin disorder which occurs due to the blockage of the hair follicles and their accompanying sebaceous glands with excess sebum and dead keratinocytes. Propionibacterium acnes (P. acnes) is a gram-positive anaerobic bacterium which plays a role in the development of inflammatory acne lesions.    Signaling description: P. acnes induces TLR2 signaling activation and provokes the inflammasome activation. The inflammasome is a protein complex comprised of NLRP3, PYCARD, and other proteins which promotes CASP1 activation. CASP1 cleaves pro-IL1B to generate its active form. TNF and IL1B play an important role in the inflammatory reaction in acne. They bind to their receptors on the cell surface and mediate inflammation through MAPK pathway.    Outcome effects: JUN/FOS induction leads to MMP synthesis and ECM degradation. In addition, NF-kB activation causes TNF and IL8 synthesis, which promotes neutrophil recruitment in the foci and also initiates IL1B, DEFB4A, IL12A, and IL12B transcription causing an immune response, contributing to the formation of acne lesions." EXACT []

