xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: In healthy premenopausal women estradiol maintains energy homeostasis via estrogen-alpha (ESR1) and estrogen-beta receptors (ESR2) by suppressing energy intake and lipogenesis, enhancing energy expenditure and ameliorating insulin sensitivity.     Signaling description: ESRs suppress expression of SREBF1 and PPARG and thereby control expression of lipogenic enzymes FASN, SCD, ACACA. They also inhibit lipoprotein lipase (LPL) expression, taking part in lipoprotein import into the adipocyte. ESRs control glucose transporter SLC2A4 expression. ESR1 is a positive regulator of SLC2A4, whereas ESR2 has a negative one.     Outcome effects: Following menopause onset, the level of estradiol production is decreased leading to an increased lipid accumulation and decreased lipid utilization contributing to obesity development.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: In healthy premenopausal women estradiol maintains energy homeostasis via estrogen-alpha (ESR1) and estrogen-beta receptors (ESR2) by suppressing energy intake and lipogenesis, enhancing energy expenditure and ameliorating insulin sensitivity.     Signaling description: ESRs suppress expression of SREBF1 and PPARG and thereby control expression of lipogenic enzymes FASN, SCD, ACACA. They also inhibit lipoprotein lipase (LPL) expression, taking part in lipoprotein import into the adipocyte. ESRs control glucose transporter SLC2A4 expression. ESR1 is a positive regulator of SLC2A4, whereas ESR2 has a negative one.     Outcome effects: Following menopause onset, the level of estradiol production is decreased leading to an increased lipid accumulation and decreased lipid utilization contributing to obesity development.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

