xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Obesity is closely associated with type 2 diabetes, hypertension, atherogenic dyslipidemias and disorders of blood coagulation and fibrinolysis.It is generally accepted that free fatty acids (FFA), a product of lipolysis, play a critical role in the development of obesity-related metabolic disturbances.    Signaling description: The key event is an increase in plasma FFA concentration. This leads to the accumulation of fatty acyl-CoA and diacylglycerol in vascular endothelial cells, and activation of PKC. Activation of PKC interrupts insulin signaling by serine phosphorylation of IRS 1/2. PKC also has been shown to activate NAD(P)H oxidase, which produces reactive oxygen species and destroys NO, contributing to vasoconstriction. Elevation of plasma FFA levels also leads to the production of inflammatory and proatherogenic proteins through activation of NFkB signaling.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Obesity is closely associated with type 2 diabetes, hypertension, atherogenic dyslipidemias and disorders of blood coagulation and fibrinolysis.It is generally accepted that free fatty acids (FFA), a product of lipolysis, play a critical role in the development of obesity-related metabolic disturbances.    Signaling description: The key event is an increase in plasma FFA concentration. This leads to the accumulation of fatty acyl-CoA and diacylglycerol in vascular endothelial cells, and activation of PKC. Activation of PKC interrupts insulin signaling by serine phosphorylation of IRS 1/2. PKC also has been shown to activate NAD(P)H oxidase, which produces reactive oxygen species and destroys NO, contributing to vasoconstriction. Elevation of plasma FFA levels also leads to the production of inflammatory and proatherogenic proteins through activation of NFkB signaling.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

