xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Adipose tissue is one of the insulin-responsive tissues, and insulin stimulates storage of triglycerides in adipose tissue by multiple mechanisms, including promoting the differentiation of preadipocytes to adipocytes, increasing the uptake of glucose and fatty acids derived from circulating lipoproteins, lipogenesis in mature adipocytes, and inhibiting lipolysis.     Signaling description: Hyperplasia (cell number increase) and hypertrophy (cell size increase) are two mechanisms of adipose tissue growth. The main transcription factors regulating adipocyte proliferation and making impact to adipocyte hyperplasia are PPARA, PPARG, CEBPA, and SREBF1.SREBF1 and PPARA also control expression of multiple lipogenic enzymes.     Outcome effects: The final products of lipogenesis are triglycerides. Redundant accumulation of triglycerides leads to adipocyte hypertrophy.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Adipose tissue is one of the insulin-responsive tissues, and insulin stimulates storage of triglycerides in adipose tissue by multiple mechanisms, including promoting the differentiation of preadipocytes to adipocytes, increasing the uptake of glucose and fatty acids derived from circulating lipoproteins, lipogenesis in mature adipocytes, and inhibiting lipolysis.     Signaling description: Hyperplasia (cell number increase) and hypertrophy (cell size increase) are two mechanisms of adipose tissue growth. The main transcription factors regulating adipocyte proliferation and making impact to adipocyte hyperplasia are PPARA, PPARG, CEBPA, and SREBF1.SREBF1 and PPARA also control expression of multiple lipogenic enzymes.     Outcome effects: The final products of lipogenesis are triglycerides. Redundant accumulation of triglycerides leads to adipocyte hypertrophy.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

