xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Diabetes mellitus type 1 is an autoimmune disease in which most of the pancreatic beta-cells are attacked and destroyed by T-cells. As a result, the pancreas does not produce an adequate amount of insulin leading to increased blood sugar levels. There is a genetic predisposition to type 1 diabetes.    Signaling description: There is ample evidence for a diabetogenic role of conventional dendritic cells (cDCs) in the initiatory steps of type 1 diabetes. Studies confirm that self-antigens released after beta-cell death are taken up by cDCs in the pancreatic islets and are processed and presented to islet-specific T-cells in the pancreatic lymph nodes with the involvement of TLR2.    Outcome effects: cDCs-mediated presentation of beta-cell antigens to T-cells initiates the diabetogenic response.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Diabetes mellitus type 1 is an autoimmune disease in which most of the pancreatic beta-cells are attacked and destroyed by T-cells. As a result, the pancreas does not produce an adequate amount of insulin leading to increased blood sugar levels. There is a genetic predisposition to type 1 diabetes.    Signaling description: There is ample evidence for a diabetogenic role of conventional dendritic cells (cDCs) in the initiatory steps of type 1 diabetes. Studies confirm that self-antigens released after beta-cell death are taken up by cDCs in the pancreatic islets and are processed and presented to islet-specific T-cells in the pancreatic lymph nodes with the involvement of TLR2.    Outcome effects: cDCs-mediated presentation of beta-cell antigens to T-cells initiates the diabetogenic response.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

