xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Pancreatic beta-cells are the insulin-secreting cells in the islets of Langerhans. Pancreatic beta-cell dysfunction is central in the pathogenesis of diabetes mellitus.    Signaling description: Cortisol infusions as well as acute treatment with high doses of oral prednisolone severely impair insulin secretion in healthy human volunteers. Glucocorticoids (GCs) have been shown to induce beta-cell dysfunction in completely healthy males. GCs have been demonstrated to impair rodent beta-cell glucose metabolism by reducing the expression levels of SLC2A2 and GCK, and by enhancing the G6PC2 activity.    Outcome effects: GCs may reduce glucose uptake and phosphorylation via the above mentioned mechanisms, and thereby decrease ATP synthesis and Ca2+ influx."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Pancreatic beta-cells are the insulin-secreting cells in the islets of Langerhans. Pancreatic beta-cell dysfunction is central in the pathogenesis of diabetes mellitus.    Signaling description: Cortisol infusions as well as acute treatment with high doses of oral prednisolone severely impair insulin secretion in healthy human volunteers. Glucocorticoids (GCs) have been shown to induce beta-cell dysfunction in completely healthy males. GCs have been demonstrated to impair rodent beta-cell glucose metabolism by reducing the expression levels of SLC2A2 and GCK, and by enhancing the G6PC2 activity.    Outcome effects: GCs may reduce glucose uptake and phosphorylation via the above mentioned mechanisms, and thereby decrease ATP synthesis and Ca2+ influx." EXACT []

