xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Pancreatic beta-cells are the insulin-secreting cells in the islets of Langerhans. Beta-cell dysfunction is central in the pathogenesis of diabetes mellitus.    Signaling description: The interaction of PTPRN/STAT5 in beta-cells is involved in the mechanism regulation of the amount of insulin stored and secreted. Prior to their linkage to the cytoskeleton, insulin granules are anchored to the actin cortex via PTPRN. Upon activation, beta-cells elevate calcium (Ca2+) levels and activate CAPN1 which cleaves off a cytosolic fragment from PTPRN.    Outcome effects: The free PTPRN cytosolic fragment then moves to the nucleus and binds to STAT5 to prevent STAT5 from dephosphorylation, which in turns upregulates insulin transcription. The sumoylation of PTPRN by PIAS4 reverses the binding of PTPRN to STAT5.    Animal data: rodent model."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Pancreatic beta-cells are the insulin-secreting cells in the islets of Langerhans. Beta-cell dysfunction is central in the pathogenesis of diabetes mellitus.    Signaling description: The interaction of PTPRN/STAT5 in beta-cells is involved in the mechanism regulation of the amount of insulin stored and secreted. Prior to their linkage to the cytoskeleton, insulin granules are anchored to the actin cortex via PTPRN. Upon activation, beta-cells elevate calcium (Ca2+) levels and activate CAPN1 which cleaves off a cytosolic fragment from PTPRN.    Outcome effects: The free PTPRN cytosolic fragment then moves to the nucleus and binds to STAT5 to prevent STAT5 from dephosphorylation, which in turns upregulates insulin transcription. The sumoylation of PTPRN by PIAS4 reverses the binding of PTPRN to STAT5.    Animal data: rodent model." EXACT []

