xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hyperparathyroidism is one of the most common endocrine disorders, defined by hypersecretion of parathormone. PTH controls calcium metabolism through its effects on intestine.    Signaling description: Hypersecretion of PTH is associated with hypercalcemia. Precise mechanisms of the molecular signalings of these processes in intestine are well known.     Outcome effects: The PTH1R is activated by PTH and mediates GNAS, which stimulates ADCY/PKA/CREB1 cascade. CREB1 promotes VDR, which regulates expression of TRPV5/6 and ATP2B1 involved in calcium reabsorption in intestine.     Highlighted proteins: PTH with red highlight has increased expression. Ca2+ with red highlight has increased level in blood serum."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hyperparathyroidism is one of the most common endocrine disorders, defined by hypersecretion of parathormone. PTH controls calcium metabolism through its effects on intestine.    Signaling description: Hypersecretion of PTH is associated with hypercalcemia. Precise mechanisms of the molecular signalings of these processes in intestine are well known.     Outcome effects: The PTH1R is activated by PTH and mediates GNAS, which stimulates ADCY/PKA/CREB1 cascade. CREB1 promotes VDR, which regulates expression of TRPV5/6 and ATP2B1 involved in calcium reabsorption in intestine.     Highlighted proteins: PTH with red highlight has increased expression. Ca2+ with red highlight has increased level in blood serum." EXACT []

