xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Primary hyperparathyroidism is a common endocrine disorder caused primarily by tumors in the parathyroid glands. In primary hyperparathyroidism, the parathyroid gland becomes overactive and secretes excess amounts of parathyroid hormone (PTH).    Signaling description: The most common cause of primary hyperparathyroidism is a mutation in one the following genes: menin (MEN1 syndrome), RET proto-oncogene (MEN2 syndrome) and HRPT2-parafibromin (hyperparathyroidism-jaw tumor syndrome). Germline-activating mutations in RET are associated with primary hyperparathyroidism and multiple endocrine neoplasia type2.    Outcome effects: Mutations in RET cause the disruption of cell survival and increase parathyrocytes proliferation."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Primary hyperparathyroidism is a common endocrine disorder caused primarily by tumors in the parathyroid glands. In primary hyperparathyroidism, the parathyroid gland becomes overactive and secretes excess amounts of parathyroid hormone (PTH).    Signaling description: The most common cause of primary hyperparathyroidism is a mutation in one the following genes: menin (MEN1 syndrome), RET proto-oncogene (MEN2 syndrome) and HRPT2-parafibromin (hyperparathyroidism-jaw tumor syndrome). Germline-activating mutations in RET are associated with primary hyperparathyroidism and multiple endocrine neoplasia type2.    Outcome effects: Mutations in RET cause the disruption of cell survival and increase parathyrocytes proliferation." EXACT []

