xref: PS:Source "Diseases"
synonym: "Source: Diseases" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hyperparathyroidism is a common endocrine disorder defined by hypersecretion of parathyroid hormone (PTH). Bone disease in hyperparathyroidism is characterized by decreased bone resorption and low bone mineral density. Pathological fractures, bone pain and deformities are features of osteitis fibrosa cystica which occur in hyperparathyroidism. In this condition, bone mineral density is usually extremely low.    Signaling description: Hypersecretion of PTH is associated with osteoclast activation and bone resorption. Precise mechanisms of the molecular signalings of these processes are well known.     Outcome effects: The PTH1R is activated by PTH and mediates GNAS, which stimulates ADCY/PKA/CREB1 cascade. BMP2 binds to BMPR1A/2 and through SMADs activates RUNX2. WNT3A signaling in osteoblast leads to E2F1 activation. CREB1, E2F1 and RUNX2 promote TNFSF11 that initiates osteoclast differentiation.    Highlighted proteins: PTH with red highlight has increased expression."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hyperparathyroidism is a common endocrine disorder defined by hypersecretion of parathyroid hormone (PTH). Bone disease in hyperparathyroidism is characterized by decreased bone resorption and low bone mineral density. Pathological fractures, bone pain and deformities are features of osteitis fibrosa cystica which occur in hyperparathyroidism. In this condition, bone mineral density is usually extremely low.    Signaling description: Hypersecretion of PTH is associated with osteoclast activation and bone resorption. Precise mechanisms of the molecular signalings of these processes are well known.     Outcome effects: The PTH1R is activated by PTH and mediates GNAS, which stimulates ADCY/PKA/CREB1 cascade. BMP2 binds to BMPR1A/2 and through SMADs activates RUNX2. WNT3A signaling in osteoblast leads to E2F1 activation. CREB1, E2F1 and RUNX2 promote TNFSF11 that initiates osteoclast differentiation.    Highlighted proteins: PTH with red highlight has increased expression." EXACT []

