xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hyperparathyroidism is one of the most common endocrine disorders, defined by hypersecretion of parathormone. PTH controls calcium and phosphorus metabolism through its effects on kidney.    Signaling description: Hypersecretion of PTH is associated with hypercalcemia and hypophosphatemia. Precise mechanisms of the molecular signalings of these processes in kidney are well known.     Outcome effects: The PTH1R is activated by PTH and mediates GNAS, which stimulates ADCY/PKA/CREB1 cascade. CREB1 promotes VDR, which regulates expression of TRPV5/6 and SLC34A1/A2, involved in calcium and phosphorus reabsorption in kidney.     Highlighted proteins: PTH with red highlight has increased expression. Pi with blue highlights has reduced level and Ca2+ with red highlight has increased level in blood serum."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hyperparathyroidism is one of the most common endocrine disorders, defined by hypersecretion of parathormone. PTH controls calcium and phosphorus metabolism through its effects on kidney.    Signaling description: Hypersecretion of PTH is associated with hypercalcemia and hypophosphatemia. Precise mechanisms of the molecular signalings of these processes in kidney are well known.     Outcome effects: The PTH1R is activated by PTH and mediates GNAS, which stimulates ADCY/PKA/CREB1 cascade. CREB1 promotes VDR, which regulates expression of TRPV5/6 and SLC34A1/A2, involved in calcium and phosphorus reabsorption in kidney.     Highlighted proteins: PTH with red highlight has increased expression. Pi with blue highlights has reduced level and Ca2+ with red highlight has increased level in blood serum." EXACT []

