xref: PS:Notes "The hyperprolactinemia of hypothyroidism is associated to several mechanisms. Thyrotropin releasing hormone (TRH) is a well-known positive regulator of prolactin (PRL) production and release. In response to the hypothyroid state (low level of thyroid hormones), a compensatory increase in hypothalamic TRH results in increased stimulation of PRL secretion. Also in hypothyroid state thyroid hormones stop to inhibit the expression of PRL gene (the proximal promoter of PRL gene contains an inhibitory region that responds to thyroid hormones).     Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: The hyperprolactinemia of hypothyroidism is associated to several mechanisms. Thyrotropin releasing hormone (TRH) is a well-known positive regulator of prolactin (PRL) production and release. In response to the hypothyroid state (low level of thyroid hormones), a compensatory increase in hypothalamic TRH results in increased stimulation of PRL secretion. Also in hypothyroid state thyroid hormones stop to inhibit the expression of PRL gene (the proximal promoter of PRL gene contains an inhibitory region that responds to thyroid hormones).     Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

