xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Chronic alcohol drinking has been shown to elevate blood levels of prolactin (PRL) resulting in hyperprolactinemia and various reproductive dysfunctions in both humans and animals.    Signaling description: Ethanol action on lactotropes involves suppression of DRD2 receptor, inhibition of G proteins and intracellular cyclic adenosine monophosphate (cAMP) signaling.An inhibitory action of GNAI3 on GNAS that is under the control of the DRD2 receptor is removed by ethanol. Ethanol, like estradiol, reduces pituitary levels of TGFB1 but increases levels of growth-stimulatory TGFB3 and FGF2. These factors have opposite effects on lactotroph cell growth. TGFB1 inhibits, TGFB3 and FGF2 stimulate the proliferation of lactotroph cells."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Chronic alcohol drinking has been shown to elevate blood levels of prolactin (PRL) resulting in hyperprolactinemia and various reproductive dysfunctions in both humans and animals.    Signaling description: Ethanol action on lactotropes involves suppression of DRD2 receptor, inhibition of G proteins and intracellular cyclic adenosine monophosphate (cAMP) signaling.An inhibitory action of GNAI3 on GNAS that is under the control of the DRD2 receptor is removed by ethanol. Ethanol, like estradiol, reduces pituitary levels of TGFB1 but increases levels of growth-stimulatory TGFB3 and FGF2. These factors have opposite effects on lactotroph cell growth. TGFB1 inhibits, TGFB3 and FGF2 stimulate the proliferation of lactotroph cells." EXACT []

