xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism (HH) is a condition which is characterized by hypogonadism due to an impaired secretion of gonadotropins by the pituitary gland and a resultant lack of sex steroids production. Loss-of-function mutations in KISS1, KISS1R, TAC3, TACR3, GNRH1 and PCSK1 in humans cause hypogonadotrophic hypogonadism.    Signaling description: Fertility in mammals is initiated at puberty by the pulsatile secretion of gonadotrophin releasing hormone (GNRH1) from a small number of neurons in the hypothalamus. GNRH1 release is regulated by kisspeptin (KISS1). KISS1 binds to its GPR54 (KISS1R) receptor, which is Gq-coupled to activate PLCB. PLC has multiple downstream actions resultant from cleaving PIP2 to InsP3 and diacylglycerol (DAG). Since PIP2 facilitates Kir channels opening, cleavage of this fatty acid attenuates these opening. DAG activates calcium TRPC1,3,4,5,6,7 channels. Once depolarized, Ca2+ entry through high voltage-activated Ca2+ channels can also contribute to facilitating TRPC channel opening. Massive Ca2+ influx stimulates GNRH1 release. Several studies also had shown the presence of TACR3 receptors on hypothalamus neurons. TACR3 and KISS1R both signal via Gq/11, so they may be expected to show synergistic activities. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism (HH) is a condition which is characterized by hypogonadism due to an impaired secretion of gonadotropins by the pituitary gland and a resultant lack of sex steroids production. Loss-of-function mutations in KISS1, KISS1R, TAC3, TACR3, GNRH1 and PCSK1 in humans cause hypogonadotrophic hypogonadism.    Signaling description: Fertility in mammals is initiated at puberty by the pulsatile secretion of gonadotrophin releasing hormone (GNRH1) from a small number of neurons in the hypothalamus. GNRH1 release is regulated by kisspeptin (KISS1). KISS1 binds to its GPR54 (KISS1R) receptor, which is Gq-coupled to activate PLCB. PLC has multiple downstream actions resultant from cleaving PIP2 to InsP3 and diacylglycerol (DAG). Since PIP2 facilitates Kir channels opening, cleavage of this fatty acid attenuates these opening. DAG activates calcium TRPC1,3,4,5,6,7 channels. Once depolarized, Ca2+ entry through high voltage-activated Ca2+ channels can also contribute to facilitating TRPC channel opening. Massive Ca2+ influx stimulates GNRH1 release. Several studies also had shown the presence of TACR3 receptors on hypothalamus neurons. TACR3 and KISS1R both signal via Gq/11, so they may be expected to show synergistic activities. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

