xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism (HH) is a condition which is characterized by hypogonadism due to an impaired secretion of gonadotropins by the pituitary gland and a resultant lack of sex steroids production. HH may be caused by mutation in a number of genes responsible for development and migration of gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GNRH) neurons. About 50% of HH are associated with Kallmann syndrome which is characterized by combination of hypogonadism and altered sense of smell (anosmia/hyposmia). The reason is that both GNRH neurons and olfactory bulb cells have common progenitors in olfactory placode.    Signaling description: Mutations in KAL1, FGF8, FGFR1, CHD7, PROC2, PROCR2, and HS6ST1 may cause either Kallmann syndrome or normosmic HH. Mutation in FLRT3, DUSP6, IL17RD, SPRY4, SEMA3A/7A cause Kallmann syndrome.Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism (HH) is a condition which is characterized by hypogonadism due to an impaired secretion of gonadotropins by the pituitary gland and a resultant lack of sex steroids production. HH may be caused by mutation in a number of genes responsible for development and migration of gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GNRH) neurons. About 50% of HH are associated with Kallmann syndrome which is characterized by combination of hypogonadism and altered sense of smell (anosmia/hyposmia). The reason is that both GNRH neurons and olfactory bulb cells have common progenitors in olfactory placode.    Signaling description: Mutations in KAL1, FGF8, FGFR1, CHD7, PROC2, PROCR2, and HS6ST1 may cause either Kallmann syndrome or normosmic HH. Mutation in FLRT3, DUSP6, IL17RD, SPRY4, SEMA3A/7A cause Kallmann syndrome.Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

