xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism refers to the disruption of gonadal function caused by deficient gonadotropin secretion, resulting from either a pituitary or hypothalamic defect.    Signaling description: Loss-of-function mutations in KISS1, TAC3, TACR3, LEP, LEPR are associated with hypogonadotrophic hypogonadism. KISS1 is a peptide which stimulates GNRH1 release form hypothalamus; whereas TAC3 and PDYN regulate KISS1 production. In addition, expression of KISS1 may be induced by LEP.    Outcome effects: As a result of mutations in genes encoding KISS1, TAC3, and LEPR, KISS1 production may be impaired.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style"
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism refers to the disruption of gonadal function caused by deficient gonadotropin secretion, resulting from either a pituitary or hypothalamic defect.    Signaling description: Loss-of-function mutations in KISS1, TAC3, TACR3, LEP, LEPR are associated with hypogonadotrophic hypogonadism. KISS1 is a peptide which stimulates GNRH1 release form hypothalamus; whereas TAC3 and PDYN regulate KISS1 production. In addition, expression of KISS1 may be induced by LEP.    Outcome effects: As a result of mutations in genes encoding KISS1, TAC3, and LEPR, KISS1 production may be impaired.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style" EXACT []

