xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hypothyroidism is pathological state caused by deficiency of thyroid hormones. About 95% of hypothyroidism cases occur from problems that start in the thyroid gland. In such cases, the disorder is called primary hypothyroidism. The two most common causes of primary hypothyroidism are (1) Hashimoto's thyroiditis which is an autoimmune condition and (2) overtreatment of hyperthyroidism (an overactive thyroid). Primary hypothyroidism may also occur as a result of insufficient introduction of iodine into body (endemic goiter). Primary hypothyroidism may also occur as a result of hereditary defects TSHR, GNAS, NKX1 and congenital hyperthyroidism.     Signaling description: Overt hypothyroidism is characterized by stable decrease synthesis of both T3 and T4. The growth of TSH level is a result of cancellation of T3 inhibitory effect on TSH synthesis in pituitary cell. The signaling through TSHR which activate synthesis of thyroid hormones is shown. TSHR activates directly CREB1 -regulator of thyroglobulin expression. TSHR can indirectly activate thyroid hormones synthesis providing cells proliferation in thyroid gland.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hypothyroidism is pathological state caused by deficiency of thyroid hormones. About 95% of hypothyroidism cases occur from problems that start in the thyroid gland. In such cases, the disorder is called primary hypothyroidism. The two most common causes of primary hypothyroidism are (1) Hashimoto's thyroiditis which is an autoimmune condition and (2) overtreatment of hyperthyroidism (an overactive thyroid). Primary hypothyroidism may also occur as a result of insufficient introduction of iodine into body (endemic goiter). Primary hypothyroidism may also occur as a result of hereditary defects TSHR, GNAS, NKX1 and congenital hyperthyroidism.     Signaling description: Overt hypothyroidism is characterized by stable decrease synthesis of both T3 and T4. The growth of TSH level is a result of cancellation of T3 inhibitory effect on TSH synthesis in pituitary cell. The signaling through TSHR which activate synthesis of thyroid hormones is shown. TSHR activates directly CREB1 -regulator of thyroglobulin expression. TSHR can indirectly activate thyroid hormones synthesis providing cells proliferation in thyroid gland.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

