xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hypothyroidism is pathological state caused by deficiency of thyroid hormones. Many factors influence synthesis of thyroid hormones, particularly levels of hormones of hypothalamus and pituitary, TRH and TSH. Because of that, symptoms of hypothyroidism may significantly vary depending on combination of altered functions of upstream regulators of these hormones. Deficiency in TRH synthesis causes tertiary hypothyroidism. Tertiary hypothyroidism accounts for less than 5% of hypothyroidism cases. It may also be termed hypothalamic-pituitary-axis hypothyroidism.    Signaling description: Main regulator of TSH synthesis is TRH which is hypothalamic hormone. A control of TRH synthesis is poorly studied. Nevertheless, it is clear that TRH release is affected by many external factors, such as cold, nutrition, circadian clock, and stress (see TRH Release pathway).    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hypothyroidism is pathological state caused by deficiency of thyroid hormones. Many factors influence synthesis of thyroid hormones, particularly levels of hormones of hypothalamus and pituitary, TRH and TSH. Because of that, symptoms of hypothyroidism may significantly vary depending on combination of altered functions of upstream regulators of these hormones. Deficiency in TRH synthesis causes tertiary hypothyroidism. Tertiary hypothyroidism accounts for less than 5% of hypothyroidism cases. It may also be termed hypothalamic-pituitary-axis hypothyroidism.    Signaling description: Main regulator of TSH synthesis is TRH which is hypothalamic hormone. A control of TRH synthesis is poorly studied. Nevertheless, it is clear that TRH release is affected by many external factors, such as cold, nutrition, circadian clock, and stress (see TRH Release pathway).    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

