xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hypoparathyroidism is an endocrine disorder characterized by deficient or absent secretion of parathyroid hormone (PTH). Loss-of-function mutations in TBX1, HOXA3, EYA1, PAX1, GCM2 protein genes lead to disruption of parathyroid glands development and may cause hypoparathyroidism.    Animal data: mouse model.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hypoparathyroidism is an endocrine disorder characterized by deficient or absent secretion of parathyroid hormone (PTH). Loss-of-function mutations in TBX1, HOXA3, EYA1, PAX1, GCM2 protein genes lead to disruption of parathyroid glands development and may cause hypoparathyroidism.    Animal data: mouse model.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

