xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Hypoparathyroidism refers to an endocrine syndrome characterized by hyposecretion of parathyroid hormone (PTH), which regulates Ca2+ and Pi metabolism through its effects on the kidney. Hence, hyposecretion of PTH is associated with impaired Renal Ca2+/Pi reabsorption leading to hypocalcemia and hyperphosphatemia.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Hypoparathyroidism refers to an endocrine syndrome characterized by hyposecretion of parathyroid hormone (PTH), which regulates Ca2+ and Pi metabolism through its effects on the kidney. Hence, hyposecretion of PTH is associated with impaired Renal Ca2+/Pi reabsorption leading to hypocalcemia and hyperphosphatemia.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

