xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The antiphospholipid syndrome (APS), is characterized by recurrent thrombosis (arterial or venous, or both) and/or morbidity during pregnancy (recurrent miscarriages / stillbirths) associated with high levels of anti-phospholipid antibodies (aPL).     Signaling description: aPL antibodies bind to beta-2GPI (APOH) which in turn binds to endothelial cell membrane receptors (TLR4 and ANXA2) and induces phosphorylation of p38 MAPK (MAPK14) and NFkB activation leading to a proinflammatory and prothrombotic effect (expression of VCAM1, ICAM1, SELE, F3, IL-1A, IL-6 and IL-8)."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The antiphospholipid syndrome (APS), is characterized by recurrent thrombosis (arterial or venous, or both) and/or morbidity during pregnancy (recurrent miscarriages / stillbirths) associated with high levels of anti-phospholipid antibodies (aPL).     Signaling description: aPL antibodies bind to beta-2GPI (APOH) which in turn binds to endothelial cell membrane receptors (TLR4 and ANXA2) and induces phosphorylation of p38 MAPK (MAPK14) and NFkB activation leading to a proinflammatory and prothrombotic effect (expression of VCAM1, ICAM1, SELE, F3, IL-1A, IL-6 and IL-8)." EXACT []

