xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is an autoimmune disease that affects the joints and causes inflammation and painful swelling. Other symptoms include fatigue, loss of appetite and a low-grade fever. Advanced RA can lead to bone erosion and joint deformity.    Signaling description: There is an increase in synovial fibroblast proliferation in RA. The proliferation is triggered by growth factors and cytokines including PDGF, IGF1, FGF2, TGFB1, INHBA, IL6, IL1B, and MIF. IL6 and PDGF are elevated in the disease and interact with the JAK-STAT pathway. IGF1 is also increased in RA and affects the MAPK3/1 pathway. Integrins also play an important role in the process. A high expression of ITGB1, ITGAV, ITGA5, and ITGA1 is observed in RA synovial fibroblasts. Integrins bind to extracellular matrix proteins such as FN1, VTN, collagen, and laminin and activate JUN and FOS transcription factors. Lastly, cytoskeleton is implicated in the process.    Outcome effects: STAT transcription factors induce MYC expression which is a positive regulator of cell proliferation. JUN and FOS directly regulate cell proliferation.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is an autoimmune disease that affects the joints and causes inflammation and painful swelling. Other symptoms include fatigue, loss of appetite and a low-grade fever. Advanced RA can lead to bone erosion and joint deformity.    Signaling description: There is an increase in synovial fibroblast proliferation in RA. The proliferation is triggered by growth factors and cytokines including PDGF, IGF1, FGF2, TGFB1, INHBA, IL6, IL1B, and MIF. IL6 and PDGF are elevated in the disease and interact with the JAK-STAT pathway. IGF1 is also increased in RA and affects the MAPK3/1 pathway. Integrins also play an important role in the process. A high expression of ITGB1, ITGAV, ITGA5, and ITGA1 is observed in RA synovial fibroblasts. Integrins bind to extracellular matrix proteins such as FN1, VTN, collagen, and laminin and activate JUN and FOS transcription factors. Lastly, cytoskeleton is implicated in the process.    Outcome effects: STAT transcription factors induce MYC expression which is a positive regulator of cell proliferation. JUN and FOS directly regulate cell proliferation.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

