xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is an autoimmune disease that affects the joints and causes inflammation and painful swelling. Other symptoms include fatigue, loss of appetite and a low-grade fever. Advanced RA can lead to bone erosion and joint deformity.    Signaling description: Elevated levels of IL6, IL1B, and TNFSF11 in RA contribute to osteoclast proliferation, differentiation, and decreased apoptosis. TNFSF11, also known as RANKL initiates osteoclast differentiation by binding to TNFRSF11A receptor on the osteoclast surface. The signaling involves TRAF1, TRAF2, TRAF3, TRAF5, and TRAF6 proteins and affects NF-kB and MAPK signaling. IL6 initiates NF-kB activation through the JAK-STAT pathway. IL1B also affects NF-kB pathway through the MYD88/IRAK4/IRAK1/TRAF6 axis.    Outcome effects: The described signaling leads to osteoclast differentiation and cell survival. In addition, TNFSF11 promotes osteoclast proliferation through the AKT1 pathway. In mature osteoclasts, the same signaling leads to bone resorption.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is an autoimmune disease that affects the joints and causes inflammation and painful swelling. Other symptoms include fatigue, loss of appetite and a low-grade fever. Advanced RA can lead to bone erosion and joint deformity.    Signaling description: Elevated levels of IL6, IL1B, and TNFSF11 in RA contribute to osteoclast proliferation, differentiation, and decreased apoptosis. TNFSF11, also known as RANKL initiates osteoclast differentiation by binding to TNFRSF11A receptor on the osteoclast surface. The signaling involves TRAF1, TRAF2, TRAF3, TRAF5, and TRAF6 proteins and affects NF-kB and MAPK signaling. IL6 initiates NF-kB activation through the JAK-STAT pathway. IL1B also affects NF-kB pathway through the MYD88/IRAK4/IRAK1/TRAF6 axis.    Outcome effects: The described signaling leads to osteoclast differentiation and cell survival. In addition, TNFSF11 promotes osteoclast proliferation through the AKT1 pathway. In mature osteoclasts, the same signaling leads to bone resorption.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

