synonym: "Source: Diseases" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Gout is a form of inflammatory arthritis caused by the deposition of monosodium urate (MSU) monohydrate crystals in the joint with clinical manifestations which include acute gouty arthritis, chronic gouty arthropathy, renal functional impairment, tophi and bone erosion. It has been shown that osteoblast viability and function are disrupted in gout.    Signaling description: BMP and TGFB signaling are crucial for osteoblast differentiation and function. TGFB2 and BMP2 bind to their receptors and through SMAD pathway lead to RUNX2 activation.    Outcome effects: In turn, RUNX2 promotes SP7, BGLAP, and IBSP expression which is responsible for osteoblast differentiation and function (biomineral formation). Further, RUNX2 along with PTH and calcitriol (vitamin D3) signaling regulates TNFSF11 and TNFRSF11B expression, thereby promoting osteoclast formation and function. In addition, monosodium urate crystal deposition results in decreased mineralization and reduced mRNA expression of genes related to all stages of osteoblast differentiation such as RUNX2, SP7, IBSP, and BGLAP.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Gout is a form of inflammatory arthritis caused by the deposition of monosodium urate (MSU) monohydrate crystals in the joint with clinical manifestations which include acute gouty arthritis, chronic gouty arthropathy, renal functional impairment, tophi and bone erosion. It has been shown that osteoblast viability and function are disrupted in gout.    Signaling description: BMP and TGFB signaling are crucial for osteoblast differentiation and function. TGFB2 and BMP2 bind to their receptors and through SMAD pathway lead to RUNX2 activation.    Outcome effects: In turn, RUNX2 promotes SP7, BGLAP, and IBSP expression which is responsible for osteoblast differentiation and function (biomineral formation). Further, RUNX2 along with PTH and calcitriol (vitamin D3) signaling regulates TNFSF11 and TNFRSF11B expression, thereby promoting osteoclast formation and function. In addition, monosodium urate crystal deposition results in decreased mineralization and reduced mRNA expression of genes related to all stages of osteoblast differentiation such as RUNX2, SP7, IBSP, and BGLAP.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red, and proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

