xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Gout is a form of inflammatory arthritis caused by the deposition of monosodium urate (MSU) monohydrate crystals in the joint with clinical manifestations which include acute gouty arthritis, chronic gouty arthropathy, tophi and renal functional impairment. Neutrophils play an important role in gout. They are attracted to the synovium and induce an inflammatory response.    Signaling description: Monocyte-derived cytokines including IL8, IL6, TNF, and IL1B promote endothelial cell activation. These cytokines bind to their receptors and through the NF-kB pathway lead to the protein synthesis which results in neutrophil recruitment. CXCL1 and CXCL2 cause neutrophil mobilization while VCAM1, ICAM1, and SELE are responsible for neutrophil adhesion on the endothelial cell surface. In addition, MSU may initiate complement activation by binding to the C5 component which also promotes neutrophil recruitment in the synovium.    Outcome effects: Activated neutrophils produce inflammatory cytokines and promote ROS generation, and elastase on the cell which causes osteoclast retraction that opens access to bone resorption by osteoclasts (not shown).    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Gout is a form of inflammatory arthritis caused by the deposition of monosodium urate (MSU) monohydrate crystals in the joint with clinical manifestations which include acute gouty arthritis, chronic gouty arthropathy, tophi and renal functional impairment. Neutrophils play an important role in gout. They are attracted to the synovium and induce an inflammatory response.    Signaling description: Monocyte-derived cytokines including IL8, IL6, TNF, and IL1B promote endothelial cell activation. These cytokines bind to their receptors and through the NF-kB pathway lead to the protein synthesis which results in neutrophil recruitment. CXCL1 and CXCL2 cause neutrophil mobilization while VCAM1, ICAM1, and SELE are responsible for neutrophil adhesion on the endothelial cell surface. In addition, MSU may initiate complement activation by binding to the C5 component which also promotes neutrophil recruitment in the synovium.    Outcome effects: Activated neutrophils produce inflammatory cytokines and promote ROS generation, and elastase on the cell which causes osteoclast retraction that opens access to bone resorption by osteoclasts (not shown).    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

