xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Metalloproteinase-mediated degradation of extracellular matrix (ECM) proteins resulting in cartilage destruction occurs in osteoarthritis (OA) and is a strong attribute of the pathology. The excessive mechanical loading of cartilage, which causes TNF and IL1B synthesis, is a proven trigger of OA.    Signaling description: The cytokines bind to their receptors on the chondrocyte surface and lead to JUN-FOS activation through MAPK8, MAPK p38, and MAPK1 pathways. The release of NF-kB from its inhibitor, NFKBIA is also provoked by these cytokines. JUN, FOS, and NF-kB bind to the promoter regions of metalloproteinases including MMP1, MMP3, and MMP13 and cause their synthesis.    Outcome effects: The metalloproteinases released into the ECM cleave collagens, thereby impairing cartilage function.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Metalloproteinase-mediated degradation of extracellular matrix (ECM) proteins resulting in cartilage destruction occurs in osteoarthritis (OA) and is a strong attribute of the pathology. The excessive mechanical loading of cartilage, which causes TNF and IL1B synthesis, is a proven trigger of OA.    Signaling description: The cytokines bind to their receptors on the chondrocyte surface and lead to JUN-FOS activation through MAPK8, MAPK p38, and MAPK1 pathways. The release of NF-kB from its inhibitor, NFKBIA is also provoked by these cytokines. JUN, FOS, and NF-kB bind to the promoter regions of metalloproteinases including MMP1, MMP3, and MMP13 and cause their synthesis.    Outcome effects: The metalloproteinases released into the ECM cleave collagens, thereby impairing cartilage function.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

