xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Arthralgia refers to pain in the joints, and is an important hallmark of osteoarthritis (OA). In conjunction with increased pressure of synovial fluid, prostaglandin E2 (PGE2) synthesis induced by interleukin 1, beta (IL1B) signaling triggers arthralgia.    Signaling description: IL1B is highly expressed in OA cartilage and upregulates PTGES and PTGS2 expression by NF-kB activation. The signaling originates with the activation of IL1R1 by IL1B. The signal is subsequently transduced to the RAC1/MAP3K1/MAP2K1/2/6/MAPK1 axis and triggers NF-kB. IL1R1 with IL1RAP allow MYD88 to recruit IRAK to this receptor-signaling complex. The complex activates TRAF6, which also activates NF-kB (through MAP3K5 and MAP3K7).    Outcome effects: NF-kB binds to the promoter regions of PTGES and PTGS2 genes leading to the synthesis of PGE2.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Arthralgia refers to pain in the joints, and is an important hallmark of osteoarthritis (OA). In conjunction with increased pressure of synovial fluid, prostaglandin E2 (PGE2) synthesis induced by interleukin 1, beta (IL1B) signaling triggers arthralgia.    Signaling description: IL1B is highly expressed in OA cartilage and upregulates PTGES and PTGS2 expression by NF-kB activation. The signaling originates with the activation of IL1R1 by IL1B. The signal is subsequently transduced to the RAC1/MAP3K1/MAP2K1/2/6/MAPK1 axis and triggers NF-kB. IL1R1 with IL1RAP allow MYD88 to recruit IRAK to this receptor-signaling complex. The complex activates TRAF6, which also activates NF-kB (through MAP3K5 and MAP3K7).    Outcome effects: NF-kB binds to the promoter regions of PTGES and PTGS2 genes leading to the synthesis of PGE2.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red.    Mutated genes: Mutated gene is shown in white-out style." EXACT []

