xref: PS:Notes "Mutations of the CD40LG gene. T cells cannot tell B cells to switch classes. X-linked (XHIGM). Mutations of the AICDA gene. B cells cannot recombine genetic material to change heavy chain production, which is a required step in switching classes. Mutations of the CD40 gene. B cells cannot receive the signal from T cells to switch classes. Mutations of the UNG gene. It does not impair Somatic Hypermutation. Mutations in NEMO cause X-linked hyper-IgM syndrome with ectodermal dysplasia (XHM-ED)."
