xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Diseases"
synonym: "Source: Diseases" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a lentivirus which causes acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS), a condition in which the progressive failure of the immune system allows life-threatening opportunistic infections and cancers to occur. The impairment of CD8 T-cell action is an important step in HIV infection.    Signaling description: Normally, T-cell receptor (TCR) with its coreceptor CD8A (of CD8 T cells) recognizes MHC class I protein complex with the infected cell antigen. In T-cells, the signal is transduced to ZAP70 and (via LAT/PLCG1) promotes the release of calcium (Ca2) from intracellular stores. Ca2 interacts with calmodulin-calcineurin complex, which leads to NF-AT activation. In turn, ZAP70 activates ERK (MAPK) pathway through PTK2B, which leads to JUN and FOS activation. At the same time, viral Nef protein downregulates the expression of MHC class I protein complex which blocks the described signal transduction and CD8 T-cell activation.    Outcome effects: NF-AT and JUN/FOS bind to the promoter regions of FASLG, LTA, and IFNG resulting in their transcription. These ligands are death signals for the infected cells. In addition, MAPK3, which is involved in the MAPK pathway, promotes the expression of PRF1 in activated cytotoxic lymphocytes and is required for the release of granzymes (GZMA/GZMB) into the target cell.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Viral proteins are shown in grey.    Reference: 1). Santos-Costa Q, Gracas-Pereira J, Azevedo-Pereira JM (2007) Death on arrival . HIV and apoptosis - an . VIII Congresso Virtual HIV/AIDS - Current research insights into HIV/AIDS and related diseases. ISBN 978-972-95977-7-0. p. 149-96."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a lentivirus which causes acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS), a condition in which the progressive failure of the immune system allows life-threatening opportunistic infections and cancers to occur. The impairment of CD8 T-cell action is an important step in HIV infection.    Signaling description: Normally, T-cell receptor (TCR) with its coreceptor CD8A (of CD8 T cells) recognizes MHC class I protein complex with the infected cell antigen. In T-cells, the signal is transduced to ZAP70 and (via LAT/PLCG1) promotes the release of calcium (Ca2) from intracellular stores. Ca2 interacts with calmodulin-calcineurin complex, which leads to NF-AT activation. In turn, ZAP70 activates ERK (MAPK) pathway through PTK2B, which leads to JUN and FOS activation. At the same time, viral Nef protein downregulates the expression of MHC class I protein complex which blocks the described signal transduction and CD8 T-cell activation.    Outcome effects: NF-AT and JUN/FOS bind to the promoter regions of FASLG, LTA, and IFNG resulting in their transcription. These ligands are death signals for the infected cells. In addition, MAPK3, which is involved in the MAPK pathway, promotes the expression of PRF1 in activated cytotoxic lymphocytes and is required for the release of granzymes (GZMA/GZMB) into the target cell.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Viral proteins are shown in grey.    Reference: 1). Santos-Costa Q, Gracas-Pereira J, Azevedo-Pereira JM (2007) Death on arrival . HIV and apoptosis - an . VIII Congresso Virtual HIV/AIDS - Current research insights into HIV/AIDS and related diseases. ISBN 978-972-95977-7-0. p. 149-96." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-558fd8f5-609d-4c95-ae97-19f95851841a
name: Th17-Cell Numbers Reduction in HIV
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:t ! T
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:blood ! Blood
