synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Diseases"
synonym: "Source: Diseases" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a lentivirus which causes acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS), a condition in which the progressive failure of the immune system allows life-threatening opportunistic infections and cancers to occur. There is a reduction in the number of Th17 cell during HIV infections.    Signaling description: Normally, CD4 T-cell produced cytokines such as IL1B, IL23A, IL6, and TGFB1 promote naive T-cells differentiation into Th17 phenotype. The cytokines bind to their receptors and the signal is transduced to STAT3 through MYD88/IRAK/TRAF6/MAP3K1 (from via IL1B), JAK (from IL23A and IL6), and SMAD3 (from TGFB1).    Outcome effects: STAT3 triggers RORC expression and they both bind to the promoters of IL21, IL22, IL17A, and IL17F genes. These cytokines promote an inflammatory response in the gut. During HIV infection, there is a reduction in the level of IL1B, IL23A, IL6, and TGFB1 cytokines due to the impairment of CD4 T-cell signaling, which results in the block of Th17 maturation.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue.    References: 1). Santos-Costa Q, Gracas-Pereira J, Azevedo-Pereira JM (2007) Death on arrival . HIV and apoptosis - an . VIII Congresso Virtual HIV/AIDS - Current research insights into HIV/AIDS and related diseases. ISBN 978-972-95977-7-0. p. 149-96."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a lentivirus which causes acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS), a condition in which the progressive failure of the immune system allows life-threatening opportunistic infections and cancers to occur. There is a reduction in the number of Th17 cell during HIV infections.    Signaling description: Normally, CD4 T-cell produced cytokines such as IL1B, IL23A, IL6, and TGFB1 promote naive T-cells differentiation into Th17 phenotype. The cytokines bind to their receptors and the signal is transduced to STAT3 through MYD88/IRAK/TRAF6/MAP3K1 (from via IL1B), JAK (from IL23A and IL6), and SMAD3 (from TGFB1).    Outcome effects: STAT3 triggers RORC expression and they both bind to the promoters of IL21, IL22, IL17A, and IL17F genes. These cytokines promote an inflammatory response in the gut. During HIV infection, there is a reduction in the level of IL1B, IL23A, IL6, and TGFB1 cytokines due to the impairment of CD4 T-cell signaling, which results in the block of Th17 maturation.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue.    References: 1). Santos-Costa Q, Gracas-Pereira J, Azevedo-Pereira JM (2007) Death on arrival . HIV and apoptosis - an . VIII Congresso Virtual HIV/AIDS - Current research insights into HIV/AIDS and related diseases. ISBN 978-972-95977-7-0. p. 149-96." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-4ba1066a-dfdc-42d2-a77e-2fa5dd16a85b
name: CD4+ T-Cell Function Decline in HIV
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:blood ! Blood
is_a: urn:agi-folder:c ! C
is_a: urn:agi-folder:hiv_type_1_infection ! HIV type 1 infection
xref: PS:Description "Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a lentivirus that causes acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS) in which infections and cancers occur. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a lentivirus that causes acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS) in which infections and cancers occur. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
