xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a lentivirus which causes acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS), a condition in which the progressive failure of the immune system allows life-threatening opportunistic infections and cancers to occur. The impairment of CD8 T-cell action is an important step in HIV infection.    Signaling description: During HIV infection, CXCR4 in macrophages is activated by the HIV envelope glycoprotein Gp120 (env), and in turn activates PI3K through LYN, PTK2, and PTK2B. PI3K generates PIP3, which interacts with PDPK1 leading to AKT1 activation. PTK2B forms a complex with SRC, BCAR1, CRK, and PXN.    Outcome effects: Activated AKT1 promotes the survival of macrophages, and PXN interacts with ELMO1-DOCK1 complex which results in actin reorganization and cell mobility through RAC1/PAK1.    Highlighted proteins: Viral proteins are shown in grey.    References: 1). Santos-Costa Q, Gracas-Pereira J, Azevedo-Pereira JM (2007) Death on arrival . HIV and apoptosis - an . VIII Congresso Virtual HIV/AIDS - Current research insights into HIV/AIDS and related diseases. ISBN 978-972-95977-7-0. p. 149-96."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a lentivirus which causes acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS), a condition in which the progressive failure of the immune system allows life-threatening opportunistic infections and cancers to occur. The impairment of CD8 T-cell action is an important step in HIV infection.    Signaling description: During HIV infection, CXCR4 in macrophages is activated by the HIV envelope glycoprotein Gp120 (env), and in turn activates PI3K through LYN, PTK2, and PTK2B. PI3K generates PIP3, which interacts with PDPK1 leading to AKT1 activation. PTK2B forms a complex with SRC, BCAR1, CRK, and PXN.    Outcome effects: Activated AKT1 promotes the survival of macrophages, and PXN interacts with ELMO1-DOCK1 complex which results in actin reorganization and cell mobility through RAC1/PAK1.    Highlighted proteins: Viral proteins are shown in grey.    References: 1). Santos-Costa Q, Gracas-Pereira J, Azevedo-Pereira JM (2007) Death on arrival . HIV and apoptosis - an . VIII Congresso Virtual HIV/AIDS - Current research insights into HIV/AIDS and related diseases. ISBN 978-972-95977-7-0. p. 149-96." EXACT []

