xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Osteopetrosis (known as marble bone disease) is a group of rare, heritable disorders of the skeleton characterized by increased bone density on radiographs and is caused by the failure of osteoclast development or function.    Signaling description: Osteoblasts regulate osteoclast function through the production of paracrine factors, mainly TNFSF11, which is involved in WNT signaling.    Outcome effects: Impairment of WNT signaling causes osteopetrosis. PORCN mutations are associated with osteopathia striata in Goltz Syndrome, while FAM123B gene mutations are linked to osteopathia striata with cranial stenosis. OSTM1 regulates CTNNB1/LEF1 interaction and causes rare forms of osteopetrosis. LRP1 mutations also lead to rare forms of the disorder.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Osteopetrosis (known as marble bone disease) is a group of rare, heritable disorders of the skeleton characterized by increased bone density on radiographs and is caused by the failure of osteoclast development or function.    Signaling description: Osteoblasts regulate osteoclast function through the production of paracrine factors, mainly TNFSF11, which is involved in WNT signaling.    Outcome effects: Impairment of WNT signaling causes osteopetrosis. PORCN mutations are associated with osteopathia striata in Goltz Syndrome, while FAM123B gene mutations are linked to osteopathia striata with cranial stenosis. OSTM1 regulates CTNNB1/LEF1 interaction and causes rare forms of osteopetrosis. LRP1 mutations also lead to rare forms of the disorder.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

