xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Osteopetrosis with renal tubular acidosis is a rare disorder characterized by osteopetrosis, renal tubular acidosis (RTA), and neurological symptoms related to cerebral calcifications. Osteopetrosis can be caused by mutations in the carbonic anhydrase II (CA2) gene.    Signaling description: Normally, renal CA2 plays an important role in blood acid-base balance maintenance. CA2 catalizes the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide to form bicarbonate and a proton.    Outcome effects: When CA2 is mutated, blood acid-base balance is impaired leading to systemic acidosis.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Osteopetrosis with renal tubular acidosis is a rare disorder characterized by osteopetrosis, renal tubular acidosis (RTA), and neurological symptoms related to cerebral calcifications. Osteopetrosis can be caused by mutations in the carbonic anhydrase II (CA2) gene.    Signaling description: Normally, renal CA2 plays an important role in blood acid-base balance maintenance. CA2 catalizes the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide to form bicarbonate and a proton.    Outcome effects: When CA2 is mutated, blood acid-base balance is impaired leading to systemic acidosis.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

