xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Osteoporosis is a disease characterized by loss of bone strength which increases the risk of fragility fractures. In osteoporosis, calcium (Ca2+) deficiency can be the cause of impaired bone mineralization.    Signaling description: Ca2+ transport is an active process and Ca2+ transport proteins are localized in the outer and inner enterocyte membranes. The process begins with Ca2+ entry in to the cell via TRPV5/6 proteins. The expression of TRPV proteins is under the control of VDR and ESR1 transcription factors. In the absence of their ligands (estrogens and/or calcitriol) or due to polymorphisms in the genes, TRPV synthesis can be impaired causing decreased Ca2+ absorption in the intestine.    Outcome effects: Following its entry in to the cell, Ca2+ is transported to the inner membrane by CALB1 protein, and then excreted by the ATP2B1 and SLC8A1 transporters to the blood.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with reduced level or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Osteoporosis is a disease characterized by loss of bone strength which increases the risk of fragility fractures. In osteoporosis, calcium (Ca2+) deficiency can be the cause of impaired bone mineralization.    Signaling description: Ca2+ transport is an active process and Ca2+ transport proteins are localized in the outer and inner enterocyte membranes. The process begins with Ca2+ entry in to the cell via TRPV5/6 proteins. The expression of TRPV proteins is under the control of VDR and ESR1 transcription factors. In the absence of their ligands (estrogens and/or calcitriol) or due to polymorphisms in the genes, TRPV synthesis can be impaired causing decreased Ca2+ absorption in the intestine.    Outcome effects: Following its entry in to the cell, Ca2+ is transported to the inner membrane by CALB1 protein, and then excreted by the ATP2B1 and SLC8A1 transporters to the blood.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with reduced level or activity are highlighted in blue.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style." EXACT []

