xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: A positive feedback regulatory loop between TERT and NFKB potentiates cancer progression.    Signaling description: TERT directly regulates NFKB-dependent gene expression by binding to the RELA, which, in turn, modulates nuclear translocation of TERT and is also responsible for expression of telomeric repeat binding factor 2 (TERF2IP). NFKB signaling may also activate TERT via NFKB1 and MYC.    Outcome effects: The interplay between TERT and NFKB promotes tumor growth and chronic inflammation.    Animal data: Some of the data were obtained from animal experiments or human cancer lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Enabling of Replicative Immortality\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: A positive feedback regulatory loop between TERT and NFKB potentiates cancer progression.    Signaling description: TERT directly regulates NFKB-dependent gene expression by binding to the RELA, which, in turn, modulates nuclear translocation of TERT and is also responsible for expression of telomeric repeat binding factor 2 (TERF2IP). NFKB signaling may also activate TERT via NFKB1 and MYC.    Outcome effects: The interplay between TERT and NFKB promotes tumor growth and chronic inflammation.    Animal data: Some of the data were obtained from animal experiments or human cancer lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Enabling of Replicative Immortality\" for details." EXACT []

