xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Kynurenine and it's metabolites are essential for cancer-associated immunosuppression.     Signaling description: Kynurenine pathway (KP) is responsible for tryptophan turnover generating multiple intermediate metabolites. Among them, kynurenine (KYN), picolinic acid (PIC), 3-hydroxykynurenine (3-HK), 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid (3-HAA) and quinolinic acid (QUIN) were found to be immunosuppressive: in micromolar concentrations they were found to inhibit T-cell proliferation in vitro. The same substances induced selective apoptosis of thymocytes and of antigen-specific CD4 T-helper 1 cells. Another notable effect 3-HAA has on T-cells is its ability to cause a reduction in the fraction of CD4 TH17 cells and a reciprocal increase in the fraction of Tregs. IDO1 and TDO2, responsible for kynurenine production are often overexpressed in cancers.     Outcome effects: Kynurenine and it's metabolites induce inhibition of proliferation and induction of apoptosis in the effector T-cells.     Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Immune Escape\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Kynurenine and it's metabolites are essential for cancer-associated immunosuppression.     Signaling description: Kynurenine pathway (KP) is responsible for tryptophan turnover generating multiple intermediate metabolites. Among them, kynurenine (KYN), picolinic acid (PIC), 3-hydroxykynurenine (3-HK), 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid (3-HAA) and quinolinic acid (QUIN) were found to be immunosuppressive: in micromolar concentrations they were found to inhibit T-cell proliferation in vitro. The same substances induced selective apoptosis of thymocytes and of antigen-specific CD4 T-helper 1 cells. Another notable effect 3-HAA has on T-cells is its ability to cause a reduction in the fraction of CD4 TH17 cells and a reciprocal increase in the fraction of Tregs. IDO1 and TDO2, responsible for kynurenine production are often overexpressed in cancers.     Outcome effects: Kynurenine and it's metabolites induce inhibition of proliferation and induction of apoptosis in the effector T-cells.     Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Immune Escape\" for details." EXACT []

