synonym: "Source: Pathological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: CD46, CD55 and CD59 are membrane complement regulatory proteins. They are overexpressed in cancer cells and inhibit complement-mediated lysis of cancer cells.     Signaling description: Both CD46 and CD55 inhibit C3 and C4B activation. CD59 binds to C8A and C9 and impairs the formation of membrane attack complex. In cancer, CD46/55/59 can be upregulated by NFKB, CREB1, STAT3 and other transcription factors.     Outcome effects: The membrane attack complex formation is blocked and complement-dependent lysis of cancer cell does not occur.     Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Immune Escape\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: CD46, CD55 and CD59 are membrane complement regulatory proteins. They are overexpressed in cancer cells and inhibit complement-mediated lysis of cancer cells.     Signaling description: Both CD46 and CD55 inhibit C3 and C4B activation. CD59 binds to C8A and C9 and impairs the formation of membrane attack complex. In cancer, CD46/55/59 can be upregulated by NFKB, CREB1, STAT3 and other transcription factors.     Outcome effects: The membrane attack complex formation is blocked and complement-dependent lysis of cancer cell does not occur.     Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Immune Escape\" for details." EXACT []

