xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The PI3K/AKT/MTOR pathway is an essential player in cell cycle regulation. Therefore, it is directly related to cellular quiescence, proliferation, longevity and is often dysregulated in cancer.    Signaling description: Direct activation of PI3K by activated G protein-coupled receptors or receptor tyrosine kinase leads to phosphorylation and activation of AKT which, in turn, activates multiple downstream targets. Activating mutations of PIK3CA, PIK3R1, AKT1/2/3 contribute to cancer progression.    Outcome effects: Due to lack of natural inhibitors, PI3K-AKT-MTOR signaling is switched on which leads to uncontrolled cell proliferation, inhibition of apoptosis and cancer progression.    Animal data: Some of the data were obtained from animal experiments or human cancer lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Evading of Growth Suppressors\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Evading of Growth Suppressors\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The PI3K/AKT/MTOR pathway is an essential player in cell cycle regulation. Therefore, it is directly related to cellular quiescence, proliferation, longevity and is often dysregulated in cancer.    Signaling description: Direct activation of PI3K by activated G protein-coupled receptors or receptor tyrosine kinase leads to phosphorylation and activation of AKT which, in turn, activates multiple downstream targets. Activating mutations of PIK3CA, PIK3R1, AKT1/2/3 contribute to cancer progression.    Outcome effects: Due to lack of natural inhibitors, PI3K-AKT-MTOR signaling is switched on which leads to uncontrolled cell proliferation, inhibition of apoptosis and cancer progression.    Animal data: Some of the data were obtained from animal experiments or human cancer lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Evading of Growth Suppressors\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Evading of Growth Suppressors\" for details." EXACT []

