xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Bradykinin is a peptide that causes blood vessels to dilate, which lowers blood pressure. It is formed during the proteolytic cleavage of its precursor, kininogen (KNG1) in response to tissue damage. The major effects of peptides in inflammation are pain, redness, and a rise in temperature in the inflammatory foci.    Signaling description: The biological actions of bradykinin are mediated by B1 (BDKRB1) and B2 (BDKRB2) receptors, which mediate similar effects. Both are typical G-protein coupled receptors. In contrast to constitutive BDKRB2, the expression of BDKRB1 is up-regulated during inflammation. Angiotensin (AGT) induces BDKRB1 expression through the signaling of PI3K. BDKRB1 is also induced by IL1 via the NF-kB transcription factor. BDKRB2 is triggered by bradykinin, but BDKRB1 is activated by the kinin metabolites such as des-Arg(9)-bradykinin or des-Arg-LBK, both of which are generated by CPN1/CPM-mediated cleavage of the C-terminal arginine residue of bradykinin. BDKRB1 and BDKRB2 mediate arachidonic acid release and prostaglandin (PG) synthesis. The activation of BDKRB1 leads to the elevation of intracellular free calcium (Ca2+) activity by increasing Ca2 entry into the cell. Conversely, BDKRB2 acts primarily to release bound intracellular Ca2+. NOS3, IL6, and PGI2 synthesis cause increased blood vessel permeability and vasodilation.    Highlighted proteins: Protein with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Bradykinin is a peptide that causes blood vessels to dilate, which lowers blood pressure. It is formed during the proteolytic cleavage of its precursor, kininogen (KNG1) in response to tissue damage. The major effects of peptides in inflammation are pain, redness, and a rise in temperature in the inflammatory foci.    Signaling description: The biological actions of bradykinin are mediated by B1 (BDKRB1) and B2 (BDKRB2) receptors, which mediate similar effects. Both are typical G-protein coupled receptors. In contrast to constitutive BDKRB2, the expression of BDKRB1 is up-regulated during inflammation. Angiotensin (AGT) induces BDKRB1 expression through the signaling of PI3K. BDKRB1 is also induced by IL1 via the NF-kB transcription factor. BDKRB2 is triggered by bradykinin, but BDKRB1 is activated by the kinin metabolites such as des-Arg(9)-bradykinin or des-Arg-LBK, both of which are generated by CPN1/CPM-mediated cleavage of the C-terminal arginine residue of bradykinin. BDKRB1 and BDKRB2 mediate arachidonic acid release and prostaglandin (PG) synthesis. The activation of BDKRB1 leads to the elevation of intracellular free calcium (Ca2+) activity by increasing Ca2 entry into the cell. Conversely, BDKRB2 acts primarily to release bound intracellular Ca2+. NOS3, IL6, and PGI2 synthesis cause increased blood vessel permeability and vasodilation.    Highlighted proteins: Protein with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red." EXACT []

