xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Blood vessel sprouting is a process necessary for physiological and pathological angiogenesis. The pathology of this process in cancers is characterized by blood vessel hypersprouting and hyperbranching induced by hyperproduced angiogenic factors as well as by inhibition of negative feedback loops.    Signaling description: Sprouting endothelial cells (ECs) are hierarchically organized into leading 'tip cells' and trailing 'stalk cells' (TCs and SCs). TCs lead and guide the blood vessel sprout, while neighbouring SCs proliferate and form the vascular lumen. The formation of TCs is induced by VEGFA signaling; whereas, DLL4/NOTCH1 signaling path represses the VEGFA/KDR signaling and TC differentiation.    Outcome effects: NOTCH1 signaling in SCs down-regulates the expression of FLT4 and up-regulates FLT1 expression. NOTCH1 activation also induces DLL4 expression in SCs to propagate the DLL4 Notch-mediated lateral inhibition of KDR. NOTCH1-induced NRARP expression enhances WNT signaling in SCs, which maintains EC-EC junctions, promotes proliferation and may augment DLL4 expression via CTNNB1. NRARP also promotes the feedback inhibition of NOTCH1 signaling. The role of DLL4-Notch signaling in suppressing TC specification is not only critical for physiological blood vessel formation but also controls tumor angiogenesis. Tumours are extensively vascularized due to antibody-mediated reduction of DLL4-Notch interactions but vessels are hypoperfused and poorly functional, resulting in tumor hypoxia and decreased growth. Hence, DLL4 is considered to be a promising target for anticancer therapeutics.    Animal data: The majority of the data regarding the role of WNT, DLL4/NOTCH1 in blood vessel sprouting and branching as well as the interplay between VEGFA and DLL4/NOTCH1 was obtained from animal model (mice and zebrafish) experiments."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Blood vessel sprouting is a process necessary for physiological and pathological angiogenesis. The pathology of this process in cancers is characterized by blood vessel hypersprouting and hyperbranching induced by hyperproduced angiogenic factors as well as by inhibition of negative feedback loops.    Signaling description: Sprouting endothelial cells (ECs) are hierarchically organized into leading 'tip cells' and trailing 'stalk cells' (TCs and SCs). TCs lead and guide the blood vessel sprout, while neighbouring SCs proliferate and form the vascular lumen. The formation of TCs is induced by VEGFA signaling; whereas, DLL4/NOTCH1 signaling path represses the VEGFA/KDR signaling and TC differentiation.    Outcome effects: NOTCH1 signaling in SCs down-regulates the expression of FLT4 and up-regulates FLT1 expression. NOTCH1 activation also induces DLL4 expression in SCs to propagate the DLL4 Notch-mediated lateral inhibition of KDR. NOTCH1-induced NRARP expression enhances WNT signaling in SCs, which maintains EC-EC junctions, promotes proliferation and may augment DLL4 expression via CTNNB1. NRARP also promotes the feedback inhibition of NOTCH1 signaling. The role of DLL4-Notch signaling in suppressing TC specification is not only critical for physiological blood vessel formation but also controls tumor angiogenesis. Tumours are extensively vascularized due to antibody-mediated reduction of DLL4-Notch interactions but vessels are hypoperfused and poorly functional, resulting in tumor hypoxia and decreased growth. Hence, DLL4 is considered to be a promising target for anticancer therapeutics.    Animal data: The majority of the data regarding the role of WNT, DLL4/NOTCH1 in blood vessel sprouting and branching as well as the interplay between VEGFA and DLL4/NOTCH1 was obtained from animal model (mice and zebrafish) experiments." EXACT []

