xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: oxLDL/LOX-1 activates signaling pathways that promote angiogenesis and cell proliferation and inhibit apoptosis. Overexpression of LOX-1 was shown in prostate, breast and some other types of cancer.    Signaling description: LOX-1 stimulated by oxLDL activates NFkB. The precise mechanism of this is not clear. The molecular path probably involves NAD(P)H oxidase/ROS signaling.    Outcome effects: NFkB activation leads to overexpression of VEGFA, MMP2, MMP9 (they induce angiogenesis), BCL-2, BCL2A1, TNFAIP3 (inhibit apoptosis) and CCND2 (activates cell proliferation). All these events promote tumor progression.    Animal data: not shown. All the data were obtained on human cancer specimens and cancer cell lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Induction of Angiogenesis\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: oxLDL/LOX-1 activates signaling pathways that promote angiogenesis and cell proliferation and inhibit apoptosis. Overexpression of LOX-1 was shown in prostate, breast and some other types of cancer.    Signaling description: LOX-1 stimulated by oxLDL activates NFkB. The precise mechanism of this is not clear. The molecular path probably involves NAD(P)H oxidase/ROS signaling.    Outcome effects: NFkB activation leads to overexpression of VEGFA, MMP2, MMP9 (they induce angiogenesis), BCL-2, BCL2A1, TNFAIP3 (inhibit apoptosis) and CCND2 (activates cell proliferation). All these events promote tumor progression.    Animal data: not shown. All the data were obtained on human cancer specimens and cancer cell lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Induction of Angiogenesis\" for details." EXACT []

