xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Vasculogenic mimicry (VM) is the formation of microvascular channels by aggressive, metastatic and genetically deregulated tumor cells. Pathology of VM is characterized by the formation of microvascular channels de novo in the absence of endothelial cells (tumor cells line tumor vessels effectively mimicking a true vascular endothelium).    Signaling description: The major signaling pathways upregulated in VM are NOTCH, NODAL/TGFB1-SMAD, EPHA2-PI3K-AKT and PTGER-RAF-MAPK pathways. PTGS2, VEGFA, TWIST1 and CDH5 are up-regulated by hypoxia-induced HIFA1 which promotes the progression of VM. The precise mechanism of this is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: The altered NODAL expression leads to cell dedifferentiation and reprogramming. Activation of MMP2 and MMP14 is mediated by EPHA2-PI3K-AKT and promotes the cleavage of LAMC2 into promigratory fragments. The release of these fragments (molecular messages or signals) into the tumor microenvironment can increase the migration, invasion and, ultimately, vasculogenic mimicry of aggressive tumor cells.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Induction of Angiogenesis\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Vasculogenic mimicry (VM) is the formation of microvascular channels by aggressive, metastatic and genetically deregulated tumor cells. Pathology of VM is characterized by the formation of microvascular channels de novo in the absence of endothelial cells (tumor cells line tumor vessels effectively mimicking a true vascular endothelium).    Signaling description: The major signaling pathways upregulated in VM are NOTCH, NODAL/TGFB1-SMAD, EPHA2-PI3K-AKT and PTGER-RAF-MAPK pathways. PTGS2, VEGFA, TWIST1 and CDH5 are up-regulated by hypoxia-induced HIFA1 which promotes the progression of VM. The precise mechanism of this is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is described on the pathway.    Outcome effects: The altered NODAL expression leads to cell dedifferentiation and reprogramming. Activation of MMP2 and MMP14 is mediated by EPHA2-PI3K-AKT and promotes the cleavage of LAMC2 into promigratory fragments. The release of these fragments (molecular messages or signals) into the tumor microenvironment can increase the migration, invasion and, ultimately, vasculogenic mimicry of aggressive tumor cells.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Induction of Angiogenesis\" for details." EXACT []

