xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Angiogenesis is a biological process wherein new blood vessels are formed from pre-existing vessels. The pathology of angiogenesis in tumors is characterized by the escape from the anti-VEGFA treatment through the induction of multiple parallel signaling cascades.    Signaling description: Altered forms of PDGFB/PDGFRB, FGF/FGFR, EFNA/EPHA2 and HGF/MET cause changes in PI3K-AKT, RAS-MAPK, PLC-PKC-RAF-MAPK signaling paths.    Outcome effects: JUN-FOS, MYC, STAT change their expression due to signaling activation. Their altered expression leads to activation of endothelial cell proliferation, migration and survival.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Induction of Angiogenesis\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Angiogenesis is a biological process wherein new blood vessels are formed from pre-existing vessels. The pathology of angiogenesis in tumors is characterized by the escape from the anti-VEGFA treatment through the induction of multiple parallel signaling cascades.    Signaling description: Altered forms of PDGFB/PDGFRB, FGF/FGFR, EFNA/EPHA2 and HGF/MET cause changes in PI3K-AKT, RAS-MAPK, PLC-PKC-RAF-MAPK signaling paths.    Outcome effects: JUN-FOS, MYC, STAT change their expression due to signaling activation. Their altered expression leads to activation of endothelial cell proliferation, migration and survival.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Induction of Angiogenesis\" for details." EXACT []

