xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Inhibitor of apoptosis proteins (IAPs) are endogenous inhibitors of caspases which can inhibit caspase activity by binding to their active sites, promoting degradation of active caspases or by keeping the caspases away from their substrates. Activated inhibitors of apoptosis inhibit caspases and block programmed cell death in cancer cells.    Signaling description: BIRC2/3 may be activated due to mutations. Other factors leading to hyperexpression of IAPs include activation by HIF1A, STAT3, NFKB1, CTNNB1, ARHGEF3 and loss of suppression from TP53, XAF1 and DIABLO.    Outcome effects: IAPS inactivate caspases 3 and 9 resulting in block of apoptosis.    Animal data: Some of the data were obtained from animal experiments.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Inhibitor of apoptosis proteins (IAPs) are endogenous inhibitors of caspases which can inhibit caspase activity by binding to their active sites, promoting degradation of active caspases or by keeping the caspases away from their substrates. Activated inhibitors of apoptosis inhibit caspases and block programmed cell death in cancer cells.    Signaling description: BIRC2/3 may be activated due to mutations. Other factors leading to hyperexpression of IAPs include activation by HIF1A, STAT3, NFKB1, CTNNB1, ARHGEF3 and loss of suppression from TP53, XAF1 and DIABLO.    Outcome effects: IAPS inactivate caspases 3 and 9 resulting in block of apoptosis.    Animal data: Some of the data were obtained from animal experiments.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details." EXACT []

