xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Caspases are a family of protease enzymes with essential roles in programmed cell death and inflammation. Apoptopic caspases are subcategorized as initiator caspases (CASP2/8/9/10) and executioner caspases (CASP3/6/7).    Signaling description: Impairment of caspase function may be either due to inactivating mutations (shown for CASP1/4/5/6/8/10) or inactivation by inhibitors of apoptosis (BIRCs, XIAP, CFLAR). Impairment of CASP3/9 activation may be also due to inactivating mutations of NTN1 and DCC which directly regulate these caspases.    Outcome effects: Executioner caspases can't cleave cellular components and apoptosis is blocked.     Animal data: some data are obtained in animal experiments.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Caspases are a family of protease enzymes with essential roles in programmed cell death and inflammation. Apoptopic caspases are subcategorized as initiator caspases (CASP2/8/9/10) and executioner caspases (CASP3/6/7).    Signaling description: Impairment of caspase function may be either due to inactivating mutations (shown for CASP1/4/5/6/8/10) or inactivation by inhibitors of apoptosis (BIRCs, XIAP, CFLAR). Impairment of CASP3/9 activation may be also due to inactivating mutations of NTN1 and DCC which directly regulate these caspases.    Outcome effects: Executioner caspases can't cleave cellular components and apoptosis is blocked.     Animal data: some data are obtained in animal experiments.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details." EXACT []

