xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Death receptors and their ligands are key participants in the extrinsic apoptotic pathway. Death receptors include TNFRSF1A, FAS, TNFRSF25, TNFRSF10A/B, TNFRSF21, NGFR. FAS and TNFRSF10A/B act through FADD and activate CASP8/10. TNFRSF1A/21/25 and NGFR use TRADD to activate CASP2 and NFKB.    Signaling description: Death receptor signaling can be impaired in cancers due to multiple mechanisms. For example, FAS, TNFRSF10A/B, TRADD can inactivated by mutations, or NGFR and FADD can be down-regulated. One of the mechanisms of FADD down-regulation is inhibition by HPV16-E6. Overexpressed CFLAR may inhibit CASP8/10. In addition, NFKB signaling may be impaired.    Outcome effects: Caspases are not activated and apoptosis is blocked.    Animal data: Some of the data were obtained from animal experiments.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details.    Description of viral proteins: HPV16-E6 shown in grey is viral protein."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Death receptors and their ligands are key participants in the extrinsic apoptotic pathway. Death receptors include TNFRSF1A, FAS, TNFRSF25, TNFRSF10A/B, TNFRSF21, NGFR. FAS and TNFRSF10A/B act through FADD and activate CASP8/10. TNFRSF1A/21/25 and NGFR use TRADD to activate CASP2 and NFKB.    Signaling description: Death receptor signaling can be impaired in cancers due to multiple mechanisms. For example, FAS, TNFRSF10A/B, TRADD can inactivated by mutations, or NGFR and FADD can be down-regulated. One of the mechanisms of FADD down-regulation is inhibition by HPV16-E6. Overexpressed CFLAR may inhibit CASP8/10. In addition, NFKB signaling may be impaired.    Outcome effects: Caspases are not activated and apoptosis is blocked.    Animal data: Some of the data were obtained from animal experiments.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Resisting to Cell Death\" for details.    Description of viral proteins: HPV16-E6 shown in grey is viral protein." EXACT []

