xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The mammalian target of rapamycin (MTOR), a highly conserved and ubiquitously expressed kinase, is a central regulator of cell growth, proliferation, differentiation and survival. MTOR has a central role in the regulation of tumor cell motility, invasion and cancer metastasis.    Signaling description: MTOR is activated through growth factor receptor/PI3K/AKT1 signaling and functions as two distinct complexes, TORC1 and mTORC2. TORC1 acts through interaction with TORC2 and through PP2A/MAPK/JUN-FOS signaling. TORC2 phosphorylates AKT1, protein kinase PRKCA, controls the activity of CDC42 and RHOA and thereby regulates F-actin polymerization.    Outcome effects: TORC activation induces F-actin polymerization and transcriptional activation of some factors (MMPs, PLAU, SERPINE1) implicated in tumor invasion.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Metastases\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The mammalian target of rapamycin (MTOR), a highly conserved and ubiquitously expressed kinase, is a central regulator of cell growth, proliferation, differentiation and survival. MTOR has a central role in the regulation of tumor cell motility, invasion and cancer metastasis.    Signaling description: MTOR is activated through growth factor receptor/PI3K/AKT1 signaling and functions as two distinct complexes, TORC1 and mTORC2. TORC1 acts through interaction with TORC2 and through PP2A/MAPK/JUN-FOS signaling. TORC2 phosphorylates AKT1, protein kinase PRKCA, controls the activity of CDC42 and RHOA and thereby regulates F-actin polymerization.    Outcome effects: TORC activation induces F-actin polymerization and transcriptional activation of some factors (MMPs, PLAU, SERPINE1) implicated in tumor invasion.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Metastases\" for details." EXACT []

