xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Upon loss of CDH1 function during epithelial to mesenchymal transition, CDH2 is highly expressed; this phenomenon is called \"cadherin switch\".    Signaling description: Several transcription factors such as TWIST1, ZEB1/2, SNAI1/2, FOXC1/2, TCF3 up-regulate CDH2 expression in different types of cancer cells. CDH2 stimulates epithelial to mesenchymal transition through forming a complex with CTNNB1 and PTPN1. CDH2 binds to FGFR1 and activates it, which results in PI3K/AKT1, PLCG/PKC and RAF/MAPK signaling and promotion of cell survival, migration, and invasion. CDH2 also facilitates FGF2 binding to FGFR1, thus, preventing ligand-induced internalization, and, thereby, yields sustained signaling. Cleavage and shedding of the extracellular domain of CDH2 by ADAM10 can neutralize CDH2-mediated cell-cell adhesion and stimulate FGFR1 signaling in neighboring cells. Also, NCAM1 can bind FGFR1 and activate it's signaling in some types of cancer cell. SLC9A3R2 links the CDH2/ CTNNB1 complex to PDGFRB to modulate the actin cytoskeleton and regulate cell motility. CDH2 may also stimulate cell migration through binding to CTNND1 and ARHGAP35.    Outcome effects: CDH2 activation is involved in cancer cell migration, proliferation and survival.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Metastases\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Upon loss of CDH1 function during epithelial to mesenchymal transition, CDH2 is highly expressed; this phenomenon is called \"cadherin switch\".    Signaling description: Several transcription factors such as TWIST1, ZEB1/2, SNAI1/2, FOXC1/2, TCF3 up-regulate CDH2 expression in different types of cancer cells. CDH2 stimulates epithelial to mesenchymal transition through forming a complex with CTNNB1 and PTPN1. CDH2 binds to FGFR1 and activates it, which results in PI3K/AKT1, PLCG/PKC and RAF/MAPK signaling and promotion of cell survival, migration, and invasion. CDH2 also facilitates FGF2 binding to FGFR1, thus, preventing ligand-induced internalization, and, thereby, yields sustained signaling. Cleavage and shedding of the extracellular domain of CDH2 by ADAM10 can neutralize CDH2-mediated cell-cell adhesion and stimulate FGFR1 signaling in neighboring cells. Also, NCAM1 can bind FGFR1 and activate it's signaling in some types of cancer cell. SLC9A3R2 links the CDH2/ CTNNB1 complex to PDGFRB to modulate the actin cytoskeleton and regulate cell motility. CDH2 may also stimulate cell migration through binding to CTNND1 and ARHGAP35.    Outcome effects: CDH2 activation is involved in cancer cell migration, proliferation and survival.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Metastases\" for details." EXACT []

