xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: CFL1 is an actin-binding protein that can regulate actin dynamics in a number of ways. In highly invasive tumor cells, CFL1 has been shown to sever actin filaments thus generating new barbed ends accessible to monomers of G-actin promoting actin polymerization at invasive and locomotory protrusions._x000D __x000D_    Signaling description: RASGRF1 and ARHGAP35 are responsible for RHOC regulation in a spatiotemporal manner. RHOC is activated by RASGRF1 near the periphery of invadopodial cores. RHOC is inactivated by ARHGAP35 within the invadopodial cores, allowing active CFL1 to generate actin barbed ends and promote polymerization. CFL1 activity may be regulated by PLCG1/ PtdIns(3,4)P2 and CTTN. SLC9A1 increases the intracellular pH to disrupt the inhibitory pH-dependent interaction between CTTN and CFL1, allowing active CFL1 to be released. EZR-MSN-RDX complex and TLN1 regulate both SLC9A1 and F-actin spatial localization._x000D__x000D_    Outcome effects: Actin polymerization promotes invadopodia / lamellipodia formation and cancer cell invasion / migration._x000D__x000D_    Highlighted proteins: not shown due to different spatiotemporal expression of key proteins."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: CFL1 is an actin-binding protein that can regulate actin dynamics in a number of ways. In highly invasive tumor cells, CFL1 has been shown to sever actin filaments thus generating new barbed ends accessible to monomers of G-actin promoting actin polymerization at invasive and locomotory protrusions._x000D __x000D_    Signaling description: RASGRF1 and ARHGAP35 are responsible for RHOC regulation in a spatiotemporal manner. RHOC is activated by RASGRF1 near the periphery of invadopodial cores. RHOC is inactivated by ARHGAP35 within the invadopodial cores, allowing active CFL1 to generate actin barbed ends and promote polymerization. CFL1 activity may be regulated by PLCG1/ PtdIns(3,4)P2 and CTTN. SLC9A1 increases the intracellular pH to disrupt the inhibitory pH-dependent interaction between CTTN and CFL1, allowing active CFL1 to be released. EZR-MSN-RDX complex and TLN1 regulate both SLC9A1 and F-actin spatial localization._x000D__x000D_    Outcome effects: Actin polymerization promotes invadopodia / lamellipodia formation and cancer cell invasion / migration._x000D__x000D_    Highlighted proteins: not shown due to different spatiotemporal expression of key proteins." EXACT []

