xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Cancer cell were shown to inhibit adipocyte differentiation. The precise mechanism and the role of this phenomenon in cancer progression is not quite clear yet. Probably, it can facilitate th metastatic spread.    Signaling description: Cancer cells produce a number of ligands, including TNF, IL6, IL11, WNT3A, WNT10B. They were shown to inhibit PPARG and CEBPA, the cardinal transcription factors for adipocyte differentiation. The precise mechanism of this signaling is yet to be determined. TNF most probably activates NFKB and thereby inhibits PPARG. ILs are proposed to act through their classical signaling routes and may inhibit PPARG and CEBPA through STAT5B. WNTs activate CTNNB1 and thereby inhibit PPARG and CEBPA.    Outcome effects: PPARG and CEBPA, the major transcription factors for adipocyte differentiation are inhibited."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Cancer cell were shown to inhibit adipocyte differentiation. The precise mechanism and the role of this phenomenon in cancer progression is not quite clear yet. Probably, it can facilitate th metastatic spread.    Signaling description: Cancer cells produce a number of ligands, including TNF, IL6, IL11, WNT3A, WNT10B. They were shown to inhibit PPARG and CEBPA, the cardinal transcription factors for adipocyte differentiation. The precise mechanism of this signaling is yet to be determined. TNF most probably activates NFKB and thereby inhibits PPARG. ILs are proposed to act through their classical signaling routes and may inhibit PPARG and CEBPA through STAT5B. WNTs activate CTNNB1 and thereby inhibit PPARG and CEBPA.    Outcome effects: PPARG and CEBPA, the major transcription factors for adipocyte differentiation are inhibited." EXACT []

