xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Cancer cachexia is a devastating syndrome that affects around 50-80% of cancer patients leading to substantial weight loss, primarily from loss of skeletal muscle and body fat.    Signaling description: Major signaling pathways activated in cancer cachexia are TNF/NFKB, Activin/MSTN/ACVR/SMAD/FOXO3, IL6/JAK/STAT3/CEBPD. IGF1 and it's signaling are down-regulated in cancer cachexia resulting in down-regulation of MTOR and protein synthesis as well as activation of proteolysis through FOXO1/3. CAST can be inhibited in cancer leading to CALP1/2 activation and apoptosis induction.    Outcome effects: FOXO1/2, NFKB and CEBPD upregulate TRIM63 and FBXO32, the main proteins, responsible for protein degradation in cachexia. FOXO3 also regulates MAP1LC3B and BNIP3 thereby inducing autophagy. CALP1/2 activate CASP3 and induce apoptosis.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Metabolic Reprogramming\" for details. Cachexia-specific decrease of IGF1 is shown on the pathway on an exceptional basis."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Cancer cachexia is a devastating syndrome that affects around 50-80% of cancer patients leading to substantial weight loss, primarily from loss of skeletal muscle and body fat.    Signaling description: Major signaling pathways activated in cancer cachexia are TNF/NFKB, Activin/MSTN/ACVR/SMAD/FOXO3, IL6/JAK/STAT3/CEBPD. IGF1 and it's signaling are down-regulated in cancer cachexia resulting in down-regulation of MTOR and protein synthesis as well as activation of proteolysis through FOXO1/3. CAST can be inhibited in cancer leading to CALP1/2 activation and apoptosis induction.    Outcome effects: FOXO1/2, NFKB and CEBPD upregulate TRIM63 and FBXO32, the main proteins, responsible for protein degradation in cachexia. FOXO3 also regulates MAP1LC3B and BNIP3 thereby inducing autophagy. CALP1/2 activate CASP3 and induce apoptosis.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Metabolic Reprogramming\" for details. Cachexia-specific decrease of IGF1 is shown on the pathway on an exceptional basis." EXACT []

