xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Activating mutations in oncogenes and inactivating mutations in tumor suppressor genes drive metabolic deregulation in cancer cells.    Signaling description: A number of oncogenes mutated in cancer are implicated in deregulation of metabolism in such cells. They include components of the RAS/PI3K/AKT signaling (HRAS, NRAS, KRAS, PIK3CA, AKT1), CTNNB1, MYC, RELA and some other proteins. Tumor suppressor genes implicated in deregulation of metabolism include NF1, PTEN, TSC1/2, STK11, TP53, RB1 and some others.    Outcome effects: Genes responsible for glucose import, glycolysis, amino acid transport and metabolism, as well as, fatty acid and triglyceride synthesis are activated providing metabolites necessary for cancer cell growth, division and spread.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathways \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Metabolic Reprogramming\" for details._    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathways \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer Metabolic Reprogramming\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Activating mutations in oncogenes and inactivating mutations in tumor suppressor genes drive metabolic deregulation in cancer cells.    Signaling description: A number of oncogenes mutated in cancer are implicated in deregulation of metabolism in such cells. They include components of the RAS/PI3K/AKT signaling (HRAS, NRAS, KRAS, PIK3CA, AKT1), CTNNB1, MYC, RELA and some other proteins. Tumor suppressor genes implicated in deregulation of metabolism include NF1, PTEN, TSC1/2, STK11, TP53, RB1 and some others.    Outcome effects: Genes responsible for glucose import, glycolysis, amino acid transport and metabolism, as well as, fatty acid and triglyceride synthesis are activated providing metabolites necessary for cancer cell growth, division and spread.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathways \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer Metabolic Reprogramming\" for details._    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathways \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer Metabolic Reprogramming\" for details." EXACT []

