xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The DREAM complex consists of RBL1 or RBL2, E2F4, E2F5, TFDP and MuvB proteins. DREAM mediates gene repression during G0 and coordinates periodic gene expression with peaks during G1/S and G2/M. Perturbations in DREAM regulation and disassembly of DREAM shifts the balance from quiescence towards proliferation and contribute to increased mitotic gene expression levels frequently observed in cancers. LIN9, LIN54, LIN37, LIN52 and RBBP4 comprise the MuvB core. MuvB also coordinates gene expression during S phase and G2/M through its interactions with MYBL2 and FOXM1.    Signaling description: The assembly and function of DREAM may be impaired via diverse mechanisms. Inactivating mutations in tumor suppressor genes LATS1/2 disrupt the DYRK1A-dependent phosphorylation and activation of MuvB subunit LIN52. RBL2 subunit of DREAM may be inactivated due to either a mutation or impairment of TP53/ CDKN1A/ CCNE1 function. MYBL2 and FOXM1 are overexpressed in a number of tumor types.    Outcome effects: The hyper-activation of MYBL2 and FOXM1 induce expression of G2-specific genes (CCNB1, CDK1 and others) and cancer cell proliferation. BIRC5 expression inhibits apoptosis.    Animal data: The majority of data concerning DREAM complex functioning were obtained in animal models.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The DREAM complex consists of RBL1 or RBL2, E2F4, E2F5, TFDP and MuvB proteins. DREAM mediates gene repression during G0 and coordinates periodic gene expression with peaks during G1/S and G2/M. Perturbations in DREAM regulation and disassembly of DREAM shifts the balance from quiescence towards proliferation and contribute to increased mitotic gene expression levels frequently observed in cancers. LIN9, LIN54, LIN37, LIN52 and RBBP4 comprise the MuvB core. MuvB also coordinates gene expression during S phase and G2/M through its interactions with MYBL2 and FOXM1.    Signaling description: The assembly and function of DREAM may be impaired via diverse mechanisms. Inactivating mutations in tumor suppressor genes LATS1/2 disrupt the DYRK1A-dependent phosphorylation and activation of MuvB subunit LIN52. RBL2 subunit of DREAM may be inactivated due to either a mutation or impairment of TP53/ CDKN1A/ CCNE1 function. MYBL2 and FOXM1 are overexpressed in a number of tumor types.    Outcome effects: The hyper-activation of MYBL2 and FOXM1 induce expression of G2-specific genes (CCNB1, CDK1 and others) and cancer cell proliferation. BIRC5 expression inhibits apoptosis.    Animal data: The majority of data concerning DREAM complex functioning were obtained in animal models.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression/activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details." EXACT []

