xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The G0/G1 cell cycle transition phase is the transition from quiescence to interphase. Mutations in genes responsible for cell cycle transition are common in cancers and cause uncontrolled malignant cell proliferation.    Signaling description: Cyclin D1 (CCND1), cyclin-dependent kinases and E2F1/2/3 transcription factors are activated due to mutations or amplifications. Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors and RB1 are inactivated due to mutations or have decreased expression. Many viral proteins promote oncogenesis through the activation of cell cycle machinery, including the adenovirus protein E1A, polyomavirus large T antigen, KSHV protein ORF72, HPV Protein HPV16-E7.    Outcome effects: Cyclins CCNA1/2, CCNE1/2 and cyclin-dependent kinase 2 (CDK2) are activated promoting uncontrolled cell proliferation.    Animal data: The experimental data were obtained both from animal models and human cancer cell lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Description of viral proteins: E1A, large T antigen, ORF72, HPV16-E7 shown in grey are viral proteins."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The G0/G1 cell cycle transition phase is the transition from quiescence to interphase. Mutations in genes responsible for cell cycle transition are common in cancers and cause uncontrolled malignant cell proliferation.    Signaling description: Cyclin D1 (CCND1), cyclin-dependent kinases and E2F1/2/3 transcription factors are activated due to mutations or amplifications. Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors and RB1 are inactivated due to mutations or have decreased expression. Many viral proteins promote oncogenesis through the activation of cell cycle machinery, including the adenovirus protein E1A, polyomavirus large T antigen, KSHV protein ORF72, HPV Protein HPV16-E7.    Outcome effects: Cyclins CCNA1/2, CCNE1/2 and cyclin-dependent kinase 2 (CDK2) are activated promoting uncontrolled cell proliferation.    Animal data: The experimental data were obtained both from animal models and human cancer cell lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red. Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Description of viral proteins: E1A, large T antigen, ORF72, HPV16-E7 shown in grey are viral proteins." EXACT []

