xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The non-canonical NFKB pathway is an important arm of NFKB signaling that predominantly targets activation of the NFKB2/RELB NFKB complex and may be activated in cancers.    Signaling description: At the core of non-canonical pathway is NFKB-inducing kinase (MAP3K14), which mediates signals from certain TNF receptor family members and positively-regulates CHUK, the downstream kinase, which induces NFKB2 phosphorylation and processing. The basal level of MAP3K14 is low due to the action of the TRAF-BIRC destruction complex, and activation of non-canonical NFKB signaling includes MAP3K14 stabilization. Activating mutations of CD40, MAP3K14, NFKB2 or inactivating mutations of natural inhibitors BIRC2/3 and TRAF3 may activate non-canonical NFKB pathway in cancers. It also may be activated by viral proteins LMP1 (EBV protein) and tax (HTLV-1 protein).    Outcome effects: Constant NFKB activation leads to uncontrolled cellular proliferation and inhibition of apoptosis.    Animal data: Some data were obtained from animal experiments or human cancer lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Description of viral proteins: Tax and LMP1 shown in grey are viral proteins."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The non-canonical NFKB pathway is an important arm of NFKB signaling that predominantly targets activation of the NFKB2/RELB NFKB complex and may be activated in cancers.    Signaling description: At the core of non-canonical pathway is NFKB-inducing kinase (MAP3K14), which mediates signals from certain TNF receptor family members and positively-regulates CHUK, the downstream kinase, which induces NFKB2 phosphorylation and processing. The basal level of MAP3K14 is low due to the action of the TRAF-BIRC destruction complex, and activation of non-canonical NFKB signaling includes MAP3K14 stabilization. Activating mutations of CD40, MAP3K14, NFKB2 or inactivating mutations of natural inhibitors BIRC2/3 and TRAF3 may activate non-canonical NFKB pathway in cancers. It also may be activated by viral proteins LMP1 (EBV protein) and tax (HTLV-1 protein).    Outcome effects: Constant NFKB activation leads to uncontrolled cellular proliferation and inhibition of apoptosis.    Animal data: Some data were obtained from animal experiments or human cancer lines.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression/activity are highlighted in red. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Mutated genes: Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. See pathway \"Genes with Mutations in Cancer-Associated Sustaining of Proliferative Signaling\" for details.    Description of viral proteins: Tax and LMP1 shown in grey are viral proteins." EXACT []

