xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: IL-6, IL-10 and VEGFA are produced at the site of inflammation by immune cells and may act on dendritic cells.    Signaling description: IL-6, IL-10 and VEGFA, through their receptors, induce STAT3 activation via JAK1/2, TYK2 and SRC. STAT3 inhibits the expression of MHC class II molecules, CD80, CD86 and IL12A by dendritic cells.     Outcome effects: MHC class II molecules, CD80, CD86 are required for normal differentiation and maturation of dendritic cells. Thus, when MHC II are downregulated, dendritic cells cannot perform as an antigen-presenting cells and stimulate the anti-tumor effects of CD8+ T cells and natural killer cells.    Animal data: not shown    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Tumor-Promoting Inflammation\" for details.    Mutated proteins: not shown."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: IL-6, IL-10 and VEGFA are produced at the site of inflammation by immune cells and may act on dendritic cells.    Signaling description: IL-6, IL-10 and VEGFA, through their receptors, induce STAT3 activation via JAK1/2, TYK2 and SRC. STAT3 inhibits the expression of MHC class II molecules, CD80, CD86 and IL12A by dendritic cells.     Outcome effects: MHC class II molecules, CD80, CD86 are required for normal differentiation and maturation of dendritic cells. Thus, when MHC II are downregulated, dendritic cells cannot perform as an antigen-presenting cells and stimulate the anti-tumor effects of CD8+ T cells and natural killer cells.    Animal data: not shown    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Tumor-Promoting Inflammation\" for details.    Mutated proteins: not shown." EXACT []

