xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: IL23A and IL10 are produced at the site of inflammation by immune cells and may act on Treg cells.    Signaling description: IL23A and IL10 signaling activates JAK/STAT. Further, STAT3 upregulates the expression of IL10 and TGFB1 and is a major player in inhibition of antitumor function. STAT5A, which controls the expression of FOXP3 and Treg cell fate commitment is also activated.    Outcome effects: IL10 and TGFB1 inhibit Th1/2 and CD8+ T-cells, which normally have antitumor functions. IL-10 inhibits tyrosine phosphorylation of CD28 on Th1 and Th2 cells; thus, blocking PI3K binding to CD28 and further signaling in Th cells (PI3K is not shown on the pathway). TGFB1 directly acts on TGFBR on the surface of Th1/2 and CD8+ T-cell (TGFBR is not shown on the pathway). The antitumor function of these cells is inhibited.    Animal data: not shown    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Tumor-Promoting Inflammation\" for details.    Mutated proteins: not shown."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: IL23A and IL10 are produced at the site of inflammation by immune cells and may act on Treg cells.    Signaling description: IL23A and IL10 signaling activates JAK/STAT. Further, STAT3 upregulates the expression of IL10 and TGFB1 and is a major player in inhibition of antitumor function. STAT5A, which controls the expression of FOXP3 and Treg cell fate commitment is also activated.    Outcome effects: IL10 and TGFB1 inhibit Th1/2 and CD8+ T-cells, which normally have antitumor functions. IL-10 inhibits tyrosine phosphorylation of CD28 on Th1 and Th2 cells; thus, blocking PI3K binding to CD28 and further signaling in Th cells (PI3K is not shown on the pathway). TGFB1 directly acts on TGFBR on the surface of Th1/2 and CD8+ T-cell (TGFBR is not shown on the pathway). The antitumor function of these cells is inhibited.    Animal data: not shown    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Tumor-Promoting Inflammation\" for details.    Mutated proteins: not shown." EXACT []

