xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Endogenous IL12, produced by antigen-presenting cells, is important for host resistance to tumors and is often downregulated in cancers. Overexpression of IL10 and TGFB1 at the sites of inflammation has a major role in downregulation of IL12.    Signaling description: Normally, IL12 acts on IL12R on the surface of Th1-cells and induces JAK/STAT4 activation. STAT4 controls the expression of IFNG that activates antitumor cytotoxic lymphocytes (CD8+T-cells and NK-cells). IL12 may also act directly on CTLs.    Outcome effects: Normally, CTLs produce perforins (PRF1), granzymes (GZMA/B) and FASLG. These molecules induce the killing of the effector cell (tumor cell). When IL12 is downregulated, the mechanisms mentioned above cease to work. Therefore, downregulation of IL12 promotes cancer progression.    Animal data: not shown    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. Proteins with blue highlights have decreased expression / activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Tumor-Promoting Inflammation\" for details.    Mutated proteins: not shown."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Endogenous IL12, produced by antigen-presenting cells, is important for host resistance to tumors and is often downregulated in cancers. Overexpression of IL10 and TGFB1 at the sites of inflammation has a major role in downregulation of IL12.    Signaling description: Normally, IL12 acts on IL12R on the surface of Th1-cells and induces JAK/STAT4 activation. STAT4 controls the expression of IFNG that activates antitumor cytotoxic lymphocytes (CD8+T-cells and NK-cells). IL12 may also act directly on CTLs.    Outcome effects: Normally, CTLs produce perforins (PRF1), granzymes (GZMA/B) and FASLG. These molecules induce the killing of the effector cell (tumor cell). When IL12 is downregulated, the mechanisms mentioned above cease to work. Therefore, downregulation of IL12 promotes cancer progression.    Animal data: not shown    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. Proteins with blue highlights have decreased expression / activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Tumor-Promoting Inflammation\" for details.    Mutated proteins: not shown." EXACT []

