xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Neutrophils can be subdivided into two groups: N1 neutrophils that have anti-tumor activity and N2 neutrophils (tumor-associated neutrophils, TANs) that may have pro-tumor activity. Hypoxia is always present in tumors due to imbalance of oxygen consumption and supply. Hypoxia induces TGFB1 production and inhibits IFNB1 production. These factors are essential for activation of N2 neutrophils.     Signaling description: TGFB1, through TGFBR2/1 receptors, activates SMAD which, in turn, activates STAT3. TGFBR1 also promotes PI3K/AKT1/MTOR signaling with subsequent activation of MYC.IFNB1 normally acts through IFNAR1/2 /JAK1/STAT1 and inhibits MYC. When IFNB1 is downregulated, MYC is activated.     Outcome effects: STAT3 and MYC regulate expression of multiple factors which participate in tumor-promoting inflammation and tumor progression. Specifically, IL6 and ILB1 enhance inflammation. CXCR4 inhibits neutrophil migration. CCL2/5 promote monocyte migration. VEGFA potentiates vasculogenesis. MMP9 promotes cell invasion, metastatic progression and VEGFA activation. ARG1 inhibits CD8+ T-cell possessing anti-tumor functions.    Animal data: not shown    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. Proteins with blue highlight have decreased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Tumor-Promoting Inflammation\" for details.    Mutated proteins: not shown."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Neutrophils can be subdivided into two groups: N1 neutrophils that have anti-tumor activity and N2 neutrophils (tumor-associated neutrophils, TANs) that may have pro-tumor activity. Hypoxia is always present in tumors due to imbalance of oxygen consumption and supply. Hypoxia induces TGFB1 production and inhibits IFNB1 production. These factors are essential for activation of N2 neutrophils.     Signaling description: TGFB1, through TGFBR2/1 receptors, activates SMAD which, in turn, activates STAT3. TGFBR1 also promotes PI3K/AKT1/MTOR signaling with subsequent activation of MYC.IFNB1 normally acts through IFNAR1/2 /JAK1/STAT1 and inhibits MYC. When IFNB1 is downregulated, MYC is activated.     Outcome effects: STAT3 and MYC regulate expression of multiple factors which participate in tumor-promoting inflammation and tumor progression. Specifically, IL6 and ILB1 enhance inflammation. CXCR4 inhibits neutrophil migration. CCL2/5 promote monocyte migration. VEGFA potentiates vasculogenesis. MMP9 promotes cell invasion, metastatic progression and VEGFA activation. ARG1 inhibits CD8+ T-cell possessing anti-tumor functions.    Animal data: not shown    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with red highlights have increased expression/activity. Proteins with blue highlight have decreased expression/activity. See pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Tumor-Promoting Inflammation\" for details.    Mutated proteins: not shown." EXACT []

