xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Tamoxifen is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) that binds to estrogen receptors (ESR1), preventing estrogen from binding.    Signaling description: Tamoxifen inhibits or activates estrogen receptor targets depending on the cell type. In mast cells, tamoxifen suppresses estrogen-induced proliferation and promotes apoptosis which reduces tumor growth, the main effect of the drug. Conversely, in endometrial cells, tamoxifen inhibits apoptosis and induces proliferation resulting in an increased risk of endometrial cancer."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Tamoxifen is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) that binds to estrogen receptors (ESR1), preventing estrogen from binding.    Signaling description: Tamoxifen inhibits or activates estrogen receptor targets depending on the cell type. In mast cells, tamoxifen suppresses estrogen-induced proliferation and promotes apoptosis which reduces tumor growth, the main effect of the drug. Conversely, in endometrial cells, tamoxifen inhibits apoptosis and induces proliferation resulting in an increased risk of endometrial cancer." EXACT []

