xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Bextra (valdecoxib) is a prescription drug used for the treatment of osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, and painful menstruation and menstrual symptoms. It is classified as a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAIDs).    Signaling description: In 2005, Bextra was removed from the U.S. market due to concerns about the possible increased risk of heart infarction and stroke. Valdecoxib is a direct inhibitor of prostaglandin synthase (PTGS2), which produces prostaglandin E2 (PGE2). Prostaglandins are secreted and bound to one out of four receptors depending on the cell type. Particularly, PGE2 is bound to PTGER4, which is essential for the late phase of ischemic preconditioning. In addition, PTGER4-induced cAMP synthesis is associated with increased degradation of AGTR1 mRNA. This receptor mediates angiotensin (AGT)-induced vasoconstriction.    Outcome effects: Bextra treatment, especially while recovering from heart surgery, significantly increases the risk of heart ischemic disease and blood flow aberrations, which in turn increase the risk of brain ischemia."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Bextra (valdecoxib) is a prescription drug used for the treatment of osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, and painful menstruation and menstrual symptoms. It is classified as a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAIDs).    Signaling description: In 2005, Bextra was removed from the U.S. market due to concerns about the possible increased risk of heart infarction and stroke. Valdecoxib is a direct inhibitor of prostaglandin synthase (PTGS2), which produces prostaglandin E2 (PGE2). Prostaglandins are secreted and bound to one out of four receptors depending on the cell type. Particularly, PGE2 is bound to PTGER4, which is essential for the late phase of ischemic preconditioning. In addition, PTGER4-induced cAMP synthesis is associated with increased degradation of AGTR1 mRNA. This receptor mediates angiotensin (AGT)-induced vasoconstriction.    Outcome effects: Bextra treatment, especially while recovering from heart surgery, significantly increases the risk of heart ischemic disease and blood flow aberrations, which in turn increase the risk of brain ischemia." EXACT []

