synonym: "Organ_System: nervous system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Pathological Process"
synonym: "Source: Pathological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Dexamethasone is a potent synthetic member of the glucocorticoid class of steroid hormones and acts as an immunosuppressant and an anti-inflammatory agent.    Signaling description: The stimulation of glucocorticoid receptor NR3C1 by dexamethasone leads to an increased production of DKK1 and SOST, which are well-known antagonists of the WNT signaling pathway required to inhibit protein kinase GSK3B.    Outcome effects: In neurons, GSK3B phosphorylates and inactivates MAPT, which is essential for microtubule formation. Therefore, dexamethasone-induced downregulation of WNT signaling pathway results in the activation of GSK3B and decreased microtubule formation, which is necessary for axon outgrowth."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Dexamethasone is a potent synthetic member of the glucocorticoid class of steroid hormones and acts as an immunosuppressant and an anti-inflammatory agent.    Signaling description: The stimulation of glucocorticoid receptor NR3C1 by dexamethasone leads to an increased production of DKK1 and SOST, which are well-known antagonists of the WNT signaling pathway required to inhibit protein kinase GSK3B.    Outcome effects: In neurons, GSK3B phosphorylates and inactivates MAPT, which is essential for microtubule formation. Therefore, dexamethasone-induced downregulation of WNT signaling pathway results in the activation of GSK3B and decreased microtubule formation, which is necessary for axon outgrowth." EXACT []

