synonym: "Source: Pathological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Dexamethasone is a potent synthetic member of the glucocorticoid class of steroid hormones and acts as an immunosuppressant and an anti-inflammatory agent.    Signaling description: The stimulation of nuclear receptor NR3C1 by glucocorticoids, particularly dexamethasone, activates the transcription of DKK1 and SOST, which are antagonists of the WNT signaling pathway. Thus, dexamethasone-induced toxic effects are generally mediated by the downregulation of WNT signaling pathway.    Outcome effects: The inhibition of WNT pathway and subsequent activation of protein kinase GSK3B in various cell types results in the phosphorylation of insulin receptor substrates, IRS1 and IRS2; and also causes an interruption of the signaling pathway connecting insulin receptor (INSR) to glucose transporter (SLC2A4), which results in the cell becoming insensitive to insulin (INS)."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Dexamethasone is a potent synthetic member of the glucocorticoid class of steroid hormones and acts as an immunosuppressant and an anti-inflammatory agent.    Signaling description: The stimulation of nuclear receptor NR3C1 by glucocorticoids, particularly dexamethasone, activates the transcription of DKK1 and SOST, which are antagonists of the WNT signaling pathway. Thus, dexamethasone-induced toxic effects are generally mediated by the downregulation of WNT signaling pathway.    Outcome effects: The inhibition of WNT pathway and subsequent activation of protein kinase GSK3B in various cell types results in the phosphorylation of insulin receptor substrates, IRS1 and IRS2; and also causes an interruption of the signaling pathway connecting insulin receptor (INSR) to glucose transporter (SLC2A4), which results in the cell becoming insensitive to insulin (INS)." EXACT []

