synonym: "Organ_System: skeletal system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Pathological Process"
synonym: "Source: Pathological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Dexamethasone is a potent synthetic member of the glucocorticoid class of steroid hormones and acts as an immunosuppressant and an anti-inflammatory agent.    Signaling description: Bone formation is controlled by two major signaling pathways that are induced by TGFB and WNT ligands. WNT signaling pathway results in the upregulation of RUNX2 transcription factor, which in turn upregulates the expression of TNF ligand (TNFSF11) and receptor (TNFRSF11B) and prevents the interaction of TNFSF11 with other surface receptors. TGFB signaling pathway leads to the activation of SP7 transcription factor and the expression of another TNF surface receptor (TNFRSF11A), which mediates bone resorption. Normally, both TGFB and WNT signaling pathways are active in osteoblasts and the balance of these pathways is important for an osteoblast to keep its identity.    Outcome effects: The stimulation of glucocorticoid receptor NR3C1 by dexamethasone leads to the upregulation of DKK1 and SOST, which are antagonists of WNT signaling pathway. Therefore, long-term dexamethasone treatment results in chronic WNT signaling pathway insufficiency and osteoporosis due to increased bone resorption."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Dexamethasone is a potent synthetic member of the glucocorticoid class of steroid hormones and acts as an immunosuppressant and an anti-inflammatory agent.    Signaling description: Bone formation is controlled by two major signaling pathways that are induced by TGFB and WNT ligands. WNT signaling pathway results in the upregulation of RUNX2 transcription factor, which in turn upregulates the expression of TNF ligand (TNFSF11) and receptor (TNFRSF11B) and prevents the interaction of TNFSF11 with other surface receptors. TGFB signaling pathway leads to the activation of SP7 transcription factor and the expression of another TNF surface receptor (TNFRSF11A), which mediates bone resorption. Normally, both TGFB and WNT signaling pathways are active in osteoblasts and the balance of these pathways is important for an osteoblast to keep its identity.    Outcome effects: The stimulation of glucocorticoid receptor NR3C1 by dexamethasone leads to the upregulation of DKK1 and SOST, which are antagonists of WNT signaling pathway. Therefore, long-term dexamethasone treatment results in chronic WNT signaling pathway insufficiency and osteoporosis due to increased bone resorption." EXACT []

