xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Ritonavir is an antiretroviral drug from the protease inhibitor class used to treat HIV infection and AIDS.    Signaling description: Ritonavir is capable of directly binding HSP90AA1 in the endoplasmic reticulum and inhibiting its chaperone activity, thus promoting unfolded protein response (UPR). HSP90AA1 normally participates in the folding of PDPK1 kinase, a key player in PIP3/AKT1 signaling pathway, which is essential for signal transduction from INSR to glucose transporter (SLC2A4).    Outcome effects: Thus, the PIP3/AKT1 pathway becomes repressed with the administration of ritonavir causing cells to become insensitive to insulin."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Ritonavir is an antiretroviral drug from the protease inhibitor class used to treat HIV infection and AIDS.    Signaling description: Ritonavir is capable of directly binding HSP90AA1 in the endoplasmic reticulum and inhibiting its chaperone activity, thus promoting unfolded protein response (UPR). HSP90AA1 normally participates in the folding of PDPK1 kinase, a key player in PIP3/AKT1 signaling pathway, which is essential for signal transduction from INSR to glucose transporter (SLC2A4).    Outcome effects: Thus, the PIP3/AKT1 pathway becomes repressed with the administration of ritonavir causing cells to become insensitive to insulin." EXACT []

