xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Clozapine is an atypical antipsychotic agent used in the treatment of schizophrenia.    Signaling description: The use of clozapine requires blood monitoring since it has been shown to cause agranulocytosis, which could prove fatal if not detected early. Agranulocytosis can be a result of hematopoiesis inhibition at the level of cytokines. Granulocyte (CSF3) and granulocyte-macrophage (CSF2) colony-stimulating factors (CSFs) are hematopoietic cytokines produced by monocytes, fibroblasts, and endothelial cells. CSFs are known to have multiple functions in normal, steady-state hematopoiesis such as the regulation of granulocyte production and release from the bone marrow and white blood cell proliferation/differentiation. They are used clinically to repair irradiation and chemotherapy-associated suppression of normal hematopoiesis in cancer patients and to stimulate normal granulocyte development in patients with infantile congenital agranulocytosis.    Outcome effects: Clozapine treatment results in an immune system response and decreased production of CSFs.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Clozapine is an atypical antipsychotic agent used in the treatment of schizophrenia.    Signaling description: The use of clozapine requires blood monitoring since it has been shown to cause agranulocytosis, which could prove fatal if not detected early. Agranulocytosis can be a result of hematopoiesis inhibition at the level of cytokines. Granulocyte (CSF3) and granulocyte-macrophage (CSF2) colony-stimulating factors (CSFs) are hematopoietic cytokines produced by monocytes, fibroblasts, and endothelial cells. CSFs are known to have multiple functions in normal, steady-state hematopoiesis such as the regulation of granulocyte production and release from the bone marrow and white blood cell proliferation/differentiation. They are used clinically to repair irradiation and chemotherapy-associated suppression of normal hematopoiesis in cancer patients and to stimulate normal granulocyte development in patients with infantile congenital agranulocytosis.    Outcome effects: Clozapine treatment results in an immune system response and decreased production of CSFs.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level or activity are highlighted in red, and entities with decreased level or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

