synonym: "Organ_System: digestive system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Pathological Process"
synonym: "Source: Pathological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Cocaine participates in several metabolic pathways in the liver.    Signaling description: One of them (the activation pathway) is catalyzed by the cytochrome P450 superfamily proteins, primarily CYP3A, as well as monooxygenases, which activate the production of N-hydroxynorcocaine and norcocaine nitroxide.    Outcome effects: N-hydroxynorcocaine and norcocaine nitroxide compounds exist in a dynamic equilibrium and both are sources of ROS production, which in turn leads to oxidative stress, mitochondrial damage, and necrosis of hepatocytes. These consequences are the major hepatotoxic effects of cocaine abuse."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Cocaine participates in several metabolic pathways in the liver.    Signaling description: One of them (the activation pathway) is catalyzed by the cytochrome P450 superfamily proteins, primarily CYP3A, as well as monooxygenases, which activate the production of N-hydroxynorcocaine and norcocaine nitroxide.    Outcome effects: N-hydroxynorcocaine and norcocaine nitroxide compounds exist in a dynamic equilibrium and both are sources of ROS production, which in turn leads to oxidative stress, mitochondrial damage, and necrosis of hepatocytes. These consequences are the major hepatotoxic effects of cocaine abuse." EXACT []

