xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Ritonavir is an antiretroviral drug from the protease inhibitor class used to treat HIV infection and AIDS.    Signaling description: Ritonavir is capable of directly binding HSP90AA1 in the endoplasmic reticulum and inhibiting its chaperone activity, thus promoting unfolded protein response (UPR). HSP90AA1 normally participates in NOS3 protein folding that is essential for nitric oxide (NO) production by endothelial cells. NO promotes the relaxation of vascular smooth muscle cells and the same pathway is involved in diastolic relaxation of the heart muscle.    Outcome effects: By inhibiting NOS3 folding and NO production, ritonavir generally impairs vasculature relaxation, particularly myocardial contraction-relaxation cycle, leading to hypertension and hypertrophic cardiomyopathy."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Ritonavir is an antiretroviral drug from the protease inhibitor class used to treat HIV infection and AIDS.    Signaling description: Ritonavir is capable of directly binding HSP90AA1 in the endoplasmic reticulum and inhibiting its chaperone activity, thus promoting unfolded protein response (UPR). HSP90AA1 normally participates in NOS3 protein folding that is essential for nitric oxide (NO) production by endothelial cells. NO promotes the relaxation of vascular smooth muscle cells and the same pathway is involved in diastolic relaxation of the heart muscle.    Outcome effects: By inhibiting NOS3 folding and NO production, ritonavir generally impairs vasculature relaxation, particularly myocardial contraction-relaxation cycle, leading to hypertension and hypertrophic cardiomyopathy." EXACT []

