xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Mast cells are dissipated in connective tissue and stored in the spleen and bone marrow and contain large amounts of cytoplasmic granules including proteoglycans (heparin), histamine, interleukins, and neutral proteases.    Signaling description: Upon activation, mast cells release the contents of granules into surrounding tissue by a process known as degranulation. At the same time, the activation of mast cells can lead to the synthesis of large amounts of mediators without degranulation. In inflammation, mast cells rarely release the entire contents of granules and synthesize de novo large amounts of molecules that control immune system activation and inflammatory response at the site of injury. It has been shown that specific stimuli (or their combinations) can selectively trigger the expression of specific mediators. The issue of selective synthesis of mediators in mast cells requires further research.    Outcome effects: NFSF8 activates human cultured mast cells to release chemokines such as IL8 and CCL2 without histamine and without degranulation."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Mast cells are dissipated in connective tissue and stored in the spleen and bone marrow and contain large amounts of cytoplasmic granules including proteoglycans (heparin), histamine, interleukins, and neutral proteases.    Signaling description: Upon activation, mast cells release the contents of granules into surrounding tissue by a process known as degranulation. At the same time, the activation of mast cells can lead to the synthesis of large amounts of mediators without degranulation. In inflammation, mast cells rarely release the entire contents of granules and synthesize de novo large amounts of molecules that control immune system activation and inflammatory response at the site of injury. It has been shown that specific stimuli (or their combinations) can selectively trigger the expression of specific mediators. The issue of selective synthesis of mediators in mast cells requires further research.    Outcome effects: NFSF8 activates human cultured mast cells to release chemokines such as IL8 and CCL2 without histamine and without degranulation." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-b7e9e463-566d-417d-bb82-c72ea5fafad9
name: Mast-Cell Activation via IgE Signaling
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:hematological_system ! Hematological system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:generic ! Generic
is_a: urn:agi-folder:m ! M
is_a: urn:agi-folder:mast_cells_activation ! Mast cells activation
xref: PS:Description "Mast cells are dissipated in connective tissue and stored in spleen and bone marrow. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Mast cells are dissipated in connective tissue and stored in spleen and bone marrow. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-b7e9e463-566d-417d-bb82-c72ea5fafad9"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-b7e9e463-566d-417d-bb82-c72ea5fafad9" EXACT []
