xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The activation of mast cells can lead to synthesis of large amounts of mediators without degranulation.    Signaling description: In inflammation, mast cells rarely release the entire contents of granules and synthesize de novo large amounts of molecules that control immune system activation and inflammatory response at the site of injury. It has been shown that specific stimuli (or their combinations) can selectively trigger the expression of specific mediators. The issue of selective synthesis of mediators in mast cells requires further research.    Outcome effects: CXCL12 selectively produces IL8 from human mast cells through its receptor, CXCR4."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The activation of mast cells can lead to synthesis of large amounts of mediators without degranulation.    Signaling description: In inflammation, mast cells rarely release the entire contents of granules and synthesize de novo large amounts of molecules that control immune system activation and inflammatory response at the site of injury. It has been shown that specific stimuli (or their combinations) can selectively trigger the expression of specific mediators. The issue of selective synthesis of mediators in mast cells requires further research.    Outcome effects: CXCL12 selectively produces IL8 from human mast cells through its receptor, CXCR4." EXACT []

