xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Ion channels on mucosal endings of vagal afferent neurons in the stomach wall are involved in appetite regulation.    Signaling description: Piezo type mechanosensitive ion channel (PIEZO1) is activated by mechanical stretch. PIEZO1 receptor in concert with TRPV4 transports calcium into the cell. Calcium stimulates acid sensing ion channel (ASIC3), membrane depolarization and more Ca2+influx. Intracellular calcium interacts with and activates GUCA1B which leads to cGMP synthesis and activation of K+ channels. Efflux of K+ leads to membrane depolarization and transmission of the nerve signal by vagal nerve. This leads to activation of gastric motility and eating behavior.    Outcome effects: Ion channels in stomach wall regulate gastrointestinal functions and eating behavior by stimulating of the nerve impulse through vagal nerve."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Ion channels on mucosal endings of vagal afferent neurons in the stomach wall are involved in appetite regulation.    Signaling description: Piezo type mechanosensitive ion channel (PIEZO1) is activated by mechanical stretch. PIEZO1 receptor in concert with TRPV4 transports calcium into the cell. Calcium stimulates acid sensing ion channel (ASIC3), membrane depolarization and more Ca2+influx. Intracellular calcium interacts with and activates GUCA1B which leads to cGMP synthesis and activation of K+ channels. Efflux of K+ leads to membrane depolarization and transmission of the nerve signal by vagal nerve. This leads to activation of gastric motility and eating behavior.    Outcome effects: Ion channels in stomach wall regulate gastrointestinal functions and eating behavior by stimulating of the nerve impulse through vagal nerve." EXACT []

