xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Arrestin-beta 2 (ARRB2) can block the TLR signaling through the activation of fatty acid receptor signaling by several fatty acids (omega-3 etc.).    Signaling description: The activation of fatty acid receptors (FFAR1, FFAR4 and GPR119) by omega-3 fatty acid or oleic acid induces ARRB2 coupling to these receptors. The ARRB2 coupling leads to the internalization of these receptors. ARRB2 can interact with the TAB1 protein, which blocks MAP3K7/TAB1 association. This, in turn disrupts the activation of classic TLR signaling pathway and blocks NF kappa B dependent mechanism of immune system activation and inflammatory response.    Outcome effects: ARRB2 activated by fatty acids blocks TLR signaling and inhibits the inflammatory response.    Animal data: Role of omega-3 in the inhibition of TLR signaling was established in animal models."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Arrestin-beta 2 (ARRB2) can block the TLR signaling through the activation of fatty acid receptor signaling by several fatty acids (omega-3 etc.).    Signaling description: The activation of fatty acid receptors (FFAR1, FFAR4 and GPR119) by omega-3 fatty acid or oleic acid induces ARRB2 coupling to these receptors. The ARRB2 coupling leads to the internalization of these receptors. ARRB2 can interact with the TAB1 protein, which blocks MAP3K7/TAB1 association. This, in turn disrupts the activation of classic TLR signaling pathway and blocks NF kappa B dependent mechanism of immune system activation and inflammatory response.    Outcome effects: ARRB2 activated by fatty acids blocks TLR signaling and inhibits the inflammatory response.    Animal data: Role of omega-3 in the inhibition of TLR signaling was established in animal models." EXACT []

