xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Taste receptor activation is a major part in regulation of eating behavior. These receptors are expressed on the surface of taste bud cells of tongue and connected with gustatory afferent nerve fiber.    Signaling description: Taste 1 receptor heterodimers (T1R2/T1R3 and T1R1/T1R3) and taste 2 receptors (TAS2Rs) are activated by various nutrients. These receptors interact with alpha-gustducin (GNAT3). At the same time, CASR interacts with unidentified G-proteins in taste bud cells. Further, the G-proteins activate PLCB2 inositol (1,4,5)P3 synthesis and intracellular Ca2+ influx. In turn, calcium activates TRPM5 leading to membrane depolarization and action potential initiation which stimulate gustatory afferent nerve fiber and transmission of signal to the brain.    Outcome effects: Activation of taste receptors on taste bud cells stimulate action potential initiation and transmission of nerve impulse."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Taste receptor activation is a major part in regulation of eating behavior. These receptors are expressed on the surface of taste bud cells of tongue and connected with gustatory afferent nerve fiber.    Signaling description: Taste 1 receptor heterodimers (T1R2/T1R3 and T1R1/T1R3) and taste 2 receptors (TAS2Rs) are activated by various nutrients. These receptors interact with alpha-gustducin (GNAT3). At the same time, CASR interacts with unidentified G-proteins in taste bud cells. Further, the G-proteins activate PLCB2 inositol (1,4,5)P3 synthesis and intracellular Ca2+ influx. In turn, calcium activates TRPM5 leading to membrane depolarization and action potential initiation which stimulate gustatory afferent nerve fiber and transmission of signal to the brain.    Outcome effects: Activation of taste receptors on taste bud cells stimulate action potential initiation and transmission of nerve impulse." EXACT []

