synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "generic"
synonym: "Organ_System: generic" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "generic"
synonym: "Tissue: generic" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "generic"
synonym: "Organ: generic" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Leukotriene LTB4 can regulate neutrophil activation via presqualene-PP conversions. Presqualene-PP is a constituent of polymorphonuclear neutrophil (PMN) cell membranes, which lack squalene cyclase and are unable to use it for cholesterol biosynthesis.    Signaling description: LTB4/LTB4R signaling initiates the rapid degradation of presqualene-PP levels, possibly through PKC and PPAPDC2 activation. Presqualene-PP directly inhibits PIK3CG and PLD2. Presqualene-PP degradation, under LTB4, unlocks these regulatory enzymes and leads to neutrophil function activation. Presqualene-PP also interacts with GRB2 and blocks NAD(P)H oxidase assembly for reactive oxygen species (ROS) generation.    Outcome effects: Presqualene-PP levels quickly return to baseline in a time frame that parallels cellular deactivation."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Leukotriene LTB4 can regulate neutrophil activation via presqualene-PP conversions. Presqualene-PP is a constituent of polymorphonuclear neutrophil (PMN) cell membranes, which lack squalene cyclase and are unable to use it for cholesterol biosynthesis.    Signaling description: LTB4/LTB4R signaling initiates the rapid degradation of presqualene-PP levels, possibly through PKC and PPAPDC2 activation. Presqualene-PP directly inhibits PIK3CG and PLD2. Presqualene-PP degradation, under LTB4, unlocks these regulatory enzymes and leads to neutrophil function activation. Presqualene-PP also interacts with GRB2 and blocks NAD(P)H oxidase assembly for reactive oxygen species (ROS) generation.    Outcome effects: Presqualene-PP levels quickly return to baseline in a time frame that parallels cellular deactivation." EXACT []

