synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-c0b5c45a-485c-4d67-b18b-fd58507f1cf1" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "epithelium"
synonym: "Tissue: epithelium" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "pancreas"
synonym: "Organ: pancreas" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "insulin-secreting cell"
synonym: "CellType: insulin-secreting cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "digestive system"
synonym: "Organ_System: digestive system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Pancreatic alpha- and beta-cells of the are involved in the synthesis and secretion of insulin. Somatostatins negatively regulate insulin secretion.    Signaling description: Alpha-cells produce GCG and glucagon-like peptide 1. The activation of SSTR2 (somatostatin receptor 2 (SSTR2)) expressed by alpha cells contributes to the blockade of the cAMP dependent signaling and to the inhibition of glucagon-like peptide 1 secretion. Beta-cells of pancreas synthesize insulin and release it under the influence of glucagon-like peptide 1. Beta-cells express somatostatin receptor 5 (SSTR5), whose activation contributes to the blockade of the cAMP dependent signaling pathway and inhibition of insulin secretion.    Outcome effects: Somatostatins block insulin secretion in the alpha and beta cells of the pancreas."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Pancreatic alpha- and beta-cells of the are involved in the synthesis and secretion of insulin. Somatostatins negatively regulate insulin secretion.    Signaling description: Alpha-cells produce GCG and glucagon-like peptide 1. The activation of SSTR2 (somatostatin receptor 2 (SSTR2)) expressed by alpha cells contributes to the blockade of the cAMP dependent signaling and to the inhibition of glucagon-like peptide 1 secretion. Beta-cells of pancreas synthesize insulin and release it under the influence of glucagon-like peptide 1. Beta-cells express somatostatin receptor 5 (SSTR5), whose activation contributes to the blockade of the cAMP dependent signaling pathway and inhibition of insulin secretion.    Outcome effects: Somatostatins block insulin secretion in the alpha and beta cells of the pancreas." EXACT []

