[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-06a45b6d-1940-4231-be90-a87b2021de57
name: V(D)J Recombination Activation
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:nucleus ! Nucleus
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:immunoglobulins_production ! Immunoglobulins production
is_a: urn:agi-folder:v ! V
xref: PS:Description "V(D)J recombination is an essential characteristic of lymphocyte development and is required for the assembly of V(D)J gene segments of TCR or immunoglobulin (Ig). Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: V(D)J recombination is an essential characteristic of lymphocyte development and is required for the assembly of V(D)J gene segments of TCR or immunoglobulin (Ig). Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-06a45b6d-1940-4231-be90-a87b2021de57"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-06a45b6d-1940-4231-be90-a87b2021de57" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "bone marrow"
synonym: "Tissue: bone marrow" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "B-cell"
synonym: "CellType: B-cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "lymphatic system"
synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The diversification of the antibody repertoire in addition to the variety of T-cell receptor (TCR) forms are obtained by the largely random recombination of variable (V), diversity (D), and joining (J) gene segments on the heavy chain locus and V and J segments on the light chain locus, immunoglobulin, and TCR genes. V(D)J recombination provides the versatility that is essential to normal immune functioning.A    Signaling description: During the process of V(D)J recombination, rearrangement is initiated by double-stranded breaks (DSBs) in the 12 and 23 bp spaced recombination signal sequences (RSS). DSBs are initiated by RAG1 and RAG2 proteins. The activation of transcription of RAG1 and RAG2 genes is up- and downregulated at each B-cell or T-cell stage. Interleukin 7 (IL7) is the main activator of RAG1 and RAG2 expression, but other interleukins that induce T- and B-cell development are also necessary. FLT3 signaling strongly activates STAT5 and PAX5-mediated RAG1 and RAG2 expression during B-cell development. In addition, CD40 and related intracytoplasmic signaling implicate adaptor proteins (such as BLNK), phospholipase activation (PLCG2), and increased concentration of secondary messengers (calcium). These pathways recruit transcription factors involved in the activation of RAG expression.    Outcome effects: V(D)J recombination is an essential characteristic of lymphocyte development and is required for the assembly of V(D)J gene segments of TCR or immunoglobulin (Ig) in somatic cell lines. These genes encode a unique receptor or Ig structure on each T or B-lymphocyte, respectively."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The diversification of the antibody repertoire in addition to the variety of T-cell receptor (TCR) forms are obtained by the largely random recombination of variable (V), diversity (D), and joining (J) gene segments on the heavy chain locus and V and J segments on the light chain locus, immunoglobulin, and TCR genes. V(D)J recombination provides the versatility that is essential to normal immune functioning.A    Signaling description: During the process of V(D)J recombination, rearrangement is initiated by double-stranded breaks (DSBs) in the 12 and 23 bp spaced recombination signal sequences (RSS). DSBs are initiated by RAG1 and RAG2 proteins. The activation of transcription of RAG1 and RAG2 genes is up- and downregulated at each B-cell or T-cell stage. Interleukin 7 (IL7) is the main activator of RAG1 and RAG2 expression, but other interleukins that induce T- and B-cell development are also necessary. FLT3 signaling strongly activates STAT5 and PAX5-mediated RAG1 and RAG2 expression during B-cell development. In addition, CD40 and related intracytoplasmic signaling implicate adaptor proteins (such as BLNK), phospholipase activation (PLCG2), and increased concentration of secondary messengers (calcium). These pathways recruit transcription factors involved in the activation of RAG expression.    Outcome effects: V(D)J recombination is an essential characteristic of lymphocyte development and is required for the assembly of V(D)J gene segments of TCR or immunoglobulin (Ig) in somatic cell lines. These genes encode a unique receptor or Ig structure on each T or B-lymphocyte, respectively." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-fe0c40be-f55d-4f75-a666-bb03dbf5f0ed
name: Immunoglobulin Class-Switch Recombination Activation
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:nucleus ! Nucleus
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:immunoglobulins_production ! Immunoglobulins production
is_a: urn:agi-folder:i ! I
xref: PS:Description "Class-switch recombination (CSR) is a biological mechanism that changes the Ig class expressed on B cells from IgM to one of the other classes (IgG, IgE, or IgA). Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Class-switch recombination (CSR) is a biological mechanism that changes the Ig class expressed on B cells from IgM to one of the other classes (IgG, IgE, or IgA). Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-fe0c40be-f55d-4f75-a666-bb03dbf5f0ed"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-fe0c40be-f55d-4f75-a666-bb03dbf5f0ed" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "bone marrow"
synonym: "Tissue: bone marrow" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "B-cell"
synonym: "CellType: B-cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "lymphatic system"
synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Class-switch recombination (CSR), also known as immunoglobulin class switching, isotype switching or isotypic commutation, is a biological mechanism that changes the Ig class expressed on B-cells from IgM to one of the other classes (IgG, IgE, or IgA).    Signaling description: During the process of Ig class switching, the constant region of the antibody heavy chain is altered, but the variable region stays constant, so antigen specificity is not affected. The antibody retains the affinity for the same antigens, but can interact with different effector molecules. CSR of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus requires activation-induced cytidine deaminase (AICDA). This enzyme catalyzes the deamination of deoxycytosines to deoxyuracils, thereby initiating immunoglobulin CSR, somatic hypermutation, and gene conversion. The major transcription factors involved in AICDA expression are STAT6, HOXC4, and NF-kB, which require 4 effectors including IL13, IL4, CD40LG, and TNFSF13."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Class-switch recombination (CSR), also known as immunoglobulin class switching, isotype switching or isotypic commutation, is a biological mechanism that changes the Ig class expressed on B-cells from IgM to one of the other classes (IgG, IgE, or IgA).    Signaling description: During the process of Ig class switching, the constant region of the antibody heavy chain is altered, but the variable region stays constant, so antigen specificity is not affected. The antibody retains the affinity for the same antigens, but can interact with different effector molecules. CSR of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus requires activation-induced cytidine deaminase (AICDA). This enzyme catalyzes the deamination of deoxycytosines to deoxyuracils, thereby initiating immunoglobulin CSR, somatic hypermutation, and gene conversion. The major transcription factors involved in AICDA expression are STAT6, HOXC4, and NF-kB, which require 4 effectors including IL13, IL4, CD40LG, and TNFSF13." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-57edbd9f-7185-4ad6-8cf5-3b651417004e
name: Immunoglobulin Class-Switch Recombination via Classical non-Homologous End-Joining
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:nucleus ! Nucleus
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:immunoglobulins_production ! Immunoglobulins production
is_a: urn:agi-folder:i ! I
xref: PS:Description "Class-switch recombination (CSR) of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus is essential for the maturation of the antibody response. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Class-switch recombination (CSR) of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus is essential for the maturation of the antibody response. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-57edbd9f-7185-4ad6-8cf5-3b651417004e"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-57edbd9f-7185-4ad6-8cf5-3b651417004e" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "bone marrow"
synonym: "Tissue: bone marrow" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "B-cell"
synonym: "CellType: B-cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "lymphatic system"
synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Class-switch recombination (CSR) of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus is essential for the maturation of the antibody response. Classical non-homologous end-joining (C-NHEJ) is a DNA repair process that joins non-homologous DNA ends together using the core components including DNA-PK complex (XRCC6, XRCC5, and PRKDC), Artemis, XRCC4, and DNA ligase IV.    Signaling description: The MRN complex, which includes MRE11A, RAD50, and NBS1, is an early sensor of activation-induced cytidine deaminase (AICDA)-induced double-strand breaks (DSBs). The MRN complex localizes to damage sites where it recruits and activates serine-protein kinase ATM.    Outcome effects: ATM phosphorylates NBS1 in the MRN complex and downstream DNA damage response proteins, thereby strengthening the DNA damage response. ATM also activates the phosphorylation of histone H2AFX and p53-binding protein 1 (TP53BP1) that mediate the synapsis of upstream and downstream DSBs."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Class-switch recombination (CSR) of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus is essential for the maturation of the antibody response. Classical non-homologous end-joining (C-NHEJ) is a DNA repair process that joins non-homologous DNA ends together using the core components including DNA-PK complex (XRCC6, XRCC5, and PRKDC), Artemis, XRCC4, and DNA ligase IV.    Signaling description: The MRN complex, which includes MRE11A, RAD50, and NBS1, is an early sensor of activation-induced cytidine deaminase (AICDA)-induced double-strand breaks (DSBs). The MRN complex localizes to damage sites where it recruits and activates serine-protein kinase ATM.    Outcome effects: ATM phosphorylates NBS1 in the MRN complex and downstream DNA damage response proteins, thereby strengthening the DNA damage response. ATM also activates the phosphorylation of histone H2AFX and p53-binding protein 1 (TP53BP1) that mediate the synapsis of upstream and downstream DSBs." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-abbc0a42-d89f-44cd-9b09-0d26cb98af99
name: Immunoglobulin Genes Transcriptional Activation
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:nucleus ! Nucleus
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:immunoglobulins_production ! Immunoglobulins production
is_a: urn:agi-folder:i ! I
xref: PS:Description "There are several mechanisms of transcriptional activation of immunoglobulin genes following the different types of rearrangement such as V(D)J recombination or immunoglobulin class-switch recombination. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: There are several mechanisms of transcriptional activation of immunoglobulin genes following the different types of rearrangement such as V(D)J recombination or immunoglobulin class-switch recombination. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-abbc0a42-d89f-44cd-9b09-0d26cb98af99"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-abbc0a42-d89f-44cd-9b09-0d26cb98af99" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "bone marrow"
synonym: "Tissue: bone marrow" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "B-cell"
synonym: "CellType: B-cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "lymphatic system"
synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: There are several mechanisms of transcriptional activation of immunoglobulin genes following different types of rearrangement processes, such as V(D)J recombination or immunoglobulin class-switch recombination.    Signaling description: The key transcription factors that bind to sequences in the promoters of immunoglobulin genes are POU2AF1 (BOB-1), POU2F2 (OCT-2), and SPI1 (PU.1). The activation of these transcription factors is initiated by the binding of interleukin 21 receptor (IL21R) and interleukin 13 receptor, alpha 1 (IL13RA1) to their ligands (IL21 and IL13). The suppression of immunoglobulin gene transcription occurs through the NOTCH1 receptor."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: There are several mechanisms of transcriptional activation of immunoglobulin genes following different types of rearrangement processes, such as V(D)J recombination or immunoglobulin class-switch recombination.    Signaling description: The key transcription factors that bind to sequences in the promoters of immunoglobulin genes are POU2AF1 (BOB-1), POU2F2 (OCT-2), and SPI1 (PU.1). The activation of these transcription factors is initiated by the binding of interleukin 21 receptor (IL21R) and interleukin 13 receptor, alpha 1 (IL13RA1) to their ligands (IL21 and IL13). The suppression of immunoglobulin gene transcription occurs through the NOTCH1 receptor." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-fccbcc57-ddc3-497e-ae2e-282380ad69e6
name: V(D)J Recombination
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:nucleus ! Nucleus
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:immunoglobulins_production ! Immunoglobulins production
is_a: urn:agi-folder:v ! V
xref: PS:Description "V(D)J recombination is an essential characteristic of lymphocyte development and is required for the assembly of V(D)J gene segments of TCR or immunoglobulin (Ig). Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: V(D)J recombination is an essential characteristic of lymphocyte development and is required for the assembly of V(D)J gene segments of TCR or immunoglobulin (Ig). Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-fccbcc57-ddc3-497e-ae2e-282380ad69e6"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-fccbcc57-ddc3-497e-ae2e-282380ad69e6" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "bone marrow"
synonym: "Tissue: bone marrow" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "B-cell"
synonym: "CellType: B-cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "lymphatic system"
synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The diversification of the antibody repertoire in addition to the variety of T-cell receptor (TCR) forms are obtained by the largely random recombination of variable (V), diversity (D), and joining (J) gene segments on the heavy chain locus and V and J segments on the light chain locus, immunoglobulin, and TCR genes.    Signaling description: V(D)J recombination occurs in developing B-cells and T-cells in the bone marrow under the regulation of recombination activating gene (RAG) 1 and RAG2 proteins. The RAG protein complex binds to 12 and 23 bp spaced recombination signal sequences (RSS). The protein complexes bind to each other and bring the segments to be joined together. The DNA is cleaved to create hairpin structures at the ends of the immunoglobulin or TCR gene segments. The DNA-PK complex (XRCC6, XRCC5, and PRKDC) bind to the hairpins and the cleaved RSS ends. The DNA hairpins are cleaved at random sites, and additional bases may be added by terminal deoxynucleotidyltransferase (DNTT) or subtracted by exonuclease to generate imprecise ends. DNA ligase IV (LIG4) and XRCC4 join the ends of the gene segments to form the coding joint and RSS ends.    Outcome effects: V(D)J recombination is an essential characteristic of lymphocyte development and is required for the assembly of V(D)J gene segments of TCR or immunoglobulin (Ig) in somatic cell lines. These genes encode a unique receptor or Ig structure on each T or B-lymphocyte, respectively."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The diversification of the antibody repertoire in addition to the variety of T-cell receptor (TCR) forms are obtained by the largely random recombination of variable (V), diversity (D), and joining (J) gene segments on the heavy chain locus and V and J segments on the light chain locus, immunoglobulin, and TCR genes.    Signaling description: V(D)J recombination occurs in developing B-cells and T-cells in the bone marrow under the regulation of recombination activating gene (RAG) 1 and RAG2 proteins. The RAG protein complex binds to 12 and 23 bp spaced recombination signal sequences (RSS). The protein complexes bind to each other and bring the segments to be joined together. The DNA is cleaved to create hairpin structures at the ends of the immunoglobulin or TCR gene segments. The DNA-PK complex (XRCC6, XRCC5, and PRKDC) bind to the hairpins and the cleaved RSS ends. The DNA hairpins are cleaved at random sites, and additional bases may be added by terminal deoxynucleotidyltransferase (DNTT) or subtracted by exonuclease to generate imprecise ends. DNA ligase IV (LIG4) and XRCC4 join the ends of the gene segments to form the coding joint and RSS ends.    Outcome effects: V(D)J recombination is an essential characteristic of lymphocyte development and is required for the assembly of V(D)J gene segments of TCR or immunoglobulin (Ig) in somatic cell lines. These genes encode a unique receptor or Ig structure on each T or B-lymphocyte, respectively." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-31e0b976-6e72-4c00-a89d-d611f7863b25
name: Immunoglobulin Class-Switch Recombination via Alternative End-Joining
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:nucleus ! Nucleus
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:immunoglobulins_production ! Immunoglobulins production
is_a: urn:agi-folder:i ! I
xref: PS:Description "Class-switch recombination (CSR) of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus is essential for the maturation of the antibody response. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Class-switch recombination (CSR) of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus is essential for the maturation of the antibody response. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: E. Klimov ORCID:0000-0003-2674-5783" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-31e0b976-6e72-4c00-a89d-d611f7863b25"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-31e0b976-6e72-4c00-a89d-d611f7863b25" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "bone marrow"
synonym: "Tissue: bone marrow" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "B-cell"
synonym: "CellType: B-cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "lymphatic system"
synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Class-switch recombination (CSR) of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus is essential for the maturation of the antibody response. Alternative end-joining (A-EJ) is a double-strand break (DSB) repair process that occurs in the absence of certain classical non-homologous end-joining components.    Signaling description: Presumably, A-EJ depends on the MRN complex, RBBP8, and/or PARP1 to produce a microhomology region between the ends of DSBs for end-joining. The ligation of the DSB ends by one or more DNA ligases, which have yet to be identified, yields S-S junctions that show more extensive microhomology than those formed in classical non-homologous end-joining.    Outcome effects: A-EJ is frequently associated with chromosomal translocations and is influenced by the expression of TP53BP1, which protects DSB ends from resection for A-EJ and by the presence of Ku70 (XRCC6) and Ku86 (XRCC5) which inhibit RBBP8."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Class-switch recombination (CSR) of the immunoglobulin heavy chain locus is essential for the maturation of the antibody response. Alternative end-joining (A-EJ) is a double-strand break (DSB) repair process that occurs in the absence of certain classical non-homologous end-joining components.    Signaling description: Presumably, A-EJ depends on the MRN complex, RBBP8, and/or PARP1 to produce a microhomology region between the ends of DSBs for end-joining. The ligation of the DSB ends by one or more DNA ligases, which have yet to be identified, yields S-S junctions that show more extensive microhomology than those formed in classical non-homologous end-joining.    Outcome effects: A-EJ is frequently associated with chromosomal translocations and is influenced by the expression of TP53BP1, which protects DSB ends from resection for A-EJ and by the presence of Ku70 (XRCC6) and Ku86 (XRCC5) which inhibit RBBP8." EXACT []

