xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC) is a prohormone synthesized in the adenohypophysis. POMC is cleaved to give multiple peptide hormones.    Signaling description: Adenohypophysial cells respond to corticotropin releasing hormone (CRH) which binds to CRHR1 and mediates ADCY/cAMP/PKA/CREB1 signaling. CREB1 promotes NR4A2/ NR4A1, the essential POMC transcription factors. PCSK2 and PCSK1 cleave POMC into ACTH (adrenocorticotropic hormone), beta-endorphin, beta-lipotropin, alpha-MSH, beta-MSH and gamma-MSH (alpha, beta and gamma melanocyte stimulating hormones). The described mechanism of molecular signaling is known in general terms and is depicted on the pathway.    Outcome effects: POMC is the source of several important biologically active substances."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC) is a prohormone synthesized in the adenohypophysis. POMC is cleaved to give multiple peptide hormones.    Signaling description: Adenohypophysial cells respond to corticotropin releasing hormone (CRH) which binds to CRHR1 and mediates ADCY/cAMP/PKA/CREB1 signaling. CREB1 promotes NR4A2/ NR4A1, the essential POMC transcription factors. PCSK2 and PCSK1 cleave POMC into ACTH (adrenocorticotropic hormone), beta-endorphin, beta-lipotropin, alpha-MSH, beta-MSH and gamma-MSH (alpha, beta and gamma melanocyte stimulating hormones). The described mechanism of molecular signaling is known in general terms and is depicted on the pathway.    Outcome effects: POMC is the source of several important biologically active substances." EXACT []

