xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Natural killer (NK) cells can specifically destroy infected and transformed cells. The activation of NK cells depends on stimulatory and inhibitory receptors whose type and copy number vary from cell to cell. NK cell stimulatory receptors with immunoreceptor tyrosine-based activation motif (ITAM) are the strongest NK cell activator receptors.    Signaling description: The ITAM motif of NK cell activator receptors binds to cytoplasmic adaptor, TYROBP and becomes phosphorylated. The phosphorylation of the ITAM motif of NK cell activator receptors induces the recruitment of the kinases, SYK and ZAP70. SYK and ZAP70 signaling results in the release of calcium and activation of JUN/FOS and NFATC2 transcription factors. NK cell activator receptors such as FCGR3B and FCGR3A induce the phosphorylation of VAV2 and VAV3, resulting in the actin-dependent clustering of activator receptors and their recruitment to lipid rafts. This leads to additional VAV phosphorylation, inducing a positive feedback loop which ultimately results in NK cell cytotoxicity.    Outcome effects: Finally, the two main NK cell-mediated responses are activated including the transcription of FAS receptor ligands and the formation of immunological synapses with granules of perforins (PRF1) and granzymes. FAS, PRF1, and granzymes lead to the death of target cells."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Natural killer (NK) cells can specifically destroy infected and transformed cells. The activation of NK cells depends on stimulatory and inhibitory receptors whose type and copy number vary from cell to cell. NK cell stimulatory receptors with immunoreceptor tyrosine-based activation motif (ITAM) are the strongest NK cell activator receptors.    Signaling description: The ITAM motif of NK cell activator receptors binds to cytoplasmic adaptor, TYROBP and becomes phosphorylated. The phosphorylation of the ITAM motif of NK cell activator receptors induces the recruitment of the kinases, SYK and ZAP70. SYK and ZAP70 signaling results in the release of calcium and activation of JUN/FOS and NFATC2 transcription factors. NK cell activator receptors such as FCGR3B and FCGR3A induce the phosphorylation of VAV2 and VAV3, resulting in the actin-dependent clustering of activator receptors and their recruitment to lipid rafts. This leads to additional VAV phosphorylation, inducing a positive feedback loop which ultimately results in NK cell cytotoxicity.    Outcome effects: Finally, the two main NK cell-mediated responses are activated including the transcription of FAS receptor ligands and the formation of immunological synapses with granules of perforins (PRF1) and granzymes. FAS, PRF1, and granzymes lead to the death of target cells." EXACT []

