xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Natural killer (NK) cells can specifically destroy infected and transformed cells. The activation of NK cells depends on stimulatory and inhibitory receptors whose type and copy number vary from cell to cell.    Signaling description: NK cell stimulatory receptors with ITSM motifs (CD244-related receptors) induce the phosphorylation of VAV1, resulting in the actin-dependent clustering of activator receptors and their recruitment to lipid rafts. This leads to additional VAV1 phosphorylation, inducing a positive feedback loop which ultimately results in NK cell cytotoxicity. The ITSM motifs of CD244-related receptors are phosphorylated by SH2D1A-associated protein and then recruit the adapters, FYN and LAT.    Outcome effects: FYN and LAT activate two main NK cell-mediated responses including the transcription of FAS receptor ligands and the formation of immunological synapses with granules of perforins (PRF1) and granzymes. FAS, PRF1, and granzymes lead to the death of target cells."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Natural killer (NK) cells can specifically destroy infected and transformed cells. The activation of NK cells depends on stimulatory and inhibitory receptors whose type and copy number vary from cell to cell.    Signaling description: NK cell stimulatory receptors with ITSM motifs (CD244-related receptors) induce the phosphorylation of VAV1, resulting in the actin-dependent clustering of activator receptors and their recruitment to lipid rafts. This leads to additional VAV1 phosphorylation, inducing a positive feedback loop which ultimately results in NK cell cytotoxicity. The ITSM motifs of CD244-related receptors are phosphorylated by SH2D1A-associated protein and then recruit the adapters, FYN and LAT.    Outcome effects: FYN and LAT activate two main NK cell-mediated responses including the transcription of FAS receptor ligands and the formation of immunological synapses with granules of perforins (PRF1) and granzymes. FAS, PRF1, and granzymes lead to the death of target cells." EXACT []

