xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Natural killer (NK) cells can specifically destroy infected and transformed cells. The activation of NK cells depends on stimulatory and inhibitory receptors, whose type and copy number vary from cell to cell.    Signaling description: The two major NK cell-mediated responses include the transcription of FAS receptor ligands and the formation of immunological synapses with granules of perforins (PRF1) and granzymes. Along with a positive feedback loop, NK cell activator receptors act through the phosphorylation of VAVs and actin organization. A number of coactivating receptors have been implicated in NK cell activation. Non-ITAM or ITSM motif stimulatory receptors such as CD226 receptor alone are not sufficient to induce activation of NK cells; however the engagement of specific pairwise combinations of receptors can induce synergistic intracellular calcium mobilization as well as degranulation and cytokine production.    Outcome effects: CD2 receptor can rapidly activate lipid raft formation and actin-dependent clustering of activator receptors. The adhesion receptors including ITGA5, ITGA4, and ITGB1 may also contribute to NK cell activation. CD226 and ITGB2 can rapidly induce signals for the activation of ITGB2 thus promoting adhesion between NK cells and a target cell."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Natural killer (NK) cells can specifically destroy infected and transformed cells. The activation of NK cells depends on stimulatory and inhibitory receptors, whose type and copy number vary from cell to cell.    Signaling description: The two major NK cell-mediated responses include the transcription of FAS receptor ligands and the formation of immunological synapses with granules of perforins (PRF1) and granzymes. Along with a positive feedback loop, NK cell activator receptors act through the phosphorylation of VAVs and actin organization. A number of coactivating receptors have been implicated in NK cell activation. Non-ITAM or ITSM motif stimulatory receptors such as CD226 receptor alone are not sufficient to induce activation of NK cells; however the engagement of specific pairwise combinations of receptors can induce synergistic intracellular calcium mobilization as well as degranulation and cytokine production.    Outcome effects: CD2 receptor can rapidly activate lipid raft formation and actin-dependent clustering of activator receptors. The adhesion receptors including ITGA5, ITGA4, and ITGB1 may also contribute to NK cell activation. CD226 and ITGB2 can rapidly induce signals for the activation of ITGB2 thus promoting adhesion between NK cells and a target cell." EXACT []

