[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-efcc1206-fd86-4dd3-8597-f26d529a6597
name: Testicular AMH Production
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:t ! T
is_a: urn:agi-folder:reproductive_biology ! Reproductive biology
is_a: urn:agi-folder:steroid_hormones ! Steroid hormones
is_a: urn:agi-folder:reproductive_system ! Reproductive system
xref: PS:Description "Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:PMID "21693691"
xref: PS:PMID "18713818"
synonym: "PMID: 21693691" EXACT []
synonym: "PMID: 18713818" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "S. Sozin www.researchgate.net/profile/Sergey-Sozin"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: S. Sozin www.researchgate.net/profile/Sergey-Sozin" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-efcc1206-fd86-4dd3-8597-f26d529a6597"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-efcc1206-fd86-4dd3-8597-f26d529a6597" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "testis"
synonym: "Organ: testis" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "reproductive system"
synonym: "Organ_System: reproductive system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Testosterone acting through the androgen receptor (AR), is a potent inhibitor of AMH production. In the normal fetus and infant the lack of AR expression results in high AMH production by Sertoli cells. During childhood, there is a physiologic hypogonadotrophic state resulting in very low testosterone level; AMH level remains high, but somewhat lower probably due to the lack of FSH stimulus. In normal puberty testosterone prevails over FSH, resulting in AMH inhibition.    Signaling description: Follicle-stimulation hormone (FSH) binds to the FSH receptor (FSHR) present on Sertoli cell membrane, and triggers protein G-mediated activation of adenylyl cyclase (ADCY), resulting in an increase of cAMP levels and activation of protein kinase A (PKA). PKA induces Sertoli cell proliferation and also nuclear translocation of transcription factors NFkB, SOX9, NR5A1, GATA4 and WT1 which bind to specific response elements on the AMH promoter, enhancing AMH expression."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Testosterone acting through the androgen receptor (AR), is a potent inhibitor of AMH production. In the normal fetus and infant the lack of AR expression results in high AMH production by Sertoli cells. During childhood, there is a physiologic hypogonadotrophic state resulting in very low testosterone level; AMH level remains high, but somewhat lower probably due to the lack of FSH stimulus. In normal puberty testosterone prevails over FSH, resulting in AMH inhibition.    Signaling description: Follicle-stimulation hormone (FSH) binds to the FSH receptor (FSHR) present on Sertoli cell membrane, and triggers protein G-mediated activation of adenylyl cyclase (ADCY), resulting in an increase of cAMP levels and activation of protein kinase A (PKA). PKA induces Sertoli cell proliferation and also nuclear translocation of transcription factors NFkB, SOX9, NR5A1, GATA4 and WT1 which bind to specific response elements on the AMH promoter, enhancing AMH expression." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-da6b55a7-ecea-4696-b055-215b64245749
name: Activin, Inhibin and Follistatin Action on Pituitary Gland
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:reproductive_biology ! Reproductive biology
is_a: urn:agi-folder:a ! A
is_a: urn:agi-folder:reproductive_system ! Reproductive system
xref: PS:Description "Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:PMID "15451565"
xref: PS:PMID "16885530"
synonym: "PMID: 15451565" EXACT []
synonym: "PMID: 16885530" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "S. Sozin www.researchgate.net/profile/Sergey-Sozin"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: S. Sozin www.researchgate.net/profile/Sergey-Sozin" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-da6b55a7-ecea-4696-b055-215b64245749"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-da6b55a7-ecea-4696-b055-215b64245749" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "pituitary gland"
synonym: "Organ: pituitary gland" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "reproductive system"
synonym: "Organ_System: reproductive system" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "pituitary cell"
synonym: "CellType: pituitary cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Activins and inhibins are produced in the ovary. Activins and inhibins are structurally related complexes. Activin is a homodimer of two b subunits and antagonizes the effect of inhibin. Inhibin consists of alpha (a) and beta (b) subunits. The b-subunit is of two types, A and B. Thus there are two forms of inhibin: inhibin A (a-bA) and inhibin B (a-bB).The genes INHA, INHBA and INHBB encode for inhibin a, inhibin bA and inhibin bB subunits, respectively.     Outcome effects: Activins and inhibins play important role in regulating ovarian function either as modulators of pituitary FSH synthesis or as a paracrine factors in the ovary. Follistatin which is produced locally in pituitary gland blocks activin action."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Activins and inhibins are produced in the ovary. Activins and inhibins are structurally related complexes. Activin is a homodimer of two b subunits and antagonizes the effect of inhibin. Inhibin consists of alpha (a) and beta (b) subunits. The b-subunit is of two types, A and B. Thus there are two forms of inhibin: inhibin A (a-bA) and inhibin B (a-bB).The genes INHA, INHBA and INHBB encode for inhibin a, inhibin bA and inhibin bB subunits, respectively.     Outcome effects: Activins and inhibins play important role in regulating ovarian function either as modulators of pituitary FSH synthesis or as a paracrine factors in the ovary. Follistatin which is produced locally in pituitary gland blocks activin action." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-5c95bae0-2659-43e0-a8ce-b90f7b31e5d9
name: Luteinizing Hormone in Oocyte Meiotic Resumption
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:reproductive_biology ! Reproductive biology
is_a: urn:agi-folder:reproductive_system ! Reproductive system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:l ! L
xref: PS:Description "Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "S. Sozin www.researchgate.net/profile/Sergey-Sozin"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: S. Sozin www.researchgate.net/profile/Sergey-Sozin" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-5c95bae0-2659-43e0-a8ce-b90f7b31e5d9"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-5c95bae0-2659-43e0-a8ce-b90f7b31e5d9" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "ovary"
synonym: "Organ: ovary" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "oocyte"
synonym: "CellType: oocyte" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "reproductive system"
synonym: "Organ_System: reproductive system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The LH surge terminates preovulatory follicle growth and initiates the processes of ovulation, oocyte meiosis, expansion of the cumulus cell oocyte complex (during which cumulus cells make a hyaluronan-rich matrix that surrounds the oocyte prior to ovulation), and luteinization.    Signaling description: As a consequence, the FSH program of gene expression is turned off while genes controlling matrix formation and luteinization are turned on. LH rapidly induces in granulosa cells the expression of the EGF-like factors amphiregulin (AREG), betacellulin (BTC), and epiregulin (EREG) in a PKA-dependent manner. AREG and/or EREG in turn activate the EGFR signaling cascade, including RAS and ERK1/2leading to phosphorylation and inactivation of gap junctions proteins.    Outcome effects: The tight contact between oocyte and cumulus cells is lost and cGMP transfer to oocyte is decreases leading to resumption of meiosis. Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The LH surge terminates preovulatory follicle growth and initiates the processes of ovulation, oocyte meiosis, expansion of the cumulus cell oocyte complex (during which cumulus cells make a hyaluronan-rich matrix that surrounds the oocyte prior to ovulation), and luteinization.    Signaling description: As a consequence, the FSH program of gene expression is turned off while genes controlling matrix formation and luteinization are turned on. LH rapidly induces in granulosa cells the expression of the EGF-like factors amphiregulin (AREG), betacellulin (BTC), and epiregulin (EREG) in a PKA-dependent manner. AREG and/or EREG in turn activate the EGFR signaling cascade, including RAS and ERK1/2leading to phosphorylation and inactivation of gap junctions proteins.    Outcome effects: The tight contact between oocyte and cumulus cells is lost and cGMP transfer to oocyte is decreases leading to resumption of meiosis. Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-181d93bc-14a4-450a-9f7b-a6b08731cf95
name: Retinoic Acid in Meiosis Regulation
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:reproductive_system ! Reproductive system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:r ! R
is_a: urn:agi-folder:reproductive_biology ! Reproductive biology
xref: PS:Description "Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:PMID "17715177"
synonym: "PMID: 17715177" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "S. Sozin www.researchgate.net/profile/Sergey-Sozin"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: S. Sozin www.researchgate.net/profile/Sergey-Sozin" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-181d93bc-14a4-450a-9f7b-a6b08731cf95"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-181d93bc-14a4-450a-9f7b-a6b08731cf95" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "ovary"
xref: PS:Organ "testis"
synonym: "Organ: ovary" EXACT []
synonym: "Organ: testis" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "reproductive system"
synonym: "Organ_System: reproductive system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Haploid gametes are produced by reductive nuclear division of a diploid germ cell in a specialized process known as meiosis. Germ cells are unique in undergoing meiosis to generate oocytes and sperm. In mammals, meiosis onset is before birth in females, or at puberty in males. Retinoic acid (RA) induces expression of the critical pre-meiosis gene STRA8 in germ cells of the fetal ovary.     Signaling description: The mesonephros attached to the ovary expresses RA synthesizing enzymes RALDH2/3 (ALDH1A2/3) and ovarian granulosa / interstitial cell expresses RALDH1 (ALDH1A1), resulting in the production of high levels of RA. RA binds RAR/RXRs on both identified RAREs of the STRA8 promoter to induce transcription. Meiosis then progresses in ovarian germ cells."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Haploid gametes are produced by reductive nuclear division of a diploid germ cell in a specialized process known as meiosis. Germ cells are unique in undergoing meiosis to generate oocytes and sperm. In mammals, meiosis onset is before birth in females, or at puberty in males. Retinoic acid (RA) induces expression of the critical pre-meiosis gene STRA8 in germ cells of the fetal ovary.     Signaling description: The mesonephros attached to the ovary expresses RA synthesizing enzymes RALDH2/3 (ALDH1A2/3) and ovarian granulosa / interstitial cell expresses RALDH1 (ALDH1A1), resulting in the production of high levels of RA. RA binds RAR/RXRs on both identified RAREs of the STRA8 promoter to induce transcription. Meiosis then progresses in ovarian germ cells." EXACT []

