xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Agomelatine (Valdoxan) is a novel antidepressant drug that simultaneously acts as a melatonin receptor (MTNR1A) agonist and as a serotonin receptor (HTR2C) antagonist.    Signaling description: Agomelatine`s dual mechanism of action is unique and is the basis of efficacy in treating both depressive symptoms and sleep-wakefulness rhythm disorders. Both melatonin and serotonin receptors are present in the suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN).    Outcome effects: Melatonin receptor signaling leads to the resynchronization of circadian and sleep rhythms. In SCN, as in the frontal cortex, excitatory HTR2C receptors are localized on GABAergic interneurons. Therefore, their blockade disinhibits fronto-cortical dopaminergic and adrenergic transmission, the activity of which may be compromised in depression."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Agomelatine (Valdoxan) is a novel antidepressant drug that simultaneously acts as a melatonin receptor (MTNR1A) agonist and as a serotonin receptor (HTR2C) antagonist.    Signaling description: Agomelatine`s dual mechanism of action is unique and is the basis of efficacy in treating both depressive symptoms and sleep-wakefulness rhythm disorders. Both melatonin and serotonin receptors are present in the suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN).    Outcome effects: Melatonin receptor signaling leads to the resynchronization of circadian and sleep rhythms. In SCN, as in the frontal cortex, excitatory HTR2C receptors are localized on GABAergic interneurons. Therefore, their blockade disinhibits fronto-cortical dopaminergic and adrenergic transmission, the activity of which may be compromised in depression." EXACT []

