xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The intrinsic signaling pathway for programmed cell death comprises non-receptor-mediated intracellular signals, which induce activities in the mitochondria that initiate apoptosis. Melatonin and its signaling effects can interfere with this apoptotic pathway, thus preventing apoptotic cell death.    Signaling description: Melatonin-induced activation of NF-kB and JUN-FOS is responsible for the control of anti-apoptotic genes such as BCL2. The activation of NFE2L2 is responsible for the antioxidant response.    Outcome effects: In addition to its receptor-mediated actions, melatonin also has direct free radical scavenging and receptor-independent effects. Melatonin detoxifies radicals via the mechanism of electron donation."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The intrinsic signaling pathway for programmed cell death comprises non-receptor-mediated intracellular signals, which induce activities in the mitochondria that initiate apoptosis. Melatonin and its signaling effects can interfere with this apoptotic pathway, thus preventing apoptotic cell death.    Signaling description: Melatonin-induced activation of NF-kB and JUN-FOS is responsible for the control of anti-apoptotic genes such as BCL2. The activation of NFE2L2 is responsible for the antioxidant response.    Outcome effects: In addition to its receptor-mediated actions, melatonin also has direct free radical scavenging and receptor-independent effects. Melatonin detoxifies radicals via the mechanism of electron donation." EXACT []

