xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The histamine H3 receptor (HRH3) functions as an auto-receptor and regulates the synthesis and release of histamine.    Signaling description: The activation of HRH3 decreases histamine production and release, thus promoting sleep. Conversely, the blockade of HRH3 promotes wakefulness. Therefore, HRH3 constitutes a brain target for the treatment of sleep-wake disorders."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The histamine H3 receptor (HRH3) functions as an auto-receptor and regulates the synthesis and release of histamine.    Signaling description: The activation of HRH3 decreases histamine production and release, thus promoting sleep. Conversely, the blockade of HRH3 promotes wakefulness. Therefore, HRH3 constitutes a brain target for the treatment of sleep-wake disorders." EXACT []

