xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Adenosine is a secondary by-product from the breakdown of ATP and cAMP.    Signaling description: Adenosine is released from leptomeningeal cells of the basal forebrain following prostaglandin D2 stimulation. Adenosine activates ADORA2A and ADORA1 on neurons in the basal forebrain and the ventrolateral preoptic nucleus (VLPO).    Outcome effects: Sleep-promoting neurons in the VLPO send inhibitory signals to suppress the histaminergic neurons in the tuberomammillary nucleus (TMN), which contribute to arousal. Caffeine binds to ADORA2A and ADORA1 with similar high affinities and acts as an antagonist at both receptor subtypes."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Adenosine is a secondary by-product from the breakdown of ATP and cAMP.    Signaling description: Adenosine is released from leptomeningeal cells of the basal forebrain following prostaglandin D2 stimulation. Adenosine activates ADORA2A and ADORA1 on neurons in the basal forebrain and the ventrolateral preoptic nucleus (VLPO).    Outcome effects: Sleep-promoting neurons in the VLPO send inhibitory signals to suppress the histaminergic neurons in the tuberomammillary nucleus (TMN), which contribute to arousal. Caffeine binds to ADORA2A and ADORA1 with similar high affinities and acts as an antagonist at both receptor subtypes." EXACT []

