synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Central tolerance is a process of T-cell clonal deletion and occurs during lymphocyte development.    Signaling description: The key factor determining the choice between positive and negative selection is the degree of binding strength between T-cell receptor (TCR) and antigen. The response to an antigen at this stage also depends on the properties of the antigen, the cell type, and the developmental stage. This may lead to the T-cell becoming non-responsive (anergic), undergoing directed suicide (negative selection), or further differentiation. High-avidity binding of antigen to the TCR complex induces negative selection. High-avidity binding may occur due to a defect in TCR maturation or from a large number of antigens. According to one (Hypothesis), the mechanism of negative selection due to the over-activation of TCRs by antigens occurs when over-phosphorylated LAT is incapable of activating the PLCG1-dependent release of calcium ions. This results in the reduced activity of transcription factors such as NR4A1 which is required for T-cell proliferation. Conversely, completely phosphorylated LAT strengthens signaling, which leads to the activation of caspases and triggers apoptosis.    Outcome effects: Finally, the activation of PDCD1 receptor on the surface of T-cells has also been shown to be necessary for the process of T-cell clonal deletion."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Central tolerance is a process of T-cell clonal deletion and occurs during lymphocyte development.    Signaling description: The key factor determining the choice between positive and negative selection is the degree of binding strength between T-cell receptor (TCR) and antigen. The response to an antigen at this stage also depends on the properties of the antigen, the cell type, and the developmental stage. This may lead to the T-cell becoming non-responsive (anergic), undergoing directed suicide (negative selection), or further differentiation. High-avidity binding of antigen to the TCR complex induces negative selection. High-avidity binding may occur due to a defect in TCR maturation or from a large number of antigens. According to one (Hypothesis), the mechanism of negative selection due to the over-activation of TCRs by antigens occurs when over-phosphorylated LAT is incapable of activating the PLCG1-dependent release of calcium ions. This results in the reduced activity of transcription factors such as NR4A1 which is required for T-cell proliferation. Conversely, completely phosphorylated LAT strengthens signaling, which leads to the activation of caspases and triggers apoptosis.    Outcome effects: Finally, the activation of PDCD1 receptor on the surface of T-cells has also been shown to be necessary for the process of T-cell clonal deletion." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-463ea690-1c95-492d-9b04-a20c97abe920
name: CD8+ T-Cell Activation
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:c ! C
is_a: urn:agi-folder:t-cell_self_tolerance ! T-cell self tolerance
xref: PS:Description "CD8 cells and NK cells kill damaged or infected cells in an organism. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: CD8 cells and NK cells kill damaged or infected cells in an organism. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
