xref: PS:Source "Receptor Signaling"
synonym: "Source: Receptor Signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: TAM receptors are a subfamily of receptor protein tyrosine kinases (RTKs), including AXL, MERTK and TYRO3. There are two well-known TAM receptors ligands - GAS6 and PROS1. TULP1 recently also has been described as AXL ligand.    Signaling description: While the MAPK/ERK pathway typically results in AXL-mediated proliferation, AXL binding to and activation of PI3K has been linked to multiple downstream pathways converging on increased cell survival. Genetic or experimental alteration of TAM receptor function can contribute to a number of disease states, including coagulopathy, autoimmune disease, retinitis pigmentosa, and cancer.    Outcome effects: The downstream pathways of PI3K activation by AXL involve PI3K stimulation of AKT1, phosphorylation of NFKB, increased expression of antiapoptotic proteins such as BCL2 and BCL2L1, and inhibition of proapoptotic proteins such as CASP3. Another AXL-induced survival pathway may involve PI3K activation of the small GTPases Rac and Rho as well as the downstream JNK. Studies of GnRH neurons suggest that AXL directs migration of these cells via a signaling pathway involving PI3K, Ras, Rac1, MAPK14, MAPKAPK2, and HSPB1, which results in actin reorganization. AXL was shown to regulate natural killer cell development through interaction with FLT3. AXL also was shown to take part in angiogenesis through AXL - PTPN11 - KDR axis."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: TAM receptors are a subfamily of receptor protein tyrosine kinases (RTKs), including AXL, MERTK and TYRO3. There are two well-known TAM receptors ligands - GAS6 and PROS1. TULP1 recently also has been described as AXL ligand.    Signaling description: While the MAPK/ERK pathway typically results in AXL-mediated proliferation, AXL binding to and activation of PI3K has been linked to multiple downstream pathways converging on increased cell survival. Genetic or experimental alteration of TAM receptor function can contribute to a number of disease states, including coagulopathy, autoimmune disease, retinitis pigmentosa, and cancer.    Outcome effects: The downstream pathways of PI3K activation by AXL involve PI3K stimulation of AKT1, phosphorylation of NFKB, increased expression of antiapoptotic proteins such as BCL2 and BCL2L1, and inhibition of proapoptotic proteins such as CASP3. Another AXL-induced survival pathway may involve PI3K activation of the small GTPases Rac and Rho as well as the downstream JNK. Studies of GnRH neurons suggest that AXL directs migration of these cells via a signaling pathway involving PI3K, Ras, Rac1, MAPK14, MAPKAPK2, and HSPB1, which results in actin reorganization. AXL was shown to regulate natural killer cell development through interaction with FLT3. AXL also was shown to take part in angiogenesis through AXL - PTPN11 - KDR axis." EXACT []

