xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) and lutenising hormone (LH) are produced in the anterior lobe of pituitary gland and their function in gonads is mediated over distinct FSH and LH receptors (FSHR and LHCGR), respectively. LH receptors are found on both granulosa and thecal cells; the expression of FSH receptors is restricted to the granulose cells.     Signaling description: LH stimulates female progesterone synthesis and ovulation and also theca cell androgen production. FSH is required for follicle maturation and stimulation of ovarian estrogen production. During the process of folliculogenesis, the conversion of cholesterol into ovarian hormones takes place. Conversion of steroids to androgens occurs within the theca cells. Androgens and are converted to estrogens by aromatase enzyme (CYP19A1) in the granulosa cells. NR5A1 is a key transcriptional regulator involved in production of key steroidogenic enzymes and transporters, including STAR, CYP11A1, CYP17A1, and CYP19A."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) and lutenising hormone (LH) are produced in the anterior lobe of pituitary gland and their function in gonads is mediated over distinct FSH and LH receptors (FSHR and LHCGR), respectively. LH receptors are found on both granulosa and thecal cells; the expression of FSH receptors is restricted to the granulose cells.     Signaling description: LH stimulates female progesterone synthesis and ovulation and also theca cell androgen production. FSH is required for follicle maturation and stimulation of ovarian estrogen production. During the process of folliculogenesis, the conversion of cholesterol into ovarian hormones takes place. Conversion of steroids to androgens occurs within the theca cells. Androgens and are converted to estrogens by aromatase enzyme (CYP19A1) in the granulosa cells. NR5A1 is a key transcriptional regulator involved in production of key steroidogenic enzymes and transporters, including STAR, CYP11A1, CYP17A1, and CYP19A." EXACT []

[Term]
