xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The recruitment of neutrophils into the injured tissue is a key component of the inflammatory response.    Signaling description: The activated neutrophils generate large amounts of reactive oxygen species (ROS) and hypochlorous acid (HOCl). With the respiratory burst, ROS and HOCl are released from neutrophils to attack various pathogens. However, neutrophil-derived oxidants are also implicated in a range of injurious effects and are involved in the pathogenesis of chronic and acute inflammatory diseases.    Outcome effects: Neutrophil-derived oxidants cause DNA base oxidation and damage to the plasma membrane by lipid peroxidation. Lipid peroxidation products such as crotonaldehyde, acrolein, 4-hydroxynonenal, and malondialdehyde damage DNA by forming exocyclic adducts, most of which are highly mutagenic.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level are highlighted in red."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The recruitment of neutrophils into the injured tissue is a key component of the inflammatory response.    Signaling description: The activated neutrophils generate large amounts of reactive oxygen species (ROS) and hypochlorous acid (HOCl). With the respiratory burst, ROS and HOCl are released from neutrophils to attack various pathogens. However, neutrophil-derived oxidants are also implicated in a range of injurious effects and are involved in the pathogenesis of chronic and acute inflammatory diseases.    Outcome effects: Neutrophil-derived oxidants cause DNA base oxidation and damage to the plasma membrane by lipid peroxidation. Lipid peroxidation products such as crotonaldehyde, acrolein, 4-hydroxynonenal, and malondialdehyde damage DNA by forming exocyclic adducts, most of which are highly mutagenic.    Highlighted proteins: Entities with increased level are highlighted in red." EXACT []

