xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Endoplasmic reticulum (ER) stress caused by the presence of an excessive amount of unfolded or misfolded proteins may lead to a cascade of intracellular stress signaling events known as unfolded protein response (UPR).    Signaling description: During the UPR, protein translation is attenuated, ER-associated protein degradation (ERAD) is accelerated, and the production of molecular chaperones is increased. The presence of unfolded proteins in the ER lumen is sensed through the transmembrane signaling proteins EIF2AK3, ERN1, and ATF6. All three sensors are maintained in an inactive state through the interaction with the protein chaperone HSPA5. ERN1/XBP1 signaling activates the transcription of a subset of UPR genes encoding chaperones, catalysts of folding, and ERAD degradation machinery including EDEM1 and EDEM2.    Outcome effects: If ER stress is not relieved, apoptosis is induced to protect from neoplasia. Apoptotic signals are produced at the ER by several mechanisms including EIF2AK3/EIF2S1-dependent induction of the proapoptotic transcription factor DDIT3, BAK1/BAX-regulated Ca2+ release from the ER, ERN1-mediated activation of MAP3K5/MAPK8, and the cleavage and activation of procaspase 12. Lastly, several drugs can directly block heat shock proteins (chaperones) in the ER, thus triggering UPR and subsequent apoptosis."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Endoplasmic reticulum (ER) stress caused by the presence of an excessive amount of unfolded or misfolded proteins may lead to a cascade of intracellular stress signaling events known as unfolded protein response (UPR).    Signaling description: During the UPR, protein translation is attenuated, ER-associated protein degradation (ERAD) is accelerated, and the production of molecular chaperones is increased. The presence of unfolded proteins in the ER lumen is sensed through the transmembrane signaling proteins EIF2AK3, ERN1, and ATF6. All three sensors are maintained in an inactive state through the interaction with the protein chaperone HSPA5. ERN1/XBP1 signaling activates the transcription of a subset of UPR genes encoding chaperones, catalysts of folding, and ERAD degradation machinery including EDEM1 and EDEM2.    Outcome effects: If ER stress is not relieved, apoptosis is induced to protect from neoplasia. Apoptotic signals are produced at the ER by several mechanisms including EIF2AK3/EIF2S1-dependent induction of the proapoptotic transcription factor DDIT3, BAK1/BAX-regulated Ca2+ release from the ER, ERN1-mediated activation of MAP3K5/MAPK8, and the cleavage and activation of procaspase 12. Lastly, several drugs can directly block heat shock proteins (chaperones) in the ER, thus triggering UPR and subsequent apoptosis." EXACT []

