xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Glutamate is the most abundant excitatory neurotransmitter in the vertebrate nervous system.    Signaling description: Nerve impulse triggers the release of glutamate from presynaptic cells, and receptors on the surface of postsynaptic cells bind glutamate and become activated. The excess of glutamate is normally removed from the synaptic cleft by glial cells, but in the event of injury or disease this mechanism may be compromised, which results in the overstimulation of ionotropic glutamate and NMDA receptors in addition to intracellular calcium (Ca2+) overload.    Outcome effects: The described events lead to oxidative stress and the induction of apoptosis."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Glutamate is the most abundant excitatory neurotransmitter in the vertebrate nervous system.    Signaling description: Nerve impulse triggers the release of glutamate from presynaptic cells, and receptors on the surface of postsynaptic cells bind glutamate and become activated. The excess of glutamate is normally removed from the synaptic cleft by glial cells, but in the event of injury or disease this mechanism may be compromised, which results in the overstimulation of ionotropic glutamate and NMDA receptors in addition to intracellular calcium (Ca2+) overload.    Outcome effects: The described events lead to oxidative stress and the induction of apoptosis." EXACT []

