xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The modulation of cytosolic Ca2+ concentration constitutes a fundamental mechanism of signal transduction in excitable cells.    Signaling description: Ca2+ oscillations are controlled by the release of Ca2+ from ER stores through inositol triphosphate receptor channels (IP3R) and by Ca2+ uptake into the ER lumen by sarco(endo)plasmic reticulum Ca2+-ATPases. In addition, mitochondria efficiently take up and release Ca2+.    Outcome effects: Mitochondrial Ca2+ overload is responsible for increased ROS production mediated by the respiratory chain. Moreover, the increase of free Ca2+ concentration in the mitochondrial matrix above a certain level activates permeability transition pore(s) (mPTP) and triggers cascades of cellular processes leading to cell death.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The modulation of cytosolic Ca2+ concentration constitutes a fundamental mechanism of signal transduction in excitable cells.    Signaling description: Ca2+ oscillations are controlled by the release of Ca2+ from ER stores through inositol triphosphate receptor channels (IP3R) and by Ca2+ uptake into the ER lumen by sarco(endo)plasmic reticulum Ca2+-ATPases. In addition, mitochondria efficiently take up and release Ca2+.    Outcome effects: Mitochondrial Ca2+ overload is responsible for increased ROS production mediated by the respiratory chain. Moreover, the increase of free Ca2+ concentration in the mitochondrial matrix above a certain level activates permeability transition pore(s) (mPTP) and triggers cascades of cellular processes leading to cell death.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue." EXACT []

