xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Ketoconazole is an antifungal agent.    Signaling description: In human epidermal keratinocytes, ketoconazole in addition to its inhibitory effects against fungi activates NF erythroid 2-related factor-2 (NFE2L2) via AHR signaling. AHR initiates dissociation of inhibitory KEAP1 from NFE2L2 and nuclear translocation of NFE2L2. This leads to activation of the target gene NQO1 with subsequent elimination of ROS.    Outcome effects: Cynaropicrin is a natural component of artichoke (Cynara scolymus) used as folk medicine due to its antioxidant and anti-inflammatory activities. Cynaropicrin was shown to attenuate UVB-induced oxidative stress via the AHR- NFE2L2-NQO1 pathway. Ligustilide, an active ingredient isolated from the medicinal plants Cnidium officinale and Angelica acutiloba was shown to induce the NFE2L2-NQO1 axis."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Ketoconazole is an antifungal agent.    Signaling description: In human epidermal keratinocytes, ketoconazole in addition to its inhibitory effects against fungi activates NF erythroid 2-related factor-2 (NFE2L2) via AHR signaling. AHR initiates dissociation of inhibitory KEAP1 from NFE2L2 and nuclear translocation of NFE2L2. This leads to activation of the target gene NQO1 with subsequent elimination of ROS.    Outcome effects: Cynaropicrin is a natural component of artichoke (Cynara scolymus) used as folk medicine due to its antioxidant and anti-inflammatory activities. Cynaropicrin was shown to attenuate UVB-induced oxidative stress via the AHR- NFE2L2-NQO1 pathway. Ligustilide, an active ingredient isolated from the medicinal plants Cnidium officinale and Angelica acutiloba was shown to induce the NFE2L2-NQO1 axis." EXACT []

