xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Chloracne is the typical toxic response of the skin to TCDD (dioxin). The key feature of chloracne is non-inflammatory alteration of keratinization of the pilosebaceous unit that results in the formation of comedones, straw-coloured cysts, pustules and noninfectious abscesses that may scar.    Signaling description: Chloracne is characterized by atrophy of the sebaceous glands, keratinocyte hyperpigmentation, and epidermal hyperplasia. Recently, the skin lesions were recognized as hamartomas and, in the case of TCDD poisoning, represent a TCDD metabolizing compartment.    Outcome effects: TCDD promotes terminal differentiation of keratinocytes, possibly mediated by changes in the expression of transforming growth factor alpha (TGFA) and epidermal growth factor (EGF). NFE2L2 was reported to be upregulated in chloracne and controls the expression of growth factor epigen (EPGN), secretory leukocyte peptidase inhibitor (SLPI), and small proline-rich protein 2d (SPRR2D). In hair follicles, the latter three were identified as the likely causes of infundibular acanthosis, hyperkeratosis, and cyst formation. TCDD also enhances filaggrin (FLG), involucrin (IVL), and IL1B expression."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Chloracne is the typical toxic response of the skin to TCDD (dioxin). The key feature of chloracne is non-inflammatory alteration of keratinization of the pilosebaceous unit that results in the formation of comedones, straw-coloured cysts, pustules and noninfectious abscesses that may scar.    Signaling description: Chloracne is characterized by atrophy of the sebaceous glands, keratinocyte hyperpigmentation, and epidermal hyperplasia. Recently, the skin lesions were recognized as hamartomas and, in the case of TCDD poisoning, represent a TCDD metabolizing compartment.    Outcome effects: TCDD promotes terminal differentiation of keratinocytes, possibly mediated by changes in the expression of transforming growth factor alpha (TGFA) and epidermal growth factor (EGF). NFE2L2 was reported to be upregulated in chloracne and controls the expression of growth factor epigen (EPGN), secretory leukocyte peptidase inhibitor (SLPI), and small proline-rich protein 2d (SPRR2D). In hair follicles, the latter three were identified as the likely causes of infundibular acanthosis, hyperkeratosis, and cyst formation. TCDD also enhances filaggrin (FLG), involucrin (IVL), and IL1B expression." EXACT []

