xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: B-cells, key components of humoral immunity, are sensitive to such toxic compounds as dioxin.    Signaling description: AHR is an important mediator of the effects of dioxin on B-cells. Dioxin induces AHR expression and results in inhibition of IgM secretion. Changes in B-cell differentiation and antibody production may depend on BACH2, a direct target of AHR.    Outcome effects: BACH2 expression in response to dioxin-AHR binding inhibits PRDM1 and regulates the suppressive effects of BCL6 and PAX5. In addition, it was shown that IL4 causes AHR expression and activation in B-cells. IL4 can also induce AHR expression in a STAT6-dependent manner and translocate the induced AHR to the nuclei in both mouse and human B-cells. AhR activated by IL4 induces the expression of a xenobiotic-metabolizing gene, CYP1A1, and dioxin synergistically acts on the induction of this gene by IL4."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: B-cells, key components of humoral immunity, are sensitive to such toxic compounds as dioxin.    Signaling description: AHR is an important mediator of the effects of dioxin on B-cells. Dioxin induces AHR expression and results in inhibition of IgM secretion. Changes in B-cell differentiation and antibody production may depend on BACH2, a direct target of AHR.    Outcome effects: BACH2 expression in response to dioxin-AHR binding inhibits PRDM1 and regulates the suppressive effects of BCL6 and PAX5. In addition, it was shown that IL4 causes AHR expression and activation in B-cells. IL4 can also induce AHR expression in a STAT6-dependent manner and translocate the induced AHR to the nuclei in both mouse and human B-cells. AhR activated by IL4 induces the expression of a xenobiotic-metabolizing gene, CYP1A1, and dioxin synergistically acts on the induction of this gene by IL4." EXACT []

