synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-785ee7d6-e699-4ac1-ba61-affb783e2d58" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "T-cell"
synonym: "CellType: T-cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "lymph node"
synonym: "Organ: lymph node" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "lymphatic system"
synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Th17 are a subset of T-helper cells that primarily produce two major members of the IL17 family, IL17A and IL17F involved in the recruitment, activation, and migration of neutrophils.    Signaling description: In addition, Th17-cells secrete IL21 and IL22. In humans, a combination of TGFB1, IL1B, and IL23 induces Th17 differentiation from naive T-cells.    Outcome effects: Interleukin (IL) receptor, T-cell receptor (TCR), and co-activator receptor (such as CD28) pathways activate transcription factors NF-kB, STAT3, RORA, and RORC for specific Th17-related cytokine expression."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Th17 are a subset of T-helper cells that primarily produce two major members of the IL17 family, IL17A and IL17F involved in the recruitment, activation, and migration of neutrophils.    Signaling description: In addition, Th17-cells secrete IL21 and IL22. In humans, a combination of TGFB1, IL1B, and IL23 induces Th17 differentiation from naive T-cells.    Outcome effects: Interleukin (IL) receptor, T-cell receptor (TCR), and co-activator receptor (such as CD28) pathways activate transcription factors NF-kB, STAT3, RORA, and RORC for specific Th17-related cytokine expression." EXACT []

