xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Vasodilation is the widening of blood vessels due to the relaxation of vascular smooth muscle cells within the vessel walls.    Signaling description: During inflammation, vascular vasodilation causes the engorgement of blood vessels, increase in blood flow, and redness and swelling from injury. Two different mechanisms modulate the relaxation of vascular smooth muscle cells including Gs-protein (GNAS)-coupled pathway and nitric oxide (NO)-cGMP pathway. GNAS-coupled pathway in vascular smooth muscle cells stimulates ADCY, which catalyzes the formation of cAMP.    Outcome effects: Unlike the heart, an increase in cAMP in vascular smooth muscle cells causes reduced contraction and increased relaxation. The reason for this is that MYLK is inhibited by cAMP. MYLK phosphorylates myosin and causes contraction. The most potent vasodilators, which act through GNAS signaling, are epinephrine, adenosine, PGI2, PGD2, PGE2, and histamine. Another mechanism that regulates vascular smooth muscle tone is the NO/cGMP pathway. Vascular endothelial cells normally produce NO which diffuses from endothelial cells to adjacent smooth muscle cells and activates guanylyl cyclase (sGC) leading to the increased formation of cGMP and vasodilation."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Vasodilation is the widening of blood vessels due to the relaxation of vascular smooth muscle cells within the vessel walls.    Signaling description: During inflammation, vascular vasodilation causes the engorgement of blood vessels, increase in blood flow, and redness and swelling from injury. Two different mechanisms modulate the relaxation of vascular smooth muscle cells including Gs-protein (GNAS)-coupled pathway and nitric oxide (NO)-cGMP pathway. GNAS-coupled pathway in vascular smooth muscle cells stimulates ADCY, which catalyzes the formation of cAMP.    Outcome effects: Unlike the heart, an increase in cAMP in vascular smooth muscle cells causes reduced contraction and increased relaxation. The reason for this is that MYLK is inhibited by cAMP. MYLK phosphorylates myosin and causes contraction. The most potent vasodilators, which act through GNAS signaling, are epinephrine, adenosine, PGI2, PGD2, PGE2, and histamine. Another mechanism that regulates vascular smooth muscle tone is the NO/cGMP pathway. Vascular endothelial cells normally produce NO which diffuses from endothelial cells to adjacent smooth muscle cells and activates guanylyl cyclase (sGC) leading to the increased formation of cGMP and vasodilation." EXACT []

