xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Vascular endothelial cell (EC) permeability is the capacity of a blood vessel wall to allow the flow of small molecules and whole cells such as lymphocytes in and out of the vessel.    Signaling description: Blood vessel walls are lined by a single layer of ECs. The regulation of cell junctions between a single layer of ECs and therefore permeability is a function of the balance between competing adhesive and contractile forces. VEGFA, F2, and histamine are the main activators of vascular EC permeability. These mediators inhibit the function of primary cell junction proteins including TJP1, CDH5, and OCLN through the increase in intracellular calcium (Ca2+) or interaction with the cytoskeleton.    Outcome effects: Subsequently, RHOA/ROCK1 and myosin light chain kinase (MYLK) signaling pathways activate MYL9 to induce cytoskeleton contraction in ECs and dissociation of cell-cell junctions. As a result, the association between epithelial cells in the blood vessel wall weakens. Additionally, the synthesis of nitric oxide (NO) is stimulated which acts as a muscle relaxant for vascular muscles."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Vascular endothelial cell (EC) permeability is the capacity of a blood vessel wall to allow the flow of small molecules and whole cells such as lymphocytes in and out of the vessel.    Signaling description: Blood vessel walls are lined by a single layer of ECs. The regulation of cell junctions between a single layer of ECs and therefore permeability is a function of the balance between competing adhesive and contractile forces. VEGFA, F2, and histamine are the main activators of vascular EC permeability. These mediators inhibit the function of primary cell junction proteins including TJP1, CDH5, and OCLN through the increase in intracellular calcium (Ca2+) or interaction with the cytoskeleton.    Outcome effects: Subsequently, RHOA/ROCK1 and myosin light chain kinase (MYLK) signaling pathways activate MYL9 to induce cytoskeleton contraction in ECs and dissociation of cell-cell junctions. As a result, the association between epithelial cells in the blood vessel wall weakens. Additionally, the synthesis of nitric oxide (NO) is stimulated which acts as a muscle relaxant for vascular muscles." EXACT []

