xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: 7-dehydrocholesterol is converted in the skin under Ultraviolet light band B (UVB) to vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol). Cholecalciferol is converted to the biologically active vitamin D3 metabolite, calcitriol.     Signaling description: Calcitriol interacts with a nuclear vitamin D receptor (VDRn). Activated VDRn forms a heterodimeric complex with Retinoid-X-Receptor (RXR) and regulate in different ways the expression of genes which have vitamin D3 response element in their promoters."
