xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: 7-dehydrocholesterol is converted in the skin under Ultraviolet light band B (UVB) to vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol). Cholecalciferol is converted to the biologically active vitamin D3 metabolite, calcitriol.     Signaling description: Calcitriol non-genomic actions are described as the activation of C and phospholipase A2, PI3K, and the rapid generation of Ca2+, cyclic AMP, fatty acids and 3-phosphoinositides which lead to the activation of several protein kinases. Calcitriol also can open Ca2+ and Cl- channels."
