xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: A central task in immune tolerance to commensal fungi is conducted by tryptophan (trp), an essential, diet-derived amino acid.    Signaling description: Fungus-induced activation of trp catabolism by indoleamine 2,3-dioxygenase 1 (IDO1) expressed by tolerogenic dendritic cells and epithelial cells leads to the production of immunologically active kynurenine.    Outcome effects: This induces the transcription of FOXP3 and down-regulates RORC transcription, thus promoting immune tolerance via Treg cells."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: A central task in immune tolerance to commensal fungi is conducted by tryptophan (trp), an essential, diet-derived amino acid.    Signaling description: Fungus-induced activation of trp catabolism by indoleamine 2,3-dioxygenase 1 (IDO1) expressed by tolerogenic dendritic cells and epithelial cells leads to the production of immunologically active kynurenine.    Outcome effects: This induces the transcription of FOXP3 and down-regulates RORC transcription, thus promoting immune tolerance via Treg cells." EXACT []

