synonym: "Source: Receptor Signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Th17 cells are T-cells producing IL-17A, IL-17F, IL-22, and IL-21. These cells play an important role in the control of specific pathogens and the development of autoimmune diseases.    Signaling description: Th17 cell differentiation is induced by IL-6 and TGFB1. These cytokines trigger STAT3 phosphorylation, which in turns induces the expression of the Th17 cell-specific transcription factors RORA and RORC, followed by IL17 and IL22 expression. AHR is also expressed in response to IL6 and TGFB1 and participates in Th17 cell differentiation. AHR ligands (FICZ and other) can boost the differentiation of Th17 cells. AHR signalling in T-helper type 17 (Th17) cells promotes the expression of IL-21 and IL-22, and it also limits the activation of STAT5, which mediate the inhibitory effects of IL-2 on Th17 cell differentiation, respectively.    Outcome effects: IL2 and IL21 are negative regulators of Th17 differentiation. AhR cooperates with STAT3 to induce the expression of the epigenetic modifier Aiolos (IKZF3). IKZF3 modifies the epigenetic status of the IL2 promoter, limiting its accessibility to transcription factors and effectively silencing IL-2 expression. During early stages, AhR might limit the inhibitory effects of IL-2 and promote IL-10 production, whereas in late stages it might contribute to the expression of IL-21 and IL-22. Activation of Ahr by FICZ enhances the Th17 differentiation via upregulating microRNA (miR)-212 / 132 that targets B-cell lymphoma (BCL6), a negative regulator of Th17."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Th17 cells are T-cells producing IL-17A, IL-17F, IL-22, and IL-21. These cells play an important role in the control of specific pathogens and the development of autoimmune diseases.    Signaling description: Th17 cell differentiation is induced by IL-6 and TGFB1. These cytokines trigger STAT3 phosphorylation, which in turns induces the expression of the Th17 cell-specific transcription factors RORA and RORC, followed by IL17 and IL22 expression. AHR is also expressed in response to IL6 and TGFB1 and participates in Th17 cell differentiation. AHR ligands (FICZ and other) can boost the differentiation of Th17 cells. AHR signalling in T-helper type 17 (Th17) cells promotes the expression of IL-21 and IL-22, and it also limits the activation of STAT5, which mediate the inhibitory effects of IL-2 on Th17 cell differentiation, respectively.    Outcome effects: IL2 and IL21 are negative regulators of Th17 differentiation. AhR cooperates with STAT3 to induce the expression of the epigenetic modifier Aiolos (IKZF3). IKZF3 modifies the epigenetic status of the IL2 promoter, limiting its accessibility to transcription factors and effectively silencing IL-2 expression. During early stages, AhR might limit the inhibitory effects of IL-2 and promote IL-10 production, whereas in late stages it might contribute to the expression of IL-21 and IL-22. Activation of Ahr by FICZ enhances the Th17 differentiation via upregulating microRNA (miR)-212 / 132 that targets B-cell lymphoma (BCL6), a negative regulator of Th17." EXACT []

