xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Kynurenine pathway (KP) is responsible for tryptophan turnover creating multiple intermediate metabolites.    Signaling description: Among KP metabolites, kynurenine (KYN), picolinic acid (PIC), 3-hydroxykynurenine (3-HK), 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid (3-HAA) and quinolinic acid (QUIN) were fond to be immunosuppressive: in micromolar concentrations they were found to inhibit T-cell proliferation in vitro. The same substances induced selective apoptosis of thymocytes and of antigen-specific CD4 T-helper 1 cells. Another notable effect 3-HAA has on T-cells is its ability to cause a reduction in CD4 TH17 cells and a reciprocal increase in the fraction of Tregs."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Kynurenine pathway (KP) is responsible for tryptophan turnover creating multiple intermediate metabolites.    Signaling description: Among KP metabolites, kynurenine (KYN), picolinic acid (PIC), 3-hydroxykynurenine (3-HK), 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid (3-HAA) and quinolinic acid (QUIN) were fond to be immunosuppressive: in micromolar concentrations they were found to inhibit T-cell proliferation in vitro. The same substances induced selective apoptosis of thymocytes and of antigen-specific CD4 T-helper 1 cells. Another notable effect 3-HAA has on T-cells is its ability to cause a reduction in CD4 TH17 cells and a reciprocal increase in the fraction of Tregs." EXACT []

