xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Type 1 regulatory (Tr1) cells have emerged as key players in the prevention of autoimmunity. They produce high levels of the immunosuppressive IL10 and confer protection against a wide panel of autoimmune diseases.    Signaling description: IL-27 has recently been identified as a differentiation factor for the generation of IL10-producing regulatory type 1 (Tr1) T-cells. Three different pathways are induced by IL27 during Tr1 cell differentiation. IL27 drives the expression of the transcription factors Maf and AHR, which bind together to transactivate the IL21 and IL10 promoters. IL21 maintains Maf and AhR expression, while IL10 is essential for the suppressive function of Tr1 cells. IL27-induced AhR, alone or with an unknown cofactor, promotes Granzyme-B (GZMB) expression that mediates the contact-dependent suppressive activity of Tr1 cells. Finally IL27 promotes TBX21 expression that results in IFNG secretion.    Outcome effects: IFNG acts on DCs to enhance IL27 expression and further supports Tr1 cell differentiation. Transcription of ICOS is also induced by IL27 and promoted IL10 production. IL27 activates STAT1 and inhibits RORC expression through TBX21-dependent as well as TBX21-independent pathways. Alternatively, IL-27 can promote TBX-21expression in a STAT1 independent pathway via GADD45G. Inhibition of RORC leads to inhibition of Th17 development program."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Type 1 regulatory (Tr1) cells have emerged as key players in the prevention of autoimmunity. They produce high levels of the immunosuppressive IL10 and confer protection against a wide panel of autoimmune diseases.    Signaling description: IL-27 has recently been identified as a differentiation factor for the generation of IL10-producing regulatory type 1 (Tr1) T-cells. Three different pathways are induced by IL27 during Tr1 cell differentiation. IL27 drives the expression of the transcription factors Maf and AHR, which bind together to transactivate the IL21 and IL10 promoters. IL21 maintains Maf and AhR expression, while IL10 is essential for the suppressive function of Tr1 cells. IL27-induced AhR, alone or with an unknown cofactor, promotes Granzyme-B (GZMB) expression that mediates the contact-dependent suppressive activity of Tr1 cells. Finally IL27 promotes TBX21 expression that results in IFNG secretion.    Outcome effects: IFNG acts on DCs to enhance IL27 expression and further supports Tr1 cell differentiation. Transcription of ICOS is also induced by IL27 and promoted IL10 production. IL27 activates STAT1 and inhibits RORC expression through TBX21-dependent as well as TBX21-independent pathways. Alternatively, IL-27 can promote TBX-21expression in a STAT1 independent pathway via GADD45G. Inhibition of RORC leads to inhibition of Th17 development program." EXACT []

