xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AHR) is a ligand-activated helix-loop-helix transcription factor involved in the regulation of biological responses to planar aromatic hydrocarbons     Signaling description: Several arachidonic acid metabolites act as endogenous AHR ligands. Prostaglandins (PGF3alpha, PGG2, PGH1, PGB2, PGD2, PGD3, and PGH2), hydroxyeicosatrienoic acid (12-HETE) and lipoxin A4 are AHR inducers. Of these compounds, PGG2 and 12-HETE are the most potent and efficacious AHR activators and are capable of inducing AhR activity at nanomolar concentrations and, in some cases, inducing a 3- to 4-fold greater level of AHR-dependent reporter activity than dioxin."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AHR) is a ligand-activated helix-loop-helix transcription factor involved in the regulation of biological responses to planar aromatic hydrocarbons     Signaling description: Several arachidonic acid metabolites act as endogenous AHR ligands. Prostaglandins (PGF3alpha, PGG2, PGH1, PGB2, PGD2, PGD3, and PGH2), hydroxyeicosatrienoic acid (12-HETE) and lipoxin A4 are AHR inducers. Of these compounds, PGG2 and 12-HETE are the most potent and efficacious AHR activators and are capable of inducing AhR activity at nanomolar concentrations and, in some cases, inducing a 3- to 4-fold greater level of AHR-dependent reporter activity than dioxin." EXACT []

