xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AHR) is a ligand-activated helix-loop-helix transcription factor involved in the regulation of biological responses to planar aromatic hydrocarbons     Signaling description: Heme-derived molecules bilirubin and biliverdin act as endogenous AHR ligands. Because the bulk of bilirubin is conjugated to albumin and thereby unavailable as an AHR ligand, its effects may be local rather than systemic. It would be expected that they act in heme-rich organs such as liver and spleen.    Outcome effects: CYP1A1 and CYP1A2 are regulated by AHR and contribute to bilirubin catabolism suggesting a negative feedback loop."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AHR) is a ligand-activated helix-loop-helix transcription factor involved in the regulation of biological responses to planar aromatic hydrocarbons     Signaling description: Heme-derived molecules bilirubin and biliverdin act as endogenous AHR ligands. Because the bulk of bilirubin is conjugated to albumin and thereby unavailable as an AHR ligand, its effects may be local rather than systemic. It would be expected that they act in heme-rich organs such as liver and spleen.    Outcome effects: CYP1A1 and CYP1A2 are regulated by AHR and contribute to bilirubin catabolism suggesting a negative feedback loop." EXACT []

