xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AHR) is a ligand-activated helix-loop-helix transcription factor involved in the regulation of biological responses to planar aromatic hydrocarbons. In assition, AHR serves as part of a ligand-dependent E3-type ubiquitin ligase complex to regulate selective protein degradation.    Signaling description: Protein ubiquitination involves ubiquitin-activating enzyme (E1), ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme (E2) and ubiquitin protein ligase (E3), which acts as a bridge between E2 and the substrate. Ligand-bound AHR assembles into the CUL4B-based atypical E3 ubiquitin ligase complex CUL4B-AHR, which includes CUL4B, DNA-binding protein 1 (DDB1), RBX1, subunits of the 19S regulatory particle of the 26S proteasome, ARNT and transducin beta-like 3 (TBL3).    Outcome effects: AHR activation by such ligands as 3-methylcholanthrene and beta-naphthoflavone decreased the levels of endogenous estrogen receptors (ESR1/2) and androgen receptor (AR)."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AHR) is a ligand-activated helix-loop-helix transcription factor involved in the regulation of biological responses to planar aromatic hydrocarbons. In assition, AHR serves as part of a ligand-dependent E3-type ubiquitin ligase complex to regulate selective protein degradation.    Signaling description: Protein ubiquitination involves ubiquitin-activating enzyme (E1), ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme (E2) and ubiquitin protein ligase (E3), which acts as a bridge between E2 and the substrate. Ligand-bound AHR assembles into the CUL4B-based atypical E3 ubiquitin ligase complex CUL4B-AHR, which includes CUL4B, DNA-binding protein 1 (DDB1), RBX1, subunits of the 19S regulatory particle of the 26S proteasome, ARNT and transducin beta-like 3 (TBL3).    Outcome effects: AHR activation by such ligands as 3-methylcholanthrene and beta-naphthoflavone decreased the levels of endogenous estrogen receptors (ESR1/2) and androgen receptor (AR)." EXACT []

