xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The adrenergic receptors (adrenoceptors, AR) are a family prototypic G protein-coupled regulatory receptors. They include three alpha-1-AR subtypes (ADRA1A, ADRA1B, and ADRA1D), three alpha-2-AR (ADRA2A, ADRA2B, and ADRA2C) subtypes and beta-2-ARs (ADRB1, ADRB2, and ADRB3).    Outcome effects: Alpha-1-ARs activate mitogenic responses, regulate growth and proliferation of many cells, and mediate vasoconstriction. Alpha-2-ARs regulate presynaptic control of transmitter release from sympathetic nerves, vasoconstriction, and blood clotting. Beta-2ARs is involved in the regulation of lipid metabolism, thermogenesis, hippocampal function, vasodilation, heart muscle contractility, myometrium and bronchi contraction, memory, and kidney excretion."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The adrenergic receptors (adrenoceptors, AR) are a family prototypic G protein-coupled regulatory receptors. They include three alpha-1-AR subtypes (ADRA1A, ADRA1B, and ADRA1D), three alpha-2-AR (ADRA2A, ADRA2B, and ADRA2C) subtypes and beta-2-ARs (ADRB1, ADRB2, and ADRB3).    Outcome effects: Alpha-1-ARs activate mitogenic responses, regulate growth and proliferation of many cells, and mediate vasoconstriction. Alpha-2-ARs regulate presynaptic control of transmitter release from sympathetic nerves, vasoconstriction, and blood clotting. Beta-2ARs is involved in the regulation of lipid metabolism, thermogenesis, hippocampal function, vasodilation, heart muscle contractility, myometrium and bronchi contraction, memory, and kidney excretion." EXACT []

