xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Toll-like receptors (TLRs) recognize small molecular motifs found on pathogens known as pathogen-associated molecular patterns (PAMPs) and activate innate immune responses protecting the organism from infection.    Signaling description: There are four classes of viral PAMPs including double-stranded RNA (dsRNA), single-stranded RNA (ssRNA), unmethylated CpG DNA, and envelope glycoproteins. TLR3 binds to dsRNA, TLR7/8 binds to ssRNA, TLR9 binds to unmethylated CpG DNA, and TLR2/TLR4 binds to envelope glycoproteins. In addition, both DDX58 and IFIH1 have been identified as cytoplasmic sensors of dsRNA.    Outcome effects: TLRs act in a MYD88- and TICAM1-dependent manner and activate the expression of antiviral TNF and interferon I (IFNA1/IFNB1)."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Toll-like receptors (TLRs) recognize small molecular motifs found on pathogens known as pathogen-associated molecular patterns (PAMPs) and activate innate immune responses protecting the organism from infection.    Signaling description: There are four classes of viral PAMPs including double-stranded RNA (dsRNA), single-stranded RNA (ssRNA), unmethylated CpG DNA, and envelope glycoproteins. TLR3 binds to dsRNA, TLR7/8 binds to ssRNA, TLR9 binds to unmethylated CpG DNA, and TLR2/TLR4 binds to envelope glycoproteins. In addition, both DDX58 and IFIH1 have been identified as cytoplasmic sensors of dsRNA.    Outcome effects: TLRs act in a MYD88- and TICAM1-dependent manner and activate the expression of antiviral TNF and interferon I (IFNA1/IFNB1)." EXACT []

