xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Dectin-1 (CLEC7A) is a recognition receptor for pathogen-associated molecular patterns (PAMPs), which are small molecular motifs found on pathogens.    Signaling description: CLEC7A recognizes 1,3-beta-glucan expressed by fungal pathogens and leads to the activation of NF-kB through both SYK-dependent and SYK-independent pathways.    Outcome effects: The main result of the SYK-dependent pathway is the activation of calcineurin and promotion of the activation of NFATC2, leading to the expression of cytokines IL2, IL10, and COX2 (PTGS2). In the SYK-independent CLEC7A-related pathway, the activation of RAF1 or CARD9 leads to the phosphorylation and acetylation of NF-kB p65 subunit (RELA). The binding of acetylated p65 to the IL10 enhancer increases the transcription of the gene."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Dectin-1 (CLEC7A) is a recognition receptor for pathogen-associated molecular patterns (PAMPs), which are small molecular motifs found on pathogens.    Signaling description: CLEC7A recognizes 1,3-beta-glucan expressed by fungal pathogens and leads to the activation of NF-kB through both SYK-dependent and SYK-independent pathways.    Outcome effects: The main result of the SYK-dependent pathway is the activation of calcineurin and promotion of the activation of NFATC2, leading to the expression of cytokines IL2, IL10, and COX2 (PTGS2). In the SYK-independent CLEC7A-related pathway, the activation of RAF1 or CARD9 leads to the phosphorylation and acetylation of NF-kB p65 subunit (RELA). The binding of acetylated p65 to the IL10 enhancer increases the transcription of the gene." EXACT []

