xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: DC-SIGN (CD209) is a transmembrane receptor on the surface of dendritic cells and macrophages.    Signaling description: CD209 functions as a pattern recognition receptor that recognizes carbohydrate antigens of viruses, bacteria, and protozoa and modulates TLR4 signaling. Upon ligand binding, CD209 activates RAF1.    Outcome effects: RAF1 activation leads to the modulation of TLR-induced NF-kB activation resulting in an augmented production of the immunosuppressive cytokine, IL10."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: DC-SIGN (CD209) is a transmembrane receptor on the surface of dendritic cells and macrophages.    Signaling description: CD209 functions as a pattern recognition receptor that recognizes carbohydrate antigens of viruses, bacteria, and protozoa and modulates TLR4 signaling. Upon ligand binding, CD209 activates RAF1.    Outcome effects: RAF1 activation leads to the modulation of TLR-induced NF-kB activation resulting in an augmented production of the immunosuppressive cytokine, IL10." EXACT []

