xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: DCIR1 (CLEC4A) is a membrane receptor with an extracellular C-type lectin-like domain.    Signaling description: CLEC4A functions as a pattern recognition receptor that recognizes a variety of beta-1,3-linked and beta-1,6-linked glucans from fungi and plants, and thus, has a role in the innate immune response. CLEC4A is found to be expressed at high levels in blood monocytes, myeloid and plasmacytoid DCs, and macrophages, while occasionally in B-cells.    Outcome effects: The activation of CLEC4A leads to its internalization into endosomal compartments, which induces the activation of an unidentified signaling pathway that leads to the downregulation of TLR8-dependent IL12 and TNF expression or TLR9-dependent IFNG and TNF production by either myeloid or plasmacytoid cells."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: DCIR1 (CLEC4A) is a membrane receptor with an extracellular C-type lectin-like domain.    Signaling description: CLEC4A functions as a pattern recognition receptor that recognizes a variety of beta-1,3-linked and beta-1,6-linked glucans from fungi and plants, and thus, has a role in the innate immune response. CLEC4A is found to be expressed at high levels in blood monocytes, myeloid and plasmacytoid DCs, and macrophages, while occasionally in B-cells.    Outcome effects: The activation of CLEC4A leads to its internalization into endosomal compartments, which induces the activation of an unidentified signaling pathway that leads to the downregulation of TLR8-dependent IL12 and TNF expression or TLR9-dependent IFNG and TNF production by either myeloid or plasmacytoid cells." EXACT []

