xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Dectin-2 (CLEC6A), Mincle (CLEC4E) and BDCA2 (CLEC4C) are recognition receptors for pathogen-associated molecular patterns (PAMPs), which are small molecular motifs found on pathogens.    Signaling description: The Dectin-2, Mincle and BDCA2 receptors are involved in fungal recognition and modulation of the innate immune response. As a result of binding to PAMPs from fungi, these proteins form a complex consisting of BLNK, BTK, and PLCG2, which induces calcium (Ca2+) mobilization and transduces signals through an Fc receptor gamma chain (FCER1G) and SYK-CARD9-NF-kB-dependent pathway.    Outcome effects: The increase in Ca2+ appears to be involved in the inhibition of MYD88 adapter recruitment to TLR9 and in the reduction of the expression of IFNB1, TNF, and IL6. CLEC4C is a specific receptor for beta-glucans, which are polymers found in the cell walls of fungi such as the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Candida albicans. CLEC6A also recognizes, in a mannose-dependent manner, allergens from house dust and soluble elements from the eggs of Shistosoma mansoni altering adaptative immune responses. CLEC4E recognizes fungal alpha-mannose and the mycobacterial glycolipid, trehalose-6'6'-dimycolate (TDM), also known as cord factor of the immunostimulatory component of Mycobacterium tuberculosis. In addition, CLEC4E recognizes the endogenous damage-associated molecular patterns (DAMPs) on damaged cells."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Dectin-2 (CLEC6A), Mincle (CLEC4E) and BDCA2 (CLEC4C) are recognition receptors for pathogen-associated molecular patterns (PAMPs), which are small molecular motifs found on pathogens.    Signaling description: The Dectin-2, Mincle and BDCA2 receptors are involved in fungal recognition and modulation of the innate immune response. As a result of binding to PAMPs from fungi, these proteins form a complex consisting of BLNK, BTK, and PLCG2, which induces calcium (Ca2+) mobilization and transduces signals through an Fc receptor gamma chain (FCER1G) and SYK-CARD9-NF-kB-dependent pathway.    Outcome effects: The increase in Ca2+ appears to be involved in the inhibition of MYD88 adapter recruitment to TLR9 and in the reduction of the expression of IFNB1, TNF, and IL6. CLEC4C is a specific receptor for beta-glucans, which are polymers found in the cell walls of fungi such as the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Candida albicans. CLEC6A also recognizes, in a mannose-dependent manner, allergens from house dust and soluble elements from the eggs of Shistosoma mansoni altering adaptative immune responses. CLEC4E recognizes fungal alpha-mannose and the mycobacterial glycolipid, trehalose-6'6'-dimycolate (TDM), also known as cord factor of the immunostimulatory component of Mycobacterium tuberculosis. In addition, CLEC4E recognizes the endogenous damage-associated molecular patterns (DAMPs) on damaged cells." EXACT []

