xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: S-cells are located in the proximal small intestine and release secretin (SCT) in response to stomach acid.    Signaling description: Stomach acid activates the acid sensing ion channels in the proximal small intestine. These channels, in turn activate calcium channels. Both types of channels are responsible for calcium influx within the cell and activate phospholipase A2, which leads to secretin release. Overall, the details of SCT expression activation are poorly understood. Secretin initiates HCO3- anion secretion leading to pH increase.     Outcome effects: Secretin release from S-cells leads to the inhibition of stomach acid secretion and activation of the bile acid secretion."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: S-cells are located in the proximal small intestine and release secretin (SCT) in response to stomach acid.    Signaling description: Stomach acid activates the acid sensing ion channels in the proximal small intestine. These channels, in turn activate calcium channels. Both types of channels are responsible for calcium influx within the cell and activate phospholipase A2, which leads to secretin release. Overall, the details of SCT expression activation are poorly understood. Secretin initiates HCO3- anion secretion leading to pH increase.     Outcome effects: Secretin release from S-cells leads to the inhibition of stomach acid secretion and activation of the bile acid secretion." EXACT []

