xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: L-cells are located at the distal part of small intestine. These cells produce glucagon and peptide YY and secrete serotonin. Also, L-cells are involved in the intestinal carbohydrate absorption.    Signaling description: L-cells can be activated by many nutrients. The taste receptors (heterodimer TAS1R3/ TAS1R2 and TAS2Rs) interact with GNAT3 leading to activation of PLCB2/ITPR1/Ca2+ signaling. Other receptors activate ADCY/cAMP pathway via interaction with G-proteins. Both pathways lead to the activation of PKA and PKC. These protein kinases activate the expression of GCG. In addition, PKA activates the expression of proprotein convertases necessary for GCG processing. PKA and PKC stimulate PYY secretion. Dipeptidyl peptidase 4 (DPP4) is involved in the processing of both peptides: GCG and PYY. PKA regulates the expression of SLC5A1 which is a key player of intestinal carbohydrate absorption. PKC also regulates serotonin secretion.    Outcome effects: GCG and PYY produced by L-cells regulate appetite, satiety and insulin release."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: L-cells are located at the distal part of small intestine. These cells produce glucagon and peptide YY and secrete serotonin. Also, L-cells are involved in the intestinal carbohydrate absorption.    Signaling description: L-cells can be activated by many nutrients. The taste receptors (heterodimer TAS1R3/ TAS1R2 and TAS2Rs) interact with GNAT3 leading to activation of PLCB2/ITPR1/Ca2+ signaling. Other receptors activate ADCY/cAMP pathway via interaction with G-proteins. Both pathways lead to the activation of PKA and PKC. These protein kinases activate the expression of GCG. In addition, PKA activates the expression of proprotein convertases necessary for GCG processing. PKA and PKC stimulate PYY secretion. Dipeptidyl peptidase 4 (DPP4) is involved in the processing of both peptides: GCG and PYY. PKA regulates the expression of SLC5A1 which is a key player of intestinal carbohydrate absorption. PKC also regulates serotonin secretion.    Outcome effects: GCG and PYY produced by L-cells regulate appetite, satiety and insulin release." EXACT []

