xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Somatostatin (SST) is expressed in Delta cells (D-cells) under VIP control. Release of SST by D-cells is under the control of nutrients (L-amino acids and lysophosphatidic acid) and acetylcholine which is coming from vagus nerve.    Signaling description: VIP activates transcription of SST through cAMP/PKA/CREB1 signaling. L-amino acids and lysophosphatidic acid receptors activate PCLE1 through specific G-proteins. Gastrin receptor (CCKBR) interacts with GNAQ and activates PCLE1. Also, acetylcholine which is secreted from post-ganglionic fibers of vagus nerve interacts with cholinergic receptor (CHRM3) and activates PLCE1. PLC induces PKC activation and causes non-selective vesicle exocytosis and secretion of SST.     Outcome effects: Activation of acid sensing ion channel (ASIC1) by H+ leads to Ca2+ influx of and changes the membrane polarization state. Secreted SST inhibits gastrins expression from G-cells of stomach providing internal regulation feedback."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Somatostatin (SST) is expressed in Delta cells (D-cells) under VIP control. Release of SST by D-cells is under the control of nutrients (L-amino acids and lysophosphatidic acid) and acetylcholine which is coming from vagus nerve.    Signaling description: VIP activates transcription of SST through cAMP/PKA/CREB1 signaling. L-amino acids and lysophosphatidic acid receptors activate PCLE1 through specific G-proteins. Gastrin receptor (CCKBR) interacts with GNAQ and activates PCLE1. Also, acetylcholine which is secreted from post-ganglionic fibers of vagus nerve interacts with cholinergic receptor (CHRM3) and activates PLCE1. PLC induces PKC activation and causes non-selective vesicle exocytosis and secretion of SST.     Outcome effects: Activation of acid sensing ion channel (ASIC1) by H+ leads to Ca2+ influx of and changes the membrane polarization state. Secreted SST inhibits gastrins expression from G-cells of stomach providing internal regulation feedback." EXACT []

