xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: M-cells are located in the small intestine and secrete motilin (MLN), a small peptide hormone released in response to the bile acid signals.    Signaling description: Bile acid interacts with G protein-coupled bile acid receptor 1 (GPBAR1) on the surface of M-cells in the small intestine. Activation of GPBAR1 leads to cAMP synthesis and PKA activation. The precise mechanism of this signaling is unknown. The secretion of motilin can be blocked by acetylcholine (via CHRM1), histamine, ghrelin and glucose. Secreted motilin interacts with motilin receptor (MLNR) located on the postsynaptic surface of vagal nerves. Activation of MLNR leads to an increase of gastric motility. Also, MLNR can interact with arrestin beta 2 (ARRB2).    Outcome effects: Bile acid dependent secretion of motilin leads to gastric motility activation."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: M-cells are located in the small intestine and secrete motilin (MLN), a small peptide hormone released in response to the bile acid signals.    Signaling description: Bile acid interacts with G protein-coupled bile acid receptor 1 (GPBAR1) on the surface of M-cells in the small intestine. Activation of GPBAR1 leads to cAMP synthesis and PKA activation. The precise mechanism of this signaling is unknown. The secretion of motilin can be blocked by acetylcholine (via CHRM1), histamine, ghrelin and glucose. Secreted motilin interacts with motilin receptor (MLNR) located on the postsynaptic surface of vagal nerves. Activation of MLNR leads to an increase of gastric motility. Also, MLNR can interact with arrestin beta 2 (ARRB2).    Outcome effects: Bile acid dependent secretion of motilin leads to gastric motility activation." EXACT []

