xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The activation of A-cells (stomach enteroendocrine cells similar to X-cells) is part of the digestive process. Activation of A-cells leads to the expression and release of ghrelin and nesfatin-1 and initiates interaction of nutrients with taste receptors.    Signaling description: The core of taste receptor related signaling leads to NUCB2 transcription activation and repression of GHR genes through two signaling pathways: PLCbeta/Ca2+ and cAMP signaling. The mechanisms of activation ghrelin expression and release are still not known. The taste receptor signaling pathways lead to the repression of ghrelin synthesis and nesfatin-1 release. Notably, ghrelin is released in the first wave of secretion, and nesfatin-1 in the second wave (10-20 minutes following ghreli release). The precise mechanism of this process is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is depicted on the pathway.    Outcome effects: Ghrelin expression stimulates pancreatic juice secretion, gastric motility activation and growth hormone release; also, ghrelin blocks the sense of satiety. Nesfatin-1 expression leads to satiety and blocks gastric motility."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The activation of A-cells (stomach enteroendocrine cells similar to X-cells) is part of the digestive process. Activation of A-cells leads to the expression and release of ghrelin and nesfatin-1 and initiates interaction of nutrients with taste receptors.    Signaling description: The core of taste receptor related signaling leads to NUCB2 transcription activation and repression of GHR genes through two signaling pathways: PLCbeta/Ca2+ and cAMP signaling. The mechanisms of activation ghrelin expression and release are still not known. The taste receptor signaling pathways lead to the repression of ghrelin synthesis and nesfatin-1 release. Notably, ghrelin is released in the first wave of secretion, and nesfatin-1 in the second wave (10-20 minutes following ghreli release). The precise mechanism of this process is poorly understood. One of hypotheses is depicted on the pathway.    Outcome effects: Ghrelin expression stimulates pancreatic juice secretion, gastric motility activation and growth hormone release; also, ghrelin blocks the sense of satiety. Nesfatin-1 expression leads to satiety and blocks gastric motility." EXACT []

