xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Activation of enterochromaffin-like cells (ECL-cell) of the stomach is one of the major mechanisms of digestion. ECL-cells do not contact with the lumen and are activated by signals from other cells, as well as mechanical signals.    Signaling description: Gastrins and PACAPs (products of adenylate cyclase activating polypeptide 1) activate signaling through phospholipase C: inositol-induced intra cellular calcium influx and PKA activation. Calcium influx also occurs by piezo type mechanosensitive ion channel (PIEZO2) which is sensitive to mechanical stretch. PACAPs also activate the ADCY/cAMP/PKA pathway through VIPR1. Activated PKA phosphorylates transcription factors CREB1 and SP1. CREB1 activates the transcription of CXCL8 and IL2 which are both are necessary for the immune response. In addition, CREB1 activates transcription of histidine decarboxylase (HDC) and pancreastatin precursor - chromogranin A (CHGA). HDC synthesizes histamine, which is loaded to vesicles by SLC18A2 and secreted following intracellular calcium overload. Secretion of histamine is necessary for stomach related secretion. Transcription of CHGA is under the control of SP1. Pancreastatin inhibits secretion of INS. Also, pancreastatin activates stomach acid secretion and inhibits pancreatic juice secretion.    Outcome effects: Activated stomach ECL-cells stimulate stomach-dependent secretion through histamine and pancreastatin release."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Activation of enterochromaffin-like cells (ECL-cell) of the stomach is one of the major mechanisms of digestion. ECL-cells do not contact with the lumen and are activated by signals from other cells, as well as mechanical signals.    Signaling description: Gastrins and PACAPs (products of adenylate cyclase activating polypeptide 1) activate signaling through phospholipase C: inositol-induced intra cellular calcium influx and PKA activation. Calcium influx also occurs by piezo type mechanosensitive ion channel (PIEZO2) which is sensitive to mechanical stretch. PACAPs also activate the ADCY/cAMP/PKA pathway through VIPR1. Activated PKA phosphorylates transcription factors CREB1 and SP1. CREB1 activates the transcription of CXCL8 and IL2 which are both are necessary for the immune response. In addition, CREB1 activates transcription of histidine decarboxylase (HDC) and pancreastatin precursor - chromogranin A (CHGA). HDC synthesizes histamine, which is loaded to vesicles by SLC18A2 and secreted following intracellular calcium overload. Secretion of histamine is necessary for stomach related secretion. Transcription of CHGA is under the control of SP1. Pancreastatin inhibits secretion of INS. Also, pancreastatin activates stomach acid secretion and inhibits pancreatic juice secretion.    Outcome effects: Activated stomach ECL-cells stimulate stomach-dependent secretion through histamine and pancreastatin release." EXACT []

