[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-06364bec-fb61-4f66-94c8-25baa54b1ecb
name: Oncogene Induced Cellular Senescence
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:o ! O
is_a: urn:agi-folder:generic ! Generic
is_a: urn:agi-folder:cell_responses_associated_with_aging ! Cell responses associated with aging
xref: PS:Description "Oncogene-induced senescence (OIS) is anti-proliferative response within the cell. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Oncogene-induced senescence (OIS) is anti-proliferative response within the cell. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:PMID "18193093"
synonym: "PMID: 18193093" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-06364bec-fb61-4f66-94c8-25baa54b1ecb"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-06364bec-fb61-4f66-94c8-25baa54b1ecb" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "stem cell"
synonym: "CellType: stem cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "generic"
synonym: "Organ_System: generic" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "generic"
synonym: "Tissue: generic" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "generic"
synonym: "Organ: generic" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Oncogene-induced senescence (OIS) is anti-proliferative response within the cell as a result of activating mutation of an oncogene, or the inactivation of a tumor-suppressor gene (Chandeck C, 2010). Pathology of OIS is characterized with proliferative arrest and tumor suppression, cellular dysfunction of normal physiological functions, impact on other cells by secreting soluble factors such as cytokines, growth factors and proteases.     Signaling description: Altered forms of PTEN , NF1 and KRAS cause changes in RAF/RAS and AKT1 downstream signalings. The core of AKT1 related signaling through MTOR regulates cell growth and autophagy. The core of RAS/RAF related signaling through MAPK cascade regulates cell cycle and mitosis. Precise mechanism of the molecular signaling on this pathway is well known and is associated with activation and accumulation of JUN/FOS, TP53 and CDKN2A. RB1 lies downstream JUN/FOS, TP53 and its persistent inhibition in OIS leads to mitosis arrest. Activated TP53 also is involved in DNA damage response regulation.    Outcome effects: A lot of proteins are changing their expression due to signaling activation in OIS. Specificity of changing in protein expression profile is depends of cell type. Lysosome protein GLB1 accumulation in cytoplasm is proposed to be one of the common marker for altered senescent cell morphology. Altered regulation of histone methyltransferase SUV39H1 in OIS could lead to changes in chromatin and transcriptional repression due to formation of senescence-associated heterochromatic foci (SAHFs).     Highlighted proteins: NF1 and SPRED1 with blue highlights have reduced expression/activity in human neurofibromas. LMNB1 with blue highlights has reduced expression/activity in human OIS fibroblasts, melanocytes and in liver of irradiated mice. For references see \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Aging\" pathway."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Oncogene-induced senescence (OIS) is anti-proliferative response within the cell as a result of activating mutation of an oncogene, or the inactivation of a tumor-suppressor gene (Chandeck C, 2010). Pathology of OIS is characterized with proliferative arrest and tumor suppression, cellular dysfunction of normal physiological functions, impact on other cells by secreting soluble factors such as cytokines, growth factors and proteases.     Signaling description: Altered forms of PTEN , NF1 and KRAS cause changes in RAF/RAS and AKT1 downstream signalings. The core of AKT1 related signaling through MTOR regulates cell growth and autophagy. The core of RAS/RAF related signaling through MAPK cascade regulates cell cycle and mitosis. Precise mechanism of the molecular signaling on this pathway is well known and is associated with activation and accumulation of JUN/FOS, TP53 and CDKN2A. RB1 lies downstream JUN/FOS, TP53 and its persistent inhibition in OIS leads to mitosis arrest. Activated TP53 also is involved in DNA damage response regulation.    Outcome effects: A lot of proteins are changing their expression due to signaling activation in OIS. Specificity of changing in protein expression profile is depends of cell type. Lysosome protein GLB1 accumulation in cytoplasm is proposed to be one of the common marker for altered senescent cell morphology. Altered regulation of histone methyltransferase SUV39H1 in OIS could lead to changes in chromatin and transcriptional repression due to formation of senescence-associated heterochromatic foci (SAHFs).     Highlighted proteins: NF1 and SPRED1 with blue highlights have reduced expression/activity in human neurofibromas. LMNB1 with blue highlights has reduced expression/activity in human OIS fibroblasts, melanocytes and in liver of irradiated mice. For references see \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Aging\" pathway." EXACT []

