xref: PS:Notes "MTHFR converts folate to its active form, 5-methyltetrahydrofolate, which is a necessary co-factor in methionine cycle and is involved in the production of universal methyl donor S-adenosylmethionine. The decreased production of 5-methyltetrahydrofolate due to an altered MTHFR function may lead to the accumulation of non-metabolized Hcy, which may cause cell senescence."
synonym: "Notes: MTHFR converts folate to its active form, 5-methyltetrahydrofolate, which is a necessary co-factor in methionine cycle and is involved in the production of universal methyl donor S-adenosylmethionine. The decreased production of 5-methyltetrahydrofolate due to an altered MTHFR function may lead to the accumulation of non-metabolized Hcy, which may cause cell senescence." EXACT []

