xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Sirtuins are proteins with deacetylase and/or ADP-ribosyltransferase activities. SIRT2 regulates a variety of biological processes, such as stress response, differentiation, metabolism, and aging.    Signaling description: SIRT2 requires NAD for its deacetylase activity. NAD+ is a classic co-enzyme that is synthesized from three major precursors - tryptophan, nicotinic acid, and nicotinamide. The level of NAD+ changes during oxidative stress or inflammation and probably with aging.    Outcome effects: NAD+ dependency of sirtuins can provide the link between metabolic activity and genome stability during aging. SIRT2 is highly expressed in the brain and can be implicated in the brain aging probably by participation in neuron cytoskeleton regulation. The role of SIRT2 in the regulation of gluconeogenesis was also shown."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Sirtuins are proteins with deacetylase and/or ADP-ribosyltransferase activities. SIRT2 regulates a variety of biological processes, such as stress response, differentiation, metabolism, and aging.    Signaling description: SIRT2 requires NAD for its deacetylase activity. NAD+ is a classic co-enzyme that is synthesized from three major precursors - tryptophan, nicotinic acid, and nicotinamide. The level of NAD+ changes during oxidative stress or inflammation and probably with aging.    Outcome effects: NAD+ dependency of sirtuins can provide the link between metabolic activity and genome stability during aging. SIRT2 is highly expressed in the brain and can be implicated in the brain aging probably by participation in neuron cytoskeleton regulation. The role of SIRT2 in the regulation of gluconeogenesis was also shown." EXACT []

