xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Sirtuins are proteins with deacetylase and/or ADP-ribosyltransferase activities. Mitochondrial SIRT3 plays role in reduction of oxidative damage.    Signaling description: SIRT3 requires NAD for its deacetylase activity. NAD+ is a classic co-enzyme that is synthesized from three major precursors - tryptophan, nicotinic acid, and nicotinamide. The level of NAD+ changes during oxidative stress or inflammation and probably with aging. SIRT3 plays role in reduction of oxidative damage in the cell via regulation of mitochondrial enzymes as well as tricarboxylic acid cycle and overall cell signalings regulation.    Outcome effects: NAD+ dependency of SIRT3 can provide the one of the link between metabolic activity and mitochondrial function during aging. SIRT3 also was shown to important in the caloric restriction - related prevention of age-related hearing loss in mammals.    Mutated proteins: G477T polymorphism of the SIRT3 gene, was found in the elderly to be associated with longevity. See all references in \"\"Genes with Mutations Associated with Aging\"\" pathway."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Sirtuins are proteins with deacetylase and/or ADP-ribosyltransferase activities. Mitochondrial SIRT3 plays role in reduction of oxidative damage.    Signaling description: SIRT3 requires NAD for its deacetylase activity. NAD+ is a classic co-enzyme that is synthesized from three major precursors - tryptophan, nicotinic acid, and nicotinamide. The level of NAD+ changes during oxidative stress or inflammation and probably with aging. SIRT3 plays role in reduction of oxidative damage in the cell via regulation of mitochondrial enzymes as well as tricarboxylic acid cycle and overall cell signalings regulation.    Outcome effects: NAD+ dependency of SIRT3 can provide the one of the link between metabolic activity and mitochondrial function during aging. SIRT3 also was shown to important in the caloric restriction - related prevention of age-related hearing loss in mammals.    Mutated proteins: G477T polymorphism of the SIRT3 gene, was found in the elderly to be associated with longevity. See all references in \"\"Genes with Mutations Associated with Aging\"\" pathway." EXACT []

