xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: The DNA damage response (DDR) is an evolutionarily conserved mechanism that senses DNA breaks and activates downstream DNA repair and cell cycle checkpoints signalings.    Signaling description: DDR begins with the recruitment of ATM to DNA double-strand breaks. ATM phosphorylates substrates in the chromatin (such as H2AFX). Phosphorylated H2AFX recruits additional DDR mediators, including MDC1.    Outcome effects: Irreparable DNA lesions trigger cell cycle arrest, apoptosis or cell senescence.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red. For references see \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Aging\" pathway."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: The DNA damage response (DDR) is an evolutionarily conserved mechanism that senses DNA breaks and activates downstream DNA repair and cell cycle checkpoints signalings.    Signaling description: DDR begins with the recruitment of ATM to DNA double-strand breaks. ATM phosphorylates substrates in the chromatin (such as H2AFX). Phosphorylated H2AFX recruits additional DDR mediators, including MDC1.    Outcome effects: Irreparable DNA lesions trigger cell cycle arrest, apoptosis or cell senescence.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red. For references see \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Aging\" pathway." EXACT []

