xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Sirtuins are proteins with deacetylase and/or ADP-ribosyltransferase activities. SIRT4 is a mitochondrial protein more efficiently works as an ADP-ribosyltransferase than deacetylase.    Signaling description: SIRT4 controls glutamate metabolism through GLUD1 and may participate in insulin secretion regulation. SIRT4 may regulate mitochondrial ATP homeostasis via the ANT2 feedback loop involving AMPK.    Outcome effects: SIRT4 is considered as a regulator of glucose and lipid homeostasis during pancreas and hepatic aging or synaptic activity regulator during brain aging."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Sirtuins are proteins with deacetylase and/or ADP-ribosyltransferase activities. SIRT4 is a mitochondrial protein more efficiently works as an ADP-ribosyltransferase than deacetylase.    Signaling description: SIRT4 controls glutamate metabolism through GLUD1 and may participate in insulin secretion regulation. SIRT4 may regulate mitochondrial ATP homeostasis via the ANT2 feedback loop involving AMPK.    Outcome effects: SIRT4 is considered as a regulator of glucose and lipid homeostasis during pancreas and hepatic aging or synaptic activity regulator during brain aging." EXACT []

