xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: DNA replication errors are a major source of unrepaired single-stranded (ss) or double-stranded DNA (dsDNA) lesions. As a result, inaccuracies in maintaining telomeres and nucleosomes, transcription of genes and remodeling of chromatin accumulate.    Signaling description: Initiation of DNA replication is a two-step process: origin licensing and firing. Origin licensing starts in early G1 with the assembly of a pre-replicative complex (pre-RC). The pre-RC consists of the origin of replication recognition complex, CDC6, CDT1 and MCM helicase complex. The second step, origin firing, involves the activation MCM helicase complex in S phase. Replication stress induced by trigger results in the generation of single strand DNA bound by RPA protein.    Outcome effects: Under conditions of persistent replication stress, the cell may not be able to repair DNA double strand break which is lead to activation DNA damage signaling and persisted DNA repair.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red. For references see pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Aging\"."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: DNA replication errors are a major source of unrepaired single-stranded (ss) or double-stranded DNA (dsDNA) lesions. As a result, inaccuracies in maintaining telomeres and nucleosomes, transcription of genes and remodeling of chromatin accumulate.    Signaling description: Initiation of DNA replication is a two-step process: origin licensing and firing. Origin licensing starts in early G1 with the assembly of a pre-replicative complex (pre-RC). The pre-RC consists of the origin of replication recognition complex, CDC6, CDT1 and MCM helicase complex. The second step, origin firing, involves the activation MCM helicase complex in S phase. Replication stress induced by trigger results in the generation of single strand DNA bound by RPA protein.    Outcome effects: Under conditions of persistent replication stress, the cell may not be able to repair DNA double strand break which is lead to activation DNA damage signaling and persisted DNA repair.    Highlighted proteins: Proteins with decreased expression or activity are highlighted in blue. Proteins with increased expression or activity are highlighted in red. For references see pathway \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Aging\"." EXACT []

