xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: One of the main epigenetic feature of the centenarian sample is its low DNA methylation density at CpG-poor promoters and tissue-specific genes. DNA methylation age lies in the Horvath's epigenetic clock method which allows comparing the ages of different areas of the human body using the same aging clock. Non-LTR type retrotransposons (which includes LINEs (long interspersed elements) and SINEs (short interspersed elements)) are sequences of DNA that can move within the genome. Retrotransposons that inserts itself into genome can disable genes and destabilize the genome.    Outcome effects: Methylated genes and histones and mobile elements alter normal transcription, lead to mutations accumulation and in the whole trigger cell senescence."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: One of the main epigenetic feature of the centenarian sample is its low DNA methylation density at CpG-poor promoters and tissue-specific genes. DNA methylation age lies in the Horvath's epigenetic clock method which allows comparing the ages of different areas of the human body using the same aging clock. Non-LTR type retrotransposons (which includes LINEs (long interspersed elements) and SINEs (short interspersed elements)) are sequences of DNA that can move within the genome. Retrotransposons that inserts itself into genome can disable genes and destabilize the genome.    Outcome effects: Methylated genes and histones and mobile elements alter normal transcription, lead to mutations accumulation and in the whole trigger cell senescence." EXACT []

