xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Sirtuins are proteins with deacetylase and/or ADP-ribosyltransferase activities. In aged people the higher protein level of SIRT1 was observed. SNV in SIRT1 was found to be significantly associated with longevity and telomere length.    Signaling description: SIRT1 is a deacetylase which has a wide array of targets in the nucleus and cytoplasm. SIRT1 requires NAD+ for its function. NAD+ is a classic co-enzyme that is synthesized from three major precursors - tryptophan, nicotinic acid, and nicotinamide. The level of NAD+ changes during oxidative stress or inflammation and probably with aging.    Outcome effects: Activated SIRT1 can play protective role in cell stress response by decreasing transcription or protein synthesis and reducing oxidative stress. NAD+ dependency of sirtuins can provide the link between metabolic activity and genome stability during aging.    Highlighted proteins: SIRT1 with red highlights have increased expression/activity in some older people (above 55 years) compared with younger people. See all references in \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Aging\" pathway.    Mutated proteins: SNV (rs7896005) in SIRT1 was found to be significantly associated with longevity and telomere length. See all references in \"\"Genes with Mutations Associated with Aging\"\" pathway."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Sirtuins are proteins with deacetylase and/or ADP-ribosyltransferase activities. In aged people the higher protein level of SIRT1 was observed. SNV in SIRT1 was found to be significantly associated with longevity and telomere length.    Signaling description: SIRT1 is a deacetylase which has a wide array of targets in the nucleus and cytoplasm. SIRT1 requires NAD+ for its function. NAD+ is a classic co-enzyme that is synthesized from three major precursors - tryptophan, nicotinic acid, and nicotinamide. The level of NAD+ changes during oxidative stress or inflammation and probably with aging.    Outcome effects: Activated SIRT1 can play protective role in cell stress response by decreasing transcription or protein synthesis and reducing oxidative stress. NAD+ dependency of sirtuins can provide the link between metabolic activity and genome stability during aging.    Highlighted proteins: SIRT1 with red highlights have increased expression/activity in some older people (above 55 years) compared with younger people. See all references in \"Proteins with Altered Expression in Aging\" pathway.    Mutated proteins: SNV (rs7896005) in SIRT1 was found to be significantly associated with longevity and telomere length. See all references in \"\"Genes with Mutations Associated with Aging\"\" pathway." EXACT []

