xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Prolactin (PRL) is the protein hormone that enables female mammals to produce milk.Signaling descripton: PRL's main function in women is to stimulate and maintain the breastfeeding directly acting on lactotrophs cells of the mammary glands. PRL is the hormone primarily responsible for the synthesis of milk proteins, lactose, and lipids, all major components of milk.    Outcome effects: Functional development of mammary epithelium during pregnancy depends mostly on PRL signaling. Proliferation and differentiation of secretory mammary epithelium is dependent on PRL and JAK2-STAT5 pathway."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Prolactin (PRL) is the protein hormone that enables female mammals to produce milk.Signaling descripton: PRL's main function in women is to stimulate and maintain the breastfeeding directly acting on lactotrophs cells of the mammary glands. PRL is the hormone primarily responsible for the synthesis of milk proteins, lactose, and lipids, all major components of milk.    Outcome effects: Functional development of mammary epithelium during pregnancy depends mostly on PRL signaling. Proliferation and differentiation of secretory mammary epithelium is dependent on PRL and JAK2-STAT5 pathway." EXACT []

