xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Oxytocin, along with prolactin, is essential for milk delivery to the baby during lactation.    Signaling description: Suckling stimulates the nipple to send a neural signal through an ascending neuronal pathway from the nipple to the hypothalamus to stimulate oxytocin release from the posterior lobe of the pituitary gland, which in turn acts on the mammary glands to cause milk ejection, this is called the milk ejection reflex."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Oxytocin, along with prolactin, is essential for milk delivery to the baby during lactation.    Signaling description: Suckling stimulates the nipple to send a neural signal through an ascending neuronal pathway from the nipple to the hypothalamus to stimulate oxytocin release from the posterior lobe of the pituitary gland, which in turn acts on the mammary glands to cause milk ejection, this is called the milk ejection reflex." EXACT []

