xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Prolactin (PRL) is the protein hormone that enables female mammals to produce milk.    Signaling description: BMP4 and TGFB1 have an important role in lactotroph physiology and prolactin (PRL) expression. While, SMAD 2/4 complex is responsible for TGFB1-induced inhibition, SMAD1/4 participates in the stimulatory action of BMP-4.    Outcome effects: A physical interaction between SMAD proteins and ESR1 has been shown. BMP-4 or estrogen treatment induces a direct physical interaction between the ESR1 and SMAD-4/1 complex. In contrast, treatment with TGFB1 induces a physical interaction between ESR1 and SMAD-4/2 complex, but not with SMAD1.    References: 1). Allyson K. Booth AK, Gutierrez-Hartmann A. Lactotrope Homeostasis and Tumorigenesis Chapter. 2. Signaling Pathways Regulating Pituitary. Available from: http://www.springer.com/cda/content/document/cda_downloaddocument/9783319121130-c1.pdf?SGWID0-0-45-1488650-p177017112."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Prolactin (PRL) is the protein hormone that enables female mammals to produce milk.    Signaling description: BMP4 and TGFB1 have an important role in lactotroph physiology and prolactin (PRL) expression. While, SMAD 2/4 complex is responsible for TGFB1-induced inhibition, SMAD1/4 participates in the stimulatory action of BMP-4.    Outcome effects: A physical interaction between SMAD proteins and ESR1 has been shown. BMP-4 or estrogen treatment induces a direct physical interaction between the ESR1 and SMAD-4/1 complex. In contrast, treatment with TGFB1 induces a physical interaction between ESR1 and SMAD-4/2 complex, but not with SMAD1.    References: 1). Allyson K. Booth AK, Gutierrez-Hartmann A. Lactotrope Homeostasis and Tumorigenesis Chapter. 2. Signaling Pathways Regulating Pituitary. Available from: http://www.springer.com/cda/content/document/cda_downloaddocument/9783319121130-c1.pdf?SGWID0-0-45-1488650-p177017112." EXACT []

