xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Prolactin (PRL) is the protein hormone that enables female mammals to produce milk.    Signaling description: Dopamine is produced by tuberoinfundibular dopamine (TIDA) neurons of the arcuate nucleus of the hypothalamus. It has been shown that prolactin (PRL) stimulates activity and transcription of tyrosine hydroxylase (TH), which would increase the stores of dopamine available for release.    Outcome effects: Dopanine is a well-known inhibitor of PRL production and release. Thereby, the high level of PRL promotes a negative feedback mechanism."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Prolactin (PRL) is the protein hormone that enables female mammals to produce milk.    Signaling description: Dopamine is produced by tuberoinfundibular dopamine (TIDA) neurons of the arcuate nucleus of the hypothalamus. It has been shown that prolactin (PRL) stimulates activity and transcription of tyrosine hydroxylase (TH), which would increase the stores of dopamine available for release.    Outcome effects: Dopanine is a well-known inhibitor of PRL production and release. Thereby, the high level of PRL promotes a negative feedback mechanism." EXACT []

