[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-9fe11ece-b51d-477b-b7e0-6e55527e6a05
name: Leukocyte Adhesion to Endothelial Cell
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:vascular_system_response ! Vascular system response
is_a: urn:agi-folder:lymphatic_system ! Lymphatic system
is_a: urn:agi-folder:l ! L
xref: PS:Description "Endothelial cells are involved in many aspects of vascular biology including inflammation and angiogenesis. Pathway is built manually using published studies."
synonym: "Description: Endothelial cells are involved in many aspects of vascular biology including inflammation and angiogenesis. Pathway is built manually using published studies." EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-9fe11ece-b51d-477b-b7e0-6e55527e6a05"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-9fe11ece-b51d-477b-b7e0-6e55527e6a05" EXACT []
xref: PS:CellType "endothelial cell"
xref: PS:CellType "leukocyte"
synonym: "CellType: endothelial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "CellType: leukocyte" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "lymphatic system"
synonym: "Organ_System: lymphatic system" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "blood vessel"
synonym: "Organ: blood vessel" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Biological Process"
synonym: "Source: Biological Process" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Headnote: Endothelial cells are involved in many aspects of vascular biology including inflammation and angiogenesis. Endothelial-leukocyte cell adhesion plays a major role in cellular communication and regulation and is significant for the development and maintenance of tissues.    Signaling description: Leukocytes are key players in the inflammatory response due to their antimicrobial, secretory, and phagocytic activities. Leukocytes leave the circulation after passing through the endothelial layer.The process of leukocyte adhesion to the endothelium involves three stages: rolling, integrin activation, and stable adhesion followed by migration through the endothelium. At each stage, special intracellular molecular bonds are required. On the endothelial cell surface, SELE and SELP are initially involved in the process of leukocyte-endothelial cell interaction. In addition, cell adhesion molecules, such as ICAM and VCAM, on the surface of endothelial cells are key proteins that provide endothelial cell adhesiveness.    Outcome effects: The passage of leukocytes through the endothelium requires the activation of leukocyte motility via a family of integrins on the surface of leukocytes. Integrin-related intra-leukocyte signaling occurs through the activation of actin-linked proteins including ACTN1, VCL, PTK2, and TLN1. The activation of actin filaments results in contraction of the cell, which helps the passage of leukocytes through the extracellular space (for more details, see \"\"Neutrophil Activation via Adherence on Endothelial Cells\"\")."
synonym: "Notes: Headnote: Endothelial cells are involved in many aspects of vascular biology including inflammation and angiogenesis. Endothelial-leukocyte cell adhesion plays a major role in cellular communication and regulation and is significant for the development and maintenance of tissues.    Signaling description: Leukocytes are key players in the inflammatory response due to their antimicrobial, secretory, and phagocytic activities. Leukocytes leave the circulation after passing through the endothelial layer.The process of leukocyte adhesion to the endothelium involves three stages: rolling, integrin activation, and stable adhesion followed by migration through the endothelium. At each stage, special intracellular molecular bonds are required. On the endothelial cell surface, SELE and SELP are initially involved in the process of leukocyte-endothelial cell interaction. In addition, cell adhesion molecules, such as ICAM and VCAM, on the surface of endothelial cells are key proteins that provide endothelial cell adhesiveness.    Outcome effects: The passage of leukocytes through the endothelium requires the activation of leukocyte motility via a family of integrins on the surface of leukocytes. Integrin-related intra-leukocyte signaling occurs through the activation of actin-linked proteins including ACTN1, VCL, PTK2, and TLN1. The activation of actin filaments results in contraction of the cell, which helps the passage of leukocytes through the extracellular space (for more details, see \"\"Neutrophil Activation via Adherence on Endothelial Cells\"\")." EXACT []

