synonym: "Organ: skin" EXACT []
xref: PS:Tissue "epidermis"
synonym: "Tissue: epidermis" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "integumentary system"
synonym: "Organ_System: integumentary system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "The acute phase, which is characterized by eczematous skin lesions,  is facilitated by allergen/IgE-bound Langerhans cells (LCs) and by IgE activated  mast cells.  Eczematous skin lesions develop as a result of the complex immune  and inflammatory responses driven by the release of proinflammatory  cytokines and chemokines from various skin-resident cell types.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: The acute phase, which is characterized by eczematous skin lesions,  is facilitated by allergen/IgE-bound Langerhans cells (LCs) and by IgE activated  mast cells.  Eczematous skin lesions develop as a result of the complex immune  and inflammatory responses driven by the release of proinflammatory  cytokines and chemokines from various skin-resident cell types.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

[Term]
