xref: PS:Notes "Psoriasis skin lesions contain increased amounts of T-helper 17 (Th17)  cells. Genetic mutations and environmental factors together act to dysregulate  the differentiation of the skin T cells and induce a shift to Th17 cell  production.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Psoriasis skin lesions contain increased amounts of T-helper 17 (Th17)  cells. Genetic mutations and environmental factors together act to dysregulate  the differentiation of the skin T cells and induce a shift to Th17 cell  production.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-93934c80-7fa4-4cb3-b168-2950e1bbf31a
name: 2_Interleukin-17 and interleukin-22 signaling in psoriasis
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
