xref: PS:Notes "Loss-of-function mutations in the gene encoding steroid sulfatase (STS)  were found in patients with X-linked ichthyosis. STS hydrolyzes several  3-beta-hydroxysteroid sulfates, which are metabolic precursors of estrogens,  androgens, and cholesterol. STS is ubiquitously expressed in tissues.  Nonfunctional STS reduces the available cholesterol to form the extracellular  lamellar bilayers in the skin.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Loss-of-function mutations in the gene encoding steroid sulfatase (STS)  were found in patients with X-linked ichthyosis. STS hydrolyzes several  3-beta-hydroxysteroid sulfates, which are metabolic precursors of estrogens,  androgens, and cholesterol. STS is ubiquitously expressed in tissues.  Nonfunctional STS reduces the available cholesterol to form the extracellular  lamellar bilayers in the skin.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

