synonym: "Organ: bone" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "skeletal system"
synonym: "Organ_System: skeletal system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "The excessive mechanical loading of cartilage is a proven trigger of osteoarthritis.  The mechanical stress initiates the release of proinflammatory  cytokines, which alter the normal function of chondrocytes and lead to  cartilage damage.  The cartilage ECM is made of water, collagens (type II), proteoglycans,  and hydrophilic macromolecules. Overexpressed in OA, aggrecanases,  metalloproteinases, and collagenases break down components of  the cartilage ECM. The progressive inflammation in OA leads to cartilage  degradation and a breakdown of all joint tissues (bone, synovium, and  ligaments).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: The excessive mechanical loading of cartilage is a proven trigger of osteoarthritis.  The mechanical stress initiates the release of proinflammatory  cytokines, which alter the normal function of chondrocytes and lead to  cartilage damage.  The cartilage ECM is made of water, collagens (type II), proteoglycans,  and hydrophilic macromolecules. Overexpressed in OA, aggrecanases,  metalloproteinases, and collagenases break down components of  the cartilage ECM. The progressive inflammation in OA leads to cartilage  degradation and a breakdown of all joint tissues (bone, synovium, and  ligaments).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

