xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Usually, estrogen  acts via the estrogen receptor 1 (ESR1) resulting in osteoblast proliferation  and differentiation. In postmenopausal osteoporosis, the lack of  osteoblast function is due to a deficiency of estrogens.  The deficiency of estrogens and polymorphisms in the genes encoding  osteoclast-specific proteins leads to impaired osteoblast function affecting  bone matrix formation and bone biomineralization.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Usually, estrogen  acts via the estrogen receptor 1 (ESR1) resulting in osteoblast proliferation  and differentiation. In postmenopausal osteoporosis, the lack of  osteoblast function is due to a deficiency of estrogens.  The deficiency of estrogens and polymorphisms in the genes encoding  osteoclast-specific proteins leads to impaired osteoblast function affecting  bone matrix formation and bone biomineralization.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

