synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-a1a87aa4-c0b0-46b4-ba17-cc561952d255" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "urinary tract"
synonym: "Organ_System: urinary tract" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "The molecular mechanisms underlying polycystic kidney disease development  are not entirely understood. The pathogenesis of this disease  results from cyst formation in the renal tubules and the subsequent tubule  dysfunction. The cysts are probably formed as dilations in the renal tubules  as a result of increased cellular proliferation and growth. An abnormal  epithelial cell phenotype and extracellular matrix alterations result in spherical but not tubular structures.  Disruption of the activity of the polycystins on renal epithelial cell  membrane stimulates cell proliferation, growth, and the fluid secretion  that cause cyst formation.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: The molecular mechanisms underlying polycystic kidney disease development  are not entirely understood. The pathogenesis of this disease  results from cyst formation in the renal tubules and the subsequent tubule  dysfunction. The cysts are probably formed as dilations in the renal tubules  as a result of increased cellular proliferation and growth. An abnormal  epithelial cell phenotype and extracellular matrix alterations result in spherical but not tubular structures.  Disruption of the activity of the polycystins on renal epithelial cell  membrane stimulates cell proliferation, growth, and the fluid secretion  that cause cyst formation.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-edbb6411-4d76-41bc-898c-62c81e2e02ab
name: 2_Dysfunction of cilia in polycystic kidney disease
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:polycystic_kidney_disease ! Polycystic kidney disease
