xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "If uropathogens penetrate in the kidney, they attach to urothelium,  move on it, and damage it. Different bacteria have their own mechanisms  of adhesion, colonization, damage causation, and avoidance of normal  protective factors. Despite this, kidney cells recognize pathogens by means  of toll-like receptors and provide an immune response via the production  of cytokines that recruit and activate immune cells.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: If uropathogens penetrate in the kidney, they attach to urothelium,  move on it, and damage it. Different bacteria have their own mechanisms  of adhesion, colonization, damage causation, and avoidance of normal  protective factors. Despite this, kidney cells recognize pathogens by means  of toll-like receptors and provide an immune response via the production  of cytokines that recruit and activate immune cells.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

