xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Angiogenesis is a critical process in the establishment and growth of endometriotic  lesions. The process of angiogenesis is stimulated by two central  pathways that involve vascular endothelial growth factor A (VEGFA)  and angiopoietin 1 (ANGPT1). Both VEGFA and ANGPT1 are strongly  overexpressed in endometriotic lesions.  VEGFA and ANGPT1 act as endothelial cell (EC) mitogens, enhancing  cell proliferation and migration and increasing the vascular permeability  in ectopic endometrium. Vascularization is necessary for the formation  and function of ectopic endometrium lesions.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Angiogenesis is a critical process in the establishment and growth of endometriotic  lesions. The process of angiogenesis is stimulated by two central  pathways that involve vascular endothelial growth factor A (VEGFA)  and angiopoietin 1 (ANGPT1). Both VEGFA and ANGPT1 are strongly  overexpressed in endometriotic lesions.  VEGFA and ANGPT1 act as endothelial cell (EC) mitogens, enhancing  cell proliferation and migration and increasing the vascular permeability  in ectopic endometrium. Vascularization is necessary for the formation  and function of ectopic endometrium lesions.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

