xref: PS:CellType "epithelial cell"
synonym: "CellType: epithelial cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ "eye"
synonym: "Organ: eye" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "sensory system"
synonym: "Organ_System: sensory system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Oxidative stress and the toxicity of all-trans-retinal and lipofuscin may  lead to RPE cell apoptosis, retinal inflammation, autoimmune response,  retinal drusen formation or choroidal neovascularization resulting in retina  degradation, and vision loss. Lipofuscin granules are by-products of  photoreceptor outer segment turnover and are seen within both healthy  and pathological RPE cells. Lipofuscin in RPE cells accumulates throughout  life and is readily detectable after age 40. Accumulation of lipofuscin  results in a significant increase in retinal phototoxicity.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Oxidative stress and the toxicity of all-trans-retinal and lipofuscin may  lead to RPE cell apoptosis, retinal inflammation, autoimmune response,  retinal drusen formation or choroidal neovascularization resulting in retina  degradation, and vision loss. Lipofuscin granules are by-products of  photoreceptor outer segment turnover and are seen within both healthy  and pathological RPE cells. Lipofuscin in RPE cells accumulates throughout  life and is readily detectable after age 40. Accumulation of lipofuscin  results in a significant increase in retinal phototoxicity.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

