xref: PS:Notes "Since cataract is a heterogeneous disease, several different mechanisms  have an impact on the development of the clinical features of the disease.  Calcium (Ca2+)-mediated toxicity in the lens cells is one of the major  pathological mechanisms leading to different forms of cataract. Further,  reactive oxygen species (ROS)–mediated and glucose-mediated toxicity  are considered underlying factors in the formation of age-related cataract.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Since cataract is a heterogeneous disease, several different mechanisms  have an impact on the development of the clinical features of the disease.  Calcium (Ca2+)-mediated toxicity in the lens cells is one of the major  pathological mechanisms leading to different forms of cataract. Further,  reactive oxygen species (ROS)–mediated and glucose-mediated toxicity  are considered underlying factors in the formation of age-related cataract.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

