id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-08700efc-83a8-4a74-b2c0-94541d1339f7
name: 2_Pathogens stimulate mucins expression in the middle ear
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:2 ! 2
is_a: urn:agi-folder:otitis_media ! Otitis media
xref: PS:Description "published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1"
synonym: "Description: published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-08700efc-83a8-4a74-b2c0-94541d1339f7"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-08700efc-83a8-4a74-b2c0-94541d1339f7" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "The Gram-positive bacterium S. pneumoniae, Gram-negative bacteria  nontypable H. influenza (NTHi) and M. catarrhalis synergistically induce  the activation of mucus production in the middle ear effusion of patients  with chronic otitis media. The viscous mucus of the middle ear is a heterogeneous  mixture of secreted polypeptides, mainly mucins. The rise of mucin  production is a vital defense response against invading microbes (also  see Asthma). Excess mucin production, however, results in a conductive  hearing loss observed in otitis media.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: The Gram-positive bacterium S. pneumoniae, Gram-negative bacteria  nontypable H. influenza (NTHi) and M. catarrhalis synergistically induce  the activation of mucus production in the middle ear effusion of patients  with chronic otitis media. The viscous mucus of the middle ear is a heterogeneous  mixture of secreted polypeptides, mainly mucins. The rise of mucin  production is a vital defense response against invading microbes (also  see Asthma). Excess mucin production, however, results in a conductive  hearing loss observed in otitis media.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

