synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-62bc9075-bbdf-4e78-b3ee-5ca28882f7f2" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Interaction of oxidated LDL (oxLDL) with vascular endothelial cells  (ECs) plays an important role in the progression of atherosclerosis. oxLDL  triggers endothelium dysfunction that is characterized by the decline of  anticoagulants and vasodilating properties while increasing the release  of proinflammatory mediators and ROS. A decrease in NO is considered  a hallmark of endothelial dysfunction.  The rapid increase of intracellular ROS results in vascular  endothelium dysfunction leading to ECM degradation, the attraction  of leukocytes and platelets, stimulation of blood clotting, and vasoconstriction.  Also, ROS cause apoptosis of epithelial cells, thus enhancing the  inflammatory reaction within the vessel. Reduction of NO causes constriction  of vascular smooth muscle cells (VSMCs) and narrowing of the  arterial lumen.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Interaction of oxidated LDL (oxLDL) with vascular endothelial cells  (ECs) plays an important role in the progression of atherosclerosis. oxLDL  triggers endothelium dysfunction that is characterized by the decline of  anticoagulants and vasodilating properties while increasing the release  of proinflammatory mediators and ROS. A decrease in NO is considered  a hallmark of endothelial dysfunction.  The rapid increase of intracellular ROS results in vascular  endothelium dysfunction leading to ECM degradation, the attraction  of leukocytes and platelets, stimulation of blood clotting, and vasoconstriction.  Also, ROS cause apoptosis of epithelial cells, thus enhancing the  inflammatory reaction within the vessel. Reduction of NO causes constriction  of vascular smooth muscle cells (VSMCs) and narrowing of the  arterial lumen.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

