xref: PS:Notes "Different molecular mechanisms increase vasoconstriction and weaken  vasodilation in PAH. Dysfunction of endothelial cells shifts the balance to  vasoconstriction and is present in all types of PAH.  The decreased production of NO and prostacyclin by endothelial cells  provokes vasoconstriction. Increased secretion of the EDN1, vascular endothelial  growth factor A (VEGFA), and serotonin causes endothelial cell  proliferation, which in turn leads to artery lumen narrowing and a predisposition  to thrombosis.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Different molecular mechanisms increase vasoconstriction and weaken  vasodilation in PAH. Dysfunction of endothelial cells shifts the balance to  vasoconstriction and is present in all types of PAH.  The decreased production of NO and prostacyclin by endothelial cells  provokes vasoconstriction. Increased secretion of the EDN1, vascular endothelial  growth factor A (VEGFA), and serotonin causes endothelial cell  proliferation, which in turn leads to artery lumen narrowing and a predisposition  to thrombosis.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

