xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Familial pulmonary arterial hypertension (FPAH) is associated with  mutations in the genes encoding bone morphogenetic protein receptor  type 2 (BMPR2), activin A receptor-like type 1 (ACVRL1), endoglin (ENG),  and some other genes.  In FPAH and  IPAH the BMP and TGFB1 signaling pathways are not fully activated,  and the balance between PASMC proliferation and differentiation shifts  toward proliferation. Excessive PASMC proliferation leads to pulmonary  artery wall thickening, lumen narrowing, elevation of pulmonary vascular  resistance, and the development of pulmonary hypertension.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Familial pulmonary arterial hypertension (FPAH) is associated with  mutations in the genes encoding bone morphogenetic protein receptor  type 2 (BMPR2), activin A receptor-like type 1 (ACVRL1), endoglin (ENG),  and some other genes.  In FPAH and  IPAH the BMP and TGFB1 signaling pathways are not fully activated,  and the balance between PASMC proliferation and differentiation shifts  toward proliferation. Excessive PASMC proliferation leads to pulmonary  artery wall thickening, lumen narrowing, elevation of pulmonary vascular  resistance, and the development of pulmonary hypertension.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

