xref: PS:Notes "Desmosomes are major cell-cell junctions that are particularly abundant  in epidermal cells and cardiomyocytes. ARVD may be caused by genetic  defects of the structure of myocardial desmosomes. Desmosomes are multiprotein  complexes that form intercellular contacts on the surface of heart  muscle cells. Mutations in many proteins that comprise desmosomes can  have harmful effects on cardiomyocyte function.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Desmosomes are major cell-cell junctions that are particularly abundant  in epidermal cells and cardiomyocytes. ARVD may be caused by genetic  defects of the structure of myocardial desmosomes. Desmosomes are multiprotein  complexes that form intercellular contacts on the surface of heart  muscle cells. Mutations in many proteins that comprise desmosomes can  have harmful effects on cardiomyocyte function.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

