xref: PS:Notes "Although the majority of ARVD-causing mutations are in genes encoding  desmosomal proteins, a few ARVD mutations have been detected in  genes unrelated to intercellular junction complexes.  Mutated proteins cause cardiomyocyte dysfunction due to defective  force transmission between cells, the disruption of normal excitation-contraction  coupling, and impairment of cardiomyocyte adhesion and  fibrosis induction.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Although the majority of ARVD-causing mutations are in genes encoding  desmosomal proteins, a few ARVD mutations have been detected in  genes unrelated to intercellular junction complexes.  Mutated proteins cause cardiomyocyte dysfunction due to defective  force transmission between cells, the disruption of normal excitation-contraction  coupling, and impairment of cardiomyocyte adhesion and  fibrosis induction.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

