xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "An imbalance in the number of factors regulating cardiovascular system  activity may cause the observed increase in arterial pressure. For example,  higher levels of aldosterone change salt and water homeostasis  that in turn leads to hypertension.  Aldosterone plays an essential role in salt and water homeostasis and  correspondingly in blood pressure regulation. Chronic activation of the aldosterone  secretion system (specifically the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone  system, RAAS) is a major contributing factor to the pathogenesis and progression  of arterial hypertension.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: An imbalance in the number of factors regulating cardiovascular system  activity may cause the observed increase in arterial pressure. For example,  higher levels of aldosterone change salt and water homeostasis  that in turn leads to hypertension.  Aldosterone plays an essential role in salt and water homeostasis and  correspondingly in blood pressure regulation. Chronic activation of the aldosterone  secretion system (specifically the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone  system, RAAS) is a major contributing factor to the pathogenesis and progression  of arterial hypertension.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

[Term]
