synonym: "CellType: epithelial cell" EXACT []
xref: PS:Organ_System "urinary tract"
synonym: "Organ_System: urinary tract" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Aldosterone regulates the activity of ion channels that control electrolyte  transport across epithelia in the nephron. Those channels are responsible  for Na+ and Cl- reabsorption into the blood and K+ excretion in the  distal renal tubules.  Excessive Na+ levels in plasma are the reason for increased blood volume  and high blood pressure. So the maintenance of Na+/Cl-/K+ homeostasis  by the kidney system is necessary for the maintenance of normal  concentrations of ions and healthy blood pressure regulation.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Aldosterone regulates the activity of ion channels that control electrolyte  transport across epithelia in the nephron. Those channels are responsible  for Na+ and Cl- reabsorption into the blood and K+ excretion in the  distal renal tubules.  Excessive Na+ levels in plasma are the reason for increased blood volume  and high blood pressure. So the maintenance of Na+/Cl-/K+ homeostasis  by the kidney system is necessary for the maintenance of normal  concentrations of ions and healthy blood pressure regulation.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

