xref: PS:Notes "Alveolar macrophages localize at the boundary between  the lungs and external environment. Macrophages are responsible  for the removal of particles, such as dust or microorganisms, from the respiratory  surfaces by phagocytosis. To be effective, they must maintain a  high level of activity.  Chronic lung inflammation and tissue remodeling by proteolytic enzymes  are the consequence of sustained macrophage activation in COPD.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Alveolar macrophages localize at the boundary between  the lungs and external environment. Macrophages are responsible  for the removal of particles, such as dust or microorganisms, from the respiratory  surfaces by phagocytosis. To be effective, they must maintain a  high level of activity.  Chronic lung inflammation and tissue remodeling by proteolytic enzymes  are the consequence of sustained macrophage activation in COPD.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

