xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Many patients with allergic asthma have an immunological reaction  that is driven predominantly by type 2 T-helper cells (Th2 cells), but not  Th1 cells. Th2 cell reactions are associated with the production of immunoglobulin  E (IgE) by B cells, activation of eosinophils, and the involvement  of other cells and mediators that enhance the characteristic bronchial  hyperresponsiveness.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Many patients with allergic asthma have an immunological reaction  that is driven predominantly by type 2 T-helper cells (Th2 cells), but not  Th1 cells. Th2 cell reactions are associated with the production of immunoglobulin  E (IgE) by B cells, activation of eosinophils, and the involvement  of other cells and mediators that enhance the characteristic bronchial  hyperresponsiveness.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

