xref: PS:Notes "Mucus overproduction is a central feature of bronchial asthma,  contributing  to mortality seen in the disease. Goblet cells are the primary  mucus-producing cells. In asthma the airway surface liquid (ASL) thickness  increases due to the overflow of water and the secretion of adds to  excessive mucin, which accumulations in the lungs with asthma.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
