xref: PS:Notes "Eosinophilic and/or neutrophilic inflammation is an important sign of  allergic asthma. In asthma, eosinophils are attracted to the lungs by cytokines  released by Th2 cells. In the lungs, eosinophils release the content of  their granules, which leads to cellular damage. On the other hand, airway  neutrophilia is one of the hallmarks of severe asthma.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Eosinophilic and/or neutrophilic inflammation is an important sign of  allergic asthma. In asthma, eosinophils are attracted to the lungs by cytokines  released by Th2 cells. In the lungs, eosinophils release the content of  their granules, which leads to cellular damage. On the other hand, airway  neutrophilia is one of the hallmarks of severe asthma.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

