id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-6dd7f23e-7a0b-4e4f-a26a-0b0319d0324c
name: 2_2_Eosinophilia and neutrophilia in asthma: eosinophil apoptosis
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:2 ! 2
is_a: urn:agi-folder:asthma ! Asthma
xref: PS:Description "published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1"
synonym: "Description: published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-6dd7f23e-7a0b-4e4f-a26a-0b0319d0324c"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-6dd7f23e-7a0b-4e4f-a26a-0b0319d0324c" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "In the absence of prosurvival factors, neutrophils, eosinophils, and basophils  die by intrinsic apoptosis within a short time after maturation. The  apoptosis and clearance of eosinophils by macrophages are attenuated in  asthma.  TGFB1 and other ligands bind to the death receptor FAS to stimulate  eosinophil apoptosis and apoptosis of other cells (not shown).  Sialic acid–binding Ig-like lectin 8 (SIGLEC8) is an important target  for asthma-related drug target research.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: In the absence of prosurvival factors, neutrophils, eosinophils, and basophils  die by intrinsic apoptosis within a short time after maturation. The  apoptosis and clearance of eosinophils by macrophages are attenuated in  asthma.  TGFB1 and other ligands bind to the death receptor FAS to stimulate  eosinophil apoptosis and apoptosis of other cells (not shown).  Sialic acid–binding Ig-like lectin 8 (SIGLEC8) is an important target  for asthma-related drug target research.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

