name: 1_Triglyceride storage in NAFLD
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:non-alcoholic_fatty_liver_disease ! Non-alcoholic fatty liver disease
is_a: urn:agi-folder:1 ! 1
is_a: urn:agi-folder:nonalcoholic_fatty_liver_disease ! Nonalcoholic fatty liver disease
xref: PS:Description "published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1"
synonym: "Description: published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-86e5842a-32a8-4fc2-914b-85e7676552bc"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-86e5842a-32a8-4fc2-914b-85e7676552bc" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Derivatives of lipids and fatty acids (palmitic acid, stearic acid, and oleic acid) in triglycerides  (TGs) are stored in cytoplasmic lipid droplets and used as a  source of energy.  A common clinical feature of patients with NAFLD is impaired lipid metabolism  associated with obesity, insulin resistance (IR), and hyperinsulinemia.  TGs accumulate in cytoplasmic lipid droplets forming steatosis.  Mitochondria in hepatocytes try to adapt to increased FFAs by enhancing  their beta-oxidation rate (the metabolic process of fatty acids degradation).  However, increased transport of beta oxidation–derived products  leads to increased reactive oxygen species (ROS) release. Excessive ROS  release causes oxidative stress (not shown) leading to mitochondrial impairment  and further hepatocyte dysfunction.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Derivatives of lipids and fatty acids (palmitic acid, stearic acid, and oleic acid) in triglycerides  (TGs) are stored in cytoplasmic lipid droplets and used as a  source of energy.  A common clinical feature of patients with NAFLD is impaired lipid metabolism  associated with obesity, insulin resistance (IR), and hyperinsulinemia.  TGs accumulate in cytoplasmic lipid droplets forming steatosis.  Mitochondria in hepatocytes try to adapt to increased FFAs by enhancing  their beta-oxidation rate (the metabolic process of fatty acids degradation).  However, increased transport of beta oxidation–derived products  leads to increased reactive oxygen species (ROS) release. Excessive ROS  release causes oxidative stress (not shown) leading to mitochondrial impairment  and further hepatocyte dysfunction.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

