xref: PS:Notes "CD4+ gluten-specific T-helper (Th) cells in celiac disease  recognize deamidated gluten-derived peptides presented by either  HLA-DQ2 or HLA-DQ8 as antigens, and they respond to those peptides  by expressing high levels of inflammatory cytokines. These cytokines in  turn affect the epithelial cells and activate intraepithelial lymphocytes.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: CD4+ gluten-specific T-helper (Th) cells in celiac disease  recognize deamidated gluten-derived peptides presented by either  HLA-DQ2 or HLA-DQ8 as antigens, and they respond to those peptides  by expressing high levels of inflammatory cytokines. These cytokines in  turn affect the epithelial cells and activate intraepithelial lymphocytes.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

