xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "The HTLVs need cell cycle progression and transition through the mitotic  phases for viral reproduction. The viral tax protein actively interacts  with and regulates some of T-cell proteins that regulate phase changes in  the cell cycle and thereby stimulate mitosis in the host cell. The activation of cell cycle progression diminishes the effectiveness of  DNA repair, and consequently, mutations accumulate in the host cell’s genome.  Persistent DNA repair mechanisms and related cellular processes  lead to T-cell death or transformation.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: The HTLVs need cell cycle progression and transition through the mitotic  phases for viral reproduction. The viral tax protein actively interacts  with and regulates some of T-cell proteins that regulate phase changes in  the cell cycle and thereby stimulate mitosis in the host cell. The activation of cell cycle progression diminishes the effectiveness of  DNA repair, and consequently, mutations accumulate in the host cell’s genome.  Persistent DNA repair mechanisms and related cellular processes  lead to T-cell death or transformation.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

