synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Interaction of viral and cellular proteins is needed for transcription and  replication of the viral genome. As virion particles or viral RNA are engulfed by the host cell, structural  proteins of the virus complete reverse transcription of the viral genome.  The newly synthesized viral DNA then incorporates into the host  genome. Expression of the virus regulatory proteins (tax, rex, p30II, p13II,  and HBZ) is necessary for viral genome replication and for transcription  of virus genes. However, the virus needs proteins of the host cell to complete  these processes.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Interaction of viral and cellular proteins is needed for transcription and  replication of the viral genome. As virion particles or viral RNA are engulfed by the host cell, structural  proteins of the virus complete reverse transcription of the viral genome.  The newly synthesized viral DNA then incorporates into the host  genome. Expression of the virus regulatory proteins (tax, rex, p30II, p13II,  and HBZ) is necessary for viral genome replication and for transcription  of virus genes. However, the virus needs proteins of the host cell to complete  these processes.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

