synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-4b62d9fd-517d-4489-a81a-ffae17622cb8" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "In order to be released into the blood after absorption, iron needs the  transporter SLC40A1. HAMP can block the transport of iron by SLC40A1.   Iron is required for erythropoiesis, oxygen transport, and a plethora of  other biological functions. When HAMP blocks the release of iron from  enterocytes, anemia gradually develops.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: In order to be released into the blood after absorption, iron needs the  transporter SLC40A1. HAMP can block the transport of iron by SLC40A1.   Iron is required for erythropoiesis, oxygen transport, and a plethora of  other biological functions. When HAMP blocks the release of iron from  enterocytes, anemia gradually develops.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

