synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-6f097b0e-d868-4a11-a6db-fb000918a772" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "In macrophage, inflammatory mediators upregulate the synthesis  of the major intracellular iron storage protein ferritin and stimulate  the ferritin-bound deposition of iron. In AI/ACD the levels of HAMP  secreted from hepatocytes is higher than normal. HAMP can inhibit iron export by binding to the iron  transporter ferroportin (SLC40A1), which is present on macrophages  to trigger its degradation. Bacterial infection may also cause the downregulation  of SLC40A1 synthesis.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: In macrophage, inflammatory mediators upregulate the synthesis  of the major intracellular iron storage protein ferritin and stimulate  the ferritin-bound deposition of iron. In AI/ACD the levels of HAMP  secreted from hepatocytes is higher than normal. HAMP can inhibit iron export by binding to the iron  transporter ferroportin (SLC40A1), which is present on macrophages  to trigger its degradation. Bacterial infection may also cause the downregulation  of SLC40A1 synthesis.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-24ed122c-0dfb-4ff2-a095-a03b7fd0b0d0
name: 1_Inflammatory mediators increase the production of hepcidin (HAMP)
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:anemia ! Anemia
is_a: urn:agi-folder:1 ! 1
xref: PS:Description "published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1"
synonym: "Description: published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-24ed122c-0dfb-4ff2-a095-a03b7fd0b0d0"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-24ed122c-0dfb-4ff2-a095-a03b7fd0b0d0" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "During general inflammation, there is an increase in the synthesis of  interleukins and other mediators by different types of cells. The interleukins  IL-6 and IL-22 and also activin B are thought to be the primary  regulators of inflammatory anemia. Inflammatory mediators induce production of HAMP  by hepatocytes. HAMP released to the blood from the liver regulates the systemic  iron balance—it prevents iron release from enterocytes and macrophages  (see Pathways 2 and 3).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: During general inflammation, there is an increase in the synthesis of  interleukins and other mediators by different types of cells. The interleukins  IL-6 and IL-22 and also activin B are thought to be the primary  regulators of inflammatory anemia. Inflammatory mediators induce production of HAMP  by hepatocytes. HAMP released to the blood from the liver regulates the systemic  iron balance—it prevents iron release from enterocytes and macrophages  (see Pathways 2 and 3).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

