xref: PS:Notes "Endogenous and exogenous erythropoietins inhibit HAMP expression  and stimulate erythrocyte differentiation. Erythropoietin (EPO) production  is reduced in AI/ACD. Erythropoietin substitutive drugs are actively used for the treatment of  AI/ACD. Restored EPO functions to reactivate erythrocyte differentiation  and facilitate the inhibition of HAMP. The inhibition of HAMP returns  iron exported from enterocytes, splenic macrophages, and hepatocytes to  the blood and thereby restores the systemic iron balance.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Endogenous and exogenous erythropoietins inhibit HAMP expression  and stimulate erythrocyte differentiation. Erythropoietin (EPO) production  is reduced in AI/ACD. Erythropoietin substitutive drugs are actively used for the treatment of  AI/ACD. Restored EPO functions to reactivate erythrocyte differentiation  and facilitate the inhibition of HAMP. The inhibition of HAMP returns  iron exported from enterocytes, splenic macrophages, and hepatocytes to  the blood and thereby restores the systemic iron balance.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

