xref: PS:Notes "As beta-cell death progresses, the pancreas compensates for the loss of  beta cells by increasing insulin production. The mass of beta cell decreases  until the ability of the pancreas to compensate for their loss is exceeded:  Pathway 3. Beta-cell proliferation and compensation:  Proliferation (Fig. 4).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: As beta-cell death progresses, the pancreas compensates for the loss of  beta cells by increasing insulin production. The mass of beta cell decreases  until the ability of the pancreas to compensate for their loss is exceeded:  Pathway 3. Beta-cell proliferation and compensation:  Proliferation (Fig. 4).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

