id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-eef2af5b-a6be-4f5a-93c2-4940952285ab
name: 1_2_Insulin synthesis and secretion: insulin secretion
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:1 ! 1
is_a: urn:agi-folder:diabetes_mellitus_type_2 ! Diabetes mellitus type 2
xref: PS:Description "published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1"
synonym: "Description: published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-eef2af5b-a6be-4f5a-93c2-4940952285ab"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-eef2af5b-a6be-4f5a-93c2-4940952285ab" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "The release of insulin from the pancreas is not continuous, but instead,  it oscillates with a period of approximately 3–6 min. Pulsatile insulin secretion  from individual beta cells is driven by the oscillation of intracellular  Ca2 levels, cyclic pacing of cellular metabolism, and the intracellular  ATP/ADP ratio. The process of insulin secretion, like any exocytosis event, involves  secretory granule trafficking, tethering, docking, priming, and fusion  with the cell membrane.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: The release of insulin from the pancreas is not continuous, but instead,  it oscillates with a period of approximately 3–6 min. Pulsatile insulin secretion  from individual beta cells is driven by the oscillation of intracellular  Ca2 levels, cyclic pacing of cellular metabolism, and the intracellular  ATP/ADP ratio. The process of insulin secretion, like any exocytosis event, involves  secretory granule trafficking, tethering, docking, priming, and fusion  with the cell membrane.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

