name: 1_1_Insulin synthesis and secretion: insulin processing and storage
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:1 ! 1
is_a: urn:agi-folder:diabetes_mellitus_type_2 ! Diabetes mellitus type 2
xref: PS:Description "published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1"
synonym: "Description: published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1" EXACT []
xref: PS:Pathway_Author "A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101"
synonym: "Pathway_Author: A. Nesterova ORCID:0000-0002-9448-8101" EXACT []
xref: PS:Link "https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-ccfe3b69-dd28-47ee-b352-993e586cfa31"
synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-ccfe3b69-dd28-47ee-b352-993e586cfa31" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Diabetes mellitus type 2 is a pathology that slowly develops over time.  Each stage of T2D is characterized by abnormalities on the cellular and  tissue levels. At the prediabetes stages, a significant number of pancreatic  beta cells become dysfunctional although they still secrete sufficient levels  of insulin.  Functional endopeptidases cleave proinsulin to release a fragment called  the C-peptide (connecting peptide) and two other peptide chains, B- and  A-, which together comprise the mature insulin. Insulin, C-peptide, and  IAPP are then stored in the secretory granules in the beta cell. Insulin is  stored as a crystal chelated with Zn2 in large dense-core secretory granules  known as beta-granules.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Diabetes mellitus type 2 is a pathology that slowly develops over time.  Each stage of T2D is characterized by abnormalities on the cellular and  tissue levels. At the prediabetes stages, a significant number of pancreatic  beta cells become dysfunctional although they still secrete sufficient levels  of insulin.  Functional endopeptidases cleave proinsulin to release a fragment called  the C-peptide (connecting peptide) and two other peptide chains, B- and  A-, which together comprise the mature insulin. Insulin, C-peptide, and  IAPP are then stored in the secretory granules in the beta cell. Insulin is  stored as a crystal chelated with Zn2 in large dense-core secretory granules  known as beta-granules.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

[Term]
