synonym: "Link: https://mammal-profservices.pathwaystudio.com/app/sd?urn=urn:agi-pathway:uuid-17d26a47-f753-4716-8631-2e9846699a86" EXACT []
xref: PS:PathwayType "signaling"
synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "The diversity of CFTR mutations in cystic fibrosis determines the penetrance  of the disease. Six different classes of mutations in the CFTR gene  have been linked to cystic fibrosis. Class I mutations  affect the biosynthesis of CFTR and include the most severe CF  phenotypes in which no protein is synthesized. Class II mutations result  in folding defects of the CFTR protein. The class II mutation delta F508  (Phe508del mutation) is the most common genetic alteration in cystic fibrosis  and leads to the deletion of phenylalanine at position 508.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: The diversity of CFTR mutations in cystic fibrosis determines the penetrance  of the disease. Six different classes of mutations in the CFTR gene  have been linked to cystic fibrosis. Class I mutations  affect the biosynthesis of CFTR and include the most severe CF  phenotypes in which no protein is synthesized. Class II mutations result  in folding defects of the CFTR protein. The class II mutation delta F508  (Phe508del mutation) is the most common genetic alteration in cystic fibrosis  and leads to the deletion of phenylalanine at position 508.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

[Term]
id: urn:agi-pathway:uuid-3b2de982-5704-4d04-bbec-12a6015668a9
name: 2_Ion channel CFTR failure in cystic fibrosis airway epithelium (class III-IV mutations)
xref: PS:NodeType "Pathway"
synonym: "NodeType: Pathway" EXACT []
is_a: urn:agi-folder:2 ! 2
is_a: urn:agi-folder:cystic_fibrosis ! Cystic fibrosis
xref: PS:Description "published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1"
synonym: "Description: published in: Disease Pathways: An Atlas of Human Disease Pathways, 2019 https://www.elsevier.com/books/disease-pathways/nesterova/978-0-12-817086-1" EXACT []
