synonym: "PathwayType: signaling" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "The chronic hyperglycemia characteristic of diabetes causes damage  to the microvessels (microangiopathy), resulting in impaired nutrition of  peripheral nerve fibers. The limited vascular supply to peripheral nerves  also makes nerves fibers susceptible to ischemia/hypoxia. Damage to the  perineurium microvessels is likely the most critical factor in neuronal injury  and dysfunction in DN.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: The chronic hyperglycemia characteristic of diabetes causes damage  to the microvessels (microangiopathy), resulting in impaired nutrition of  peripheral nerve fibers. The limited vascular supply to peripheral nerves  also makes nerves fibers susceptible to ischemia/hypoxia. Damage to the  perineurium microvessels is likely the most critical factor in neuronal injury  and dysfunction in DN.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

