xref: PS:Organelle "plasma membrane"
synonym: "Organelle: plasma membrane" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "Known mutations associated with FHM are the basis of glutamate and  K+ accumulation in the synapse. Excess glutamate leads to the release of increased levels of K+ in the  synaptic cleft. Excess K+ results in postsynaptic membrane depolarization, which  plays an important role in the progression of cortical depression  (spreading depolarization, cortical spreading depression, CSD).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Known mutations associated with FHM are the basis of glutamate and  K+ accumulation in the synapse. Excess glutamate leads to the release of increased levels of K+ in the  synaptic cleft. Excess K+ results in postsynaptic membrane depolarization, which  plays an important role in the progression of cortical depression  (spreading depolarization, cortical spreading depression, CSD).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

