xref: PS:Organ_System "nervous system"
synonym: "Organ_System: nervous system" EXACT []
xref: PS:Source "Atlas"
synonym: "Source: Atlas" EXACT []
xref: PS:Notes "High levels of glutamate in the synaptic cleft are found in each type of  a hemiplegic migraine (familial and sporadic). Excess glutamate triggers the synthesis of high levels of prostaglandin  E2 (PGE2) and nitric oxide (NO) by both neurons and astrocytes in  migraines. Increased amounts of PGE2 were detected in patients prior to  and during a migraine attack. Synthesized in neurons and astrocytes, PGE2 and NO in turn induce  the synthesis of NO in endothelial cells and smooth muscle cells in dura  meter.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: High levels of glutamate in the synaptic cleft are found in each type of  a hemiplegic migraine (familial and sporadic). Excess glutamate triggers the synthesis of high levels of prostaglandin  E2 (PGE2) and nitric oxide (NO) by both neurons and astrocytes in  migraines. Increased amounts of PGE2 were detected in patients prior to  and during a migraine attack. Synthesized in neurons and astrocytes, PGE2 and NO in turn induce  the synthesis of NO in endothelial cells and smooth muscle cells in dura  meter.    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

