xref: PS:Notes "Iodine and hormones released by the hypothalamus and the pituitary  gland are primary regulators of thyroid gland function. However, other  triggers also may affect the function of thyroid follicular cells leading to  decreased secretion of the thyroid hormones, namely, triiodothyronine  (T3) and thyroxine (T4).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey."
synonym: "Notes: Iodine and hormones released by the hypothalamus and the pituitary  gland are primary regulators of thyroid gland function. However, other  triggers also may affect the function of thyroid follicular cells leading to  decreased secretion of the thyroid hormones, namely, triiodothyronine  (T3) and thyroxine (T4).    Entitiy with increased expression or activity is highlighted in red. Entity with low activity is highlighted in blue. Mutated genes are shown in white-out style. Viral proteins are grey." EXACT []

